// Auto-generated for the Unit Board (Zone 4: Verbal Advantage Lv.1–5 / 字彙的力量1)
window.VA_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit": 1, "level": 1, "cards": [{"w": "paraphrase", "p": "v.", "d": "To restate something in different words.", "c": "改述；釋義", "s": "Rather than copying the scientist's dense explanation word for word, the journalist chose to paraphrase it in plain language, so that readers without a background in genetics could follow the argument about inherited disease risk.", "t": "這位記者沒有逐字照抄科學家艱澀的解釋，而是選擇用淺白的語言加以改述，讓沒有遺傳學背景的讀者也能理解有關遺傳疾病風險的論點。", "as": "Asked to paraphrase the verbose committee report, the intern produced a terse one-page summary that preserved every key finding while omitting the authors' lengthy remarks on minor procedural matters.", "at": "被要求改述那份冗長的委員會報告時，這名實習生寫出一份簡潔的一頁摘要，保留了每一項重要發現，同時刪去作者對枝微末節程序問題的冗長評論。"}, {"w": "ostensible", "p": "adj.", "d": "Appearing or claimed to be true, but perhaps not actually so.", "c": "表面上的；表面宣稱的", "s": "The ostensible purpose of the 1880s railway survey was to map farmland for settlers, but historians now argue that the expedition's real goal was to locate coal deposits for wealthy investors back east.", "t": "1880年代那次鐵路勘測表面上的目的是為移民繪製農地地圖，但歷史學家如今認為，這支探勘隊真正的目標是替東部富有的投資者尋找煤礦。", "as": "Although the ostensible reason for the minister's visit was a ceremonial ribbon-cutting, observers noted the clandestine meetings he held with rival officials and suspected that a tacit agreement was being negotiated.", "at": "雖然部長此行表面上的理由是出席剪綵典禮，但觀察人士注意到他與敵對官員舉行的秘密會議，並懷疑雙方正在協商一項心照不宣的協議。"}, {"w": "digress", "p": "v.", "d": "To stray from the main topic in speaking or writing.", "c": "離題；偏離主題", "s": "Professor Lin warned her students that essays which digress into unrelated personal anecdotes would lose points, because the assignment required a focused analysis of how the Treaty of Shimonoseki reshaped Taiwan's colonial administration.", "t": "林教授提醒學生，若文章離題去寫無關的個人軼事就會被扣分，因為這份作業要求的是聚焦分析《馬關條約》如何重塑台灣的殖民統治。", "as": "The garrulous tour guide tended to digress from the museum's history into long stories about his childhood, yet his candor and droll humor made most visitors forgive the detours.", "at": "這位多話的導覽員常常從博物館的歷史離題，講起自己童年的長篇故事，但他的坦率和詼諧的幽默感讓大多數遊客都原諒了這些岔題。"}, {"w": "uncanny", "p": "adj.", "d": "Strange or mysterious in a way that is hard to explain.", "c": "不可思議的；神秘的", "s": "The young chess player displayed an uncanny ability to predict her opponents' moves several turns in advance, a talent so mysterious that even veteran coaches struggled to explain how she calculated the possibilities so quickly.", "t": "這位年輕棋手展現出一種不可思議的能力，能提前好幾步預測對手的走法，這種天賦神秘到連資深教練都難以解釋她是如何如此迅速地算出各種可能。", "as": "The novelist's uncanny portrait of a morose, aloof detective struck readers as almost autobiographical, though she insisted the character was pure invention drawn from no real person.", "at": "這位小說家對一名陰鬱又冷漠的偵探的描寫逼真得不可思議，讓讀者覺得幾乎像是自傳，但她堅稱這個角色純屬虛構，並非取材自任何真人。"}, {"w": "candor", "p": "n.", "d": "Honest, open, and sincere expression; frankness.", "c": "坦率；直言不諱", "s": "Voters praised the senator's candor when she admitted during a televised town hall that her earlier housing policy had failed, explaining exactly which predictions were wrong instead of blaming her opponents or the economy.", "t": "這位參議員在一場電視轉播的市民座談會上坦承她先前的住宅政策失敗，並具體說明哪些預測出了錯，而不是歸咎於對手或經濟情勢，選民對她的坦率讚譽有加。", "as": "The memoir's unflinching candor about the author's own complicity in the political scandal surprised critics, who had expected a self-serving narrative full of evasive platitudes.", "at": "這本回憶錄毫不避諱地坦白作者本人在這起政治醜聞中的共謀角色，令評論家大感意外，因為他們原本預期會讀到一篇充滿閃爍其詞的陳腔濫調、只為自己開脫的敘述。"}, {"w": "morose", "p": "adj.", "d": "Gloomy, sullen, and in a bad mood.", "c": "陰鬱的；悶悶不樂的", "s": "After his research grant was rejected for the third time, the usually cheerful biologist became morose and withdrawn, sitting silently through lab meetings and refusing invitations to lunch with colleagues who tried to lift his spirits.", "t": "在研究經費第三度被駁回後，這位平時開朗的生物學家變得陰鬱又孤僻，在實驗室會議上一語不發，也婉拒了想讓他振作起來的同事們的午餐邀約。", "as": "Though critics found the poet's late verses morose and lugubrious, her admirers argued that their bleak imagery reflected not despair but a stoic acceptance of mortality.", "at": "雖然評論家認為這位詩人晚年的詩作陰鬱而悲淒，她的仰慕者卻主張，那些淒涼的意象反映的並非絕望，而是以堅忍的態度坦然接受生命的有限。"}, {"w": "adept", "p": "adj.", "d": "Highly skilled or proficient at something.", "c": "熟練的；擅長的", "s": "Having spent three summers volunteering at a wildlife rescue center, Mei became adept at handling injured birds, calmly wrapping their wings and administering medicine with a confidence that impressed even the veterinarians on staff.", "t": "在野生動物救援中心當了三個暑假的志工後，小美變得很擅長照顧受傷的鳥類，她能冷靜地包紮牠們的翅膀並餵藥，那份自信連中心裡的獸醫都印象深刻。", "as": "An adept negotiator, the envoy managed to mollify both factions and reconcile their competing claims without making a single concession that her government would later regret.", "at": "這位特使是一名老練的談判者，她設法安撫了雙方派系，調和了彼此衝突的主張，而且沒有做出任何一項日後會令本國政府後悔的讓步。"}, {"w": "saturated", "p": "adj.", "d": "Completely filled or soaked with something.", "c": "浸透的；飽和的", "s": "After four days of typhoon rain, the hillside soil was so saturated that it could absorb no more water, and geologists warned residents of the mountain village that a landslide could occur at any moment.", "t": "經過四天的颱風豪雨，山坡上的土壤已飽和到無法再吸收任何水分，地質學家警告山村居民隨時可能發生山崩。", "as": "Analysts argued that the saturated market for streaming services had become a morass of copycat platforms, each offering a myriad of nearly identical dramas and reality shows.", "at": "分析師認為，已經飽和的串流服務市場淪為一灘充斥模仿者的泥淖，每個平台都提供無數幾乎一模一樣的戲劇和實境節目。"}, {"w": "pragmatic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Dealing with problems in a practical, sensible way.", "c": "務實的；講求實際的", "s": "Instead of waiting years for funding to build a new library, the pragmatic principal converted an unused storage room into a reading space, borrowing shelves from local businesses and asking parents to donate books.", "t": "這位務實的校長沒有花好幾年等待經費興建新圖書館，而是將一間閒置的儲藏室改造成閱讀空間，向在地商家借來書架，並請家長捐書。", "as": "Rejecting quixotic schemes to rebuild the entire transit network at once, the pragmatic mayor chose to ameliorate congestion through modest, incremental improvements to existing bus routes.", "at": "這位務實的市長否決了一口氣重建整個交通網路的不切實際計畫，選擇透過對現有公車路線進行適度、漸進的改善來緩解交通壅塞。"}, {"w": "congenial", "p": "adj.", "d": "Pleasant and friendly; agreeable to one's tastes or nature.", "c": "意氣相投的；令人愉快的", "s": "The exchange students quickly found their host families congenial, sharing meals, jokes, and weekend trips to the night markets, so that by the end of the semester many of them were reluctant to return home.", "t": "這些交換學生很快就發現寄宿家庭親切又合得來，大家一起吃飯、說笑、週末去逛夜市，以致到學期結束時，許多學生都捨不得回國。", "as": "The research team proved remarkably congenial, and its jovial weekly dinners fostered such convivial camaraderie that even the most aloof newcomers soon joined the conversation.", "at": "這個研究團隊相處得格外融洽，每週一次歡樂的聚餐培養出熱絡的同袍情誼，就連最冷漠的新成員也很快加入了談話。"}, {"w": "capricious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Changing suddenly and unpredictably; impulsive.", "c": "反覆無常的；善變的", "s": "Farmers in the region have learned to plant several different crops each season, because the capricious mountain weather can shift from bright sunshine to hailstorms within a single afternoon, destroying an entire harvest without warning.", "t": "該地區的農民學會了每一季都種植好幾種不同的作物，因為反覆無常的山區天氣可能在一個下午之內就從陽光普照轉為冰雹，毫無預警地摧毀整季收成。", "as": "The emperor's capricious edicts, issued and rescinded within weeks, left provincial officials paralyzed, unsure whether obeying an order might later be construed as an act of treason.", "at": "皇帝反覆無常的詔令往往在數週內頒布又撤銷，令地方官員無所適從，不確定服從某道命令日後是否會被解讀為叛國之舉。"}, {"w": "blatant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Very obvious and done openly, often shamelessly.", "c": "公然的；明目張膽的", "s": "The judges disqualified the science fair project after discovering that whole paragraphs of its report had been copied from a university website, calling it a blatant violation of the competition's rules on academic honesty.", "t": "評審發現該科展作品的報告整段整段抄自某大學網站後，取消了它的參賽資格，並稱這是公然違反競賽學術誠信規定的行為。", "as": "The senator's blatant attempt to obfuscate the budget figures provoked fervent censure from independent auditors, who accused him of deliberately hiding the growing deficit from taxpayers.", "at": "這位參議員公然企圖混淆預算數字，招致獨立審計人員強烈的譴責，指控他刻意向納稅人隱瞞日益擴大的赤字。"}, {"w": "obligatory", "p": "adj.", "d": "Required by law, rule, or custom; compulsory.", "c": "義務的；強制的", "s": "At many Taiwanese universities, a physical education course is obligatory for all first-year students, so even computer science majors who rarely exercise must pass swimming or basketball before they can graduate.", "t": "在台灣許多大學，體育課是所有大一新生的必修課，所以即使是很少運動的資訊工程系學生，也必須通過游泳或籃球課才能畢業。", "as": "Wearing a helmet is obligatory on the construction site, and the foreman, adamant about safety, will censure any worker who flouts the rule, even for a moment.", "at": "在工地戴安全帽是強制規定，而對安全問題態度堅決的工頭，會嚴厲斥責任何違反規定的工人，即使只是片刻也不例外。"}, {"w": "negligible", "p": "adj.", "d": "So small or unimportant that it can be ignored.", "c": "微不足道的；可忽略的", "s": "Engineers concluded that the tiny crack in the bridge's support beam posed a negligible risk, since tests showed it had not grown in ten years and would not affect the structure's strength under normal traffic.", "t": "工程師的結論是，橋梁支撐樑上那道細小的裂縫所構成的風險微乎其微，因為檢測顯示它十年來並未擴大，在正常交通流量下也不會影響結構強度。", "as": "Although the new drug's deleterious side effects proved negligible in clinical trials, circumspect regulators still required further studies before approving it for use in young children.", "at": "雖然這種新藥的有害副作用在臨床試驗中被證實微不足道，行事謹慎的主管機關仍要求進一步研究，才肯核准用於幼童。"}, {"w": "adamant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Refusing to change one's mind; unyielding.", "c": "堅定不移的；堅決的", "s": "Despite pressure from developers and the city council, the residents remained adamant that the century-old banyan tree in the town square must not be cut down, collecting thousands of signatures and staging daily protests beneath its branches.", "t": "儘管面臨開發商和市議會的壓力，居民們仍堅決主張不能砍伐鎮上廣場那棵百年老榕樹，他們蒐集了數千份連署，並每天在樹下舉行抗議。", "as": "The scientist was adamant that her data were sound, and when a rival lab finally managed to corroborate her findings, she was vindicated after years of ridicule.", "at": "這位科學家堅稱她的數據可靠，而當一間競爭實驗室終於證實了她的研究結果時，她在多年的嘲諷之後終於獲得平反。"}, {"w": "sporadic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Occurring occasionally or at irregular intervals.", "c": "零星的；斷斷續續的", "s": "Although the ceasefire largely held, reporters described sporadic gunfire in the outer districts of the city, with brief exchanges breaking out every few days before falling silent again for long, uneasy stretches.", "t": "雖然停火協議大致維持，但記者描述該市外圍地區仍有零星槍響，每隔幾天就爆發短暫交火，隨後又陷入長時間令人不安的沉寂。", "as": "Funding for the project was sporadic at best, so the researchers learned to be frugal, stretching each meager grant and relying on the munificence of a few private donors.", "at": "這項計畫的經費充其量只是斷斷續續，因此研究人員學會了節儉，把每一筆微薄的補助發揮到極致，並仰賴少數私人捐助者的慷慨解囊。"}, {"w": "vanguard", "p": "n.", "d": "The leading position in a movement, field, or development.", "c": "先鋒；前衛；最前線", "s": "In the 1960s, a small group of Taiwanese painters placed themselves in the vanguard of modern art on the island, abandoning traditional ink landscapes to experiment with abstract forms that later generations would widely imitate.", "t": "1960年代，一小群台灣畫家走在島上現代藝術的最前線，揚棄傳統水墨山水，嘗試後來被各世代廣泛模仿的抽象形式。", "as": "Once proudly in the vanguard of the student reform movement, the young iconoclast eventually became a pariah when his fellow activists repudiated his increasingly extreme views.", "at": "這位年輕的反傳統人士曾自豪地站在學生改革運動的最前線，但當他的社運夥伴公開否定他日益偏激的觀點時，他最終淪為眾人排斥的對象。"}, {"w": "concur", "p": "v.", "d": "To agree or have the same opinion.", "c": "同意；意見一致", "s": "Most paleontologists who have independently examined the fossil now concur with the original team's conclusion that the bones belong to a previously unknown species of feathered dinosaur from the early Cretaceous period.", "t": "大多數獨立檢驗過這件化石的古生物學家，如今都同意原研究團隊的結論，認為這些骨骸屬於一種前所未知、生存於白堊紀早期的有羽毛恐龍。", "as": "Though she did not concur with every detail of the proposal, the delegate chose to acquiesce rather than prolong a contentious debate that had already lasted three days.", "at": "雖然她並不同意這項提案的每一個細節，這位代表仍選擇默許，而不願讓這場已持續三天、爭議不斷的辯論再拖延下去。"}, {"w": "precociousness", "p": "n.", "d": "Unusually early development of abilities or maturity.", "c": "早熟；早慧", "s": "Mozart's precociousness astonished the courts of Europe: by the age of five he was composing short pieces, and before turning ten he had written symphonies that rivaled the work of adult professional musicians.", "t": "莫札特的早慧令歐洲各國宮廷驚嘆不已：他五歲時就在創作短曲，未滿十歲便寫出足以媲美成年職業音樂家作品的交響曲。", "as": "The child's precociousness was undeniable, yet her teachers worried that constant praise might make her supercilious and that her erudite vocabulary masked a callow understanding of the world.", "at": "這孩子的早慧毋庸置疑，但老師們擔心不斷的稱讚可能讓她變得目中無人，也擔心她那博學的詞彙底下，掩藏的其實是對世界幼稚而不成熟的理解。"}, {"w": "aloof", "p": "adj.", "d": "Distant and uninvolved; not friendly or open.", "c": "冷漠的；疏遠的", "s": "The new transfer student seemed aloof during her first weeks, eating lunch alone and answering classmates' questions with single words, though her teachers later learned that she was simply shy and struggling with a new language.", "t": "這位新轉學生在剛來的前幾週顯得很冷漠，總是獨自吃午餐，回答同學問題也只用一兩個字，不過老師們後來才得知，她只是個性害羞，而且正努力適應新的語言。", "as": "Critics described the reclusive composer as aloof and taciturn, but his letters reveal a warm, effusive personality that he shared only with a few trusted friends.", "at": "評論家形容這位離群索居的作曲家冷漠寡言，但他的書信卻顯露出溫暖而熱情洋溢的個性，只有少數他信任的朋友才得以見識。"}]}, {"unit": 2, "level": 1, "cards": [{"w": "creed", "p": "n.", "d": "A set of fundamental beliefs that guide one's actions.", "c": "信條；信念", "s": "The school's founders summarized their educational creed in a single sentence carved above the main entrance: every student, regardless of family background, deserves a rigorous education and the chance to serve the community.", "t": "這所學校的創辦人將他們的教育信條濃縮為一句話，刻在正門上方：每位學生不論家庭背景，都應獲得紮實的教育，並有機會服務社群。", "as": "Her political creed rested on altruism and probity, so she refused to tolerate the nepotism that had long allowed officials to reward unqualified relatives with government posts.", "at": "她的政治信條建立在利他精神與正直之上，因此她無法容忍長久以來讓官員以政府職位酬庸不夠格親屬的任人唯親現象。"}, {"w": "tawdry", "p": "adj.", "d": "Cheap, showy, and of poor quality; gaudy.", "c": "俗麗的；廉價而花俏的", "s": "Critics dismissed the remodeled theater lobby as tawdry, complaining that its plastic chandeliers, glittering gold paint, and fake marble columns looked like cheap imitations of luxury rather than an elegant setting for serious drama.", "t": "評論家認為重新裝修後的劇院大廳俗不可耐，抱怨那些塑膠吊燈、閃亮的金色油漆和仿大理石柱看起來只是廉價的奢華仿製品，根本不是適合嚴肅戲劇的高雅場所。", "as": "Beneath the tawdry neon signs of the old harbor district, the photographer found an unexpected beauty, capturing the squalid alleys and itinerant vendors with remarkable tenderness.", "at": "在老港區俗豔的霓虹招牌下，這位攝影師發現了意想不到的美，以非凡的溫柔捕捉了骯髒破敗的巷弄和四處流動的攤販。"}, {"w": "peevish", "p": "adj.", "d": "Easily irritated, especially by unimportant things; cranky.", "c": "易怒的；脾氣暴躁的", "s": "After twelve hours on a delayed flight, the normally patient professor grew peevish, snapping at the gate agent over a misprinted boarding pass and complaining loudly that even the airport coffee was too cold to drink.", "t": "在延誤的航班上耗了十二個小時後，這位平時很有耐心的教授變得暴躁易怒，因為登機證印錯而對櫃檯人員發脾氣，還大聲抱怨連機場的咖啡都冷得無法入口。", "as": "Exhausted by the arduous mountain expedition, the peevish explorer greeted every minor setback with a sharp retort, gradually alienating the local guides on whom his survival depended.", "at": "被艱辛的登山探險折騰得筋疲力盡，這位暴躁的探險家對每一個小挫折都以尖銳的話回嘴，逐漸疏遠了攸關他性命的當地嚮導們。"}, {"w": "arduous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Requiring great effort, energy, or endurance; very difficult.", "c": "艱鉅的；費力的", "s": "Climbing Yushan, Taiwan's highest peak, is an arduous journey that requires two days of steep hiking at high altitude, and rangers advise trekkers to train for months beforehand to build the necessary strength and endurance.", "t": "攀登台灣最高峰玉山是一段艱辛的旅程，需要在高海拔地區進行兩天的陡峭健行，因此保育巡查員建議登山客事先訓練好幾個月，以培養必要的體力和耐力。", "as": "Translating the abstruse philosophical treatise proved so arduous that the scholar spent a decade on it, and her assiduous efforts finally earned her the field's most prestigious accolade.", "at": "翻譯這部艱深的哲學論著極為費力，這位學者耗費了十年心血，而她孜孜不倦的努力最終為她贏得了該領域最崇高的榮譽。"}, {"w": "personable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Pleasant in appearance and manner; likable.", "c": "討人喜歡的；風度翩翩的", "s": "The hiring committee chose the more personable of the two finalists for the museum guide position, because visitors would respond better to someone warm, approachable, and easy to talk to than to a brilliant but awkward expert.", "t": "招聘委員會在兩位最終人選中選了較討人喜歡的那位擔任博物館導覽員，因為比起才華洋溢卻不擅交際的專家，遊客會更喜歡親切、平易近人又好溝通的人。", "as": "The personable young diplomat had a remarkable knack for mollifying irascible ministers, and his droll stories about his own blunders could ease the tension in almost any meeting.", "at": "這位討人喜歡的年輕外交官有安撫脾氣暴躁部長們的非凡本領，而他講述自身糗事的詼諧故事，幾乎能化解任何會議中的緊張氣氛。"}, {"w": "resolute", "p": "adj.", "d": "Firmly determined and unwavering in purpose.", "c": "堅決的；果斷的", "s": "Despite losing her first three elections, the candidate remained resolute in her campaign for clean drinking water in rural villages, returning each year with new evidence, more volunteers, and the same unshakable commitment.", "t": "儘管前三次選舉都落敗，這位候選人仍堅定不移地推動為偏鄉村落爭取乾淨飲用水的訴求，每年都帶著新的證據、更多志工和同樣堅定不移的決心捲土重來。", "as": "Even when her coalition partners began to vacillate, the prime minister stayed resolute, refusing to capitulate to demands that she rescind the controversial pension reform.", "at": "即使聯合執政的夥伴開始搖擺不定，總理仍堅定不移，拒絕屈服於要求她撤回這項具爭議性年金改革的壓力。"}, {"w": "supposition", "p": "n.", "d": "An assumption or belief held without full proof.", "c": "假定；推測", "s": "Early astronomers worked from the supposition that the Earth stood motionless at the center of the universe, an idea that went unchallenged for centuries until careful observations of planetary motion finally overturned it.", "t": "早期天文學家所依據的假定是地球靜止不動地位於宇宙中心，這個觀念數百年來無人質疑，直到對行星運動的仔細觀測才終於將它推翻。", "as": "The detective's theory was mere supposition, and without evidence to corroborate it, the prosecutor feared that the jury would find the allegation tenuous at best.", "at": "這位探員的理論只是推測而已，若沒有證據加以證實，檢察官擔心陪審團頂多會認為這項指控站不住腳。"}, {"w": "arbitrary", "p": "adj.", "d": "Based on random choice or personal whim, not reason.", "c": "任意的；專斷的", "s": "Students protested the dormitory's new curfew, arguing that the arbitrary rule had been imposed without any explanation, data, or consultation and seemed to reflect nothing more than one administrator's personal preference.", "t": "學生們抗議宿舍新訂的門禁，認為這項專斷的規定未經任何說明、數據佐證或意見徵詢便強制實施，似乎只反映出某位行政人員的個人好惡。", "as": "Citizens grew weary of the governor's arbitrary decrees, which seemed as capricious as the weather, and many began to remonstrate openly against his autocratic style.", "at": "市民對州長專斷的命令日益厭倦，這些命令就像天氣一樣反覆無常，許多人開始公開抗議他的專制作風。"}, {"w": "monotonous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Dull and tedious because of lack of variety.", "c": "單調乏味的；一成不變的", "s": "Factory workers on the assembly line described their jobs as monotonous, explaining that they performed the same three hand movements thousands of times every shift, with no variation, no conversation, and no chance to learn new skills.", "t": "生產線上的工人形容他們的工作單調乏味，說明每一個班次都要重複同樣的三個手部動作數千次，沒有任何變化、無法交談，也沒有機會學習新技能。", "as": "The guest lecturer's monotonous delivery and banal examples induced such lethargy in the audience that, by the second hour, even the most diligent graduate students were struggling to stay awake.", "at": "客座講者單調的講課方式和平庸的例子讓聽眾昏昏欲睡，到了第二個小時，連最用功的研究生都快撐不住了。"}, {"w": "legacy", "p": "n.", "d": "Something handed down from the past or a predecessor.", "c": "遺產；遺緒", "s": "The Japanese colonial period left a complex legacy in Taiwan, including railways, public health systems, and architecture that still shape daily life, alongside painful memories that historians continue to examine today.", "t": "日治時期在台灣留下了複雜的遺緒，包括至今仍影響日常生活的鐵路、公共衛生體系與建築，以及歷史學家至今仍持續探究的痛苦記憶。", "as": "The philanthropist's legacy endures in the scholarships she funded, and her extraordinary munificence continues to edify generations of rural students who never had the chance to meet her.", "at": "這位慈善家的遺澤延續在她所資助的獎學金之中，她非凡的慷慨持續啟迪著一代又一代從未有機會見到她的偏鄉學生。"}, {"w": "manifold", "p": "adj.", "d": "Many and of several different kinds.", "c": "多種多樣的；繁多的", "s": "The benefits of learning a second language are manifold: research links bilingualism to better memory, stronger problem-solving skills, wider career opportunities, and a deeper understanding of cultures beyond one's own.", "t": "學習第二語言的好處多不勝數：研究顯示雙語能力與更好的記憶力、更強的解決問題能力、更廣的職涯機會，以及對其他文化更深的理解息息相關。", "as": "The challenges facing the refugee camp were manifold, from a dearth of clean water to a plethora of infectious diseases spreading through its crowded tents.", "at": "難民營面臨的挑戰多不勝數，從乾淨飲水的匱乏，到在擁擠帳篷間蔓延的大量傳染病。"}, {"w": "pliant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Easily bent or influenced; flexible or yielding.", "c": "柔韌的；易受影響的", "s": "Basket weavers in the Amis community soak rattan strips in water overnight so that the fibers become pliant enough to bend into tight curves without cracking, allowing the artisans to shape intricate patterns by hand.", "t": "阿美族的編織工匠會將藤條在水中浸泡一整夜，讓纖維變得夠柔韌，能彎成緊密的弧度而不斷裂，使工匠能以手工編出精細的圖案。", "as": "The aging dictator surrounded himself with pliant advisers and obsequious sycophants who praised every decree and would never dare to question his increasingly disastrous economic policies.", "at": "這位年邁的獨裁者身邊圍繞著唯命是從的顧問和阿諛奉承的馬屁精，他們讚美每一道命令，從不敢質疑他日益災難性的經濟政策。"}, {"w": "retort", "p": "n.", "d": "A quick, sharp, or witty reply.", "c": "反駁；機智的回嘴", "s": "When a heckler shouted that the young candidate was too inexperienced to govern, she delivered a swift retort that silenced the crowd: experience, she noted, had not stopped the previous mayor from bankrupting the city.", "t": "當有人起鬨大喊這位年輕候選人經驗不足、無法治理時，她迅速機智地反駁，讓全場鴉雀無聲：她指出，經驗並沒能阻止前任市長讓這座城市破產。", "as": "The playwright was famous for her mordant retorts, and even her most acerbic critics admitted that her wit made their reviews seem pedantic by comparison.", "at": "這位劇作家以尖刻的機智反駁聞名，就連最尖酸的評論家也承認，相較於她的妙語，他們的評論顯得迂腐。"}, {"w": "obstinate", "p": "adj.", "d": "Stubbornly refusing to change one's opinion or course.", "c": "頑固的；固執的", "s": "The obstinate committee chair refused to consider any alternatives to his original design for the stadium, even after engineers produced three independent reports showing that the roof could collapse under heavy typhoon winds.", "t": "這位固執的委員會主席拒絕考慮任何取代他原始體育場設計的方案，即使工程師提出三份獨立報告，顯示屋頂在強烈颱風下可能崩塌也一樣。", "as": "The obstinate old farmer ignored the agronomist's repeated admonitions about crop rotation, and his intractable refusal to adapt eventually left his once fertile fields barren and his family indigent.", "at": "這位頑固的老農夫無視農學家一再提出的輪作告誡，他那難以動搖、拒絕調整的態度，最終讓曾經肥沃的田地變得貧瘠，也讓家人陷入貧困。"}, {"w": "lacerate", "p": "v.", "d": "To tear or cut deeply; to wound severely.", "c": "撕裂；割傷；深深刺痛", "s": "Divers are warned to wear thick gloves near the coral reef, because the sharp edges of the coral can easily lacerate unprotected skin, leaving deep wounds that heal slowly and often become infected in warm seawater.", "t": "潛水員被告誡在珊瑚礁附近要戴厚手套，因為珊瑚鋒利的邊緣很容易割傷沒有防護的皮膚，留下癒合緩慢、在溫暖海水中常常感染的深深傷口。", "as": "The reviewer's caustic essay seemed designed to lacerate the young author, and many readers dismissed its relentless invective as gratuitous cruelty rather than thoughtful literary criticism.", "at": "這位書評家那篇尖酸的文章似乎是存心要狠狠刺傷這位年輕作家，許多讀者認為其毫不留情的抨擊是無端的殘酷，而非深思熟慮的文學評論。"}, {"w": "omnipotent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having unlimited power or authority; all-powerful.", "c": "全能的；權力無限的", "s": "In many ancient myths, the king of the gods is portrayed as omnipotent, able to summon storms, raise mountains, and decide the fate of every mortal, yet even he is sometimes outwitted by clever heroes.", "t": "在許多古代神話中，眾神之王被描繪成全能的存在，能呼風喚雨、移山造嶽，並決定每個凡人的命運，然而就連他有時也會被聰明的英雄智取。", "as": "The ruling oligarchy considered itself omnipotent, yet its arrogance proved pernicious, and a nascent reform movement gradually eroded what had once seemed an unassailable grip on power.", "at": "執政的寡頭集團自認權力無限，然而它的傲慢最終證明是有害的，一場新興的改革運動逐漸侵蝕了它曾經看似牢不可破的權力掌控。"}, {"w": "unscrupulous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having no moral principles; dishonest or unfair.", "c": "不擇手段的；無道德原則的", "s": "Consumer groups warned elderly residents about unscrupulous salespeople who pretend to be government inspectors, frighten homeowners with false claims about unsafe wiring, and then charge outrageous prices for unnecessary repairs.", "t": "消費者團體提醒年長居民，要提防不肖的推銷員：他們冒充政府稽查人員，以電線不安全的不實說法恐嚇屋主，再為不必要的維修收取離譜的費用。", "as": "The unscrupulous broker would beguile naive investors with glib promises of quick profits, then vanish with their savings, leaving behind a trail of ruined families and broken trust.", "at": "這名不擇手段的經紀人會用快速獲利的油嘴滑舌承諾誘騙天真的投資人，然後帶著他們的積蓄消失無蹤，留下一連串破碎的家庭和崩壞的信任。"}, {"w": "renaissance", "p": "n.", "d": "A revival or renewed interest in something.", "c": "復興；再生", "s": "Traditional Taiwanese puppet theater is enjoying a renaissance, as young directors blend classic glove puppetry with digital effects and pop music, drawing audiences who had never before shown interest in the old art form.", "t": "台灣傳統布袋戲正迎來一波復興，年輕導演將經典布袋戲與數位特效、流行音樂結合，吸引了從前從未對這項古老藝術感興趣的觀眾。", "as": "The city's cultural renaissance began when a few itinerant artists turned abandoned warehouses into studios, and their prolific output soon drew galleries, cafés, and curious tourists to the district.", "at": "這座城市的文化復興始於幾位四處漂泊的藝術家將廢棄倉庫改造成工作室，而他們豐碩的創作很快吸引了藝廊、咖啡館和好奇的觀光客來到這一區。"}, {"w": "genesis", "p": "n.", "d": "The origin or beginning of something.", "c": "起源；開端", "s": "The genesis of the bubble-tea craze can be traced to a small teahouse in Taichung in the 1980s, where an employee reportedly dropped tapioca balls into iced milk tea during a staff meeting.", "t": "珍珠奶茶熱潮的起源可追溯至1980年代台中的一家小茶館，據說一名員工在員工會議上把粉圓加進了冰奶茶裡。", "as": "The genesis of the reform lay in a single dissident's pamphlet, whose trenchant critique of official corruption galvanized university students and sparked a nascent democratic movement.", "at": "這場改革的起源在於一位異議人士的小冊子，其對官方貪腐一針見血的批判激勵了大學生，點燃了一場萌芽中的民主運動。"}, {"w": "warrant", "p": "v.", "d": "To justify or make necessary.", "c": "使有正當理由；使成為必要", "s": "The principal decided that a single late assignment did not warrant a meeting with the student's parents, but she agreed to call them if the pattern of missed deadlines continued through the rest of the semester.", "t": "校長認為，單單一次遲交作業並不足以構成約談學生家長的理由，但她同意若這種錯過期限的情形在學期剩餘時間裡持續發生，就會打電話通知家長。", "as": "The minor procedural error hardly warranted such a furious tirade, and the senator's colleagues found his public display of umbrage both disproportionate and faintly absurd.", "at": "這個輕微的程序錯誤根本不值得如此憤怒的長篇抨擊，參議員的同僚們都覺得他公開表現出的憤慨既過了頭，又有點荒謬。"}]}, {"unit": 3, "level": 1, "cards": [{"w": "cantankerous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Bad-tempered, quarrelsome, and difficult to deal with.", "c": "脾氣壞的；愛爭吵的", "s": "The cantankerous old librarian argued with nearly every patron who entered the reading room, scolding students for whispering, complaining about the noise of turning pages, and refusing to help anyone who asked a question twice.", "t": "那位脾氣暴躁的老圖書館員幾乎和每一位走進閱覽室的讀者爭吵，他斥責學生竊竊私語、抱怨翻書聲太吵，還拒絕幫助任何把問題問第二次的人。", "as": "The cantankerous senator, notorious for his irascible outbursts and captious objections to every amendment, nonetheless commanded grudging respect for his scrupulous knowledge of parliamentary procedure.", "at": "這位脾氣暴躁的參議員以動輒發怒和對每一項修正案吹毛求疵聞名，但他對議事程序一絲不苟的熟稔，仍讓人不得不對他心存敬意。"}, {"w": "flippant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Not showing proper seriousness or respect; glib.", "c": "輕率的；不當一回事的", "s": "Reporters criticized the minister's flippant response to questions about the flooded villages, noting that he had joked about residents needing swimming lessons while hundreds of families were still waiting for emergency shelter and clean water.", "t": "記者們批評部長在回答淹水村落相關問題時態度輕率，指出當數百個家庭仍在等待緊急安置和乾淨飲水時，他竟開玩笑說居民需要上游泳課。", "as": "The student's flippant remarks during the memorial ceremony struck the faculty as gratuitously disrespectful, and the principal admonished him privately to show more decorum and contrition.", "at": "這名學生在追思典禮上輕率的言論，讓教職員認為是毫無必要的不敬，校長私下告誡他要更合乎禮節，並表現出悔意。"}, {"w": "subjugate", "p": "v.", "d": "To bring under complete control; to conquer.", "c": "征服；使屈服", "s": "Historians describe how the empire used heavy taxes, military garrisons, and bans on local languages to subjugate the conquered provinces, crushing every rebellion and forcing the population to obey distant rulers for nearly two centuries.", "t": "歷史學家描述這個帝國如何利用重稅、駐軍和禁止使用當地語言來征服所佔領的省份，鎮壓每一次叛亂，迫使人民服從遠方的統治者將近兩個世紀。", "as": "The colonial regime sought to subjugate the island through a promulgated code of harsh laws, but its efforts to efface indigenous culture only strengthened the people's resolve.", "at": "殖民政權試圖透過頒布一套嚴苛的法典來征服這座島嶼，但它抹除原住民文化的企圖，反而更堅定了人民的決心。"}, {"w": "wry", "p": "adj.", "d": "Dryly or ironically humorous, often with mild mockery.", "c": "帶嘲諷的；挖苦的；苦笑的", "s": "With a wry smile, the veteran astronaut told the students that space travel was not very glamorous after all, since she had spent most of her six months in orbit fixing broken toilets and chasing floating crumbs.", "t": "這位資深太空人帶著一抹自嘲的微笑告訴學生們，太空旅行其實沒那麼光鮮亮麗，因為她在軌道上的六個月裡，大多時間都在修理壞掉的馬桶和追著飄浮的碎屑跑。", "as": "The essayist's wry observations about bureaucratic jargon delighted readers, and her droll account of a single permit requiring forty signatures captured the absurdity of the system perfectly.", "at": "這位散文作家對官僚術語略帶嘲諷的觀察令讀者大為喜愛，而她以詼諧筆調描述一張許可證竟需四十個簽名，完美地捕捉了這套制度的荒謬。"}, {"w": "urbane", "p": "adj.", "d": "Courteous, refined, and elegant in manner.", "c": "溫文儒雅的；有教養的", "s": "The urbane ambassador charmed guests at the embassy reception, moving gracefully from conversation to conversation in fluent French, Mandarin, and English, and handling even awkward political questions with unfailing courtesy and gentle humor.", "t": "這位溫文儒雅的大使在大使館的招待會上風靡全場，他以流利的法語、中文和英語優雅地穿梭於各個談話之間，即使面對尷尬的政治問題，也總是以得體的禮貌和溫和的幽默應對。", "as": "Beneath his urbane manners and genteel conversation, the celebrated art dealer was a consummate charlatan who sold spurious paintings to unsuspecting collectors for enormous sums.", "at": "在他溫文儒雅的舉止和高雅的談吐之下，這位知名的藝術品商人其實是個徹頭徹尾的騙子，以高昂的價格將假畫賣給毫無戒心的收藏家。"}, {"w": "jargon", "p": "n.", "d": "Specialized language of a profession, hard for outsiders to understand.", "c": "術語；行話", "s": "The hospital rewrote its patient brochures after surveys showed that most readers could not understand the medical jargon they contained, replacing terms like \"myocardial infarction\" with plain phrases such as \"heart attack.\"", "t": "這家醫院在調查顯示多數讀者看不懂病患手冊中的醫學術語後，重新改寫了手冊，將「心肌梗塞」之類的用語換成「心臟病發作」這種淺白的說法。", "as": "The consultant's report was so laden with jargon and so abstruse that the board suspected its convoluted prose was meant to obfuscate a lack of real recommendations.", "at": "這位顧問的報告充斥著專業術語又艱澀難懂，董事會懷疑那些拐彎抹角的文字是為了掩飾其中根本沒有實質建議。"}, {"w": "prudent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Wise and careful in planning for the future.", "c": "謹慎的；精明的", "s": "Financial advisers consider it prudent for young workers to save at least ten percent of every paycheck, so that unexpected expenses such as medical bills or sudden unemployment do not push them into serious debt.", "t": "理財顧問認為，年輕上班族每份薪水至少存下百分之十是明智之舉，這樣醫療費用或突然失業等意外開銷才不會讓他們陷入嚴重的債務。", "as": "A prudent and provident manager, she set aside funds during prosperous years, so the company survived the downturn without the onerous layoffs that devastated its competitors.", "at": "她是一位謹慎且有遠見的經理，在景氣好的年頭就預留資金，因此公司安然度過經濟衰退，沒有像競爭對手那樣進行沉重的大規模裁員。"}, {"w": "inviolable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Too sacred or important to be broken or violated.", "c": "不可侵犯的；不容違背的", "s": "The founders of the democracy regarded freedom of the press as inviolable, writing into the constitution that no future government, however popular, could ever pass laws allowing officials to censor newspapers or imprison journalists.", "t": "這個民主國家的開國者視新聞自由為不可侵犯的權利，在憲法中明文規定，未來任何政府無論多受歡迎，都不得通過允許官員審查報紙或監禁記者的法律。", "as": "The judge declared that the right to counsel was inviolable, and she excoriated prosecutors for their attempt to abrogate it through a clever but specious procedural maneuver.", "at": "法官宣告聘請律師的權利不可侵犯，並嚴厲斥責檢察官企圖透過一項巧妙卻似是而非的程序手段來廢除這項權利。"}, {"w": "commodious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Roomy and comfortable; having plenty of space.", "c": "寬敞的；寬敞舒適的", "s": "After years of squeezing into a tiny classroom, the robotics club moved into a commodious workshop with high ceilings, long workbenches, and enough floor space to test three full-sized robots at the same time.", "t": "在狹小的教室擠了好幾年後，機器人社搬進了一間寬敞的工作坊，那裡天花板挑高、工作台長，地板空間足以同時測試三台全尺寸機器人。", "as": "The commodious mansion, with its opulent ballroom and capacious library, struck visitors as a monument to the parvenu owner's craving for status rather than to genuine taste.", "at": "這座寬敞的豪宅擁有富麗堂皇的舞廳和空間廣闊的圖書室，在訪客看來，這與其說是品味的展現，不如說是那位暴發戶屋主渴望地位的紀念碑。"}, {"w": "proximity", "p": "n.", "d": "Nearness in space, time, or relationship.", "c": "鄰近；接近", "s": "Many families choose apartments in the proximity of a good public school, accepting higher rents and smaller living spaces so that their children can walk to class in five minutes instead of commuting across the city.", "t": "許多家庭選擇住在好的公立學校附近的公寓，寧願接受較高的租金和較小的居住空間，好讓孩子五分鐘就能走路上學，而不必穿越整座城市通勤。", "as": "The factory's proximity to the river proved pernicious, as its fetid waste gradually poisoned the water and decimated the fish on which local villagers depended.", "at": "工廠鄰近河川的位置後來證明為害甚大，因為它惡臭的廢水逐漸毒害河水，使當地村民賴以維生的魚群大量死亡。"}, {"w": "advocate", "p": "v.", "d": "To publicly support or recommend a cause or policy.", "c": "提倡；擁護", "s": "Several public health researchers now advocate a later start time for high schools, citing studies showing that teenagers who sleep an extra hour perform better on exams and are less likely to suffer from depression.", "t": "數位公共衛生研究人員如今主張高中延後上課時間，他們引用研究指出，多睡一小時的青少年考試表現較佳，也較不容易罹患憂鬱症。", "as": "Environmental groups advocate a ban on single-use plastics, and their fervent, persistent lobbying has finally begun to sway even the most intransigent members of the legislature.", "at": "環保團體提倡禁用一次性塑膠製品，而他們熱切且持續不懈的遊說，終於開始動搖立法機關中最不肯妥協的成員。"}, {"w": "delegate", "p": "v.", "d": "To entrust a task or authority to another person.", "c": "委派；授權", "s": "Effective team leaders learn to delegate routine tasks such as scheduling, note-taking, and ordering supplies to other members, which frees them to concentrate on the strategic decisions that only they are qualified to make.", "t": "有效率的團隊領導者會學著把排程、記錄和訂購用品等例行工作委派給其他成員，讓自己能專注於只有他們才有資格做的策略性決策。", "as": "Reluctant to delegate any real authority, the officious director insisted on approving every minor expense himself, a habit that protracted even simple projects for months and frustrated his staff.", "at": "這位愛管閒事的主任不願下放任何實權，堅持每一筆小額支出都要親自核准，這個習慣讓連簡單的計畫都拖延了好幾個月，也讓部屬備感挫折。"}, {"w": "unprecedented", "p": "adj.", "d": "Never done or known before; without previous example.", "c": "前所未有的；空前的", "s": "The 2020 pandemic forced an unprecedented shift to online learning, as millions of students worldwide attended classes from their bedrooms for months, something no education system had ever attempted on such a massive scale.", "t": "2020年的疫情迫使教育前所未有地轉向線上學習，全球數百萬名學生連續數月在臥室裡上課，這是任何教育體系從未在如此大規模下嘗試過的事。", "as": "The drought was unprecedented in the region's recorded history, and its cataclysmic effects on agriculture left thousands of rice farmers indigent within a single season.", "at": "這場乾旱在該地區有紀錄的歷史中前所未見，它對農業造成的災難性衝擊，使數千名稻農在短短一季之內便陷入貧困。"}, {"w": "poignant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Deeply moving; causing a sharp feeling of sadness.", "c": "令人心酸的；深刻感人的", "s": "The documentary's most poignant scene shows an elderly veteran returning to the battlefield where his brother died seventy years earlier, kneeling silently in the grass as tears run down his weathered face.", "t": "這部紀錄片最令人心酸的一幕，是一位年邁的退伍軍人回到七十年前他哥哥陣亡的戰場，默默跪在草地上，淚水從他飽經風霜的臉龐滑落。", "as": "The exhibit's most poignant artifacts were the soldiers' letters home, whose callow optimism about a swift victory now seems almost unbearably sad, a mournful reminder of how ephemeral youthful hope can be.", "at": "展覽中最令人心酸的文物是士兵們寫回家的信，信中對速戰速決的稚嫩樂觀，如今讀來幾乎令人悲傷得難以承受，哀傷地提醒著人們，年少的希望是多麼短暫易逝。"}, {"w": "nebulous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Vague, unclear, or not well defined.", "c": "模糊的；含糊不清的", "s": "The committee rejected the startup's funding application because its business plan remained nebulous, offering only general promises to \"transform education\" without explaining what product it would build, who would buy it, or how much it would cost.", "t": "委員會駁回了這家新創公司的資金申請，因為它的營運計畫仍然含糊不清，只是籠統地承諾要「改變教育」，卻沒有說明要開發什麼產品、誰會購買，或者成本是多少。", "as": "The candidate's nebulous promises of change, couched in ambiguous slogans and grandiloquent rhetoric, left many voters uncertain what policies he would actually pursue once elected.", "at": "這位候選人對改變的承諾模糊不清，包裝在模稜兩可的口號和浮誇的言辭之中，讓許多選民無法確定他當選後究竟會推行哪些政策。"}, {"w": "clandestine", "p": "adj.", "d": "Kept secret or done secretly, often illicitly.", "c": "秘密的；暗中的", "s": "During the martial law era, students organized clandestine reading groups in rented apartments, passing banned books from hand to hand and changing their meeting places every week to avoid the attention of government informants.", "t": "戒嚴時期，學生們在租來的公寓裡組織秘密讀書會，私下傳閱禁書，並且每週更換聚會地點，以躲避政府線民的注意。", "as": "The spy's clandestine meetings with the dissident were conducted with surreptitious care, yet a single careless phone call was ultimately enough to incriminate them both.", "at": "這名間諜與異議人士的秘密會面進行得極為隱密謹慎，然而一通不經意的電話最終就足以讓兩人都被定罪。"}, {"w": "tirade", "p": "n.", "d": "A long, angry, and critical speech.", "c": "長篇激烈的抨擊；激烈的長篇大論", "s": "After losing the championship, the furious coach launched into a twenty-minute tirade at the post-game press conference, attacking the referees, the league officials, and even his own players before finally storming out of the room.", "t": "輸掉冠軍賽後，盛怒的教練在賽後記者會上發表了長達二十分鐘的激烈抨擊，砲轟裁判、聯盟官員，甚至自己的球員，最後才怒氣沖沖地離開會場。", "as": "The chairman's furious tirade against his critics was so bombastic and full of personal invective that even his most loyal supporters began to question his judgment.", "at": "董事長對批評者那番憤怒的長篇抨擊既浮誇又充滿人身攻擊，連他最忠實的支持者都開始質疑他的判斷力。"}, {"w": "recur", "p": "v.", "d": "To happen again, especially repeatedly.", "c": "重現；反覆發生", "s": "Doctors warned the patient that the migraines might recur whenever she skipped meals or slept too little, so they advised her to keep a diary of her daily habits to identify what triggered each painful attack.", "t": "醫生提醒這位病人，每當她不吃飯或睡眠不足時，偏頭痛就可能再度發作，因此建議她記錄每天的生活習慣，以找出每次疼痛發作的誘因。", "as": "Certain themes recur throughout the prolific novelist's long career: the transitory nature of happiness, the fragile bonds of friendship, and the slow decay of rural communities.", "at": "這位多產小說家漫長的創作生涯中，某些主題反覆出現：幸福的短暫易逝、友誼的脆弱，以及鄉村社區的緩慢衰落。"}, {"w": "tacit", "p": "adj.", "d": "Understood or implied without being directly stated.", "c": "心照不宣的；默許的", "s": "Although no rule was ever written down, there was a tacit agreement among the roommates that whoever cooked dinner would not have to wash the dishes, an arrangement that worked smoothly for the entire school year.", "t": "雖然從未寫下任何規定，室友之間卻有個心照不宣的默契：負責煮晚餐的人就不必洗碗，這個安排在整個學年都運作得很順利。", "as": "The two rival nations maintained a tacit truce, neither one willing to acquiesce publicly to a formal treaty, yet both quietly eschewing any provocation along the border.", "at": "這兩個敵對國家維持著一種心照不宣的休戰，雙方都不願公開默認一份正式條約，卻又都悄悄避免在邊界上做出任何挑釁行為。"}, {"w": "allegation", "p": "n.", "d": "A claim of wrongdoing, made without proof yet.", "c": "指控；（未經證實的）聲稱", "s": "The university launched an independent investigation into the allegation that a professor had falsified research data, but it stressed that the claim had not yet been proven and that the professor would remain in his position until the review was complete.", "t": "大學針對一名教授偽造研究數據的指控展開獨立調查，但校方強調該指控尚未證實，在審查完成前，這位教授仍將留任原職。", "as": "The allegation of bribery was never corroborated, and the minister was eventually exonerated, though the stigma of the scandal followed him for the rest of his career.", "at": "這項賄賂指控始終未獲證實，部長最終也被證明清白，但這起醜聞的污名仍伴隨了他往後的整個職業生涯。"}]}, {"unit": 4, "level": 1, "cards": [{"w": "gullible", "p": "adj.", "d": "Easily deceived or tricked; too trusting.", "c": "容易受騙的；輕信的", "s": "Researchers studying online misinformation found that even well-educated users could be surprisingly gullible, sharing fabricated headlines without checking the source simply because the stories confirmed what they already believed about a political issue.", "t": "研究網路錯誤資訊的學者發現，即使是受過良好教育的使用者也可能出乎意料地容易受騙，只因報導符合他們對某個政治議題的既有看法，便在未查證來源的情況下分享捏造的標題。", "as": "The charlatan's polished pitch convinced only the most gullible investors, while more astute observers quickly recognized within weeks that his promises of effortless wealth were nothing but fantasy.", "at": "那名江湖騙子圓滑的推銷話術只說服了最容易受騙的投資人，而較精明的觀察者在幾週內便看穿，他輕鬆致富的承諾不過是幻想。"}, {"w": "benign", "p": "adj.", "d": "Gentle and kindly; not harmful.", "c": "溫和的；無害的", "s": "Although the bright orange caterpillar looks threatening to predators, biologists have confirmed that it is entirely benign to humans, lacking the venomous spines and toxic chemicals that make several closely related species dangerous to touch.", "t": "雖然這種亮橘色的毛毛蟲在掠食者看來具有威脅性，生物學家已證實牠對人類完全無害，因為牠沒有那些讓幾種近親物種一碰就有危險的毒刺與毒性化學物質。", "as": "Far from the cantankerous tyrant his critics described, the aging monarch proved remarkably benign in his final years, showing magnanimous mercy even toward former rebels who had once opposed him.", "at": "這位年邁的君主並非批評者口中那個脾氣暴躁的暴君；他在晚年表現得格外仁慈溫和，甚至對曾經反對他的昔日叛軍也展現寬宏大量的憐憫。"}, {"w": "peripheral", "p": "adj.", "d": "Located at the outer edge; not central or essential.", "c": "周邊的；次要的", "s": "During the debate, the candidate kept steering the conversation toward peripheral issues such as the color of the new campus buses, avoiding the central question of how the university would cover its growing budget deficit.", "t": "辯論中，那位候選人一再把話題導向新校車的顏色等次要議題，迴避了大學將如何填補日益擴大的預算赤字這個核心問題。", "as": "The professor's habit of digressing into peripheral anecdotes made his lectures entertaining, but students preparing for the exam found the tangential stories more confusing than edifying.", "at": "這位教授習慣離題講些枝微末節的軼事，讓課堂生動有趣，但準備考試的學生覺得這些離題的故事與其說有啟發性，不如說令人困惑。"}, {"w": "rebuff", "p": "v.", "d": "To reject bluntly or refuse in an unkind way.", "c": "斷然拒絕；冷淡回絕", "s": "When the young scientist offered to share her data with the rival laboratory, she was surprised to see its director rebuff the proposal coldly, insisting that his team needed no help from a junior researcher.", "t": "當這位年輕科學家提議與對手實驗室分享她的數據時，她驚訝地看到該實驗室主任冷淡地斷然拒絕這項提議，堅稱他的團隊不需要一名資淺研究員的幫助。", "as": "Despite the ambassador's conciliatory overtures, the intransigent regime continued to rebuff every offer of rapprochement, insisting that no compromise over the disputed border region was even remotely possible.", "at": "儘管大使釋出和解的善意，那個毫不妥協的政權仍持續回絕每一次修好的提議，堅稱在爭議邊境地區的問題上根本不可能有任何妥協。"}, {"w": "animosity", "p": "n.", "d": "A feeling of strong dislike or hostility.", "c": "敵意；仇恨", "s": "Decades of bitter competition over water rights had created deep animosity between the two farming communities, so that even after a fair agreement was signed, neighbors from opposite sides of the river still refused to speak to one another.", "t": "數十年來爭奪水權的激烈競爭，在兩個農業社區之間造成了深刻的敵意，以至於即使簽署了一份公平的協議，河兩岸的鄰居仍拒絕彼此交談。", "as": "The vindictive senator's long-standing animosity toward the governor surfaced in a scathing tirade during the televised budget hearing that shocked even colleagues accustomed to his acerbic style.", "at": "那位記仇的參議員對州長長久以來的敵意，在電視轉播的預算聽證會上化為一場尖刻的激烈抨擊，連早已習慣他尖酸作風的同僚都大為震驚。"}, {"w": "tenuous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Very weak, thin, or slight; lacking substance.", "c": "薄弱的；站不住腳的", "s": "The historian admitted that the link between the ancient coin and the lost city was tenuous at best, since it rested on a single faded inscription that other experts had interpreted in at least three different ways.", "t": "這位歷史學家承認，這枚古錢幣與那座失落之城之間的關聯充其量相當薄弱，因為它僅依據一段褪色的銘文，而其他專家對這段銘文至少有三種不同的詮釋。", "as": "The prosecutor's case, built on tenuous evidence and a single witness's nebulous recollections, collapsed when the defense produced documents that completely exonerated the accused bank clerk.", "at": "檢方的案子建立在薄弱的證據和一名證人模糊不清的記憶之上，當辯方提出足以完全洗清那名銀行職員罪嫌的文件時，便徹底瓦解了。"}, {"w": "complacent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Too satisfied with oneself to notice dangers or problems.", "c": "自滿的；自鳴得意的", "s": "After winning the national championship three years in a row, the robotics team grew complacent and stopped testing new designs, so they were stunned when a first-year team from a small rural school defeated them in the opening round.", "t": "在連續三年贏得全國冠軍後，這支機器人隊變得自滿，不再測試新設計，因此當一支來自鄉下小學校的新隊伍在首輪擊敗他們時，他們大感震驚。", "as": "Lulled by years of prosperity, the complacent board ignored the ubiquitous warning signs of decline in its industry until the once-dominant camera company became virtually defunct.", "at": "多年的繁榮讓這個自滿的董事會鬆懈下來，忽視了業界隨處可見的衰退警訊，直到這家曾稱霸一時的相機公司幾乎名存實亡。"}, {"w": "acme", "p": "n.", "d": "The highest point of achievement or excellence.", "c": "頂點；巔峰", "s": "Many art historians regard the ceiling of the Sistine Chapel as the acme of Michelangelo's career, the moment when his technical mastery, religious devotion, and bold imagination combined to produce a work that later painters could only admire.", "t": "許多藝術史學家認為西斯汀禮拜堂的天花板是米開朗基羅職業生涯的巔峰，是他精湛的技藝、虔誠的信仰與大膽的想像力結合，創作出後世畫家只能讚嘆之作的時刻。", "as": "Critics hailed the novel as the acme of her prolific career, praising its lucid prose and the poignant ending that left many readers in tears.", "at": "評論家盛讚這部小說是她多產創作生涯的巔峰之作，稱讚其清晰流暢的文筆，以及讓許多讀者落淚的動人結局。"}, {"w": "defunct", "p": "adj.", "d": "No longer existing, operating, or in use.", "c": "已不存在的；已停止運作的", "s": "The museum's new exhibit features advertisements from defunct companies that once dominated American shopping malls, reminding visitors how quickly familiar brands can vanish when consumer habits shift toward online retailers and streaming services.", "t": "博物館的新展覽展出一些已倒閉公司的廣告，這些公司曾稱霸美國的購物中心，提醒參觀者當消費習慣轉向網路零售商和串流服務時，熟悉的品牌會消失得多快。", "as": "Although the treaty is technically extant, most diplomats consider it defunct, since neither nation has honored its provisions since the cataclysm of the civil war.", "at": "雖然這項條約在技術上仍然存在，大多數外交官都認為它已形同廢止，因為自從那場浩劫般的內戰以來，兩國都不曾遵守其條款。"}, {"w": "abet", "p": "v.", "d": "To help or encourage someone to do something wrong.", "c": "教唆；協助（犯罪）", "s": "The court ruled that the bank employee who secretly disabled the security cameras had chosen to abet the robbery, even though she never entered the vault herself, because her actions made it far easier for the thieves to escape unnoticed.", "t": "法院裁定，那名暗中關閉監視器的銀行員工是蓄意協助這起搶案，即使她本人從未進入金庫，因為她的行為讓竊賊更容易在不被發現的情況下逃脫。", "as": "Investigators suspected that several officials had abetted the scheme to peculate public funds, though proving their complicity would require documents the ministry had conveniently lost.", "at": "調查人員懷疑有幾名官員協助了盜用公款的計畫，但要證明他們共謀，需要那些被該部會「恰好」遺失的文件。"}, {"w": "haggard", "p": "adj.", "d": "Looking exhausted and unwell, especially from worry or lack of sleep.", "c": "憔悴的；形容枯槁的", "s": "After seventy-two hours of searching the collapsed building for survivors, the rescue workers looked haggard, their faces pale and hollow-eyed, yet they refused to rest until the last missing family had been found.", "t": "在倒塌的建築物中搜尋生還者七十二小時後，救難人員看起來憔悴不堪，臉色蒼白、眼窩深陷，但他們拒絕休息，直到找到最後一個失蹤的家庭為止。", "as": "Weeks of lassitude and insomnia had left the formerly jovial composer haggard and morose, and his friends feared he would never complete the ambitious symphony he had begun.", "at": "數週的倦怠與失眠，讓這位昔日開朗風趣的作曲家變得憔悴又鬱鬱寡歡，朋友們擔心他永遠無法完成他已著手的那首宏大交響曲。"}, {"w": "waive", "p": "v.", "d": "To voluntarily give up a right, claim, or requirement.", "c": "放棄（權利）；免除（費用、規定）", "s": "To encourage more low-income students to apply, the university decided to waive its usual seventy-dollar application fee for anyone whose family qualified for government assistance, a change that nearly doubled the number of applications from rural counties.", "t": "為了鼓勵更多低收入學生申請，這所大學決定對家庭符合政府補助資格的申請者免除一般七十美元的申請費，這項改變讓來自鄉村郡縣的申請數量幾乎增加了一倍。", "as": "By agreeing to waive his right to a jury trial, the defendant hoped a judge would prove more clement than twelve citizens swayed by scurrilous press coverage.", "at": "被告同意放棄接受陪審團審判的權利，希望一位法官會比十二位受到惡意中傷的媒體報導影響的公民更寬容。"}, {"w": "carnal", "p": "adj.", "d": "Relating to the body or physical appetites rather than the spirit.", "c": "肉體的；世俗慾望的", "s": "In many medieval sermons, preachers urged believers to turn away from carnal pleasures such as feasting and luxury and to focus instead on prayer, fasting, and the spiritual rewards they believed awaited the faithful after death.", "t": "在許多中世紀的佈道中，傳道者勸誡信徒遠離宴飲和奢華等肉體上的享樂，轉而專注於祈禱、禁食，以及他們相信信徒死後將獲得的屬靈獎賞。", "as": "The ascetic monk renounced all carnal comforts, choosing an austere cell and a diet so abstemious that visitors wondered how he survived the harsh winters.", "at": "這位苦行僧捨棄了一切肉體上的舒適，選擇住在簡樸的小室裡，飲食極為節制，訪客們都納悶他如何熬過嚴酷的冬天。"}, {"w": "sanction", "p": "v.", "d": "To give official permission or approval for something.", "c": "批准；認可", "s": "The city council voted unanimously to sanction the student-run farmers' market on the town square, giving the organizers official permission to sell fresh produce there every Saturday morning throughout the summer and early autumn.", "t": "市議會一致投票批准在鎮上廣場設立由學生經營的農夫市集，正式允許主辦單位在整個夏季和初秋的每週六早上於該處販售新鮮農產品。", "as": "The committee refused to sanction the proposed research, arguing that the scientists' claims were not demonstrable and their conclusions rested on little more than conjecture.", "at": "委員會拒絕批准這項研究提案，理由是科學家們的主張無法證實，而他們的結論不過是建立在臆測之上。"}, {"w": "ambiguous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Open to more than one interpretation; not clear.", "c": "模稜兩可的；含糊不清的", "s": "The poet's final line is deliberately ambiguous: readers have argued for decades over whether the closing image of an open door represents hope for a new beginning or a quiet acceptance of death.", "t": "這位詩人的最後一行刻意寫得模稜兩可：數十年來，讀者一直爭論結尾那扇敞開之門的意象，究竟代表對新開始的希望，還是對死亡的平靜接受。", "as": "The diplomat's ambiguous statement, an artful exercise in obfuscation, allowed both rival factions to construe it as quiet support for their own fiercely opposed positions.", "at": "這位外交官模稜兩可的聲明是一次刻意混淆視聽的巧妙操作，讓兩個敵對派系都能將它解讀為對自己那截然對立立場的默默支持。"}, {"w": "spendthrift", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who spends money wastefully and recklessly.", "c": "揮霍無度的人；敗家子", "s": "Her grandfather had saved carefully for fifty years, but her uncle was a notorious spendthrift who wasted his entire inheritance on sports cars, luxury vacations, and failed business ventures within just three years of receiving it.", "t": "她的祖父五十年來一直謹慎存錢，但她的叔叔卻是出了名的揮霍無度之人，在拿到遺產後短短三年內，就把全部遺產浪費在跑車、豪華度假和失敗的投資事業上。", "as": "Unlike his frugal sister, who invested every spare dollar prudently, the young spendthrift squandered his salary on ostentatious watches and lavish parties for friends he barely knew.", "at": "不同於把每一塊閒錢都謹慎投資的節儉姊姊，這個年輕的敗家子把薪水揮霍在炫耀用的名錶，以及為幾乎不認識的朋友舉辦的奢華派對上。"}, {"w": "mollify", "p": "v.", "d": "To calm or soothe someone's anger or anxiety.", "c": "平息（怒氣）；安撫", "s": "Hoping to mollify the angry residents who had protested the new highway, the mayor promised to build a sound barrier, plant hundreds of trees along the route, and hold monthly public meetings to address their concerns.", "t": "為了安撫抗議新高速公路的憤怒居民，市長承諾興建隔音牆、沿線種植數百棵樹，並每月舉行公聽會以回應他們的疑慮。", "as": "The manager's effusive apology did little to mollify the irascible customer, who continued to castigate the staff loudly for nearly ten minutes in front of the entire crowded restaurant.", "at": "經理熱情洋溢的道歉，幾乎無法平息那位易怒顧客的怒氣，他當著擁擠餐廳裡所有人的面，持續大聲斥責員工將近十分鐘。"}, {"w": "unequivocal", "p": "adj.", "d": "Clear and certain; leaving no doubt.", "c": "明確的；毫不含糊的", "s": "The results of the ten-year study were unequivocal: students who slept at least eight hours a night consistently earned higher test scores than those who slept less, a pattern that held true across every school and age group examined.", "t": "這項十年研究的結果毫不含糊：每晚至少睡八小時的學生，考試成績始終高於睡得較少的學生，而這個模式在所有受調查的學校和年齡層中都成立。", "as": "Her unequivocal denial, delivered with stoic calm, silenced the allegations that had dogged her campaign for months, though a few dissident reporters remained privately skeptical.", "at": "她以堅忍沉著的態度發表毫不含糊的否認，平息了數月來糾纏她競選活動的指控，不過仍有少數持不同意見的記者私下存疑。"}, {"w": "malleable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Easily shaped or influenced; adaptable.", "c": "可塑的；易受影響的", "s": "Because gold is so malleable, ancient craftsmen could hammer a single small nugget into sheets thinner than paper, which they then used to decorate temple walls, royal furniture, and the burial masks of powerful rulers.", "t": "由於黃金的延展性極佳，古代工匠能將一小塊金塊捶打成比紙還薄的金箔，再用來裝飾神殿牆面、王室家具以及有權勢統治者的陪葬面具。", "as": "Young children's malleable minds make them especially vulnerable to propaganda, which is why the regime sought to indoctrinate students with didactic textbooks and ubiquitous slogans.", "at": "幼童的心智可塑性高，因此特別容易受到宣傳的影響，這正是該政權試圖用說教式的教科書和隨處可見的標語向學生灌輸思想的原因。"}, {"w": "verbose", "p": "adj.", "d": "Using more words than are needed.", "c": "冗長的；囉嗦的", "s": "The editor returned the student's essay with a single comment in red ink, warning that the writing was far too verbose and that the main argument could easily be expressed in half the space without losing any important ideas.", "t": "編輯把那名學生的文章退回，只用紅筆寫了一條評語，提醒他文筆太過冗長，主要論點大可用一半的篇幅表達，而不會遺漏任何重要觀點。", "as": "The senator's verbose speech, larded with platitudes and grandiloquent promises, put half the audience to sleep before he finally reached his main point about tax reform.", "at": "那位參議員冗長的演說充斥著陳腔濫調和浮誇的承諾，在他終於講到有關稅制改革的重點之前，已有一半聽眾睡著了。"}]}, {"unit": 5, "level": 1, "cards": [{"w": "transient", "p": "adj.", "d": "Lasting only a short time; temporary.", "c": "短暫的；轉瞬即逝的", "s": "Psychologists distinguish between lasting changes in mood and transient emotions, such as the brief irritation people feel when stuck in traffic, which usually disappear within minutes and leave no long-term effect on overall well-being.", "t": "心理學家區分持久的情緒變化與短暫的情緒，例如人們塞車時感受到的短暫煩躁，這類情緒通常幾分鐘內就會消失，對整體身心健康不會留下長期影響。", "as": "Fame on social media is often transient, and many influencers who enjoyed a meteoric rise discover that public adoration is as ephemeral as it is lucrative.", "at": "社群媒體上的名氣往往轉瞬即逝，許多經歷過爆紅的網紅發現，大眾的追捧既能帶來豐厚收入，也同樣曇花一現。"}, {"w": "nettle", "p": "v.", "d": "To irritate or annoy someone.", "c": "惹惱；激怒", "s": "The coach's repeated comments about her slow starts began to nettle the young sprinter, who felt that he ignored her steady improvement and focused only on the single weakness she was already working hard to correct.", "t": "教練一再評論她起跑太慢，開始惹惱這位年輕的短跑選手，她覺得教練忽略了她穩定的進步，只盯著她早已努力改正的那一個弱點。", "as": "The critic's supercilious remarks about regional cuisine never failed to nettle the chef, who resented being lectured by someone so pedantic about dishes he had cooked for thirty years.", "at": "那位評論家對地方菜餚高傲自大的評語總是惹惱這位主廚，他厭惡被一個如此賣弄學問的人教訓自己已經烹調了三十年的菜餚。"}, {"w": "repudiate", "p": "v.", "d": "To reject or refuse to accept something as true or valid.", "c": "否認；拒絕接受", "s": "Years after publishing his controversial theory, the economist chose to repudiate his own earlier conclusions, publicly admitting that new data had shown his predictions about rising unemployment to be completely mistaken.", "t": "在發表那項具爭議性的理論多年後，這位經濟學家選擇公開否定自己先前的結論，坦承新數據已證明他對失業率上升的預測完全錯誤。", "as": "The scientist issued a categorical statement repudiating the spurious claims attributed to her, insisting that her research had never suggested the supplement was a panacea for aging.", "at": "這位科學家發表一份斷然的聲明，否認外界歸諸於她的那些虛假說法，堅稱她的研究從未暗示這種補充品是對抗老化的萬靈丹。"}, {"w": "impetuous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Acting quickly without thinking carefully; rash.", "c": "衝動的；魯莽的", "s": "In a moment of impetuous anger, the young king declared war on his neighbor without consulting his generals, a reckless decision that cost his kingdom thousands of soldiers and nearly half of its territory.", "t": "在一時衝動的怒氣之下，這位年輕的國王沒有徵詢將領的意見便向鄰國宣戰，這個魯莽的決定讓他的王國損失了數千名士兵和將近一半的領土。", "as": "His impetuous decision to quit his job and invest his savings in a dubious venture alarmed his more circumspect friends, who considered the scheme quixotic and urged him to think carefully before acting.", "at": "他衝動地決定辭職，並將積蓄投入一項可疑的事業，令他那些較為謹慎的朋友大感擔憂；他們認為這個計畫不切實際，力勸他三思而後行。"}, {"w": "frugal", "p": "adj.", "d": "Careful to spend little money or use few resources.", "c": "節儉的；樸素的", "s": "Raised by parents who had survived the Great Depression, Martha remained frugal all her life, reusing wrapping paper, repairing old clothes, and saving enough money to donate a generous scholarship fund to her hometown high school.", "t": "瑪莎由經歷過經濟大蕭條的父母撫養長大，一生都保持節儉，重複使用包裝紙、修補舊衣服，並存下足夠的錢，為家鄉的高中捐贈一筆可觀的獎學金。", "as": "Though she lived in a frugal apartment and ate simple meals, the retired teacher was remarkably philanthropic, quietly funding scholarships for indigent students across the district.", "at": "雖然這位退休教師住在簡樸的公寓、吃著簡單的飯菜，她卻非常樂善好施，默默資助全區貧困學生的獎學金。"}, {"w": "incongruous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Out of place; not fitting with its surroundings.", "c": "不協調的；不相稱的", "s": "The bright neon sign advertising a fast-food restaurant looked strangely incongruous beside the quiet, centuries-old stone temple, and many visitors complained that it ruined the peaceful atmosphere of the historic neighborhood.", "t": "那塊宣傳速食餐廳的亮眼霓虹招牌，矗立在寧靜的百年石造寺廟旁顯得格格不入，許多遊客抱怨它破壞了這個歷史街區的寧靜氛圍。", "as": "The architect's decision to juxtapose a sleek glass tower with the ornate Victorian library created an incongruous effect that some critics found refreshing and others dismissed as a tawdry, meretricious stunt.", "at": "建築師決定讓一座線條俐落的玻璃大樓與華麗的維多利亞式圖書館並置，造成一種不協調的效果，有些評論家覺得耳目一新，另一些則斥之為俗麗浮誇的噱頭。"}, {"w": "assuage", "p": "v.", "d": "To make an unpleasant feeling less intense; to ease.", "c": "緩和；減輕（痛苦、憂慮）", "s": "To assuage parents' fears about the new online learning program, the principal invited families to attend a hands-on demonstration, where they could try the software themselves and ask teachers detailed questions about student privacy.", "t": "為了減輕家長對新線上學習計畫的疑慮，校長邀請家長參加實際操作示範，讓他們能親自試用軟體，並向老師詳細詢問學生隱私的問題。", "as": "Nothing could assuage the widow's grief, though her friends tried to commiserate with her and offer what little succor they could during those first bleak months.", "at": "沒有什麼能減輕這位遺孀的悲痛，儘管朋友們在最初那幾個淒涼的月份裡，試著與她同感哀傷，並盡力給予微薄的慰藉。"}, {"w": "corroborate", "p": "v.", "d": "To confirm or support with additional evidence.", "c": "證實；確證", "s": "Before publishing the story, the journalist needed at least two independent sources to corroborate the whistleblower's account, since a single unverified claim about government corruption could expose the newspaper to a costly lawsuit.", "t": "在刊登這則報導之前，這名記者需要至少兩個獨立消息來源來證實那位吹哨者的說法，因為單一未經查證的政府貪腐指控，可能讓報社面臨代價高昂的訴訟。", "as": "No reliable witness could corroborate the defendant's alibi, and the jury found his story about the missing hours too circuitous and implausible to grant it any credence.", "at": "沒有可靠的證人能證實被告的不在場證明，而陪審團認為他對那幾個小時下落不明的說法太過迂迴且難以置信，無法採信。"}, {"w": "embellish", "p": "v.", "d": "To make a story more interesting by adding details, often untrue.", "c": "潤飾；添油加醋", "s": "Every time Grandpa told the story of his fishing trip, he seemed to embellish it a little more, until the modest trout he had actually caught became a giant fish that nearly dragged him overboard.", "t": "爺爺每次講他釣魚之旅的故事，似乎都會再添油加醋一些，直到他實際釣到的那條普通鱒魚，變成了一條差點把他拖下船的大魚。", "as": "The memoirist was accused of embellishing her childhood hardships, and critics argued that such hyperbole undermined the probity that readers expect from a work of nonfiction.", "at": "這位回憶錄作家被指控誇大了她童年的艱辛，評論家認為這種誇飾損害了讀者對非虛構作品所期待的誠實正直。"}, {"w": "avaricious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having an extreme desire for wealth; greedy.", "c": "貪婪的；貪得無厭的", "s": "In the classic novel, the avaricious landlord raises rents every winter and evicts poor families without mercy, caring only about adding more gold coins to the locked chest he keeps hidden beneath his bed.", "t": "在這部經典小說中，那個貪得無厭的地主每年冬天都調漲房租，毫不留情地趕走貧困家庭，一心只想著往藏在床底下那個上鎖的箱子裡添更多金幣。", "as": "The avaricious merchant's insatiable cupidity eventually ruined him, for he cheated so many loyal customers over the years that no one in the entire city would trade with him anymore.", "at": "那名貪婪商人永不滿足的貪欲最終毀了他自己，因為多年來他欺騙了太多忠實顧客，以致全城再也沒有人願意和他做生意。"}, {"w": "cursory", "p": "adj.", "d": "Done quickly and without attention to detail.", "c": "粗略的；草率的", "s": "A cursory glance at the report suggested that the bridge was safe, but engineers who examined every page carefully discovered hidden cracks in two support beams that required immediate and expensive repairs.", "t": "粗略瀏覽這份報告，似乎顯示這座橋很安全，但仔細檢視每一頁的工程師發現，有兩根支撐樑存在隱藏的裂縫，需要立即進行昂貴的修繕。", "as": "The inspector's cursory review of the textile factory was so perfunctory that he entirely missed the squalid conditions in the workers' crowded dormitory, which journalists exposed only a few weeks later.", "at": "那名檢查員對這家紡織廠的檢查草率敷衍，完全沒有注意到擁擠的工人宿舍裡髒亂不堪的環境，直到幾週後才被記者揭露。"}, {"w": "vacillate", "p": "v.", "d": "To keep changing one's mind; to waver.", "c": "猶豫不決；搖擺不定", "s": "Students who vacillate between majors for too long may need extra semesters to graduate, so advisors encourage them to explore their interests early and make a firm decision by the end of their second year.", "t": "在主修科系之間搖擺不定太久的學生，可能需要多讀幾個學期才能畢業，因此導師鼓勵他們及早探索興趣，並在大二結束前做出明確決定。", "as": "Ambivalent about the proposed merger, the board continued to vacillate for several months, and the costly delay allowed a more astute rival to acquire the struggling company first.", "at": "董事會對這項合併提案心情矛盾，持續搖擺不定了好幾個月，而這段代價高昂的拖延讓一個更精明的對手搶先收購了那家陷入困境的公司。"}, {"w": "clement", "p": "adj.", "d": "Mild and pleasant, especially of weather; merciful.", "c": "溫和的（氣候）；仁慈寬厚的", "s": "Because the island enjoys clement weather throughout the year, with gentle breezes and temperatures rarely falling below twenty degrees, it has become a popular destination for retirees seeking relief from harsh northern winters.", "t": "由於這座島全年氣候溫和，微風輕拂，氣溫很少低於二十度，它已成為想逃離北方嚴冬的退休人士熱門的去處。", "as": "The judge proved unexpectedly clement, sentencing the contrite teenager to community service rather than prison, since his offense was a minor peccadillo and his compunction seemed entirely sincere.", "at": "法官出乎意料地寬大為懷，判處那名悔過的青少年從事社區服務而非入獄，因為他的過錯只是小過失，而且他的悔意看來完全真誠。"}, {"w": "lucrative", "p": "adj.", "d": "Producing a large amount of money; profitable.", "c": "有利可圖的；賺錢的", "s": "After the company's mobile game was downloaded by millions of players worldwide, the small startup signed a lucrative contract with a major film studio, earning more in a single year than it had in the previous decade.", "t": "這家公司的手機遊戲在全球被數百萬玩家下載後，這間小新創公司與一家大型電影公司簽下一紙利潤豐厚的合約，一年的收入就超過了過去十年。", "as": "Though medicine offered a far more lucrative career, she felt an inexorable pull toward teaching in rural schools, which she considered a much more edifying vocation than any hospital job.", "at": "雖然從醫能提供優渥得多的收入，她卻感受到一股無法抗拒的力量將她引向鄉村學校的教職，她認為那是一份比任何醫院工作都更具啟發意義的志業。"}, {"w": "allocate", "p": "v.", "d": "To distribute or set aside resources for a particular purpose.", "c": "分配；撥出", "s": "Facing a tight budget, the school board had to decide how to allocate its limited funds, ultimately choosing to spend most of the money on hiring reading specialists rather than replacing the old gym floor.", "t": "面對緊縮的預算，學校董事會必須決定如何分配有限的經費，最終選擇把大部分經費用來聘請閱讀專家，而非更換老舊的體育館地板。", "as": "Critics charged that the ministry allocated public funds with a nepotism so egregious that the minister's cousins received lucrative contracts while far more competent firms were simply ignored.", "at": "批評者指控該部會分配經費時任人唯親，情形惡劣至極，部長的表親們拿到了利潤豐厚的合約，而能力好得多的公司卻完全遭到忽視。"}, {"w": "reconcile", "p": "v.", "d": "To make two conflicting things or people compatible again.", "c": "調和；使和解", "s": "The biography explores how the scientist tried to reconcile her deep religious faith with her research on evolution, eventually concluding after years of reflection that the two could coexist without contradicting each other.", "t": "這本傳記探討這位科學家如何試圖調和她深厚的宗教信仰與她的演化研究，經過多年思索後，她最終得出結論：兩者可以並存而互不矛盾。", "as": "The mediator worked to reconcile the contentious factions, but their mutual animosity was so deep that even a modest compromise proved elusive and the negotiations soon collapsed.", "at": "調解人努力讓爭執不休的各派系和解，但他們彼此的敵意太深，即使是小小的妥協都難以達成，談判很快就破裂了。"}, {"w": "paragon", "p": "n.", "d": "A perfect example of a particular quality.", "c": "典範；模範", "s": "Admired by students and colleagues alike, the retired principal was considered a paragon of fairness, never showing favoritism and always listening patiently to every side before making a decision about school discipline.", "t": "這位退休校長深受學生與同事敬重，被視為公正的典範，從不偏袒任何人，在對校規處分做出決定前，總是耐心聆聽各方意見。", "as": "Once hailed as a paragon of probity, the veteran senator was publicly disgraced when investigative reporters revealed an elaborate scheme of duplicity and bribery stretching back two decades.", "at": "這位資深參議員曾被譽為正直的典範，但當調查記者揭露一樁可追溯至二十年前、充滿欺騙與賄賂的精密陰謀時，他便公開聲名掃地。"}, {"w": "analogous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Similar or comparable in certain ways.", "c": "類似的；可類比的", "s": "The biology teacher explained that the heart is analogous to a water pump, since both push liquid through a system of tubes by repeatedly squeezing and relaxing in a steady, rhythmic pattern.", "t": "生物老師解釋說，心臟類似於抽水機，因為兩者都是透過穩定而有節奏地反覆收縮與放鬆，將液體推送通過一套管路系統。", "as": "The essayist argued that today's ubiquitous smartphones are analogous to the printing press, a technology whose effects on society were at first impalpable but ultimately revolutionary.", "at": "這位散文家認為，今日無所不在的智慧型手機類似於印刷機——這項科技對社會的影響起初難以察覺，最終卻帶來革命性的改變。"}, {"w": "diurnal", "p": "adj.", "d": "Active during the daytime; occurring every day.", "c": "白天活動的；每日的", "s": "Unlike owls, which hunt at night, hawks are diurnal predators that rely on their remarkably sharp eyesight in bright sunlight to spot mice and rabbits moving through open fields far below.", "t": "不同於夜間獵食的貓頭鷹，老鷹是白天活動的掠食者，牠們仰賴在明亮陽光下極為銳利的視力，發現遠在下方空曠田野中移動的老鼠和兔子。", "as": "Researchers found that the lizard's diurnal habits were not immutable; in hot summers it became noctivagant, foraging under moonlight to escape the heat that left it lethargic at noon.", "at": "研究人員發現，這種蜥蜴白天活動的習性並非一成不變；在炎熱的夏季，牠會變成夜行性，在月光下覓食，以避開讓牠中午無精打采的酷熱。"}, {"w": "pretext", "p": "n.", "d": "A false reason given to hide the real reason.", "c": "藉口；託辭", "s": "The general used a minor border incident as a pretext for invading the neighboring country, although historians later found letters proving he had planned the attack months before the incident ever occurred.", "t": "這位將軍以一起輕微的邊境事件作為入侵鄰國的藉口，但歷史學家後來發現信件，證明他早在事件發生數月前就已策劃了這次攻擊。", "as": "Under the pretext of a routine tax audit, the officials staged an elaborate subterfuge to search the outspoken dissident's office for incriminating documents that might justify his arrest.", "at": "官員們以例行稅務稽核為藉口，精心策劃了一場詭計，搜查那名直言不諱的異議人士的辦公室，尋找可作為逮捕他理由的入罪文件。"}]}, {"unit": 6, "level": 2, "cards": [{"w": "defray", "p": "v.", "d": "To pay or provide money for costs or expenses.", "c": "支付；負擔（費用）", "s": "To help defray the rising cost of attending the international science fair in Geneva, the students organized bake sales, washed cars on weekends, and applied for a small grant from the local chamber of commerce.", "t": "為了幫忙支付前往日內瓦參加國際科展日益上漲的費用，學生們舉辦了烘焙義賣、週末幫人洗車，並向當地商會申請了一小筆補助金。", "as": "A philanthropic alumna offered to defray the travel expenses of indigent students, allowing several talented but impoverished teenagers to attend the summer academy for the first time.", "at": "一位樂善好施的女校友提議負擔貧困學生的旅費，讓幾位有才華但家境清寒的青少年首次得以參加這個暑期學院。"}, {"w": "taciturn", "p": "adj.", "d": "Habitually saying very little; reserved in speech.", "c": "沉默寡言的；不愛說話的", "s": "The taciturn farmer rarely spoke more than a few words at the town meetings, so everyone fell silent in surprise when he stood up and delivered a passionate ten-minute speech against the proposed factory.", "t": "那位沉默寡言的農夫在鎮民大會上很少說超過幾個字，所以當他站起來發表一場反對興建工廠提案、長達十分鐘的熱情演說時，大家都驚訝得安靜下來。", "as": "The taciturn detective, a stark contrast to his garrulous partner, preferred to listen silently while suspects talked, often noticing the small inconsistencies that exposed their duplicity.", "at": "那位沉默寡言的警探與他喋喋不休的搭檔形成鮮明對比，他寧可在嫌犯說話時靜靜聆聽，常常察覺到那些揭穿他們欺瞞的小矛盾。"}, {"w": "terse", "p": "adj.", "d": "Brief and to the point, sometimes rudely so.", "c": "簡潔的；簡短生硬的", "s": "Instead of the long apology the customers expected, the airline posted a terse two-sentence message on its website announcing that all flights were cancelled, which angered travelers who wanted a full explanation.", "t": "航空公司沒有發表顧客期待的長篇道歉，而是在網站上貼出一則只有兩句話的簡短訊息，宣布所有航班取消，這激怒了想要完整解釋的旅客。", "as": "The editor's terse comments in the margins, a welcome change from her predecessor's verbose critiques, helped the young novelist trim the prolix chapters into lean, vivid prose.", "at": "編輯在頁邊寫下的簡潔評語，和她前任那些冗長的評論相比令人耳目一新，幫助這位年輕小說家把冗長的章節刪修成精簡生動的文字。"}, {"w": "boon", "p": "n.", "d": "Something helpful or beneficial; a blessing.", "c": "恩惠；益處", "s": "The new subway line has been a boon to commuters in the northern suburbs, cutting their travel time to the city center in half and allowing many parents to spend more evenings at home with their children.", "t": "這條新捷運路線對北部郊區的通勤族來說是一大福音，讓他們前往市中心的通勤時間縮短一半，許多父母也因此能有更多晚上在家陪伴孩子。", "as": "The discovery of penicillin was an incalculable boon to medicine, serving as a nearly ubiquitous treatment for infections that had once been pernicious and often fatal.", "at": "盤尼西林的發現對醫學而言是無可估量的恩惠，成為幾乎普及各地的感染治療藥物，而這些感染過去曾是有害且經常致命的。"}, {"w": "proletariat", "p": "n.", "d": "The working class, especially industrial wage earners.", "c": "無產階級；勞工階級", "s": "In nineteenth-century factory towns, the proletariat worked fourteen-hour days for meager wages, and the harsh conditions they endured led thinkers such as Karl Marx to predict that ordinary workers would someday rise up against factory owners.", "t": "在十九世紀的工廠城鎮中，無產階級每天工作十四小時卻只領微薄工資，他們所忍受的嚴苛條件，使卡爾‧馬克思等思想家預言普通勞工終有一天會起而反抗工廠老闆。", "as": "The revolutionary pamphlets urged the proletariat to resist the oligarchy, condemning the wealthy factory owners for paying their workers a pittance while living in opulent mansions.", "at": "這些革命傳單呼籲無產階級反抗寡頭統治，譴責富有的工廠老闆付給工人微薄的工資，自己卻住在奢華的豪宅裡。"}, {"w": "heterogeneous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Made up of different or varied kinds of parts.", "c": "由不同成分組成的；混雜的", "s": "The class was highly heterogeneous, including students from twelve different countries, ranging in age from seventeen to sixty, and bringing backgrounds as varied as nursing, engineering, music, and professional basketball.", "t": "這個班級的組成非常多元，包括來自十二個不同國家的學生，年齡從十七歲到六十歲不等，背景也五花八門，有護理、工程、音樂，甚至職業籃球。", "as": "The anthology gathers a heterogeneous collection of essays, from esoteric meditations on philosophy to droll sketches of village life, united only by the editor's eclectic taste.", "at": "這本選集收錄了內容各異的散文，從探討哲學的深奧沉思，到描寫鄉村生活的詼諧小品都有，唯一的共通點是編者兼容並蓄的品味。"}, {"w": "pittance", "p": "n.", "d": "A very small or inadequate amount of money.", "c": "微薄的收入；少量的錢", "s": "Many artists in the early twentieth century sold their paintings for a pittance, sometimes trading a canvas for a single meal, only to have those same works auctioned for millions of dollars decades after their deaths.", "t": "二十世紀初，許多藝術家以極微薄的價錢出售畫作，有時一幅畫只換得一頓飯，但數十年後在他們過世之後，同樣的作品卻在拍賣會上賣出數百萬美元。", "as": "The mercenary employer paid his seasonal laborers a mere pittance, yet he lived in opulent luxury and boasted of his business acumen at every dinner party.", "at": "那個唯利是圖的雇主只付給季節性工人微薄的工資，自己卻過著奢華的生活，在每場晚宴上吹噓自己的經商頭腦。"}, {"w": "glib", "p": "adj.", "d": "Speaking smoothly and easily but without sincerity or depth.", "c": "油嘴滑舌的；圓滑而膚淺的", "s": "The salesman's glib answers sounded impressive at first, but when the customer asked specific questions about the car's safety record, it became clear that his smooth confidence hid a complete lack of real knowledge.", "t": "那名業務員油腔滑調的回答起初聽來令人印象深刻，但當顧客問到有關這輛車安全紀錄的具體問題時，就清楚看出他圓滑的自信底下完全沒有真正的知識。", "as": "The candidate's glib promises and facile solutions to complex problems charmed the cheering crowd, but seasoned journalists recognized his speeches as little more than polished sophistry.", "at": "那位候選人油嘴滑舌的承諾和對複雜問題的膚淺解決方案迷住了歡呼的群眾，但經驗老到的記者看出他的演說不過是包裝精美的詭辯。"}, {"w": "penchant", "p": "n.", "d": "A strong liking or tendency to do something.", "c": "嗜好；傾向", "s": "The famous detective novelist had a penchant for hiding important clues in ordinary objects, such as a teacup or a train ticket, so devoted readers learned to examine every small detail in her books very carefully.", "t": "這位知名推理小說家偏好把重要線索藏在茶杯或火車票之類的日常物品中，所以忠實讀者學會非常仔細地檢視她書中的每一個小細節。", "as": "The professor's penchant for esoteric allusions to medieval poetry made her lectures fascinating to graduate students but nearly inscrutable to the bewildered freshmen sitting in the back row.", "at": "這位教授偏好引用中世紀詩歌中深奧的典故，讓她的課對研究生而言引人入勝，但對坐在後排、一頭霧水的大一新生來說卻幾乎難以理解。"}, {"w": "solicitous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Showing care and concern for someone's well-being.", "c": "關切的；體貼的", "s": "The nurses on the children's ward were remarkably solicitous, checking on each young patient every hour, bringing extra blankets on cold nights, and patiently answering every worried question from anxious parents.", "t": "兒童病房的護理師格外體貼周到，每小時探視每位小病患、在寒冷的夜晚多送毯子來，並耐心回答焦慮父母提出的每個擔憂問題。", "as": "The courtier's solicitous attention to the queen seemed sincere at first, but his ingratiating manner soon revealed itself as obsequious flattery aimed at securing a lucrative post.", "at": "那名朝臣對女王殷勤的關切起初看似真誠，但他討好的態度很快就顯露出，那其實是為了謀取一份肥缺而卑躬屈膝的奉承。"}, {"w": "circumscribe", "p": "v.", "d": "To restrict or limit something within boundaries.", "c": "限制；約束", "s": "The new regulations circumscribe the role of private companies in the national park, permitting them to run small cafés and bicycle rentals but forbidding any hotels, billboards, or construction near the protected lakes.", "t": "新法規限制了民營企業在國家公園中的角色，允許他們經營小型咖啡館和自行車租賃，但禁止在受保護的湖泊附近興建任何旅館、設立廣告看板或進行任何工程。", "as": "The constitution carefully circumscribes executive power, preventing any president from wielding the omnipotent authority that the founders associated with the capricious and despotic monarchs who had once ruled much of Europe.", "at": "這部憲法嚴格限制行政權力，避免任何總統擁有開國元勳們聯想到昔日統治歐洲大部分地區、反覆無常的專制君主的那種無上權威。"}, {"w": "dearth", "p": "n.", "d": "A lack or scarcity of something.", "c": "缺乏；不足", "s": "Because of a dearth of qualified science teachers in rural areas, many village schools must rely on online video lessons, and some students reach high school without ever having performed a real laboratory experiment.", "t": "由於鄉村地區缺乏合格的自然科學教師，許多村莊學校必須依賴線上影片課程，有些學生直到上高中都沒有做過一次真正的實驗。", "as": "Despite the copious data the team collected, there was a dearth of demonstrable evidence linking the chemical to the disease, so the committee declined to ban it.", "at": "儘管研究團隊收集了大量數據，卻缺乏可證實該化學物質與疾病有關的證據，因此委員會拒絕禁用它。"}, {"w": "ingratiating", "p": "adj.", "d": "Intended to gain approval or favor, often insincerely.", "c": "討好的；逢迎的", "s": "The new employee's ingratiating habit of complimenting the manager's every idea and bringing her coffee each morning annoyed his coworkers, who suspected he cared more about a promotion than about doing good work.", "t": "這名新進員工討好的習慣——稱讚主管的每個想法，每天早上還幫她買咖啡——讓同事們很反感，他們懷疑他在乎升遷勝過把工作做好。", "as": "His ingratiating smile and effusive praise of the director failed to conceal his duplicity, and his colleagues began to regard him as nothing more than a scheming sycophant.", "at": "他討好的笑容和對主管熱情洋溢的讚美，掩飾不了他的表裡不一，同事們開始把他看成不過是個工於心計的馬屁精。"}, {"w": "mercenary", "p": "adj.", "d": "Motivated chiefly by a desire for money or gain.", "c": "唯利是圖的；貪財的", "s": "Critics accused the drug company of being purely mercenary after it raised the price of a life-saving medicine by five hundred percent overnight, knowing that desperate patients would have no choice but to pay.", "t": "這家藥廠一夜之間將一種救命藥物的價格調漲百分之五百，明知走投無路的病患別無選擇只能付錢，批評者因此指責它完全唯利是圖。", "as": "The novel's villain is a mercenary lawyer whose avaricious schemes ruin a dozen families, until a parsimonious old clerk exposes his fraud to the court.", "at": "這部小說的反派是一個唯利是圖的律師，他貪婪的詭計毀了十幾個家庭，直到一位吝嗇的老書記員向法庭揭發了他的詐騙行為。"}, {"w": "extemporize", "p": "v.", "d": "To speak or perform without preparation; to improvise.", "c": "即興表演；即席演說", "s": "When the projector failed halfway through her presentation, the student calmly set aside her slides and chose to extemporize, explaining her research on coral reefs so clearly that the judges awarded her first prize.", "t": "當投影機在她報告到一半時故障，這位學生冷靜地把投影片擱在一旁，選擇即席發揮，把她對珊瑚礁的研究講解得清楚透徹，評審因而頒給她第一名。", "as": "Forced to extemporize when the keynote speaker failed to appear, the adroit host delivered an impromptu talk so witty and lucid that many guests preferred it to the scheduled program.", "at": "主講人沒有現身，被迫即席發揮的主持人以機敏的臨場反應，發表了一場風趣又清晰的即興談話，許多來賓甚至覺得比原訂節目還要精彩。"}, {"w": "erudite", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having or showing great knowledge from study.", "c": "博學的；有學問的", "s": "The erudite historian could read seven ancient languages and seemed to remember every detail of every source she had studied, so younger scholars often visited her office for advice on difficult research questions.", "t": "這位博學的歷史學家能閱讀七種古代語言，似乎記得她研究過的每一份文獻的每個細節，所以年輕學者經常到她的辦公室，請教困難的研究問題。", "as": "Although the essay was undeniably erudite, its abstruse vocabulary and pedantic footnotes made it almost impenetrable to the general readers whom the popular magazine had hoped to attract.", "at": "雖然這篇文章無疑內容博學，但其艱澀的用字和賣弄學問的註腳，讓這本大眾雜誌原本希望吸引的一般讀者幾乎無法讀懂。"}, {"w": "austere", "p": "adj.", "d": "Severely simple and plain; strict or stern.", "c": "樸素的；嚴峻的", "s": "The monks lived in an austere stone building with bare walls, wooden benches, and no heating, believing that a simple life without comfort or decoration would help them concentrate on prayer and study.", "t": "修士們住在一棟樸素的石造建築中，牆壁光禿、只有木製長椅，也沒有暖氣，他們相信一種沒有舒適與裝飾的簡樸生活，能幫助他們專注於祈禱和研讀。", "as": "The austere headmaster, a stern martinet who prized discipline above all, had little patience for levity in his classrooms and punished even minor pranks severely.", "at": "那位嚴峻的校長是一個極重紀律、嚴厲的人，他在課堂上容不得一點輕浮，即使是小小的惡作劇也會嚴加懲罰。"}, {"w": "laconic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Using very few words; concise to the point of seeming brief.", "c": "簡潔的；言簡意賅的", "s": "When reporters asked the champion how she felt about breaking the world record, her laconic reply was simply “Good,” after which she smiled, waved to the crowd, and walked off to rejoin her teammates.", "t": "當記者問這位冠軍打破世界紀錄有何感想時，她簡潔的回答只有一句「很好」，接著她微笑著向群眾揮手，然後走去與隊友會合。", "as": "Unlike his voluble predecessor, the new coach was famously laconic, and his brief, trenchant comments to reporters often revealed more than an hour of grandiloquent speeches ever had.", "at": "不同於他那位口若懸河的前任，新教練出了名地言簡意賅，他對記者簡短而犀利的評論，往往比一小時的浮誇演說透露得更多。"}, {"w": "ameliorate", "p": "v.", "d": "To make a bad situation better or more tolerable.", "c": "改善；改進", "s": "To ameliorate the severe traffic congestion downtown, city planners added dedicated bus lanes, expanded the bicycle-sharing program, and introduced a small fee for private cars entering the central business district during rush hour.", "t": "為了改善市中心嚴重的交通壅塞，都市規劃者增設了公車專用道、擴大公共自行車計畫，並對尖峰時段進入中心商業區的私家車酌收少量費用。", "as": "Volunteers worked tirelessly to ameliorate the squalid conditions in the refugee camp, though they knew such efforts could only palliate, not cure, the underlying crisis.", "at": "志工們不辭辛勞地努力改善難民營中髒亂惡劣的環境，雖然他們知道這些努力只能緩解、而無法根治潛在的危機。"}, {"w": "expunge", "p": "v.", "d": "To erase or remove completely.", "c": "刪除；抹去", "s": "After the investigation proved that the teenager had been falsely accused, the judge ordered the police to expunge the arrest from his record so that it would never appear in background checks by future employers or universities.", "t": "調查證明這名青少年遭到誣告後，法官命令警方將逮捕紀錄從他的檔案中徹底刪除，讓這筆紀錄永遠不會出現在未來雇主或大學的背景調查中。", "as": "The regime tried to expunge every trace of the dissident poet from public memory, banning his books and attempting to efface his name from school textbooks.", "at": "該政權企圖從公眾記憶中抹去那位異議詩人的一切痕跡，查禁他的著作，並設法把他的名字從學校教科書中抹除。"}]}, {"unit": 7, "level": 2, "cards": [{"w": "circumspect", "p": "adj.", "d": "Cautious and careful to consider all possible risks.", "c": "謹慎的；小心周到的", "s": "Because the archive's medieval manuscripts were fragile and irreplaceable, the curator remained circumspect about lending them, insisting on climate-controlled transport, armed escorts, and a detailed insurance review before approving any request from another museum.", "t": "由於檔案館的中世紀手稿脆弱且無可取代，館長對於出借一事始終十分謹慎，堅持在核准其他博物館的任何申請之前，必須採用恆溫恆濕運輸、武裝護送，並進行詳細的保險審查。", "as": "A circumspect diplomat, she avoided glib promises during the negotiations, knowing that one flippant remark could undermine months of careful work between the two wary governments.", "at": "身為一位謹慎的外交官，她在談判期間避免做出油腔滑調的承諾，因為她知道一句輕率的話就可能毀掉兩國政府之間數月來的苦心經營，畢竟雙方都對彼此心存戒備。"}, {"w": "quiescent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Quiet, inactive, or at rest, often only temporarily.", "c": "靜止的；暫時不活動的", "s": "Geologists warned residents that although the volcano had been quiescent for nearly two centuries, recent tremors and rising gas emissions suggested that its long period of inactivity might soon come to an end.", "t": "地質學家警告居民，雖然這座火山已沉寂將近兩個世紀，但近來的震動和不斷增加的氣體排放顯示，它漫長的靜止期可能即將結束。", "as": "The opposition movement remained quiescent for years, but the regime's latest tirade against journalists ignited a fervent wave of protest that no amount of censorship could suppress.", "at": "反對運動沉寂多年，但政權最近一次對記者的激烈抨擊，點燃了一波熱烈的抗議浪潮，任何審查都無法壓制。"}, {"w": "foible", "p": "n.", "d": "A minor weakness or odd habit in someone's character.", "c": "小缺點；怪癖", "s": "Biographers often note that Albert Einstein's habit of never wearing socks was a harmless foible rather than a serious flaw, a small personal quirk that made the brilliant physicist seem more approachable to the public.", "t": "傳記作家常指出，愛因斯坦從不穿襪子的習慣只是無傷大雅的小怪癖，而非嚴重的缺陷；這個個人的小毛病讓這位傑出的物理學家在大眾眼中顯得更平易近人。", "as": "Readers forgive the narrator's many foibles, such as his vanity, his penchant for exaggeration, and his peevish complaints about the weather, because his candor about his own flaws makes him oddly endearing.", "at": "讀者能原諒敘事者的種種小缺點，例如他的虛榮、他愛誇大的習性，以及他對天氣的暴躁抱怨，因為他坦率面對自己的缺陷，反而讓他出奇地討人喜歡。"}, {"w": "fervent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Showing intense, passionate feeling or enthusiasm.", "c": "熱烈的；熱忱的", "s": "Rachel Carson's fervent commitment to protecting wildlife was evident in every chapter of Silent Spring, where her passionate warnings about pesticides inspired readers across the nation to demand stronger environmental regulations.", "t": "瑞秋．卡森對保護野生動物的熱忱，在《寂靜的春天》每一章都清晰可見；她對殺蟲劑的激昂警告，激勵了全國讀者要求更嚴格的環境法規。", "as": "Her fervent speech in support of the new recycling program was persuasive, but her opponents dismissed it as a tirade full of nebulous promises and unprecedented costs.", "at": "她支持新回收計畫的熱情演說很有說服力，但反對者斥之為一場充滿模糊承諾、成本空前的長篇激烈言論。"}, {"w": "protract", "p": "v.", "d": "To prolong or extend something in time.", "c": "延長；拖延", "s": "Hoping to protract the negotiations until public opinion shifted in their favor, the company's lawyers filed motion after motion, requested repeated delays, and questioned every minor detail of the proposed settlement.", "t": "公司的律師希望拖延談判，直到輿論轉向對他們有利，因此一再提出動議、多次要求延期，並對和解提案的每一個細節提出質疑。", "as": "The senator's verbose speech protracted the debate for hours, and even his allies grew weary of a monologue so monotonous that several reporters in the gallery dozed off.", "at": "這位參議員冗長的演說使辯論拖延了好幾個小時，就連他的盟友都對這段單調至極的獨白感到厭倦，旁聽席上好幾位記者甚至打起瞌睡。"}, {"w": "ostentatious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Showy and designed to impress others with wealth.", "c": "炫耀的；鋪張浮誇的", "s": "Critics complained that the new city hall, with its gold-plated columns, marble fountains, and enormous crystal chandeliers, was far too ostentatious for a town that was struggling to pay its teachers and repair its roads.", "t": "批評者抱怨，新市政廳有鍍金圓柱、大理石噴泉和巨大的水晶吊燈，對一個連教師薪水和道路修繕都難以負擔的小鎮來說，實在太過鋪張炫耀。", "as": "Unlike his ostentatious rivals, the frugal billionaire drove an old sedan, wore plain clothes, and regarded lavish public displays of personal wealth as tawdry and vulgar.", "at": "與他那些愛炫耀的對手不同，這位節儉的億萬富翁開著一輛老舊轎車、穿著樸素的衣服，並認為公開炫富既俗麗又粗俗。"}, {"w": "quandary", "p": "n.", "d": "A state of uncertainty about what to do.", "c": "困惑；進退兩難的處境", "s": "When two prestigious universities offered her full scholarships on the same day, Mei-ling found herself in a quandary, unable to decide between studying marine biology in California or pursuing engineering closer to her family in Taipei.", "t": "當兩所名校在同一天提供她全額獎學金時，美玲陷入了兩難，無法決定要去加州攻讀海洋生物學，還是留在離台北家人較近的地方念工程。", "as": "Faced with an ethical quandary, the journalist had to decide whether publishing the clandestine documents would serve the public good or merely incriminate an innocent source.", "at": "面對道德上的兩難，這位記者必須決定，公開這些祕密文件究竟是為了公眾利益，還是只會讓一位無辜的消息來源受到牽連。"}, {"w": "censure", "p": "v.", "d": "To criticize strongly and formally express disapproval.", "c": "譴責；嚴厲批評", "s": "After an investigation revealed that he had used campaign funds for private vacations, the legislature voted overwhelmingly to censure the senator, formally condemning his conduct even though it stopped short of removing him from office.", "t": "在調查揭露他挪用競選經費支付私人度假費用後，議會以壓倒性多數投票通過譴責這位參議員，正式表達對其行為的非難，但並未將他解職。", "as": "The ethics committee censured the mayor for his unscrupulous dealings with developers, but critics argued that a mere reprimand was a negligible penalty for such blatant corruption.", "at": "倫理委員會譴責市長與開發商之間不擇手段的交易，但批評者認為，對如此明目張膽的貪腐而言，僅僅訓誡只是微不足道的懲罰。"}, {"w": "cavil", "p": "v.", "d": "To raise petty, unnecessary objections; to quibble.", "c": "挑剔；吹毛求疵", "s": "The review board approved the excellent research proposal quickly, since even its strictest members could find nothing to cavil about except a few misplaced commas and a slightly outdated citation in the bibliography.", "t": "審查委員會很快就核准了這份出色的研究計畫，因為就連最嚴格的委員也挑不出毛病，只能指出幾個放錯位置的逗號，以及參考書目中一筆稍嫌過時的引用。", "as": "Rather than cavil over minor grammatical errors, the editor focused on the essay's central claims, which she found tenuous and impossible to corroborate with reliable evidence.", "at": "這位編輯沒有在細微的文法錯誤上吹毛求疵，而是把重點放在文章的核心論點上；她認為這些論點站不住腳，而且無法以可靠的證據加以證實。"}, {"w": "assimilate", "p": "v.", "d": "To absorb and fully understand or integrate.", "c": "吸收；同化", "s": "Because the immigrant children were surrounded by classmates who spoke only English, they were able to assimilate the new language, customs, and slang far more quickly than their parents, who worked long hours in a family restaurant.", "t": "由於這些移民孩子身邊的同學都只說英語，他們吸收新語言、習俗和俚語的速度遠比在家族餐廳長時間工作的父母快得多。", "as": "Students who try to assimilate copious amounts of information the night before an exam often find that their cursory review leaves them confused rather than prepared.", "at": "在考前一晚試圖吸收大量資訊的學生，往往會發現草率的複習反而讓他們更加困惑，而不是準備得更充分。"}, {"w": "rescind", "p": "v.", "d": "To officially cancel or revoke a law or decision.", "c": "廢除；撤銷", "s": "After thousands of students signed a petition and staged peaceful protests outside the administration building, the principal agreed to rescind the unpopular rule banning cell phones during lunch, restoring the policy that had existed for years.", "t": "在數千名學生連署請願並在行政大樓外和平抗議後，校長同意撤銷午餐時間禁用手機這項不受歡迎的規定，恢復實施多年的原有政策。", "as": "Under pressure from passionate advocates of free speech, the council rescinded the ordinance, conceding that its ambiguous wording had allowed officials to enforce it in an arbitrary manner.", "at": "在言論自由熱情擁護者的壓力下，議會撤銷了這項條例，並承認其措辭含糊，使官員得以任意執法。"}, {"w": "discernible", "p": "adj.", "d": "Able to be seen, noticed, or understood.", "c": "可辨別的；看得出的", "s": "Although the changes were not obvious at first, by the end of the semester there was a clearly discernible improvement in the students' writing, with stronger thesis statements, smoother transitions, and far fewer grammatical errors.", "t": "雖然一開始變化並不明顯，但到了學期末，學生的寫作已有明顯可見的進步：論點陳述更有力、段落轉折更流暢，文法錯誤也少了許多。", "as": "The differences between the two paintings were barely discernible to the untrained eye, but an adept art historian quickly identified one as a tawdry imitation of the original.", "at": "對未受訓練的眼睛來說，這兩幅畫幾乎看不出差異，但一位老練的藝術史學家很快就辨識出其中一幅是原作的俗劣仿品。"}, {"w": "cataclysm", "p": "n.", "d": "A sudden, violent event causing great destruction or upheaval.", "c": "大災難；劇變", "s": "Many scientists believe that a massive asteroid striking the Yucatán Peninsula sixty-six million years ago was the cataclysm that wiped out the dinosaurs, filling the sky with dust and transforming Earth's climate almost overnight.", "t": "許多科學家相信，六千六百萬年前撞擊猶加敦半島的巨大小行星，就是導致恐龍滅絕的大災難，它讓天空布滿塵埃，幾乎在一夜之間改變了地球的氣候。", "as": "Historians describe the First World War as a cataclysm that shattered the old European order and engendered the political animosity that would erupt again two decades later.", "at": "歷史學家將第一次世界大戰描述為一場大災難，它粉碎了歐洲舊秩序，並催生出二十年後再度爆發的政治敵意。"}, {"w": "narcissism", "p": "n.", "d": "Excessive love and admiration of one's own self.", "c": "自戀；自我陶醉", "s": "Psychologists studying social media have found that constantly posting carefully edited selfies and counting likes can encourage narcissism, as users become increasingly obsessed with their own image and less interested in the lives of others.", "t": "研究社群媒體的心理學家發現，不斷張貼精心修飾的自拍照並計算按讚數，可能助長自戀心態，使用者會越來越執著於自己的形象，對他人的生活則越來越不感興趣。", "as": "The emperor's narcissism was legendary: he commissioned ostentatious statues of himself in every city and rebuffed even mild criticism with a furious, hour-long tirade against his advisers.", "at": "這位皇帝的自戀眾所皆知：他下令在每座城市建造浮誇炫耀的自身雕像，即使是溫和的批評，他也會對顧問發表長達一小時的激烈抨擊，斷然回絕。"}, {"w": "incriminate", "p": "v.", "d": "To make someone appear guilty of a crime.", "c": "使負罪；使（某人）涉入罪嫌", "s": "The defendant's lawyer advised him to remain silent during questioning, warning that even an innocent-sounding answer about his whereabouts that night could incriminate him and give prosecutors the evidence they needed for a conviction.", "t": "被告的律師建議他在偵訊時保持沉默，並警告說，即使是一句關於他當晚行蹤、聽起來無害的回答，都可能使他陷入罪嫌，並讓檢察官取得定罪所需的證據。", "as": "The clandestine recordings incriminated several officials, but the minister issued an unequivocal denial and dismissed the allegations as nothing more than a politically motivated attack by his rivals.", "at": "這些祕密錄音使數名官員涉入罪嫌，但部長發表了斬釘截鐵的否認聲明，並將這些指控斥為對手出於政治動機的攻擊而已。"}, {"w": "stigma", "p": "n.", "d": "A mark of disgrace associated with something.", "c": "恥辱；汙名", "s": "Public health campaigns in recent years have worked hard to reduce the stigma attached to mental illness, encouraging people who suffer from depression or anxiety to seek treatment without fear of being judged by others.", "t": "近年來的公共衛生宣導活動致力於減少精神疾病所背負的汙名，鼓勵罹患憂鬱症或焦慮症的人勇於尋求治療，而不必害怕被他人評斷。", "as": "In Victorian England, the stigma of poverty was so severe that indigent families were often ostracized by their neighbors and confined to squalid, overcrowded workhouses.", "at": "在維多利亞時代的英國，貧窮的汙名極為沉重，貧困家庭常遭鄰居排擠，並被關進骯髒擁擠的濟貧院。"}, {"w": "brevity", "p": "n.", "d": "Shortness of time or concise use of words.", "c": "簡短；簡潔", "s": "Abraham Lincoln's Gettysburg Address is admired not only for its moving ideas but also for its brevity; in just 272 words and about two minutes, he redefined the purpose of the Civil War.", "t": "林肯的蓋茲堡演說之所以受人推崇，不僅在於其動人的理念，也在於其簡潔；他只用了短短272個字、大約兩分鐘，就重新定義了南北戰爭的目的。", "as": "The professor praised the essay's brevity, noting that the student had avoided verbose explanations and irrelevant digressions while still presenting a lucid, well-supported argument about climate policy.", "at": "教授稱讚這篇文章簡潔扼要，指出這位學生避免了冗長的解釋和無關的離題，同時仍就氣候政策提出了清晰且論據充分的論點。"}, {"w": "perquisite", "p": "n.", "d": "A benefit or privilege that comes with a job.", "c": "（職務上的）額外津貼；特權", "s": "Besides a generous salary, the new position offered several attractive benefits, but the most appealing perquisite was free housing in an apartment just two blocks from the office, which saved her hours of commuting every week.", "t": "除了優渥的薪水之外，這份新工作還提供了多項誘人的福利，但最吸引人的額外待遇是一間離辦公室只有兩個街區的免費公寓，每週為她省下好幾個小時的通勤時間。", "as": "Critics argued that the chief executive's perquisites, including a private jet, a lavish expense account, and lucrative stock options, were egregious at a time when the company was laying off workers.", "at": "批評者認為，在公司裁員之際，執行長所享有的種種特權，包括私人噴射機、奢華的交際費帳戶以及豐厚的股票選擇權，實在太過離譜。"}, {"w": "indigent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Extremely poor; lacking money and basic necessities.", "c": "貧窮的；貧困的", "s": "Under the Sixth Amendment, courts must provide a lawyer at public expense to any indigent criminal defendant who cannot afford one, ensuring that even the poorest citizens receive a fair trial.", "t": "根據美國憲法第六修正案，法院必須以公費為任何請不起律師的貧困刑事被告指派律師，以確保即使是最窮困的公民也能獲得公平審判。", "as": "The philanthropic foundation provided meals and shelter to indigent families throughout the long winter, and its founder's munificence became a paragon of generosity for the entire city.", "at": "這個慈善基金會在漫長的冬季為貧困家庭提供餐食和住所，而創辦人的慷慨大方也成為全市樂善好施的典範。"}, {"w": "clairvoyant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Able to perceive future events beyond normal senses.", "c": "有預知能力的；有超人洞察力的", "s": "The investor seemed almost clairvoyant, selling all her technology stocks just weeks before the market crashed, though she insisted her decision was based on careful analysis rather than any mysterious ability to predict the future.", "t": "這位投資人似乎幾乎能未卜先知，就在股市崩盤前幾週賣光了所有科技股，但她堅稱這個決定是基於審慎的分析，而不是什麼預知未來的神秘能力。", "as": "No one needed to be clairvoyant to predict the championship result; despite his assistants' adamant warnings, the coach's obstinate refusal to change his outdated strategy made defeat almost inevitable.", "at": "不需要未卜先知也能預料冠軍賽的結果；儘管助理教練們堅決提出警告，教練仍固執地拒絕改變過時的戰術，使得落敗幾乎無可避免。"}]}, {"unit": 8, "level": 2, "cards": [{"w": "adroit", "p": "adj.", "d": "Skillful and clever, especially in handling situations.", "c": "熟練的；機敏靈巧的", "s": "An adroit negotiator, the ambassador managed to calm both angry delegations, find common ground on the trade dispute, and persuade each side that it had won the more important concessions.", "t": "這位大使是一位手腕高明的談判者，他設法安撫了雙方憤怒的代表團，在貿易爭端中找到共識，並說服雙方都相信自己贏得了更重要的讓步。", "as": "The adroit lawyer exposed the witness's testimony as fallacious, pointing out inconsistencies so subtle that only an astute observer would have noticed them during the trial.", "at": "這位機敏的律師揭穿了證人證詞中的謬誤，指出其中極為細微的矛盾之處，只有眼光敏銳的旁觀者才可能在審判過程中察覺。"}, {"w": "platitude", "p": "n.", "d": "A dull, overused remark presented as if meaningful.", "c": "陳腔濫調；老生常談", "s": "The graduation speaker disappointed many students by offering nothing but the familiar platitude that they should \"follow their dreams,\" without giving any practical advice about careers, money, or the challenges ahead.", "t": "這位畢業典禮演講者讓許多學生失望，因為他只說了「追隨你的夢想」這類老掉牙的陳腔濫調，卻沒有提供任何關於職涯、金錢或未來挑戰的實用建議。", "as": "Instead of addressing the city's housing crisis, the candidate offered banal platitudes about hope and unity, a vacuous performance that left even his loyal supporters unimpressed.", "at": "這位候選人沒有正面回應城市的住房危機，反而發表了關於希望與團結的平庸陳腔濫調，這種空洞的表現讓就連他的忠實支持者都不以為然。"}, {"w": "fastidious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Very attentive to detail; extremely hard to please.", "c": "一絲不苟的；挑剔的", "s": "The fastidious chef inspected every plate before it left the kitchen, wiping away stray drops of sauce and sending back any dish in which the vegetables were not arranged perfectly.", "t": "這位一絲不苟的主廚會在每一盤菜離開廚房前親自檢查，擦掉多餘的醬汁滴痕，只要蔬菜擺放得不夠完美，就會把整道菜退回重做。", "as": "A fastidious editor, she scrutinized every footnote, eliminating verbose phrases and correcting even the most negligible errors before the prestigious scholarly journal finally went to press.", "at": "身為一位一絲不苟的編輯，她仔細審視每一條註腳，在這份頗具聲望的學術期刊終於付印前，刪去冗長的詞句，連最微不足道的錯誤也一一更正。"}, {"w": "vendetta", "p": "n.", "d": "A long, bitter feud involving repeated acts of revenge.", "c": "世仇；長期的報復行動", "s": "The famous vendetta between the Hatfield and McCoy families began with a dispute over a stolen pig and lasted for decades, resulting in a series of revenge killings along the Kentucky–West Virginia border.", "t": "哈特菲爾德與麥考伊兩大家族之間著名的世仇，起因於一頭被偷的豬所引發的爭執，並持續了數十年，在肯塔基州與西維吉尼亞州的邊界上釀成一連串的報復性殺戮。", "as": "Critics charged that the investigation was less a pursuit of justice than a personal vendetta, driven by the prosecutor's long-standing animosity toward the governor and his vindictive temperament.", "at": "批評者指控，這項調查與其說是在追求正義，不如說是一場私人報復，背後的動機是檢察官長期以來對州長的敵意，以及他睚眥必報的性格。"}, {"w": "lucid", "p": "adj.", "d": "Clear and easy to understand; mentally clear.", "c": "清晰易懂的；神智清楚的", "s": "Students appreciated the physics textbook because its explanations were so lucid; even complicated topics like quantum mechanics were presented in simple language, supported by helpful diagrams and familiar everyday examples.", "t": "學生們很喜歡這本物理課本，因為它的解說非常清晰易懂；即使是量子力學這樣複雜的主題，也以簡單的語言呈現，並輔以實用的圖表和日常生活中的例子。", "as": "Unlike the abstruse lectures of his colleagues, Professor Lin's lucid explanations helped even complete neophytes grasp the basic principles of economics within just a few weeks.", "at": "不同於其他同事艱深難懂的講課，林教授清晰的解說讓即使是完全的初學者也能在短短幾週內掌握經濟學的基本原理。"}, {"w": "salient", "p": "adj.", "d": "Most noticeable or important; standing out.", "c": "顯著的；最重要的", "s": "In her summary of the novel, the student focused only on the most salient points of the plot, leaving out minor characters and side stories so that the main conflict would be clear to readers.", "t": "這位學生在小說摘要中只聚焦於情節中最重要的幾個要點，省略了次要角色和支線故事，好讓讀者能清楚掌握主要衝突。", "as": "The salient feature of the report was its candor; rather than offering ambiguous reassurances, the auditors stated plainly that the company's finances were precarious and its current strategy no longer tenable.", "at": "這份報告最顯著的特點是它的坦率；稽核人員沒有給出模稜兩可的保證，而是直截了當地指出公司財務岌岌可危，目前的策略也已站不住腳。"}, {"w": "categorical", "p": "adj.", "d": "Absolute and unconditional; without any exceptions.", "c": "斷然的；絕對的", "s": "When reporters asked whether he planned to run for president, the senator issued a categorical denial, stating clearly that he would not seek the office under any circumstances, now or in the future.", "t": "當記者問到他是否打算競選總統時，這位參議員斷然否認，清楚表示無論在任何情況下，現在或將來，他都不會角逐這個職位。", "as": "The scientist made a categorical statement that the vaccine was safe, citing copious data from clinical trials that corroborated her conclusion beyond any reasonable doubt.", "at": "這位科學家斷然表示該疫苗是安全的，並引用了臨床試驗的大量數據，這些數據毫無疑義地證實了她的結論。"}, {"w": "inscrutable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Impossible to understand, interpret, or read.", "c": "不可理解的；高深莫測的", "s": "Throughout the poker tournament, the champion kept an inscrutable expression on her face throughout every round, so her opponents could never tell whether she was holding a winning hand or simply bluffing.", "t": "在整場撲克錦標賽中，這位冠軍每一局臉上都始終保持著高深莫測的表情，讓對手完全看不出她手上究竟是一副好牌，還是只是在虛張聲勢。", "as": "The ancient script remained inscrutable for centuries, an enigma that baffled even erudite scholars until the discovery of the Rosetta Stone finally made its meaning discernible.", "at": "這種古代文字數百年來始終難以解讀，是一個連博學多聞的學者都困惑不已的謎團，直到羅塞塔石碑的發現，其意義才終於得以辨識。"}, {"w": "construe", "p": "v.", "d": "To interpret or understand the meaning of something.", "c": "解釋；理解", "s": "Because the contract's wording was vague, the two companies tended to construe the same clause in completely different ways, with each side claiming that the agreement supported its own position.", "t": "由於合約措辭含糊，兩家公司對同一條款往往有完全不同的解讀，雙方都聲稱這份協議支持自己的立場。", "as": "The teacher worried that her terse reply might be construed as a rebuff, so she sent the student a second, warmer message praising his ingenious, if unconventional, idea.", "at": "老師擔心自己簡短的回覆可能被解讀為冷淡的拒絕，於是又寄給那位學生第二封較溫暖的訊息，稱讚他那雖不按常理卻很巧妙的點子。"}, {"w": "allude", "p": "v.", "d": "To refer to something indirectly or by suggestion.", "c": "暗指；間接提到", "s": "Without ever mentioning the scandal directly, the comedian managed to allude to it several times during his ninety-minute performance, and the audience laughed knowingly at each subtle, carefully crafted reference.", "t": "這位喜劇演員從未直接提到那樁醜聞，卻在長達九十分鐘的表演中好幾次巧妙地暗指此事，觀眾每聽到一個精心設計的隱晦影射，都心領神會地笑了出來。", "as": "In his poems, the reclusive writer often alluded to clandestine love affairs and tacit betrayals, leaving critics to speculate about the real events behind his cryptic verses.", "at": "這位隱居的作家常在詩中暗指祕密戀情與心照不宣的背叛，留給評論家去揣測他那些隱晦詩句背後的真實事件。"}, {"w": "provident", "p": "adj.", "d": "Wisely preparing for future needs; thrifty.", "c": "有遠見的；未雨綢繆的", "s": "Thanks to a provident decision to save part of every harvest, the farming village had enough grain to survive the three-year drought, while neighboring communities that had sold all their crops faced famine.", "t": "由於做出了把每次收成留下一部分的遠見決定，這個農村儲存了足夠的穀物度過三年的乾旱，而那些把作物全部賣光的鄰近村落則面臨饑荒。", "as": "Unlike her spendthrift brother, Grace was provident and frugal, investing a portion of every paycheck so that she would never depend on anyone's charity in old age.", "at": "不同於她揮霍無度的哥哥，葛瑞絲有遠見又節儉，每次領薪水都會拿出一部分去投資，這樣到了晚年就永遠不必仰賴別人的施捨。"}, {"w": "impute", "p": "v.", "d": "To attribute something, usually blame, to someone.", "c": "歸咎於；把……歸因於", "s": "Historians are careful not to impute modern values to people of the distant past, recognizing that ancient societies often judged right and wrong according to very different religious beliefs and social circumstances.", "t": "歷史學家謹慎地避免把現代的價值觀強加歸諸於遙遠過去的人們，因為他們明白，古代社會往往是依據截然不同的宗教信仰和社會處境來判斷是非對錯。", "as": "The tabloid imputed sinister motives to the senator's philanthropic donations, but the allegations proved spurious when an independent audit found no evidence of any wrongdoing whatsoever.", "at": "這份小報把參議員的慈善捐款歸咎於不可告人的動機，但當獨立稽核未發現任何不當行為的絲毫證據時，這些指控便被證實是捏造的。"}, {"w": "astute", "p": "adj.", "d": "Clever at understanding situations and turning them to advantage.", "c": "精明的；敏銳的", "s": "An astute investor, Warren Buffett has built his fortune by carefully studying companies, recognizing their long-term value, and buying shares when other people are too frightened or too impatient to act.", "t": "身為一位精明的投資人，華倫．巴菲特藉由仔細研究公司、看出其長期價值，並在別人過於恐懼或缺乏耐心而不敢行動時買進股票，因而累積了大量財富。", "as": "An astute reader will notice that the narrator's account is riddled with incongruous details, which suggests that his ostensible honesty conceals a more calculating motive.", "at": "精明的讀者會注意到，敘事者的陳述中充斥著前後矛盾的細節，這暗示他表面上的誠實背後隱藏著更工於心計的動機。"}, {"w": "neophyte", "p": "n.", "d": "A beginner or newcomer to a subject or activity.", "c": "新手；初學者", "s": "As a neophyte in the laboratory, Kevin was not allowed to handle dangerous chemicals until he had completed three weeks of safety training and carefully observed experienced researchers at work.", "t": "身為實驗室的新手，凱文在完成三週的安全訓練並仔細觀察資深研究人員工作之前，不得處理危險化學物品。", "as": "Though only a neophyte in politics, the young mayor proved remarkably adroit, winning over cantankerous council members who had opposed every reform proposed by her predecessors.", "at": "雖然只是政壇新手，這位年輕的市長卻展現出驚人的高明手腕，贏得了那些脾氣暴躁、反對前任市長所有改革提案的議員支持。"}, {"w": "enigma", "p": "n.", "d": "A person or thing that is mysterious or puzzling.", "c": "謎；令人費解的人或事", "s": "For more than a century, the purpose of the giant stone statues on Easter Island remained an enigma to archaeologists, who struggled to explain how and why the islanders had created them.", "t": "一百多年來，復活節島上巨型石像的用途一直是考古學家眼中的謎，他們難以解釋島民是如何以及為何建造這些石像的。", "as": "The reclusive author remained an enigma to his readers; his aloof manner and inscrutable smile in rare interviews only deepened the mystery surrounding his private life.", "at": "這位深居簡出的作家對讀者來說始終是個謎；他在罕見的訪談中冷漠疏離的態度和高深莫測的微笑，只讓他私生活的神祕色彩更加濃厚。"}, {"w": "credence", "p": "n.", "d": "Belief in or acceptance of something as true.", "c": "相信；可信度", "s": "New fossil evidence discovered in China has given greater credence to the theory that birds evolved from small feathered dinosaurs, persuading many respected scientists who had once seriously doubted the idea.", "t": "在中國發現的新化石證據，讓「鳥類是由小型有羽毛恐龍演化而來」的理論更具可信度，說服了許多曾經對此深表懷疑的知名科學家。", "as": "Few historians give credence to the apocryphal story that the general wept after the battle, since no contemporary source written by eyewitnesses corroborates such a poignant scene.", "at": "很少有歷史學家相信那則將軍在戰後落淚的杜撰故事，因為沒有任何由目擊者撰寫的同時代史料能證實如此令人心酸的場景。"}, {"w": "venerate", "p": "v.", "d": "To regard with great respect and deep reverence.", "c": "尊敬；崇敬", "s": "In many East Asian cultures, families venerate their ancestors by keeping memorial tablets at home, offering food and incense during important festivals, and visiting and cleaning family graves every spring.", "t": "在許多東亞文化中，家庭會在家中供奉祖先牌位、在重要節日時奉上供品和焚香，並在每年春天前往祭掃祖墳，藉此表達對祖先的崇敬。", "as": "Though villagers once venerated the old philosopher as a paragon of wisdom, a younger generation dismissed his teachings as archaic and his sayings as tired platitudes.", "at": "雖然村民曾把這位老哲學家奉為智慧的典範而崇敬不已，但年輕一代卻認為他的教誨過時，他的格言也只是陳腔濫調。"}, {"w": "garrulous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Excessively talkative, especially about trivial matters.", "c": "喋喋不休的；多話的", "s": "The garrulous tour guide talked nonstop for the entire four-hour bus ride, sharing endless stories about his childhood, his pets, and his favorite restaurants instead of explaining the history of the places we passed.", "t": "那位喋喋不休的導遊在整整四小時的車程中說個不停，不斷講述他的童年、寵物和最愛的餐廳，卻沒有介紹我們沿途經過的地方有什麼歷史。", "as": "At the dinner party, the garrulous professor's verbose anecdotes contrasted sharply with the laconic replies of his guest, who clearly wished the evening would end.", "at": "在晚宴上，那位多話教授冗長的軼事，和他那位客人簡短的回應形成強烈對比，客人顯然巴不得晚宴早點結束。"}, {"w": "trenchant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Sharp, forceful, and clear in expression or criticism.", "c": "一針見血的；尖銳有力的", "s": "George Orwell's trenchant essays on politics and language remain influential today because they cut straight to the heart of each issue, exposing dishonest propaganda with sharp, forceful, and remarkably clear arguments.", "t": "喬治．歐威爾關於政治與語言的文章至今仍深具影響力，因為它們直指每個議題的核心，以犀利有力且極為清晰的論證揭露不誠實的宣傳。", "as": "The critic's trenchant review exposed the novel's hackneyed plot and banal dialogue, though some readers felt her acerbic tone was unnecessarily harsh toward a first-time author.", "at": "這位評論家一針見血的書評揭露了這部小說陳腐的情節和平庸的對白，但有些讀者認為，她尖酸刻薄的語氣對一位初次出書的作者而言過於嚴苛。"}, {"w": "autonomous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Independent and self-governing; acting without outside control.", "c": "自治的；自主的", "s": "After decades of struggle, the region finally became autonomous, gaining the right to elect its own parliament, collect its own taxes, and make its own laws without interference from the central government.", "t": "經過數十年的抗爭，這個地區終於獲得自治，有權選出自己的議會、徵收自己的稅款，並在不受中央政府干預的情況下制定自己的法律。", "as": "Engineers are designing autonomous vehicles that can navigate traffic without human drivers, but skeptics argue that the technology is too nascent and its safety record too tenuous for public roads.", "at": "工程師正在設計能在沒有人類駕駛的情況下穿梭車陣的自動駕駛車，但懷疑者認為這項技術仍處於萌芽階段，安全紀錄也過於薄弱，還不適合上公共道路。"}]}, {"unit": 9, "level": 2, "cards": [{"w": "panacea", "p": "n.", "d": "A remedy believed to cure all problems or diseases.", "c": "萬靈丹；萬能解方", "s": "Although many politicians promote new technology as a panacea for the problems facing public schools, education researchers warn that tablets and online programs cannot replace well-trained teachers, smaller classes, and strong family support.", "t": "雖然許多政治人物把新科技宣傳為解決公立學校問題的萬靈丹，但教育研究人員警告，平板電腦和線上課程無法取代訓練有素的教師、小班教學以及健全的家庭支持。", "as": "The charlatan sold bottles of colored water as a panacea for every ailment, preying on gullible villagers who were too indigent to afford a real doctor.", "at": "那個江湖騙子把一瓶瓶有顏色的水當作能治百病的萬靈丹來販售，專門欺騙那些窮得請不起真正醫生、又容易上當的村民。"}, {"w": "ephemeral", "p": "adj.", "d": "Lasting for only a very short time.", "c": "短暫的；瞬息即逝的", "s": "Japanese poets have long celebrated cherry blossoms precisely because they are so ephemeral; the delicate flowers bloom for only a week or two before the wind scatters their petals across the ground.", "t": "日本詩人長久以來歌頌櫻花，正是因為它如此短暫；嬌嫩的花朵只綻放一兩週，隨後風便將花瓣吹散一地。", "as": "Fame on social media is often ephemeral; a video that attracts myriad viewers one week may be forgotten the next, replaced by an equally transient trend.", "at": "社群媒體上的名氣往往轉瞬即逝；一支影片可能這週吸引了無數觀眾，下週就被遺忘，取而代之的是另一個同樣短暫的潮流。"}, {"w": "onerous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Involving heavy effort, burden, or difficulty.", "c": "繁重的；費力的", "s": "Small business owners complained that the new regulations were far too onerous, requiring them to fill out dozens of complicated forms each month and hire expensive accountants simply to stay in compliance with the law.", "t": "小企業主抱怨新法規實在太過繁重，他們每個月都得填寫數十份複雜的表格，還得聘請昂貴的會計師，才能勉強符合法律規定。", "as": "Caring for her ailing father was an onerous responsibility, yet she never complained, accepting the arduous daily routine with a quiet, resolute devotion that her siblings admired.", "at": "照顧生病的父親是一項沉重的責任，但她從不抱怨，以一種沉靜而堅定的奉獻接受這份艱辛的日常，令她的兄弟姊妹敬佩不已。"}, {"w": "laity", "p": "n.", "d": "Ordinary people, as distinguished from clergy or experts.", "c": "（相對於神職人員的）平信徒；外行人", "s": "During the Reformation, Martin Luther translated the Bible into German so that the laity, not just priests and scholars who could read Latin, would be able to study the scriptures for themselves.", "t": "在宗教改革期間，馬丁．路德把《聖經》翻譯成德文，讓一般平信徒，而不只是懂拉丁文的神職人員和學者，都能自行研讀經文。", "as": "Medical jargon often confuses the laity, so the hospital hired writers to produce lucid pamphlets that explain complex treatments and their risks without using abstruse technical terms.", "at": "醫學術語常讓一般大眾困惑，因此醫院聘請寫手製作清晰易懂的小冊子，在不使用艱深專業術語的情況下解釋複雜的療法及其風險。"}, {"w": "pungent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having a sharp, strong smell or taste.", "c": "刺鼻的；辛辣的", "s": "Visitors to Taipei's night markets are often surprised by the pungent smell of stinky tofu, which can be detected from half a block away, although many people who try the dish discover that it tastes much milder than it smells.", "t": "來到台北夜市的遊客常對臭豆腐的刺鼻氣味感到驚訝，遠在半個街區外就聞得到，不過許多嘗試過的人發現，它吃起來比聞起來溫和得多。", "as": "The columnist was known for her pungent wit and trenchant observations, which delighted readers but infuriated the pompous politicians whose platitudes she ridiculed every week.", "at": "這位專欄作家以辛辣的機智和一針見血的觀察聞名，讀者讀得大呼過癮，卻激怒了那些自命不凡的政治人物，因為她每週都在嘲諷他們的陳腔濫調。"}, {"w": "prosaic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Dull, ordinary, and lacking imagination or excitement.", "c": "平淡無奇的；乏味的", "s": "Although the film promised a thrilling adventure, its plot turned out to be surprisingly prosaic, following a predictable story about an office worker who simply commutes, eats lunch, and goes home each day.", "t": "雖然這部電影標榜著一場驚險刺激的冒險，但劇情卻出奇地平淡乏味，只是一個可想而知的故事，講述一名上班族每天通勤、吃午餐、然後回家。", "as": "Critics found the poet's later work disappointingly prosaic; the vibrant imagery of her early years had given way to mundane descriptions of suburban life and monotonous rhythms.", "at": "評論家認為這位詩人後期的作品平淡得令人失望；她早年鮮明生動的意象，已被對郊區生活的平凡描寫和單調的節奏所取代。"}, {"w": "charlatan", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who falsely claims special knowledge or skill.", "c": "騙子；冒充內行的人", "s": "The self-proclaimed doctor turned out to be a charlatan with no medical training at all; he had simply bought a white coat, printed fake diplomas, and charged desperate patients for useless herbal treatments.", "t": "這位自稱醫師的人原來是個騙子，根本沒受過任何醫學訓練；他只是買了一件白袍、印了假文憑，然後向走投無路的病人收取無效草藥療法的費用。", "as": "The charlatan's sophistry convinced many gullible investors to hand over their life savings, but an astute journalist eventually exposed his scheme as nothing more than an elaborate fraud.", "at": "那個騙子的詭辯說服了許多容易上當的投資人交出畢生積蓄，但一位精明的記者最終揭穿了他的計謀，那不過是一場精心設計的騙局。"}, {"w": "perfunctory", "p": "adj.", "d": "Done quickly and without real care or interest.", "c": "敷衍的；草率的", "s": "The security guard gave our bags only a perfunctory glance before waving us through the gate, clearly more interested in finishing his shift than in actually checking for anything dangerous.", "t": "保全只是敷衍地瞄了一眼我們的包包，就揮手讓我們通過大門，顯然他比較在意趕快下班，而不是真的檢查有沒有危險物品。", "as": "The manager's perfunctory apology did little to mollify the angry customers, who regarded his cursory explanation as further proof of the company's indifference to their complaints.", "at": "經理敷衍了事的道歉根本無法平息顧客的怒氣，他們認為他草率的解釋更證明了公司對他們的抱怨漠不關心。"}, {"w": "morass", "p": "n.", "d": "A complicated situation that is hard to escape.", "c": "困境；泥淖", "s": "The new mayor quickly found herself trapped in a morass of conflicting regulations, unfinished lawsuits, and unpaid debts left by the previous administration, which made even simple reforms extremely difficult to carry out.", "t": "新任市長很快就發現自己深陷前任市府留下的泥淖之中：互相矛盾的法規、懸而未決的訴訟以及未償還的債務，使得即使是簡單的改革也極難推行。", "as": "The inquiry soon sank into a morass of contradictory testimony, as each witness offered an ambiguous account that seemed designed to obfuscate rather than clarify what had happened.", "at": "這項調查很快就陷入了證詞相互矛盾的泥淖，因為每位證人的說法都模稜兩可，似乎有意混淆視聽，而不是釐清事情的真相。"}, {"w": "sophistry", "p": "n.", "d": "Clever but misleading and deceptive reasoning.", "c": "詭辯；似是而非的推論", "s": "The debate judges were not impressed by his argument that cheating on homework helps students learn teamwork; they recognized it as sophistry, a clever-sounding but deeply misleading way to justify dishonest behavior.", "t": "辯論評審對他「作業作弊能幫助學生學習團隊合作」的論點不以為然；他們看出這是一種詭辯，聽起來很巧妙，實則是為不誠實行為開脫的嚴重誤導說法。", "as": "Socrates criticized the Sophists for teaching sophistry to wealthy young men, arguing that their specious and often fallacious arguments valued winning debates over discovering the truth.", "at": "蘇格拉底批評詭辯學派向富家子弟傳授詭辯術，認為他們那些似是而非、往往謬誤百出的論證只重視贏得辯論，而非探求真理。"}, {"w": "prolific", "p": "adj.", "d": "Producing many works, results, or offspring.", "c": "多產的；豐富的", "s": "Agatha Christie was an extraordinarily prolific author, writing sixty-six detective novels and fourteen short-story collections during her career, which made her one of the best-selling writers in the history of literature.", "t": "阿嘉莎．克莉絲蒂是一位極為多產的作家，她在寫作生涯中創作了六十六部偵探小說和十四本短篇小說集，成為文學史上最暢銷的作家之一。", "as": "A prolific inventor, Thomas Edison held more than a thousand patents, though some critics argue that his fame obscures the laudable contributions of his many assiduous assistants.", "at": "湯瑪斯．愛迪生是一位多產的發明家，擁有一千多項專利，但有些批評者認為，他的名氣掩蓋了眾多勤奮助手值得稱讚的貢獻。"}, {"w": "mundane", "p": "adj.", "d": "Ordinary, everyday, and lacking interest or excitement.", "c": "平凡的；世俗的", "s": "Astronauts on the International Space Station spend much of their time on mundane tasks such as cleaning air filters, exercising, and repairing equipment, rather than on the exciting spacewalks that appear in the news.", "t": "國際太空站上的太空人大部分時間都在做平凡的例行工作，例如清潔空氣濾網、運動和維修設備，而不是新聞上出現的那些刺激的太空漫步。", "as": "The novelist transforms the mundane details of daily life into poignant scenes, revealing how even prosaic moments like washing dishes can carry profound emotional weight.", "at": "這位小說家把日常生活中平凡的細節轉化為令人動容的場景，揭示出即使是洗碗這種平淡無奇的時刻，也能承載深刻的情感分量。"}, {"w": "myriad", "p": "adj.", "d": "Countless; extremely great in number.", "c": "無數的；極多的", "s": "Coral reefs support myriad forms of marine life, from tiny shrimp and colorful fish to sea turtles and sharks, making them some of the most diverse ecosystems on the entire planet.", "t": "珊瑚礁孕育了無數種海洋生物，從微小的蝦子、色彩繽紛的魚類到海龜和鯊魚，使其成為全球生物多樣性最豐富的生態系之一。", "as": "The young scientist faced myriad obstacles, from meager funding to skeptical colleagues, yet her resolute dedication eventually produced an unprecedented breakthrough in childhood cancer research.", "at": "這位年輕科學家面臨無數障礙，從微薄的經費到抱持懷疑的同事都有，但她堅定不移的投入，最終在兒童癌症研究上取得了前所未有的突破。"}, {"w": "dissident", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who openly opposes an official policy or government.", "c": "異議分子；持不同政見者", "s": "Because he had openly criticized the government in newspaper articles and organized peaceful protests, the writer was labeled a dissident by the authorities and forced to live in exile for more than twenty years.", "t": "由於這位作家曾在報紙文章中公開批評政府並組織和平抗議，他被當局冠上異議分子的標籤，被迫流亡海外二十多年。", "as": "The regime tried to subjugate every dissident through censorship and surveillance, but clandestine networks of students and teachers continued to smuggle their banned writings across the border.", "at": "該政權試圖透過審查與監控來壓制每一位異議分子，但由學生和教師組成的祕密網絡仍持續將他們的禁書偷運出境。"}, {"w": "laudable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Deserving praise and commendation.", "c": "值得稱讚的；可嘉的", "s": "The students' effort to collect ten thousand plastic bottles for recycling was certainly laudable, and the principal publicly praised them at the school assembly for setting such a good example for the community.", "t": "學生們收集一萬個塑膠瓶回收的努力確實值得稱許，校長也在全校集會上公開表揚他們為社區樹立了良好的榜樣。", "as": "Although the senator's goals were laudable, critics argued that his proposals were nebulous and that funding them would impose an onerous burden on ordinary taxpayers.", "at": "雖然這位參議員的目標值得稱讚，但批評者認為他的提案含糊不清，而且為這些提案籌措經費將對一般納稅人造成沉重的負擔。"}, {"w": "inimitable", "p": "adj.", "d": "So unique or excellent that it cannot be copied.", "c": "無法模仿的；獨一無二的", "s": "Many artists have tried to copy Vincent van Gogh's swirling brushstrokes and vivid colors, but his inimitable style remains instantly recognizable and has never been successfully reproduced by anyone else.", "t": "許多藝術家都嘗試模仿梵谷旋轉般的筆觸和鮮豔的色彩，但他那無法模仿的風格至今仍一眼就能認出，從未有人能成功複製。", "as": "With her inimitable blend of candor and wry humor, the comedian could turn even the most mundane story about grocery shopping into a hilarious performance.", "at": "憑著她那獨一無二、融合坦率與冷面幽默的風格，這位喜劇演員即使是講述最平凡的買菜故事，也能化為一場令人捧腹的表演。"}, {"w": "jaded", "p": "adj.", "d": "Tired, bored, or lacking enthusiasm from overexposure.", "c": "厭倦的；麻木的", "s": "After working as a food critic for thirty years and eating at thousands of restaurants, he had become so jaded that even the most creative dishes no longer excited him or surprised his palate.", "t": "在擔任美食評論家三十年、吃過數千家餐廳之後，他已經變得麻木厭倦，即使是最有創意的菜餚也無法再讓他興奮，或讓他的味蕾感到驚喜。", "as": "Jaded by years of empty and broken campaign promises, many voters dismissed the candidate's fervent speeches as mere platitudes and simply stayed home on election day.", "at": "多年來聽膩了空洞又不兌現的競選承諾，許多選民把這位候選人熱情激昂的演說斥為陳腔濫調，選舉當天就乾脆待在家裡。"}, {"w": "myopic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Lacking foresight; narrow-minded in planning or thinking.", "c": "短視的；目光短淺的", "s": "Environmental groups criticized the government's myopic decision to cut down the ancient forest for quick profits, arguing that it ignored the long-term damage to wildlife, water supplies, and the local climate.", "t": "環保團體批評政府為了快速獲利而砍伐古老森林的短視決定，認為這忽略了對野生動物、水源和當地氣候的長期損害。", "as": "The company's myopic focus on quarterly profits proved deleterious, and analysts noted that a more provident strategy could easily have prevented its eventual and painful bankruptcy.", "at": "這家公司短視地只看重季度獲利，結果證明有害無益；分析師指出，若採取更有遠見的策略，原本可以輕易避免最終慘痛的破產。"}, {"w": "demonstrable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Clearly able to be proved or shown.", "c": "可證明的；明顯的", "s": "Before the new reading program can be adopted in every school, its supporters must provide demonstrable evidence of success, such as test scores showing that students actually read faster and understand more.", "t": "在這套新的閱讀課程能夠推行到每一所學校之前，支持者必須提出可證明其成效的證據，例如顯示學生確實讀得更快、理解得更多的測驗成績。", "as": "The lawyer insisted that the allegations were demonstrably false, citing documents that corroborated her client's alibi and refuted every single claim made by the prosecution during the trial.", "at": "律師堅稱這些指控顯然是錯誤的，並引用文件證實當事人的不在場證明，駁斥了檢方在審判中提出的每一項主張。"}, {"w": "callow", "p": "adj.", "d": "Young, inexperienced, and immature.", "c": "幼稚的；乳臭未乾的", "s": "Looking back at the diary she had written as a callow teenager, the famous novelist laughed at her naive opinions about love, politics, and success, which seemed so childish to her now.", "t": "回頭看自己還是個青澀少女時寫下的日記，這位知名小說家對當年關於愛情、政治和成功的天真見解笑了出來，如今在她看來那些想法實在太幼稚了。", "as": "The callow intern made a flippant remark during the board meeting, and his supervisor later admonished him to be more circumspect when speaking in front of senior executives.", "at": "那位乳臭未乾的實習生在董事會上說了一句輕率的話，事後主管告誡他，在高階主管面前發言要更加謹慎。"}]}, {"unit": 10, "level": 2, "cards": [{"w": "acquiesce", "p": "v.", "d": "To accept or agree to something reluctantly, without protest.", "c": "默許；勉強同意", "s": "After weeks of heated debate, the student council finally chose to acquiesce to the principal's new dress code, deciding that further protest would only delay the spring festival they had spent months planning.", "t": "經過數週激烈的辯論，學生會最終選擇默許校長新的服裝規定，認為繼續抗議只會延誤他們籌劃了好幾個月的春季園遊會。", "as": "Rather than remain adamant, the weary council chose to acquiesce in the end, reasoning that a tacit compromise would serve its students far better than a protracted and bitter standoff.", "at": "疲憊的委員會最終沒有繼續堅持己見，而是選擇默許，認為一個心照不宣的妥協遠比曠日持久又激烈的僵持更能造福學生。"}, {"w": "pontificate", "p": "v.", "d": "To express opinions in a pompous and dogmatic way.", "c": "自以為是地發表意見；高談闊論", "s": "Instead of answering the reporters' simple question about the budget shortfall, the senator began to pontificate at length about the moral decline of modern society, leaving the audience bored and the actual issue unaddressed.", "t": "參議員沒有回答記者關於預算短缺的簡單問題，反而開始長篇大論、自以為是地談論現代社會的道德淪喪，讓聽眾感到乏味，真正的問題也懸而未決。", "as": "The verbose professor tended to pontificate on every topic, yet his students found his lectures so nebulous that they rarely understood a single argument he made.", "at": "那位冗長囉嗦的教授往往對每個話題都自以為是地高談闊論，但學生們覺得他的講課內容含糊不清，幾乎無法理解他提出的任何論點。"}, {"w": "deleterious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Causing harm or damage, often in a subtle way.", "c": "有害的；有毒的", "s": "Researchers found that prolonged exposure to blue light from screens late at night can have a deleterious effect on sleep quality, disrupting the release of melatonin and leaving teenagers tired and unfocused during morning classes.", "t": "研究人員發現，深夜長時間接觸螢幕發出的藍光會對睡眠品質產生有害的影響，干擾褪黑激素的分泌，使青少年在早上的課堂中感到疲倦且無法專心。", "as": "Although the pesticide's short-term benefits seemed salient, ecologists soon gathered copious evidence of its deleterious impact on bee colonies, a finding that farmers could no longer ignore.", "at": "雖然這種農藥的短期效益看似顯著，生態學家很快就蒐集到大量證據，證明它對蜂群有害，這項發現讓農民再也無法忽視。"}, {"w": "ambivalent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having mixed or contradictory feelings about something.", "c": "矛盾的；猶豫不決的", "s": "Many residents felt ambivalent about the proposed stadium: they welcomed the jobs and tourism it promised, yet they worried that the construction would destroy a beloved park and increase traffic in their quiet neighborhood.", "t": "許多居民對擬建的體育場感到矛盾：他們歡迎它所承諾帶來的就業機會與觀光收益，卻又擔心工程會破壞一座深受喜愛的公園，並讓他們安靜的社區交通更加壅塞。", "as": "Torn between a lucrative offer abroad and her ailing parents at home, Mei remained ambivalent for weeks, and her vacillating replies increasingly frustrated the eager recruiter.", "at": "小梅在國外一份待遇優渥的工作機會與家中年邁多病的父母之間左右為難，好幾週都拿不定主意，她反覆不定的答覆讓那位急切的招聘人員越來越沮喪。"}, {"w": "pensive", "p": "adj.", "d": "Deeply, often sadly, thoughtful.", "c": "沉思的；憂思的", "s": "After reading the letter from his grandfather, written during the war and never sent, Daniel sat pensive by the window for nearly an hour, quietly considering how little he had known about his family's past.", "t": "讀完祖父在戰爭期間寫下卻從未寄出的信後，丹尼爾若有所思地在窗邊坐了將近一個小時，靜靜地思索自己對家族的過往竟然所知甚少。", "as": "The usually jovial coach grew pensive after the defeat, reflecting on whether his complacent training methods had left the team unprepared for such a formidable opponent.", "at": "平時總是開朗愉快的教練在落敗後變得沉思不語，反省是否是自己自滿的訓練方式，讓球隊對如此強大的對手毫無準備。"}, {"w": "impromptu", "p": "adj.", "d": "Done or said without planning or preparation.", "c": "即興的；臨時的", "s": "When the guest speaker's flight was canceled, the club president delivered an impromptu talk on her own research, and despite having no notes or slides, she held the audience's attention for the entire forty minutes.", "t": "當客座講者的班機取消時，社團社長即興發表了一場關於自己研究的演講，儘管沒有任何筆記或投影片，她在整整四十分鐘內都牢牢吸引住聽眾的注意力。", "as": "His impromptu toast at the wedding was surprisingly lucid, though his brevity disappointed guests who had expected the garrulous uncle to speak for at least ten minutes.", "at": "他在婚禮上的即興祝酒詞出奇地條理清晰，不過他的簡短讓賓客們有些失望，因為他們原本預期這位愛說話的叔叔至少會講上十分鐘。"}, {"w": "conjecture", "p": "n.", "d": "An opinion or guess formed without complete evidence.", "c": "推測；猜想", "s": "Because no written records from the settlement survive, any claim about why its inhabitants suddenly abandoned it remains pure conjecture, though historians have proposed drought, disease, and war as possible explanations.", "t": "由於該聚落沒有任何書面紀錄留存下來，任何關於居民為何突然棄之而去的說法都純屬推測，不過歷史學家已提出乾旱、疾病和戰爭等可能的解釋。", "as": "The journalist's allegation rested on mere conjecture rather than demonstrable fact, so the editor refused to publish it until another source could corroborate the story.", "at": "這名記者的指控僅僅建立在推測之上，而非可證實的事實，因此在另一個消息來源能證實此事之前，總編輯拒絕刊登。"}, {"w": "surreptitious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Done secretly, especially because it would not be approved.", "c": "偷偷摸摸的；秘密的", "s": "During the exam, the proctor noticed one student's surreptitious glances at a phone hidden beneath his desk, and although he tried to act casual, the device was confiscated before he could finish the test.", "t": "考試期間，監考人員注意到一名學生偷偷瞄向藏在桌子底下的手機，雖然他試圖裝作若無其事，手機仍在他寫完考卷之前被沒收了。", "as": "The dissident writers held surreptitious meetings in a basement every Thursday night, circulating clandestine pamphlets that the regime later tried to repudiate as foreign propaganda.", "at": "那些異議作家每週四晚上都在一處地下室秘密聚會，散發地下小冊子，而政權後來試圖將這些小冊子斥為外國的宣傳品而加以否認。"}, {"w": "exemplary", "p": "adj.", "d": "Serving as an excellent example; worthy of imitation.", "c": "模範的；可作楷模的", "s": "The volunteer firefighter received a city award for her exemplary conduct during the floods, having rescued twelve stranded residents while also organizing shelter and meals for families who had lost their homes.", "t": "這位義消因在水災期間的模範表現而獲得市政府頒獎，她不僅救出十二名受困居民，還為失去家園的家庭安排了住處和餐點。", "as": "The headmaster praised the student's exemplary essay for its lucid structure and laudable research, noting that it carefully avoided the verbose style so common among her peers.", "at": "校長稱讚這名學生的模範文章結構清晰、研究值得嘉許，並指出這篇文章刻意避免了同儕之間常見的冗長文風。"}, {"w": "impeccable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Without any flaws or errors; perfect.", "c": "無瑕疵的；完美無缺的", "s": "The translator's work was so impeccable that even the author, a notoriously demanding perfectionist, could not find a single error in the four-hundred-page manuscript after reviewing it line by line.", "t": "這位譯者的作品無懈可擊，就連以極度苛求、追求完美著稱的作者，在逐行審閱這份四百頁的手稿後，也找不出任何一個錯誤。", "as": "Her impeccable credentials lent credence to her testimony, and even the most astute members of the jury could find no fallacious reasoning anywhere in her analysis.", "at": "她無可挑剔的資歷讓她的證詞更具可信度，即使是陪審團中最精明的成員，也無法在她的分析中找到任何錯誤的推理。"}, {"w": "attest", "p": "v.", "d": "To show or prove clearly that something is true.", "c": "證明；證實", "s": "Dozens of letters from former students attest to the retiring teacher's lasting influence, describing in vivid detail how her patient encouragement inspired them to pursue careers in medicine, engineering, and public service.", "t": "數十封來自昔日學生的信件證明了這位即將退休的老師影響深遠，信中生動詳述她耐心的鼓勵如何激勵他們投身醫學、工程與公共服務等領域。", "as": "Several witnesses could attest that the defendant had been abroad that week, an alibi that made the prosecutor's attempt to incriminate him seem tenuous at best.", "at": "數名證人能證實被告那週人在國外，這項不在場證明使得檢察官試圖讓他入罪的做法顯得非常站不住腳。"}, {"w": "copious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Abundant in quantity; plentiful.", "c": "大量的；豐富的", "s": "Determined to ace her history final, Lin took copious notes during every lecture, filling three thick notebooks with dates, quotations, and diagrams that she later turned into color-coded study guides.", "t": "小琳下定決心要在歷史期末考拿高分，每堂課都做了大量筆記，寫滿了三本厚厚的筆記本，內容包括日期、引文和圖表，後來她再把這些整理成以顏色分類的讀書指南。", "as": "Despite copious data showing that the additive was deleterious to children, the manufacturer remained complacent, continuing production until public outrage finally forced it to rescind its claims.", "at": "儘管有大量數據顯示這種添加物對兒童有害，製造商仍然自滿而無動於衷，持續生產，直到民眾的憤怒終於迫使它撤回先前的聲明。"}, {"w": "fallacious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Based on a mistaken belief or faulty reasoning.", "c": "謬誤的；不合邏輯的", "s": "The essay's central argument proved fallacious, since it assumed that because two events happened at the same time, one must have caused the other, a classic error that careful scientists learn to avoid.", "t": "這篇文章的核心論點被證明是謬誤的，因為它假設兩件事同時發生，其中一件就必定是另一件的成因，這是嚴謹的科學家會學著避免的典型錯誤。", "as": "The charlatan's fallacious claims about his miracle panacea persuaded many desperate and gullible buyers, until scientists exposed the product as nothing more than flavored water.", "at": "那個江湖郎中對他所謂的萬靈丹提出了荒謬的說法，說服了許多走投無路又容易受騙的買家，直到科學家揭穿這種產品不過是加了調味的水而已。"}, {"w": "stoic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Enduring pain or hardship calmly, without complaining.", "c": "堅忍的；不動聲色的", "s": "Despite the painful injury to her ankle, the gymnast remained stoic throughout the medal ceremony, smiling for the cameras and thanking her coaches without revealing how much she was suffering.", "t": "儘管腳踝受了疼痛的傷，這位體操選手在頒獎典禮全程依然堅忍、不動聲色，對著鏡頭微笑並感謝教練們，絲毫沒有透露她承受了多少痛苦。", "as": "Even when his business became defunct and his savings dwindled to a pittance, the old baker remained stoic, refusing to vilify the competitors who had ruined him.", "at": "即使他的店已經倒閉，積蓄也縮減到少得可憐，這位老麵包師傅依然堅忍以對，拒絕詆毀那些讓他破產的競爭對手。"}, {"w": "recrimination", "p": "n.", "d": "An accusation made in response to someone else's accusation.", "c": "反控；互相指責", "s": "After the group project received a failing grade, the meeting quickly descended into bitter recrimination, with each member blaming the others for missed deadlines instead of discussing how to improve their final presentation.", "t": "小組專題拿到不及格的分數後，會議很快就淪為激烈的互相指責，每個成員都怪罪其他人錯過截止期限，而不是討論如何改善他們的期末報告。", "as": "The collapse of the merger led to months of recrimination between the two firms, and the animosity grew so intense that every attempt to reconcile them failed.", "at": "合併案破局後，兩家公司之間互相指責長達數月，敵意變得如此強烈，以致於每一次試圖讓雙方和解的努力都以失敗告終。"}, {"w": "affinity", "p": "n.", "d": "A natural liking for or attraction to something.", "c": "天生的喜好；親近感", "s": "From an early age, Kevin showed a remarkable affinity for languages, picking up Taiwanese from his grandmother and Japanese from cartoons long before he took any formal classes in school.", "t": "凱文從小就對語言展現出非凡的天生喜好，早在學校上任何正式課程之前，他就已經跟著奶奶學會台語，並從卡通裡學會了日語。", "as": "Her affinity for rural life made the bucolic village feel like home, and she soon developed a penchant for rising at dawn to tend the vegetable garden.", "at": "她對鄉村生活天生的喜愛讓這座田園村莊感覺就像家一樣，不久她便養成了黎明即起、照料菜園的喜好。"}, {"w": "volatile", "p": "adj.", "d": "Likely to change suddenly and unpredictably, often explosively.", "c": "易變的；不穩定的", "s": "Investors grew nervous as the stock market became increasingly volatile, rising sharply one day and plunging the next, so many decided to move their savings into safer options such as government bonds.", "t": "隨著股市變得越來越動盪不穩，某天急遽上漲，隔天又暴跌，投資人變得緊張不安，許多人決定把積蓄轉移到政府公債等較安全的選項。", "as": "The volatile situation at the border required a prudent diplomat, one who could mollify both angry sides before a single impetuous decision escalated into open war.", "at": "邊境一觸即發的局勢需要一位審慎的外交官，一位能在任何一個魯莽決定升級為全面戰爭之前，安撫雙方怒氣的人。"}, {"w": "squalid", "p": "adj.", "d": "Extremely dirty and unpleasant, especially from poverty or neglect.", "c": "骯髒的；污穢不堪的", "s": "The investigative report exposed the squalid conditions inside the factory dormitories, where dozens of workers shared a single broken toilet, slept on damp mattresses, and lived among rats and piles of uncollected garbage.", "t": "這篇調查報導揭露了工廠宿舍內骯髒惡劣的環境：數十名工人共用一間壞掉的廁所，睡在潮濕的床墊上，與老鼠和堆積如山、無人清運的垃圾生活在一起。", "as": "The reformer's poignant photographs of squalid tenements nettled the city's officials, who had for years ignored the indigent families crowded into those dark, airless rooms.", "at": "這位改革者所拍攝的骯髒廉價公寓照片令人心酸，激怒了市府官員，他們多年來一直忽視擠在那些陰暗、不通風房間裡的貧困家庭。"}, {"w": "expedite", "p": "v.", "d": "To make a process happen more quickly.", "c": "加速；促進", "s": "To expedite the rescue effort after the earthquake, the government suspended normal paperwork requirements, allowing volunteer doctors and engineers from abroad to enter the country and begin working within hours of arrival.", "t": "為了加速地震後的救援行動，政府暫停了一般的文書作業規定，讓來自國外的志工醫師和工程師得以入境，並在抵達後數小時內就開始工作。", "as": "To expedite the merger, the lawyers agreed to waive several onerous requirements, a pragmatic choice that saved both companies months of otherwise tedious and costly negotiation.", "at": "為了加快合併進程，律師們同意免除數項繁重的規定，這個務實的決定為兩家公司省下了好幾個月原本冗長又昂貴的協商。"}, {"w": "abject", "p": "adj.", "d": "Extremely miserable, hopeless, or humiliating.", "c": "悲慘的；極度可憐的", "s": "The documentary followed families living in abject poverty on the outskirts of the city, where children scavenged for food in garbage dumps and entire households survived on less than one dollar a day.", "t": "這部紀錄片記錄了住在城市邊緣、生活在赤貧之中的家庭，那裡的孩子在垃圾場裡翻找食物，整戶人家每天靠不到一美元過活。", "as": "After the abject failure of his campaign, the candidate issued a terse statement conceding defeat, without any of the bombastic rhetoric that had characterized his earlier speeches.", "at": "在競選慘敗之後，這位候選人發表了一份簡短的聲明承認落敗，完全不見他先前演講中那種浮誇的言詞。"}]}, {"unit": 11, "level": 3, "cards": [{"w": "voluble", "p": "adj.", "d": "Talking easily, rapidly, and at great length.", "c": "健談的；口若懸河的", "s": "Although she had been shy and quiet as a freshman, Amy became remarkably voluble by her senior year, chatting enthusiastically with visiting professors and easily filling every awkward silence at club meetings.", "t": "雖然艾美在高一時既害羞又安靜，到了高三她卻變得非常健談，能熱情地和來訪的教授聊天，也總能輕鬆地化解社團會議中每一次尷尬的沉默。", "as": "The voluble tour guide, never at a loss for words, offered a torrent of anecdotes, though her taciturn husband rarely contributed more than a terse nod.", "at": "那位健談的導遊從不詞窮，滔滔不絕地講述各種趣聞軼事，而她沉默寡言的丈夫則很少多說什麼，頂多簡短地點個頭。"}, {"w": "commiserate", "p": "v.", "d": "To express sympathy and share someone's sorrow or disappointment.", "c": "同情；表示慰問", "s": "After the results of the national exam were announced, classmates gathered in the cafeteria to commiserate with those who had missed their target scores, sharing stories of their own setbacks and offering words of encouragement.", "t": "全國考試成績公布後，同學們聚集在學生餐廳，安慰那些未達到目標分數的人，分享自己曾經歷的挫折，並給予鼓勵的話語。", "as": "Rather than gloat over his rival's defeat, the magnanimous champion chose to commiserate with him, a gesture of such probity that even cynical reporters praised it.", "at": "這位寬宏大量的冠軍沒有因對手落敗而幸災樂禍，反而選擇去安慰他，這種正直的舉動連憤世嫉俗的記者都讚譽有加。"}, {"w": "dilemma", "p": "n.", "d": "A difficult situation requiring a choice between two undesirable options.", "c": "兩難；困境", "s": "The young doctor faced a painful dilemma: she could follow hospital policy and send the uninsured patient away, or she could treat him anyway and risk losing the job she had worked years to obtain.", "t": "這位年輕醫師面臨痛苦的兩難：她可以遵照醫院規定讓那名沒有保險的病患離開，或者照樣替他治療，但要冒著失去她多年努力才得到的工作的風險。", "as": "Caught in a moral dilemma, the senator had to choose between loyalty to her party and her own probity, a quandary that left her ambivalent for weeks.", "at": "陷入道德兩難的這名參議員，必須在對黨的忠誠與自身的正直之間做出抉擇，這個困境讓她好幾週都猶豫不決。"}, {"w": "transitory", "p": "adj.", "d": "Lasting only a short time; not permanent.", "c": "短暫的；轉瞬即逝的", "s": "The economist warned that the sudden rise in tourism after the festival was likely transitory, since visitor numbers in similar cities had returned to normal within a few months once the media attention faded.", "t": "這位經濟學家警告，節慶過後觀光人潮的突然增加很可能只是短暫的，因為類似城市的遊客數量在媒體關注退去後幾個月內就恢復正常了。", "as": "Fame on social media is often transitory, and many young influencers soon learn, sometimes painfully, that their ephemeral popularity cannot be a panacea for deeper financial worries or a lasting career.", "at": "社群媒體上的名氣往往轉瞬即逝，許多年輕網紅很快就會明白（有時是痛苦地明白），他們短暫的人氣無法成為解決更深層財務問題的萬靈丹，也無法成就長久的事業。"}, {"w": "philanthropic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Generously giving money or help to improve others' welfare.", "c": "慈善的；博愛的", "s": "After selling her software company, the retired engineer devoted most of her fortune to philanthropic causes, funding scholarships for rural students, building libraries in remote villages, and donating millions to research on childhood diseases.", "t": "這位退休工程師賣掉她的軟體公司後，將大部分財富投入慈善事業，資助偏鄉學生的獎學金、在偏遠村落興建圖書館，並捐出數百萬元支持兒童疾病的研究。", "as": "The tycoon's philanthropic gifts displayed remarkable munificence, yet critics argued that his motives were mercenary, since every donation earned him generous tax deductions and favorable press coverage.", "at": "這位大亨的慈善捐款展現了非凡的慷慨，但批評者認為他的動機唯利是圖，因為每筆捐款都為他換來大筆的減稅優惠與正面的媒體報導。"}, {"w": "lethargy", "p": "n.", "d": "A lack of energy, enthusiasm, or alertness; sluggishness.", "c": "無精打采；倦怠", "s": "Doctors noted that the patient's constant lethargy was not simply laziness but a symptom of iron deficiency, and after several weeks of supplements, he regained the energy to exercise and focus at work.", "t": "醫師指出，這名病患持續的倦怠並非單純的懶惰，而是缺鐵的症狀，在服用補充劑數週後，他重新有了運動和專心工作的精力。", "as": "The summer heat induced a general lethargy among the students, and even the teacher's usual ebullience could not dispel their lassitude during the afternoon lessons.", "at": "夏日的炎熱讓學生們普遍無精打采，即使是老師一貫的熱情洋溢，也無法驅散他們在下午課堂上的倦怠。"}, {"w": "exonerate", "p": "v.", "d": "To officially clear someone of blame or guilt.", "c": "宣告無罪；免除責任", "s": "New DNA evidence helped exonerate the man who had spent fifteen years in prison for a robbery he did not commit, and the court issued a formal apology along with financial compensation.", "t": "新的DNA證據幫助這名男子洗清罪名，他曾因一樁自己沒有犯下的搶案入獄十五年，法院正式向他道歉並給予金錢賠償。", "as": "The lengthy investigation, which had at first seemed poised to incriminate the mayor, ultimately exonerated her, and the leaked documents proved the bribery allegation entirely spurious from the very beginning.", "at": "這項漫長的調查起初似乎即將讓市長入罪，最終卻還了她清白，外洩的文件也證明那項賄賂指控從一開始就完全是捏造的。"}, {"w": "pugnacious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Eager or quick to argue, quarrel, or fight.", "c": "好鬥的；愛爭吵的", "s": "The pugnacious talk-show host was famous for interrupting his guests, provoking angry arguments over minor details, and challenging anyone who disagreed with him to settle the matter in a live debate.", "t": "這位好鬥的脫口秀主持人以打斷來賓、為小細節挑起激烈爭吵，並挑戰任何與他意見相左的人在直播辯論中一決高下而聞名。", "as": "The pugnacious lawyer's acerbic remarks and truculent manner quickly alienated the jury, whose members found his combative courtroom tactics far less persuasive than his opponent's calm and carefully documented reasoning.", "at": "這位好鬥的律師尖酸刻薄的言論和咄咄逼人的態度很快就疏遠了陪審團，陪審員們覺得他在法庭上好戰的手法，遠不如對手冷靜且證據充分的推理有說服力。"}, {"w": "contrition", "p": "n.", "d": "Sincere regret or remorse for having done wrong.", "c": "懊悔；痛悔", "s": "In a handwritten letter to the school, the student expressed deep contrition for vandalizing the art room, offering to repaint the walls himself and to spend his weekends helping younger students with their projects.", "t": "這名學生在一封寫給學校的親筆信中，對自己破壞美術教室深表懊悔，並主動提出要親手重新粉刷牆壁，還要利用週末協助學弟妹完成作品。", "as": "The judge doubted the defendant's contrition, suspecting that his tearful apology was merely a pretext to mollify the court and secure a more lenient sentence.", "at": "法官懷疑被告的悔意，懷疑他聲淚俱下的道歉只是安撫法庭、爭取較輕刑罰的藉口。"}, {"w": "abrogate", "p": "v.", "d": "To formally abolish or cancel a law or agreement.", "c": "廢除；廢止", "s": "When the neighboring country repeatedly violated the fishing treaty over a period of several years, the government announced that it would abrogate the agreement entirely and begin patrolling its coastal waters with naval ships.", "t": "當鄰國在數年間一再違反漁業條約時，政府宣布將全面廢除該協定，並開始派遣海軍艦艇巡邏其沿海水域。", "as": "The new parliament voted to abrogate the oppressive law, a decision that rescinded decades of unjust restrictions and was hailed as an unprecedented victory for civil rights.", "at": "新國會投票廢除這項壓迫性的法律，此一決定撤銷了數十年來不公正的限制，被譽為民權史上前所未有的勝利。"}, {"w": "officious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Annoyingly eager to give unwanted advice or exercise authority.", "c": "愛管閒事的；好施號令的", "s": "Everyone at the school avoided the officious hall monitor, who insisted on inspecting every student's pass, lecturing them about punctuality, and reporting minor offenses to the principal, even when no rule had actually been broken.", "t": "學校裡每個人都躲著那位愛管閒事的走廊糾察，他堅持要檢查每個學生的通行證，對他們說教要守時，並把雞毛蒜皮的小過失都報告給校長，即使根本沒有違反任何規定。", "as": "The officious clerk insisted on following every trivial rule, and his pedantic objections only served to protract a process that should have taken five minutes.", "at": "那個愛擺官架子的辦事員堅持遵守每一條瑣碎的規定，他吹毛求疵的異議只是讓原本五分鐘就能完成的程序拖得更久。"}, {"w": "intractable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Hard to control, manage, or solve; stubborn.", "c": "棘手的；難以駕馭的", "s": "Traffic congestion in the capital has proven an intractable problem: despite new subway lines, higher parking fees, and wider roads, commuting times have barely improved over the past two decades.", "t": "首都的交通壅塞已被證實是一個棘手的難題：儘管增設了新的捷運路線、提高了停車費並拓寬了道路，過去二十年來通勤時間幾乎沒有改善。", "as": "The peace negotiations stalled because both sides remained intractable, and the weary mediator, after months of vacillation about whether to continue, finally declared the impasse an insoluble quandary.", "at": "由於雙方都固執己見，和平談判陷入停滯，疲憊的調解人在數個月來對是否繼續猶豫不決之後，終於宣布這個僵局是一個無解的困境。"}, {"w": "altruism", "p": "n.", "d": "Selfless concern for the well-being of others.", "c": "利他主義；無私", "s": "Biologists have long debated the origins of altruism in animals, puzzled by vampire bats that share blood with hungry neighbors and meerkats that risk their own lives to warn the group of approaching predators.", "t": "生物學家長久以來一直在爭論動物利他行為的起源，對於吸血蝠會與飢餓的同伴分享血液、狐獴會冒著生命危險警告群體有掠食者靠近等現象感到困惑。", "as": "Her altruism was evident in decades of philanthropic work, though she disdained ostentatious displays of generosity and preferred to remain anonymous, politely rejecting every accolade that grateful cities offered her.", "at": "她的無私從她數十年的慈善工作中顯而易見，不過她鄙視炫耀式的慷慨，寧可保持匿名，婉拒了所有心懷感激的城市頒給她的榮譽。"}, {"w": "accolade", "p": "n.", "d": "An award, honor, or expression of high praise.", "c": "讚揚；榮譽", "s": "The director's documentary about Taiwan's indigenous languages earned the festival's highest accolade, and critics praised its sensitive portrayal of elders working to pass their mother tongues down to the next generation.", "t": "這位導演關於台灣原住民語言的紀錄片榮獲影展最高榮譽，影評人讚揚它細膩地描繪了長者們努力將母語傳承給下一代的情景。", "as": "The elderly scientist received every accolade the academy could bestow, yet her diffident nature made such ostentatious ceremonies, with their speeches and flashing cameras, more uncomfortable than gratifying.", "at": "這位年長的科學家獲得了學會所能頒發的每一項榮譽，然而她羞怯的個性讓這類充斥著致詞與閃光燈的鋪張典禮對她來說與其說是欣慰，不如說是不自在。"}, {"w": "vernacular", "p": "n.", "d": "The everyday language spoken by ordinary people in a region.", "c": "方言；白話；本地話", "s": "Medieval scholars usually wrote in Latin, but Dante chose to compose his great poem in the Italian vernacular, making his work accessible to ordinary readers who had never studied classical languages.", "t": "中世紀學者通常以拉丁文寫作，但但丁選擇用義大利的白話文創作他的偉大詩篇，讓從未學過古典語言的一般讀者也能讀懂他的作品。", "as": "The novelist's use of the local vernacular gave her dialogue an authenticity that critics found poignant, though some readers struggled with its unfamiliar, colloquial expressions.", "at": "這位小說家使用當地的方言，讓她筆下的對話充滿真實感，評論家認為十分動人，不過有些讀者對其中陌生的口語用法感到吃力。"}, {"w": "judicious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having or showing good judgment and sound sense.", "c": "明智的；審慎的", "s": "With only a limited budget for the science fair, the team made judicious choices, borrowing equipment from the university instead of buying it and spending their savings on the materials that mattered most.", "t": "由於科展的預算有限，這個團隊做出了明智的選擇，向大學借用設備而不是購買，並把節省下來的錢花在最重要的材料上。", "as": "A judicious editor will carefully expunge unnecessary words from a verbose manuscript, trusting that brevity often conveys an author's central argument far more forcefully than elaborate prose.", "at": "一位明智的編輯會刪除冗長手稿中不必要的字詞，深信簡潔往往比華麗的文字更能有力地傳達作者的核心論點。"}, {"w": "chrysalis", "p": "n.", "d": "The pupa of a butterfly or moth; a transitional stage.", "c": "蛹；蛻變前的階段", "s": "Inside its hard, green chrysalis, the caterpillar's body breaks down almost completely and reorganizes itself, and after about two weeks a fully formed butterfly emerges, ready to dry its wings in the sun.", "t": "在堅硬的綠色蛹殼中，毛毛蟲的身體幾乎完全分解並重新組合，大約兩週後，一隻完全成形的蝴蝶破蛹而出，準備在陽光下晾乾翅膀。", "as": "Her years at the conservatory were a chrysalis from which she emerged as a prolific composer, transforming from a callow student into a confident artist.", "at": "她在音樂學院的那幾年就像一段蛹期，她從中蛻變成一位多產的作曲家，從一個青澀的學生轉變為一位自信的藝術家。"}, {"w": "genteel", "p": "adj.", "d": "Polite, refined, or respectable, often in an affected way.", "c": "文雅的；有教養的", "s": "The novel portrays a genteel family in nineteenth-century Boston who carefully maintain their elegant manners and afternoon tea parties, even as they secretly struggle to pay the debts left by their late father.", "t": "這部小說描繪了一個十九世紀波士頓的上流家庭，他們小心翼翼地維持著優雅的禮儀和下午茶會，即使私底下正為了償還已故父親留下的債務而苦苦掙扎。", "as": "Beneath their genteel manners and soft voices, the old aristocrats harbored a supercilious contempt for the parvenu merchants who had recently bought grand estates in their once-exclusive neighborhood.", "at": "在文雅的舉止與輕聲細語之下，這些老派貴族對那些最近在他們昔日專屬的社區買下豪華莊園的暴發戶商人，懷著傲慢的鄙視。"}, {"w": "jovial", "p": "adj.", "d": "Cheerful, friendly, and full of good humor.", "c": "快活的；愉快友善的", "s": "The jovial museum guide kept the tour lively for the young visitors, telling jokes about the ancient emperors, inviting children to imitate statues, and laughing loudly whenever someone asked a silly question.", "t": "那位開朗愉快的博物館導覽員讓年輕參觀者的導覽行程充滿活力，他講述古代皇帝的笑話、邀請孩子們模仿雕像，每當有人問了傻問題時便開懷大笑。", "as": "The jovial host's congenial manner put every nervous guest at ease, and his natural levity soon transformed what had begun as a stiff, formal gathering into a lively, convivial evening.", "at": "這位快活的主人親切友善的態度讓每位緊張的賓客都感到自在，他天生的幽默很快便將一開始拘謹正式的聚會轉變為熱鬧歡樂的夜晚。"}, {"w": "subterfuge", "p": "n.", "d": "Deceit or trickery used to achieve a goal.", "c": "詭計；托辭", "s": "During World War II, the Allies used elaborate subterfuge to mislead the enemy, building fake tanks out of rubber and broadcasting false radio messages about an invasion that was never actually planned.", "t": "第二次世界大戰期間，盟軍使用精心設計的詭計來誤導敵軍，用橡膠製作假坦克，並廣播關於一場根本未曾計畫的入侵行動的假無線電訊息。", "as": "During the Cold War, the spy relied on subterfuge and surreptitious coded messages, and her duplicity was so skillful that even her closest colleagues never suspected her true allegiance.", "at": "冷戰期間，這名間諜仰賴詭計和秘密的密碼訊息行事，她的兩面手法如此高明，就連她最親近的同事都從未懷疑過她真正效忠的對象。"}]}, {"unit": 12, "level": 3, "cards": [{"w": "ebullience", "p": "n.", "d": "Cheerful, bubbling enthusiasm and high spirits.", "c": "熱情洋溢；興高采烈", "s": "The new drama teacher's ebullience was contagious; within weeks, students who had once dreaded performing were volunteering for lead roles, staying after school to rehearse, and cheering loudly for one another's progress.", "t": "新來的戲劇老師那股熱情洋溢的活力極具感染力；短短幾週內，原本害怕上台表演的學生紛紛自願擔任主角，放學後留下來排練，並大聲為彼此的進步喝采。", "as": "The young conductor's ebullience on the podium was a welcome contrast to the phlegmatic style of his predecessor, whose lugubrious interpretations had left audiences half asleep for years.", "at": "這位年輕指揮家在指揮台上熱情洋溢的表現，與他那位冷淡的前任形成可喜的對比，前任指揮那陰鬱沉悶的詮釋多年來讓觀眾昏昏欲睡。"}, {"w": "impervious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Not affected or influenced by something; impenetrable.", "c": "不受影響的；不能滲透的", "s": "The senator seemed impervious to criticism; no matter how many editorials attacked her proposal or how many protesters gathered outside her office, she calmly repeated her position and refused to change a single word.", "t": "這位參議員似乎完全不受批評影響；無論有多少社論抨擊她的提案，或有多少抗議者聚集在她的辦公室外，她都平靜地重申自己的立場，不肯修改任何一個字。", "as": "The incorrigible prankster seemed completely impervious to every reprimand, and even the principal's stern public censure failed to curb his penchant for mischief in the crowded cafeteria at lunchtime.", "at": "那個屢教不改的惡作劇者似乎對每一次責罵都無動於衷，就連校長嚴厲的公開譴責，也無法遏止他午餐時間在擁擠的學生餐廳搗蛋的癖好。"}, {"w": "remonstrate", "p": "v.", "d": "To protest or object forcefully; to plead in protest.", "c": "抗議；規勸；告誡", "s": "When the city announced plans to cut down the century-old banyan trees outside the library, local residents gathered at the town hall to remonstrate with officials, arguing that the trees were part of the community's history.", "t": "當市政府宣布計畫砍伐圖書館外那些百年榕樹時，當地居民聚集在市政廳向官員抗議，主張這些樹是社區歷史的一部分。", "as": "Several professors went to remonstrate with the dean about the arbitrary budget cuts, but their objections seemed only to nettle him and harden his intransigent stance.", "at": "幾位教授去向院長抗議那些武斷的預算刪減，但他們的反對似乎只是激怒了他，讓他不妥協的立場更加強硬。"}, {"w": "efface", "p": "v.", "d": "To erase or wipe out; to make oneself inconspicuous.", "c": "抹去；消除；使不顯眼", "s": "Centuries of wind and rain had nearly managed to efface the inscription on the ancient stone tablet, so archaeologists used special lighting and digital imaging to recover the faded characters.", "t": "數百年來的風吹雨打幾乎抹去了這塊古老石碑上的銘文，因此考古學家利用特殊照明和數位影像技術，還原那些已經褪色的文字。", "as": "The regime tried for decades to efface every record of the massacre, but dissident historians had secretly preserved copious evidence, including letters and photographs, that eventually proved impossible to expunge.", "at": "該政權數十年來試圖抹去那場大屠殺的所有紀錄，但持不同政見的歷史學家秘密保存了大量證據，包括信件和照片，這些證據最終證明是無法被抹除的。"}, {"w": "chimera", "p": "n.", "d": "An impossible or foolish fantasy; an illusion.", "c": "幻想；不切實際的妄想", "s": "For centuries, alchemists pursued the chimera of turning lead into gold, spending fortunes on secret experiments that modern chemistry has shown could never have succeeded with the tools available to them.", "t": "數百年來，煉金術士一直在追求將鉛變成黃金的幻想，耗費大量財富進行秘密實驗，而現代化學已證明，憑藉他們當時所擁有的工具，這些實驗根本不可能成功。", "as": "The salesman's promise of effortless wealth was a chimera, and only the most gullible investors believed that his so-called panacea for poverty could possibly work.", "at": "那名推銷員所承諾不費吹灰之力就能致富的說法只是幻想，只有最容易受騙的投資人才會相信他所謂消除貧窮的萬靈丹真的有效。"}, {"w": "incorrigible", "p": "adj.", "d": "Unable to be corrected, reformed, or improved.", "c": "無可救藥的；屢教不改的", "s": "Despite countless detentions and several long meetings with his worried parents, the incorrigible student continued to sneak snacks into the computer lab, hide classmates' shoes, and invent creative excuses for missing homework.", "t": "儘管被留校察看無數次，也和他憂心的父母開過好幾次冗長的會，這名屢教不改的學生仍繼續偷帶零食進電腦教室、藏同學的鞋子，並為沒交的作業編造各種有創意的藉口。", "as": "The novel's incorrigible hero is a spendthrift who squanders his inheritance, yet his droll humor makes him so likable that readers forgive his every foible.", "at": "這部小說中無可救藥的主角是一個揮霍無度的人，把遺產揮霍殆盡，但他滑稽詼諧的幽默感讓他極為討喜，讀者因此原諒他的每一個小缺點。"}, {"w": "juxtapose", "p": "v.", "d": "To place side by side, especially to compare or contrast.", "c": "並列；並置對比", "s": "In her photography exhibition, the artist chose to juxtapose images of luxury high-rise apartments with pictures of crowded street markets, forcing viewers to confront the growing gap between rich and poor in the city.", "t": "在她的攝影展中，這位藝術家選擇將豪華高樓公寓的影像與擁擠街頭市場的照片並列展出，迫使觀眾正視這座城市日益擴大的貧富差距。", "as": "By juxtaposing footage of the opulent palace with scenes of the squalid slums just outside its walls, the award-winning documentary made the regime's indifference to suffering impossible to ignore.", "at": "這部得獎紀錄片將富麗堂皇的宮殿畫面與宮牆外骯髒貧民窟的景象並置對比，讓該政權對人民苦難的漠不關心變得無從忽視。"}, {"w": "conversant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Familiar with or knowledgeable about a subject.", "c": "熟悉的；精通的", "s": "Because the position required frequent meetings and negotiations with overseas partners, the trading company only hired candidates who were thoroughly conversant with both Japanese business customs and international trade law.", "t": "由於這個職位需要經常與海外合作夥伴開會和協商，這家貿易公司只錄取同時徹底熟悉日本商業慣例與國際貿易法的應徵者。", "as": "Although he was conversant with the jargon of finance, the neophyte analyst lacked the astute judgment that only years of experience in the market could provide.", "at": "雖然這位新手分析師熟悉金融術語，卻缺乏唯有多年市場經驗才能培養出的精明判斷力。"}, {"w": "esoteric", "p": "adj.", "d": "Understood by only a small group with special knowledge.", "c": "深奧的；只有少數人懂的", "s": "The physics lecture quickly became too esoteric for the high school visitors, as the professor filled the whiteboard with complex equations and referred to specialized theories that only graduate students could follow.", "t": "這場物理講座很快就變得太過深奧，高中生訪客聽不懂，因為教授在白板上寫滿了複雜的方程式，並提到一些只有研究生才能理解的專業理論。", "as": "The poet's esoteric allusions to forgotten myths and medieval texts were so inscrutable that even the most erudite critics struggled to construe the meaning of her latest collection.", "at": "這位詩人引用被遺忘的神話與中世紀文本的深奧典故如此難以理解，就連最學識淵博的評論家也難以詮釋她最新詩集的含義。"}, {"w": "auspicious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Showing signs that suggest future success; favorable.", "c": "吉利的；有利的", "s": "The startup's first month was remarkably auspicious: thousands of users downloaded the app, a major investor offered funding, and several tech magazines named the young founders among the year's most promising entrepreneurs.", "t": "這家新創公司的第一個月極為順利、前景看好：數千名用戶下載了這款應用程式，一位大投資人提供了資金，幾家科技雜誌也將這群年輕創辦人列為年度最有潛力的創業家。", "as": "The treaty's signing seemed an auspicious beginning, but the fragile rapprochement between the two former enemies proved transient, collapsing within a single year amid fresh recrimination over the disputed border.", "at": "這項條約的簽署看似一個吉祥的開端，但這兩個昔日敵國之間脆弱的修好卻只是短暫的，不到一年就在針對爭議邊界的新一輪互相指責中破裂。"}, {"w": "itinerant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Traveling from place to place, especially for work.", "c": "巡迴的；流動的", "s": "In the nineteenth century, itinerant doctors rode on horseback from village to village across the frontier, treating patients in farmhouses and general stores because most rural communities had no hospital at all.", "t": "在十九世紀，巡迴醫生騎著馬往返於邊疆的一個個村莊之間，在農舍和雜貨店裡為病患看診，因為大多數鄉村社區根本沒有醫院。", "as": "The itinerant preacher who traveled the frontier was a voluble orator whose fervent sermons drew enormous crowds in every town, though skeptics dismissed him as a charlatan.", "at": "這位在邊疆四處遊走的巡迴傳道人是一位口若懸河的演說家，他熱情激昂的佈道在每個城鎮都吸引了眾多群眾，不過懷疑者認為他只是個江湖騙子。"}, {"w": "cull", "p": "v.", "d": "To select or gather from a large source.", "c": "挑選；揀選；採集", "s": "For her research paper on Taiwan's indigenous music, Grace had to cull relevant quotations from dozens of interviews, old newspapers, and recordings, keeping only the most reliable sources for her final draft.", "t": "為了撰寫關於台灣原住民音樂的研究報告，葛瑞絲必須從數十份訪談、舊報紙和錄音中挑選出相關的引文，最終定稿只保留最可靠的資料來源。", "as": "The experienced editor culled the most salient facts from a verbose two-hundred-page report, producing a terse one-page summary that the busy executives greatly appreciated before their morning meeting.", "at": "這位經驗豐富的編輯從一份長達兩百頁的冗長報告中挑出最顯著的事實，整理出一頁精簡的摘要，忙碌的高階主管們在晨會前對此非常讚賞。"}, {"w": "promulgate", "p": "v.", "d": "To make known officially or publicly; to proclaim.", "c": "頒布；宣傳；傳播", "s": "After years of heated public debate, the Ministry of Education finally decided to promulgate the new curriculum guidelines nationwide, requiring every high school to offer courses in media literacy and critical thinking.", "t": "經過多年激烈的公開辯論，教育部終於決定在全國頒布新的課程綱要，要求每所高中都必須開設媒體素養和批判性思考的課程。", "as": "The city council promulgated a new code of conduct, but its ambiguous wording invited endless cavils from critics who complained that the rules were impossible to enforce.", "at": "議會頒布了一套新的行為準則，但其模稜兩可的措辭招致批評者無休止的挑剔，他們抱怨這些規定根本無法執行。"}, {"w": "gratuitous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Uncalled for; done without good reason or justification.", "c": "無端的；不必要的", "s": "Critics praised the war film's emotional power but complained that its gratuitous scenes of violence added nothing to the story and seemed designed only to shock the audience rather than deepen their understanding.", "t": "評論家稱讚這部戰爭片的情感張力，但抱怨其中不必要的暴力場面對劇情毫無助益，似乎只是為了震撼觀眾，而非加深他們的理解。", "as": "The reviewer's gratuitous insults about the young novelist seemed motivated less by sincere criticism than by personal animosity, and many readers found her caustic tirade more vindictive than insightful.", "at": "這位評論家對那位年輕小說家無端的侮辱，與其說是出於真誠的批評，不如說是出於個人敵意，許多讀者覺得她尖酸刻薄的長篇抨擊與其說有見地，不如說是挾怨報復。"}, {"w": "nomenclature", "p": "n.", "d": "A system of names or terms used in a field.", "c": "命名法；術語系統", "s": "Biology students must master the nomenclature developed by Carl Linnaeus, in which every living organism receives a two-part Latin name indicating its genus and species, such as Homo sapiens for humans.", "t": "生物系學生必須熟練掌握由林奈所發展的命名法，在此系統中，每種生物都會獲得一個由兩部分組成的拉丁文名稱，標示其屬與種，例如人類的學名為Homo sapiens。", "as": "At first, the chemistry textbook's nomenclature seemed esoteric to most beginners, but the author's lucid explanations and helpful diagrams made even the most abstruse compounds easier to remember.", "at": "起初，對大多數初學者來說，這本化學教科書的命名法顯得艱深難懂，但作者清晰的解說和實用的圖表讓即使是最深奧的化合物也比較容易記住。"}, {"w": "droll", "p": "adj.", "d": "Amusing in a dry, odd, or whimsical way.", "c": "滑稽的；幽默逗趣的", "s": "The professor's droll comments about his own clumsiness, delivered with a perfectly straight face, made his lectures on economic theory surprisingly entertaining, and students often quoted his dry jokes long after the semester ended.", "t": "這位教授總是一本正經地說出關於自己笨手笨腳的詼諧評語，讓他的經濟理論課出乎意料地有趣，學期結束很久之後，學生們仍常引用他那冷面的笑話。", "as": "The author's droll observations on everyday family life lend a welcome levity to the memoir, sparing it from becoming merely a prosaic list of mundane events and forgettable dinners.", "at": "作者對日常家庭生活滑稽逗趣的觀察為這本回憶錄增添了令人愉快的輕鬆感，使它不至於淪為只是一份平淡無奇、羅列瑣事與平凡晚餐的清單。"}, {"w": "insatiable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Impossible to satisfy; always wanting more.", "c": "貪得無厭的；無法滿足的", "s": "Marie Curie had an insatiable curiosity about the natural world, often working late into the night in her cold laboratory and continuing her experiments even after she had become internationally famous.", "t": "居禮夫人對大自然有著永不滿足的好奇心，經常在她寒冷的實驗室裡工作到深夜，即使在成為國際知名人物之後，仍持續進行她的實驗。", "as": "The tycoon's insatiable appetite for wealth made him both avaricious and unscrupulous, and by the end of his career he would stop at nothing to acquire yet another lucrative company.", "at": "這位大亨對財富貪得無厭的慾望使他變得既貪婪又不擇手段，到了事業晚期，為了再收購一家賺錢的公司，他會無所不用其極。"}, {"w": "beguile", "p": "v.", "d": "To charm or enchant, sometimes in a deceptive way.", "c": "迷惑；使著迷；欺騙", "s": "The con artist used flattery and fake credentials to beguile elderly investors, persuading them to hand over their retirement savings for a project that, as police later discovered, had never existed at all.", "t": "這名詐騙犯利用奉承和偽造的資歷來迷惑年長的投資人，說服他們交出退休積蓄投資一項計畫，而警方後來發現，這項計畫根本從未存在過。", "as": "The candidate's urbane charm and polished speeches beguiled many voters during the campaign, but astute journalists soon exposed the sophistry behind his grand promises of lower taxes and better schools.", "at": "這位候選人溫文儒雅的魅力和圓滑的演說在競選期間迷住了許多選民，但精明的記者很快就揭穿了他承諾減稅和改善學校等宏大政見背後的詭辯。"}, {"w": "vindictive", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having a strong desire for revenge; spiteful.", "c": "懷恨在心的；報復性的", "s": "After losing the election, the vindictive former mayor spent years filing lawsuits against his rivals and spreading rumors about the journalists who had criticized him, determined to punish everyone he blamed for his defeat.", "t": "落選之後，這位懷恨在心的前市長花了好幾年對他的對手提起訴訟，並散播有關批評過他的記者的謠言，決心懲罰每一個他歸咎為導致自己落敗的人。", "as": "The vindictive emperor ordered all of his former rivals to be ostracized, refusing every attempt to reconcile with their families and nurturing a bitter vendetta that outlasted his reign.", "at": "這位懷恨報復的皇帝下令放逐他所有昔日的對手，拒絕與他們的家族進行任何和解的嘗試，並助長了一場延續到他統治結束之後的激烈世仇。"}, {"w": "replete", "p": "adj.", "d": "Filled or well supplied with something; abundant.", "c": "充滿的；裝滿的", "s": "The museum's new exhibit on ancient Taiwan is replete with artifacts, from jade earrings and bronze tools to painted pottery, giving visitors a vivid picture of daily life thousands of years ago.", "t": "博物館關於古代台灣的新展覽充滿了各式文物，從玉耳飾、青銅工具到彩陶，讓參觀者對數千年前的日常生活有生動的認識。", "as": "The senator's long campaign speech was replete with platitudes, and even her most loyal supporters privately admitted that its bombastic tone and banal arguments had grown tiresome.", "at": "這位參議員冗長的競選演講充斥著陳腔濫調，就連她最忠實的支持者私下也承認，那浮誇的語氣和平庸的論點已令人厭煩。"}]}, {"unit": 13, "level": 3, "cards": [{"w": "preclude", "p": "v.", "d": "to make something impossible; to prevent in advance.", "c": "排除；阻止", "s": "The researchers worried that the small sample size would preclude any firm conclusions, so they spent another two years recruiting volunteers from rural clinics before publishing their findings on childhood asthma.", "t": "研究人員擔心樣本數太小會讓他們無法得出任何確切的結論，因此他們又花了兩年時間從鄉間診所招募受試者，才發表關於兒童氣喘的研究結果。", "as": "The committee's abstruse regulations seemed designed to preclude ordinary citizens from participating, and critics castigated officials for language that obfuscated rather than clarified the process.", "at": "委員會深奧難懂的規定似乎是刻意要阻止一般民眾參與，批評者痛斥官員使用的語言反而模糊了流程，而非加以釐清。"}, {"w": "castigate", "p": "v.", "d": "to criticize or punish someone severely.", "c": "嚴厲批評；懲罰", "s": "In her scathing editorial, the columnist went on to castigate the city council for approving the highway expansion without consulting the neighborhoods that would lose parks, schools, and dozens of small family businesses.", "t": "在那篇措辭尖銳的社論中，這位專欄作家接著嚴厲抨擊市議會，指責其在未諮詢那些將失去公園、學校和數十家小型家族企業的社區之前，就批准了公路擴建案。", "as": "Critics castigated the senator's grandiloquent speech as vacuous, arguing that its soaring phrases about national greatness concealed a complete absence of practical proposals for the struggling farmers in her own state.", "at": "批評者痛斥這位參議員浮誇的演說空洞無物，認為那些關於國家偉大的華麗辭藻，掩蓋了她對自己州內困頓農民毫無具體可行方案的事實。"}, {"w": "colloquial", "p": "adj.", "d": "used in informal, everyday conversation rather than formal writing.", "c": "口語的；非正式的", "s": "Because the novelist wanted her teenage characters to sound authentic, she filled their dialogue with colloquial expressions overheard on buses and in cafeterias, rather than the polished, formal English her editors had expected.", "t": "由於這位小說家希望筆下的青少年角色聽起來真實，她在他們的對白中填滿了在公車上和學生餐廳裡聽來的口語用語，而不是編輯們原本期待的精緻正式英文。", "as": "Although the professor's lectures were famously abstruse, his colloquial asides and convivial manner during office hours made even the most diffident first-year students feel welcome to ask questions.", "at": "雖然這位教授的講課出了名地深奧難懂，但他在辦公時間裡口語化的閒聊與和藹友善的態度，讓即使是最羞怯的大一新生也敢於發問。"}, {"w": "obfuscate", "p": "v.", "d": "to make something deliberately unclear or confusing.", "c": "使模糊；混淆", "s": "Investigators discovered that the company had used dense technical jargon and dozens of confusing footnotes to obfuscate the true risks of its investment product, leaving many retirees unaware of how much money they could lose.", "t": "調查人員發現，該公司利用艱澀的技術術語和數十個令人困惑的註腳，刻意混淆其投資商品的真正風險，使許多退休人士根本不知道自己可能損失多少錢。", "as": "The witness's attempt to obfuscate the timeline only reinforced the jury's suspicion of his complicity, since his story seemed less like honest confusion than a deliberate effort to dissemble.", "at": "證人企圖混淆事件時間順序的做法，反而加深了陪審團對他涉案共謀的懷疑，因為他的說詞看起來與其說是單純的困惑，不如說是刻意的掩飾。"}, {"w": "facile", "p": "adj.", "d": "too simple; showing little careful thought or effort.", "c": "膚淺的；輕而易舉的", "s": "The historian rejected the facile explanation that the empire collapsed simply because its rulers were greedy, arguing instead that drought, disease, trade disruptions, and military overreach had all worked together over many decades.", "t": "這位歷史學家駁斥了「帝國崩潰只因統治者貪婪」這種膚淺的解釋，主張乾旱、疾病、貿易中斷與軍事過度擴張在數十年間共同造成了帝國的衰亡。", "as": "Dismissing the problem with a facile slogan, the mayor offered no plan commensurate with the crisis, and residents soon grew tired of his glib and empty reassurances.", "at": "市長用一句膚淺的口號帶過問題，卻提不出與這場危機相稱的計畫，居民很快就對他油腔滑調又空洞的保證感到厭倦。"}, {"w": "convivial", "p": "adj.", "d": "friendly, cheerful, and enjoying good company.", "c": "歡樂的；好交際的", "s": "After weeks of tense negotiations, the delegates finally relaxed at a convivial dinner where scientists from rival nations shared stories, laughed over local dishes, and toasted the new agreement to protect the Antarctic environment.", "t": "經過數週緊張的談判後，代表們終於在一場歡樂的晚宴上放鬆下來；來自敵對國家的科學家們分享故事、邊品嘗在地料理邊談笑，並舉杯慶祝這項保護南極環境的新協議。", "as": "The host's convivial manner put every guest at ease, yet beneath his jovial laughter lay an idiosyncrasy few noticed: he never ate a single bite of the food he served.", "at": "主人歡快熱情的態度讓每位賓客都感到自在，然而在他爽朗的笑聲背後，藏著一個很少人注意到的怪癖：他從不吃自己端出來的任何一口食物。"}, {"w": "eschew", "p": "v.", "d": "to deliberately avoid using or doing something.", "c": "避開；戒絕", "s": "To keep her research as objective as possible, the anthropologist chose to eschew any gifts or payments from the villagers she studied, believing that even small favors might influence what they told her.", "t": "為了讓研究盡可能保持客觀，這位人類學家選擇刻意避免接受所研究村民的任何禮物或報酬，她認為即使是小小的恩惠也可能影響他們告訴她的內容。", "as": "Determined to eschew the bombastic style of his predecessors, the new editor favored terse, lucid prose that readers in small towns and large cities alike found refreshingly direct.", "at": "新任主編決心摒棄前任們浮誇的文風，偏好簡潔明晰的文字，無論是小鎮還是大城市的讀者，都覺得這種直截了當的風格令人耳目一新。"}, {"w": "prodigious", "p": "adj.", "d": "remarkably great in size, amount, or degree.", "c": "巨大的；驚人的", "s": "Building the Great Wall required a prodigious amount of labor; historians estimate that hundreds of thousands of soldiers, peasants, and prisoners worked on its various sections across many centuries, often in brutal conditions.", "t": "修築長城需要極其龐大的勞力；歷史學家估計，數百年來有數十萬名士兵、農民和囚犯在各段城牆上勞動，而且往往身處極其惡劣的環境。", "as": "The sycophant's prodigious flattery could not disguise his vacuous ideas, and the director soon grew weary of advice that was as plentiful as it was useless.", "at": "那名馬屁精驚人的奉承話也掩飾不了他空洞的想法，導演很快就厭倦了這些數量雖多卻毫無用處的建議。"}, {"w": "idiosyncrasy", "p": "n.", "d": "a peculiar personal habit or way of behaving.", "c": "怪癖；個人特質", "s": "One idiosyncrasy of the famous physicist was that he refused to wear socks, claiming they always developed holes; colleagues found this habit amusing but agreed it never distracted from his brilliant work on relativity.", "t": "這位知名物理學家的一個怪癖是拒絕穿襪子，他聲稱襪子總是會破洞；同事們覺得這個習慣很有趣，但都同意這從未影響他在相對論上的卓越研究。", "as": "Her habit of humming during exams was a harmless idiosyncrasy, but the proctor, mistaking it for a mnemonic signal to classmates, suspected her of complicity in cheating.", "at": "她考試時哼歌的習慣只是一個無害的怪癖，但監考老師誤以為那是給同學的記憶提示暗號，因而懷疑她參與共謀作弊。"}, {"w": "approbation", "p": "n.", "d": "official approval or praise.", "c": "認可；讚許", "s": "The young architect's design for the public library won the approbation of both the city planning board and local residents, who praised its energy-efficient windows, accessible entrances, and quiet reading gardens.", "t": "這位年輕建築師設計的公共圖書館方案贏得了市府都市計畫委員會與當地居民的一致認可，他們稱讚其節能窗戶、無障礙入口以及寧靜的閱讀花園。", "as": "The proposal received unanimous approbation from the board, though one outspoken member privately disparaged it as banal, merely a safe, familiar idea dressed up in grandiloquent language.", "at": "這項提案獲得董事會一致認可，不過一位直言不諱的成員私下貶低它平庸無奇，不過是用華麗浮誇的辭藻包裝起來的安全、老套點子。"}, {"w": "legerdemain", "p": "n.", "d": "sleight of hand; skillful trickery or deception.", "c": "戲法；花招", "s": "After months of careful investigation, auditors eventually exposed the accountant's financial legerdemain: by secretly shifting money between dozens of hidden accounts, he had made a failing company appear profitable for nearly five years.", "t": "經過數月的仔細調查，稽核人員最終揭穿了這名會計師的財務花招：他藉由在數十個隱密帳戶之間暗中轉移資金，讓一家經營不善的公司在將近五年間看起來都有獲利。", "as": "Through a kind of verbal legerdemain, the lawyer managed to obfuscate the facts so thoroughly that the jury could no longer tell which version of events was tenable.", "at": "這位律師靠著一種語言上的戲法，把事實混淆得極為徹底，以致陪審團再也分不清哪一種事件版本站得住腳。"}, {"w": "puerile", "p": "adj.", "d": "childishly silly and immature.", "c": "幼稚的；愚蠢的", "s": "The debate moderator warned both candidates that puerile name-calling and mocking each other's appearance would not be tolerated, reminding them that voters expected a serious discussion of health care and education.", "t": "辯論主持人警告兩位候選人，幼稚的互相謾罵和嘲笑彼此外表的行為將不被容許，並提醒他們選民期待的是對醫療與教育議題的嚴肅討論。", "as": "The senator's puerile tirade against reporters struck even his allies as odious, and several colleagues began to ostracize him from important committee discussions the following week.", "at": "這位參議員對記者發表的幼稚長篇謾罵，連他的盟友都覺得可憎，好幾位同僚在接下來的一週開始把他排除在重要的委員會討論之外。"}, {"w": "complicity", "p": "n.", "d": "involvement with others in a crime or wrongdoing.", "c": "共謀；串通", "s": "Historians continue to debate the extent of ordinary citizens' complicity in the regime's crimes, asking whether people who stayed silent shared some responsibility with the officials who actually gave the orders.", "t": "歷史學家持續爭論一般民眾在該政權罪行中的共謀程度，探討那些保持沉默的人是否與實際下令的官員共同負有某種責任。", "as": "Accused of complicity in the fraud, the clerk tried to dissemble, but investigators soon found emails proving she had helped her manager peculate thousands of dollars.", "at": "這名職員被控共謀詐欺，她試圖掩飾，但調查人員很快就找到電子郵件，證明她曾協助主管盜用數千美元公款。"}, {"w": "transmute", "p": "v.", "d": "to change something completely in form or nature.", "c": "使變形；使變質", "s": "Medieval alchemists spent their lives trying to transmute lead into gold, and although they never succeeded, their careful experiments with metals and acids helped lay the foundations of modern chemistry.", "t": "中世紀的煉金術士窮盡一生試圖將鉛變成黃金；雖然他們從未成功，但他們對金屬與酸類的細心實驗，為現代化學奠定了基礎。", "as": "The composer sought to transmute the cacophony of city traffic into something sonorous and beautiful, layering recorded car horns and sirens beneath a slow, lugubrious cello melody.", "at": "這位作曲家試圖把城市交通的嘈雜噪音轉化為渾厚而優美的聲音，他將錄下的汽車喇叭聲與警笛聲疊在一段緩慢而哀傷的大提琴旋律之下。"}, {"w": "abstruse", "p": "adj.", "d": "difficult to understand; obscure.", "c": "深奧的；難懂的", "s": "Although the philosopher's theories were notoriously abstruse, her student wrote a clear, lively guide that explained the key ideas with everyday examples, making the work accessible to high school readers for the first time.", "t": "雖然這位哲學家的理論出了名地深奧難懂，她的學生卻寫了一本清楚又生動的導讀，用日常生活中的例子解釋重要概念，首次讓高中讀者也能讀懂這部作品。", "as": "Critics complained that the novel's abstruse philosophical digressions were tangential to the plot, yet admirers praised its discursive style as deeply rewarding for patient readers.", "at": "評論家抱怨這部小說深奧難懂的哲學離題段落與情節關係不大，但支持者稱讚其漫談式的風格對有耐心的讀者而言收穫豐富。"}, {"w": "edify", "p": "v.", "d": "to instruct and improve someone morally or intellectually.", "c": "啟發；教化", "s": "The museum's new exhibit aims not only to entertain visitors but also to edify them, using interactive displays and survivor interviews to teach lessons about tolerance, courage, and the dangers of prejudice.", "t": "博物館的新展覽不僅希望娛樂參觀者，也希望啟發他們，透過互動式展示與倖存者訪談，傳達關於包容、勇氣以及偏見之危險的教訓。", "as": "Hoping to edify rather than merely entertain, the documentary avoided didactic narration and instead let farmers describe their bucolic lives in their own colloquial words.", "at": "這部紀錄片希望啟發觀眾而非只是娛樂，因此避免說教式的旁白，改讓農民用自己口語化的言語描述他們的田園生活。"}, {"w": "supercilious", "p": "adj.", "d": "behaving as if one is superior to others.", "c": "高傲的；目中無人的", "s": "The new manager's supercilious attitude quickly alienated her team; she rolled her eyes at their suggestions, corrected their grammar in meetings, and openly implied that nobody else in the office was as intelligent as she was.", "t": "新任經理高傲的態度很快就讓團隊疏遠了她；她對同事的建議翻白眼、在會議中糾正他們的文法，還公開暗示辦公室裡沒有人跟她一樣聰明。", "as": "The critic's supercilious review castigated the young author for writing such colloquial dialogue in a serious literary novel, though many teenage readers found that same informal language refreshingly authentic.", "at": "那位評論家高傲的書評嚴厲批評這位年輕作家在一本嚴肅文學小說中寫出如此口語化的對白，但許多青少年讀者卻覺得同樣的非正式語言真實得令人耳目一新。"}, {"w": "dissemble", "p": "v.", "d": "to hide one's true feelings, motives, or intentions.", "c": "掩飾；假裝", "s": "When reporters asked whether the factory had been dumping chemicals into the river, the spokesperson tried to dissemble, smiling calmly and talking about community programs while avoiding any direct answer to the question.", "t": "當記者詢問工廠是否一直將化學物質傾倒入河中時，發言人試圖掩飾真相，一邊冷靜微笑、大談社區計畫，一邊迴避對問題做出任何直接回答。", "as": "Unable to dissemble his contempt, the supercilious professor sneered at every question, and his students soon learned to eschew his office hours entirely for the rest of the semester.", "at": "那位高傲的教授無法掩飾他的輕蔑，對每個問題都嗤之以鼻，學生們很快就學會在學期剩下的時間裡完全避開他的辦公時間。"}, {"w": "vacuous", "p": "adj.", "d": "lacking intelligence, thought, or meaningful content.", "c": "空洞的；愚蠢的", "s": "Media critics argue that many celebrity interviews are vacuous, filled with rehearsed compliments and questions about fashion rather than any meaningful discussion of the artists' work, influences, or creative process.", "t": "媒體評論者認為，許多名人訪談內容空洞，充斥著事先排練好的讚美以及關於時尚的提問，而非對藝人作品、影響來源或創作過程的任何有意義討論。", "as": "Beneath the banal jokes and vacuous chatter of the late-night talk show lay a sharper satire, one that quietly disparaged the very celebrities who appeared as guests.", "at": "在那個深夜脫口秀平庸的笑話與空洞的閒聊之下，其實藏著更尖銳的諷刺，悄悄貶低了那些上節目當來賓的名人。"}, {"w": "capacious", "p": "adj.", "d": "having a lot of space inside; roomy.", "c": "寬敞的；容量大的", "s": "The old train station was converted into a capacious public market, its enormous hall now holding more than two hundred food stalls, a children's play area, and long communal tables that seat over a thousand visitors.", "t": "這座老舊火車站被改建成一座寬敞的公共市場，其巨大的大廳如今容納了兩百多個美食攤位、一個兒童遊戲區，以及可容納一千多名遊客的長型共用餐桌。", "as": "The capacious reading room, with its commodious leather chairs, was a favorite retreat for the erudite professor, who could ruminate there for hours on ancient philosophy among thousands of rare volumes.", "at": "那間寬敞的閱覽室擺著舒適寬大的皮椅，是那位博學教授最喜愛的避靜之所，他可以在那裡的數千冊珍本之間，連續數小時沉思古代哲學。"}]}, {"unit": 14, "level": 3, "cards": [{"w": "mnemonic", "p": "n.", "d": "a pattern, rhyme, or device that aids memory.", "c": "記憶術；助記方法", "s": "To help her biology students remember the order of taxonomic ranks, the teacher taught them a mnemonic: \"King Philip Came Over For Good Soup,\" in which each word's first letter stands for kingdom, phylum, class, order, family, genus, and species.", "t": "為了幫助生物課的學生記住生物分類階層的順序，老師教了他們一個記憶口訣：「King Philip Came Over For Good Soup」，每個字的首字母分別代表界、門、綱、目、科、屬、種。", "as": "The tutor offered a clever mnemonic for remembering ubiquitous Latin roots, a strategy so effective that even students with no proclivity for languages could recall dozens of words.", "at": "這位家教提供了一個巧妙的記憶法，用來記住隨處可見的拉丁字根；這個方法非常有效，連對語言毫無天分傾向的學生都能記住數十個單字。"}, {"w": "sonorous", "p": "adj.", "d": "having a deep, full, and impressive sound.", "c": "聲音宏亮的；渾厚的", "s": "The cathedral's ancient bronze bells produced a sonorous tone that rolled across the valley every Sunday morning, so deep and full that farmers working in fields several kilometers away could hear it clearly.", "t": "大教堂古老的青銅鐘每逢週日早晨便發出渾厚的鐘聲，迴盪整個山谷；鐘聲深沉而飽滿，連在數公里外田間工作的農民都能清楚聽見。", "as": "The radio host's sonorous voice lent authority to even his most banal remarks, and loyal listeners rarely noticed how often his commentary turned grandiloquent and empty.", "at": "這位電台主持人渾厚宏亮的嗓音，讓他即使是最平庸的言論也顯得有分量，忠實聽眾很少察覺他的評論有多常變得浮誇而空洞。"}, {"w": "admonish", "p": "v.", "d": "to warn or criticize someone gently but firmly.", "c": "告誡；勸誡", "s": "Before the field trip to the national park, the guide took a moment to admonish the students not to feed the monkeys, explaining that human food can make the animals sick and aggressive toward visitors.", "t": "在國家公園校外教學出發前，導覽員特別花時間告誡學生不要餵食猴子，並解釋人類的食物會讓這些動物生病，還可能使牠們對遊客產生攻擊性。", "as": "The coach would admonish any player who tried to goad opponents with insults, insisting that such puerile behavior had no place on a team that valued respect.", "at": "教練會告誡任何試圖用侮辱言語挑釁對手的球員，堅持這種幼稚行為在一支重視尊重的球隊中毫無容身之處。"}, {"w": "paradigm", "p": "n.", "d": "a typical model or framework of thinking.", "c": "典範；範例", "s": "Copernicus challenged the ancient paradigm that placed Earth at the center of the universe, and his sun-centered model eventually transformed the way astronomers, philosophers, and ordinary people understood humanity's place in the cosmos.", "t": "哥白尼挑戰了將地球置於宇宙中心的古老典範，而他以太陽為中心的模型最終改變了天文學家、哲學家和一般大眾理解人類在宇宙中地位的方式。", "as": "The young economist was an iconoclast who rejected the prevailing paradigm, and although her heterodox theories were ridiculed at first, later data seemed to vindicate her completely.", "at": "這位年輕經濟學家是一位打破傳統的人，她拒絕當時主流的典範；雖然她的非正統理論起初備受嘲笑，但後來的數據似乎完全證明了她是對的。"}, {"w": "circuitous", "p": "adj.", "d": "longer than necessary; not direct; roundabout.", "c": "迂迴的；繞道的", "s": "Because the main bridge had been washed away by the typhoon, relief trucks were forced to take a circuitous route through the mountains, turning a two-hour journey into an exhausting nine-hour drive.", "t": "由於主要橋樑被颱風沖毀，救援卡車被迫繞道山區、走迂迴的路線，原本兩小時的車程變成了令人筋疲力盡的九小時。", "as": "His circuitous explanation was so discursive that listeners grew restless, and the chairperson finally had to admonish him to stop wandering and address the budget question directly.", "at": "他迂迴的解釋拉拉雜雜、離題甚遠，聽眾愈來愈不耐煩，主席最後不得不告誡他別再東拉西扯，直接回答預算問題。"}, {"w": "vindicate", "p": "v.", "d": "to prove that someone or something was right or blameless.", "c": "證明…正確；洗清嫌疑", "s": "After spending twelve years in prison for a robbery he did not commit, the man hoped that new DNA evidence would finally vindicate him and restore the reputation his family had defended for so long.", "t": "在為一件他沒有犯下的搶案坐了十二年牢之後，這名男子希望新的 DNA 證據終於能洗清他的冤屈，恢復家人長久以來為他捍衛的名譽。", "as": "Years later, the discovery of fossil evidence would vindicate the heterodox scientist, whose colleagues had once ostracized her for questioning the field's dominant theory of extinction.", "at": "多年後，化石證據的發現證明了這位非正統科學家是對的；她的同事們曾因她質疑該領域主流的物種滅絕理論而排擠她。"}, {"w": "bucolic", "p": "adj.", "d": "relating to the pleasant aspects of country life.", "c": "田園的；鄉村風味的", "s": "The painter left the noisy city for a bucolic village in the hills, where she spent her days sketching grazing sheep, wooden farmhouses, and wildflower meadows that later appeared in her most celebrated landscapes.", "t": "這位畫家離開喧囂的城市，搬到山丘上一個田園風光的小村莊，每天素描吃草的綿羊、木造農舍和野花草地，這些景物後來都出現在她最負盛名的風景畫中。", "as": "The poet's bucolic verses idealized farm life, yet critics noted that their lugubrious undertones revealed the poet's ambivalent feelings about the hardships rural families actually endured.", "at": "這位詩人的田園詩將農村生活理想化，但評論家指出，詩中悲戚的弦外之音透露出詩人對鄉村家庭真實承受的艱辛，懷有矛盾複雜的感受。"}, {"w": "ostracize", "p": "v.", "d": "to exclude someone from a group or society.", "c": "排擠；放逐", "s": "In some traditional societies, families would ostracize any member who married without permission, refusing to speak to the person, share meals, or invite him or her to festivals for many years.", "t": "在一些傳統社會中，家族會排擠任何未經許可就結婚的成員，多年來拒絕與那人交談、一起吃飯，或邀請他或她參加節慶活動。", "as": "Ancient Athenians could ostracize a politician they found odious, voting to banish him for ten years; some historians disparage the practice as a tool for settling personal grudges.", "at": "古代雅典人可以投票放逐他們認為可憎的政治人物，將其驅逐十年；一些歷史學家貶低這種做法，認為它是解決私人恩怨的工具。"}, {"w": "plethora", "p": "n.", "d": "an excessive amount or number of something.", "c": "過多；過剩", "s": "Unlike earlier generations, today's students face a plethora of online information about almost every topic, which makes learning to evaluate sources, check facts, and identify bias more important than ever before.", "t": "與前幾代人不同，現今的學生幾乎在每個主題上都面對過量的網路資訊，這使得學會評估資料來源、查核事實和辨識偏見比以往任何時候都更加重要。", "as": "Faced with a plethora of choices, the indecisive shopper began to vacillate, comparing dozens of nearly identical phones until the salesperson's incessant chatter finally drove her from the store.", "at": "面對過多的選擇，這位優柔寡斷的顧客開始猶豫不決，比較了數十支幾乎一模一樣的手機，直到店員喋喋不休的推銷終於把她趕出了店門。"}, {"w": "proclivity", "p": "n.", "d": "a natural tendency to do something.", "c": "傾向；癖好", "s": "From an early age, the future engineer showed a strong proclivity for taking things apart; by the age of eight she had dismantled two radios, a toaster, and her grandfather's old clock to see how they worked.", "t": "這位未來的工程師從小就表現出喜歡拆解東西的強烈傾向；八歲時，她已經拆過兩台收音機、一台烤麵包機和祖父的舊時鐘，只為了看看它們如何運作。", "as": "Her proclivity for tangential remarks made the history lectures unpredictable, yet her students insisted that these discursive detours were often more memorable than any chapter in their assigned textbook.", "at": "她喜歡講些題外話的習性讓歷史課變得難以預料，但她的學生們堅稱，這些漫談式的岔題往往比指定教科書中的任何章節都更令人難忘。"}, {"w": "commensurate", "p": "adj.", "d": "corresponding in size, amount, or degree; proportionate.", "c": "相稱的；相當的", "s": "Union leaders argued that nurses deserved salaries commensurate with their long hours, advanced training, and heavy responsibilities, pointing out that many hospital administrators earned three times as much for less demanding work.", "t": "工會領袖主張護理師應該獲得與其長時工作、專業訓練以及沉重責任相稱的薪資，並指出許多醫院行政主管做較輕鬆的工作，薪水卻是護理師的三倍。", "as": "The workers demanded remuneration commensurate with the dangers they faced underground, arguing that their meager wages were a pittance compared with the company's enormous profits.", "at": "工人們要求與他們在地底所面臨危險相稱的報酬，主張他們微薄的工資與公司的巨額利潤相比，簡直少得可憐。"}, {"w": "incessant", "p": "adj.", "d": "continuing without stopping; constant.", "c": "不停的；持續不斷的", "s": "Residents near the construction site complained about the incessant noise of drills and trucks, which began before dawn and continued late into the night, making it nearly impossible for them to sleep or work from home.", "t": "工地附近的居民抱怨鑽孔機和卡車的噪音持續不斷，從黎明前開始一直延續到深夜，讓他們幾乎無法睡覺或在家工作。", "as": "The incessant cacophony of car horns outside the apartment would enervate even the most patient tenant, so the writer moved to a quiet cabin to finish her novel.", "at": "公寓外汽車喇叭不絕於耳的刺耳噪音，就連最有耐心的房客都會被磨得筋疲力盡，所以這位作家搬到一間寧靜的小木屋去完成她的小說。"}, {"w": "sycophant", "p": "n.", "d": "a person who flatters powerful people to gain advantage.", "c": "諂媚者；馬屁精", "s": "The king surrounded himself with courtiers who praised every decision he made, and historians believe that relying on such a sycophant instead of honest advisers led him to start a disastrous and unnecessary war.", "t": "這位國王身邊圍繞著對他每項決定都歌功頌德的朝臣；歷史學家認為，他倚賴這種阿諛奉承之人而非誠實的顧問，導致他發動了一場災難性且毫無必要的戰爭。", "as": "The CEO, surrounded by obsequious advisers, could no longer distinguish honest counsel from the empty praise of a sycophant, and his company's decline was soon inexorable.", "at": "這位執行長身邊圍繞著卑躬屈膝的顧問，再也分辨不出誠實的建言與馬屁精的空洞讚美，他的公司很快就無可挽回地走向衰敗。"}, {"w": "tangential", "p": "adj.", "d": "only slightly related to the main subject.", "c": "離題的；關係不大的", "s": "The professor reminded her students that their research papers should focus on the causes of the French Revolution and that tangential details about Marie Antoinette's fashion choices, however entertaining, should be cut.", "t": "教授提醒學生，他們的研究報告應該聚焦於法國大革命的起因，至於瑪麗．安東尼的穿著打扮之類與主題關係不大的細節，不論多有趣都應該刪掉。", "as": "The speaker's tangential anecdotes made his lecture discursive, and his digressions about childhood vacations were peripheral to the topic of climate policy he had been invited to discuss.", "at": "講者那些離題的軼事讓他的演講顯得散漫，他關於童年假期的題外話與他受邀討論的氣候政策主題毫不相干。"}, {"w": "tenable", "p": "adj.", "d": "able to be defended or maintained against criticism.", "c": "站得住腳的；可防守的", "s": "As new satellite data showed glaciers melting faster than predicted, the claim that global temperatures were not rising became less and less tenable, and even former skeptics began to revise their positions.", "t": "隨著新的衛星數據顯示冰河融化速度比預測的更快，「全球氣溫沒有上升」的說法愈來愈站不住腳，就連過去的懷疑者也開始修正自己的立場。", "as": "The theory had seemed tenable for decades, but new evidence suggested it was specious, and the young researcher who disproved it was hailed as an iconoclast.", "at": "這個理論數十年來似乎都站得住腳，但新證據顯示它只是似是而非，推翻它的年輕研究者因此被譽為打破傳統的人。"}, {"w": "impalpable", "p": "adj.", "d": "unable to be felt by touch; hard to grasp mentally.", "c": "無法觸知的；難以理解的", "s": "Visitors to the abandoned mansion often described an impalpable sense of sadness in its empty halls, a feeling they could not explain or point to, yet one that lingered long after they had left.", "t": "造訪那座廢棄宅邸的人經常描述，空蕩蕩的大廳中瀰漫著一股難以捉摸的哀傷，那種感覺他們既無法解釋也說不出從何而來，卻在離開後久久不散。", "as": "An impalpable tension filled the crowded courtroom as the jury slowly returned to their seats; the defendant, struggling to maintain his equanimity, hoped the verdict would finally vindicate him.", "at": "陪審團緩緩回到座位時，一股難以言喻的緊張氣氛籠罩著擠滿人的法庭；被告努力保持鎮定，希望判決終能還他清白。"}, {"w": "odious", "p": "adj.", "d": "extremely unpleasant; deserving hatred.", "c": "可憎的；令人厭惡的", "s": "Most citizens found the dictator's policy of punishing young children for their parents' political opinions truly odious, and human rights groups and international leaders condemned it as a clear violation of basic human rights.", "t": "大多數民眾都認為那位獨裁者因父母的政治立場而懲罰年幼兒童的政策極為可憎，人權團體與國際領袖也譴責這是明顯違反基本人權的行為。", "as": "The journalist's odious attempts to vilify the grieving family drew widespread condemnation, and readers who had once admired his writing now dismissed him as a mere sycophant to powerful politicians.", "at": "那位記者企圖詆毀悲痛家屬的可憎行為招致各方譴責，曾經欣賞他文筆的讀者如今都認為他不過是權勢政客的馬屁精。"}, {"w": "ubiquitous", "p": "adj.", "d": "seeming to be everywhere at the same time.", "c": "無所不在的；普遍存在的", "s": "Convenience stores are so ubiquitous in Taipei that residents can usually find one within a few minutes' walk of any home, school, or office, buying everything from hot meals to train tickets around the clock.", "t": "便利商店在台北無所不在，居民通常從任何住家、學校或辦公室步行幾分鐘內就能找到一家，全天候都能買到從熱食到火車票等各種東西。", "as": "Smartphones have become ubiquitous on campus, and some educators disparage them as distractions that enervate students' attention, while others praise their prodigious potential for learning.", "at": "智慧型手機在校園裡已經無所不在，一些教育工作者貶抑它們是削弱學生專注力的干擾物，另一些人則稱讚它們在學習上具有巨大潛力。"}, {"w": "ruminate", "p": "v.", "d": "to think deeply and carefully about something for a long time.", "c": "沉思；反覆思考", "s": "After losing the national championship by a single point, the swimmer would often ruminate on her performance for hours, replaying each turn and stroke in her mind to understand what she might have done differently.", "t": "在以一分之差輸掉全國冠軍後，這位泳者常常花上好幾個小時反覆思考自己的表現，在腦中重播每一次轉身和划水，想弄清楚自己原本可以怎麼做。", "as": "Retired from public life, the elderly diplomat liked to ruminate on the vicissitudes of his career, recalling with equanimity both his triumphs and his most painful failures.", "at": "這位年邁的外交官退出公共生活後，喜歡沉思自己職涯中的種種起伏，平靜地回顧他的成就與最痛苦的失敗。"}, {"w": "remuneration", "p": "n.", "d": "payment for work or services.", "c": "報酬；酬勞", "s": "The survey found that remuneration was not the only factor young workers considered when choosing a job; many valued flexible schedules, opportunities for learning, and a positive workplace culture just as highly as pay.", "t": "調查發現，報酬並不是年輕人選擇工作時唯一考量的因素；許多人對彈性工時、學習機會和正向職場文化的重視程度，與薪資不相上下。", "as": "The executive's remuneration seemed opulent compared with the meager wages of factory workers, and shareholders began to disparage the board for rewarding failure so generously.", "at": "與工廠工人微薄的工資相比，這位高階主管的酬勞顯得極為豐厚，股東們開始抨擊董事會如此慷慨地獎勵失敗。"}]}, {"unit": 15, "level": 3, "cards": [{"w": "peccadillo", "p": "n.", "d": "a small, relatively unimportant sin or fault.", "c": "小過失；小毛病", "s": "Voters were willing to forgive the mayor's occasional peccadillo, such as arriving late to ribbon-cutting ceremonies, but they grew angry when reporters revealed that she had secretly used public funds to renovate her vacation home.", "t": "選民願意原諒市長偶爾犯的小過失，例如在剪綵典禮上遲到，但當記者揭露她暗中挪用公款整修自己的度假別墅時，他們就憤怒了。", "as": "The tabloids tried to inflate the actor's peccadillo into a scandal, but their grandiloquent headlines only made readers disparage the newspapers rather than the actor himself.", "at": "八卦小報試圖把這位演員的小過失渲染成醜聞，但那些浮誇的標題反而讓讀者貶低報社，而不是這位演員本人。"}, {"w": "supine", "p": "adj.", "d": "lying face upward; also, passive or inactive.", "c": "仰臥的；消極被動的", "s": "Critics accused the legislature of being supine in the face of the governor's growing power, noting that lawmakers had approved every one of his controversial proposals without debate, amendment, or a single dissenting vote.", "t": "批評者指責立法機關面對州長日益擴大的權力時消極被動，並指出議員們對他每一項具爭議性的提案都照單全收，既沒有辯論、沒有修正，也沒有任何一張反對票。", "as": "The supine press, eager to please the regime, never challenged its odious policies, and the few journalists who dared to criticize the government were swiftly ostracized.", "at": "消極順從的媒體一心討好政權，從未質疑其可憎的政策，而少數敢於批評政府的記者很快就遭到排擠。"}, {"w": "banal", "p": "adj.", "d": "so ordinary that it is boring; lacking originality.", "c": "陳腐的；平庸的", "s": "The film's special effects were spectacular, but reviewers complained that its banal dialogue, filled with tired phrases like \"We've got company\" and \"Let's do this,\" made the characters feel like cardboard cutouts.", "t": "這部電影的特效十分壯觀，但影評人抱怨其對白陳腐乏味，充斥著「有人來了」、「放手一搏吧」之類的老套台詞，讓角色顯得像紙板人偶般單薄。", "as": "The student's essay was technically correct but banal, and her teacher urged her to eschew platitudes and take a more heterodox position that would genuinely challenge readers.", "at": "這名學生的文章在技術上沒有錯誤，但內容平庸，老師敦促她避開陳腔濫調，採取更不落俗套的立場，真正挑戰讀者的思維。"}, {"w": "heterodox", "p": "adj.", "d": "not conforming to accepted beliefs or standards.", "c": "非正統的；異端的", "s": "In the seventeenth century, Galileo's heterodox claim that Earth moved around the sun brought him into conflict with church authorities, who placed him under house arrest for the rest of his life.", "t": "十七世紀時，伽利略提出地球繞太陽運轉這一非正統的主張，使他與教會當局發生衝突，教會因此將他終身軟禁。", "as": "An outspoken iconoclast, the critic championed heterodox artists whom the national academy had long dismissed, and he loved to goad conservative curators into heated public debates on television.", "at": "這位直言不諱、打破傳統的評論家力挺那些長期被國家藝術學院排斥的非正統藝術家，而且他很喜歡激怒保守的策展人，在電視上引發激烈的公開辯論。"}, {"w": "grandiloquent", "p": "adj.", "d": "using pompous, overly elaborate language to impress.", "c": "誇張的；言辭浮誇的", "s": "The senator's grandiloquent speech, filled with references to ancient Rome and phrases like \"the eternal flame of liberty,\" impressed few listeners, who wanted simple, concrete answers about rising rents and long commutes.", "t": "這位參議員言辭浮誇的演說，充斥著對古羅馬的引述以及「永恆的自由之火」之類的辭藻，卻沒打動多少聽眾，他們想要的是關於房租上漲和長途通勤的簡單具體答案。", "as": "His grandiloquent toast at the convivial dinner went on so long that the guests grew restless, and the food grew cold before he finally reached his bombastic conclusion.", "at": "他在歡樂晚宴上那篇浮誇的祝酒詞講得太久，賓客們都坐立不安，直到他終於講完誇大其詞的結語時，菜都已經涼了。"}, {"w": "lugubrious", "p": "adj.", "d": "looking or sounding sad and gloomy, often exaggeratedly.", "c": "悲哀的；陰鬱的", "s": "The orchestra opened the memorial concert with a slow, lugubrious piece for cellos and low brass, and many audience members quietly wiped away tears as the dark, mournful melody filled the hall.", "t": "管弦樂團以一首緩慢而哀戚的大提琴與低音銅管樂曲揭開追思音樂會的序幕，當那陰鬱悲傷的旋律充滿整個大廳時，許多觀眾默默拭去淚水。", "as": "The actor's lugubrious performance of the dying king moved the audience to tears, though some critics found his sonorous sighs overdone and his gestures almost grandiloquent.", "at": "這位演員以哀戚的方式詮釋垂死的國王，感動得觀眾落淚，不過有些評論家認為他渾厚的嘆息聲太過頭，手勢也幾近浮誇。"}, {"w": "infinitesimal", "p": "adj.", "d": "extremely small; too small to measure.", "c": "極微小的；無窮小的", "s": "Although the chance of being struck by a meteorite is infinitesimal, astronomers still track thousands of near-Earth objects, because even a very unlikely impact could have devastating consequences for life on our planet.", "t": "雖然被隕石擊中的機率極其微小，天文學家仍持續追蹤數千個近地天體，因為即使是極不可能發生的撞擊，也可能對地球上的生命造成毀滅性的後果。", "as": "The difference between the results of the two drug trials was infinitesimal, an impalpable variation that hardly warranted the company's opulent advertising campaign or its claims of a medical breakthrough.", "at": "兩項藥物試驗結果之間的差異微乎其微，這種難以察覺的變化根本不足以支持該公司那場奢華的廣告宣傳，更遑論宣稱這是醫學上的突破。"}, {"w": "goad", "p": "v.", "d": "to provoke or urge someone into action.", "c": "激勵；刺激", "s": "Angry fans tried to goad the visiting players into fighting by shouting insults and throwing plastic bottles onto the field, but the team's captain calmly reminded everyone to stay focused on winning the match.", "t": "憤怒的球迷大聲辱罵並把塑膠瓶丟進球場，企圖激怒客隊球員動手打架，但球隊隊長冷靜地提醒大家專心贏得比賽。", "as": "Bullies tried to goad him into a fight, but the boy maintained his equanimity, refusing to let their puerile insults provoke him into anything he would later regret.", "at": "惡霸們試圖激怒他打架，但這個男孩保持鎮定，拒絕讓他們幼稚的侮辱刺激他做出日後會後悔的事。"}, {"w": "malinger", "p": "v.", "d": "to pretend to be ill to avoid work or duty.", "c": "裝病；詐病逃避", "s": "During the long war, army doctors were instructed to watch for soldiers who might malinger by faking headaches or stomach pains in order to avoid being sent back to the dangerous front lines.", "t": "在漫長的戰爭期間，軍醫被要求留意可能裝病的士兵，這些士兵會假裝頭痛或胃痛，以避免被送回危險的前線。", "as": "The factory manager accused workers of trying to malinger, but a doctor later averred that their exhaustion was real, caused by heat so intense it could enervate anyone.", "at": "工廠經理指控工人想裝病偷懶，但一位醫師後來斷言他們的疲憊是真的，是由足以讓任何人虛脫的酷熱所造成。"}, {"w": "aver", "p": "v.", "d": "to state firmly and confidently that something is true.", "c": "斷言；堅稱", "s": "In her testimony before the committee, the scientist was careful to aver only what her data clearly supported, firmly stating that the chemical caused liver damage in rats but refusing to speculate about its effects on humans.", "t": "在委員會作證時，這位科學家謹慎地只斷言數據明確支持的內容：她堅定表示該化學物質會造成大鼠肝臟損傷，但拒絕推測它對人類的影響。", "as": "The diplomat would aver that his country's intentions were peaceful, yet skeptical reporters noted the circuitous, disingenuous way he answered questions about the troops gathering near the border.", "at": "那位外交官會堅稱他的國家意圖和平，但抱持懷疑的記者們注意到，每當被問及邊境附近集結的部隊時，他總以迂迴又不誠懇的方式作答。"}, {"w": "cacophony", "p": "n.", "d": "a harsh, unpleasant mixture of loud sounds.", "c": "刺耳的噪音；不和諧音", "s": "As the orchestra's musicians tuned their instruments before the concert, a brief cacophony of squeaking violins, honking horns, and rumbling drums filled the hall, until the conductor raised his baton and everyone fell silent.", "t": "音樂會開始前，管弦樂團的樂手們在調音，大廳裡短暫充斥著小提琴的吱嘎聲、號角的嘟嘟聲和鼓聲隆隆的刺耳噪音，直到指揮舉起指揮棒，全場才安靜下來。", "as": "The incessant cacophony of construction outside the library made it impossible to ruminate on anything, so the students moved to a quiet, capacious reading room upstairs.", "at": "圖書館外施工持續不斷的刺耳噪音讓人根本無法沉思任何事，於是學生們搬到樓上一間安靜又寬敞的閱覽室。"}, {"w": "refractory", "p": "adj.", "d": "stubbornly resistant to authority, control, or treatment.", "c": "倔強的；難治療的", "s": "Doctors were frustrated by the patient's refractory infection, which had resisted three different antibiotics over two months, so they finally sent samples to a research laboratory to identify the unusual bacteria responsible.", "t": "醫師們對病人頑固難治的感染感到挫折，這種感染在兩個月內對三種不同的抗生素都無效，因此他們最後將檢體送到研究實驗室，以找出造成感染的罕見細菌。", "as": "Even the most refractory students responded to the teacher's levity, and her gentle humor achieved what years of harsh strictures from the principal had never managed to accomplish.", "at": "就連最桀驁不馴的學生都會被這位老師的幽默打動，她溫和的風趣做到了校長多年來嚴厲的限制規定所未能達成的事。"}, {"w": "iconoclast", "p": "n.", "d": "a person who attacks cherished beliefs or traditional institutions.", "c": "打破傳統者；反傳統者", "s": "Known as an iconoclast in the art world, the young sculptor mocked famous museums, refused every prestigious award, and created works from garbage to challenge traditional ideas about what deserved to be called beautiful.", "t": "這位年輕雕塑家被視為藝術界的反傳統者，他嘲諷知名美術館、拒絕所有聲望卓著的獎項，並用垃圾創作作品，挑戰「什麼才配稱為美」的傳統觀念。", "as": "A brilliant iconoclast, the physicist proposed a heterodox paradigm that challenged nearly everything her colleagues believed, and several decades of careful experiments would eventually vindicate her.", "at": "這位才華洋溢、打破傳統的物理學家提出了一個非正統的典範，挑戰了同事們幾乎所有的信念，而數十年嚴謹的實驗最終證明了她是對的。"}, {"w": "enervate", "p": "v.", "d": "to weaken or drain someone of energy.", "c": "使衰弱；使無力", "s": "The scorching summer heat seemed to enervate the entire town; by early afternoon, even the most energetic children had stopped playing outside and lay quietly in the shade, too tired to move.", "t": "炙熱的夏季高溫似乎讓整個小鎮都虛脫無力；到了午後，就連最活潑的孩子都停止在戶外玩耍，安靜地躺在樹蔭下，累得動也不想動。", "as": "Weeks of lethargy began to enervate the once-energetic writer, and his novels, formerly sharp and inventive, became banal stories that even loyal readers found tedious.", "at": "數週的倦怠開始讓這位曾經精力充沛的作家日漸衰弱，他過去犀利又富創意的小說，變成了連忠實讀者都覺得乏味的平庸故事。"}, {"w": "levity", "p": "n.", "d": "humor or lack of seriousness, especially when inappropriate.", "c": "輕率；輕浮", "s": "Although the funeral was a solemn occasion, the grandson's gentle levity during his speech, recalling his grandmother's terrible jokes and burnt cookies, brought smiles to the faces of mourners who had been weeping all morning.", "t": "雖然喪禮是莊嚴肅穆的場合，孫子在致詞時溫和的幽默，回憶奶奶講的冷笑話和烤焦的餅乾，讓整個早上一直在哭泣的弔唁者臉上露出了笑容。", "as": "The president's levity at the press conference struck many as flippant, and editorial writers castigated him for joking about a crisis that had left thousands homeless.", "at": "總統在記者會上的輕率態度讓許多人覺得輕浮無禮，社論作者嚴厲批評他竟拿一場讓數千人無家可歸的危機開玩笑。"}, {"w": "equanimity", "p": "n.", "d": "mental calmness and composure, especially in difficult situations.", "c": "鎮定；沉著", "s": "The pilot's equanimity during the emergency landing impressed investigators; despite losing both engines over the river, she calmly communicated with air traffic control and guided the plane down without a single passenger being injured.", "t": "這位機長在緊急迫降時的沉著鎮定令調查人員印象深刻；儘管在河流上空兩具引擎都失去動力，她仍冷靜地與塔台聯繫，並引導飛機安全降落，沒有任何一名乘客受傷。", "as": "The veteran diplomat accepted the vicissitudes of his long career with remarkable equanimity, never letting the incessant criticism from political rivals disturb his calm or cloud his judgment.", "at": "這位資深外交官以非凡的平靜心態接受漫長職涯中的起起落落，從不讓政敵不斷的批評擾亂他的平靜或影響他的判斷。"}, {"w": "stricture", "p": "n.", "d": "a strict limit or rule; also, harsh criticism.", "c": "限制；苛責", "s": "Many independent bookstores struggled under the government's new stricture on imported publications, which required months of paperwork and expensive inspections before a single foreign novel could be placed on the shelves.", "t": "許多獨立書店在政府針對進口出版品的新限制下苦苦掙扎，這些規定要求在任何一本外國小說上架之前，都必須經過數月的文書作業和昂貴的檢查。", "as": "The board's strictures against heterodox research seemed odious to the young scientists in the laboratory, who felt such rigid rules would preclude any genuinely original discoveries in their field.", "at": "董事會針對非正統研究所設下的限制，在實驗室年輕科學家眼中顯得可憎，他們認為這些僵化的規定會阻礙他們領域中任何真正原創的發現。"}, {"w": "opulent", "p": "adj.", "d": "showing great wealth and luxury.", "c": "富麗堂皇的；奢華的", "s": "Tourists visiting the palace were dazzled by its opulent ballroom, where crystal chandeliers, gold-framed mirrors, and silk curtains reflected the enormous wealth of the royal family that had once ruled the empire.", "t": "參觀宮殿的遊客被其富麗堂皇的舞廳所震懾，水晶吊燈、金框鏡子和絲綢窗簾，展現出曾經統治帝國的王室所擁有的龐大財富。", "as": "The opulent mansion, with its capacious halls and marble staircases, stood in stark contrast to the squalid huts of the workers whose labor had paid for it.", "at": "那座富麗堂皇的宅邸擁有寬敞的大廳和大理石階梯，與那些以勞力為它付出代價的工人們骯髒破舊的小屋形成強烈對比。"}, {"w": "disparage", "p": "v.", "d": "to speak about someone or something as having little value.", "c": "貶低；輕視", "s": "Some critics once tended to disparage comic books as cheap entertainment for children, but today many universities offer courses on graphic novels, recognizing their complex storytelling and powerful artistic achievements.", "t": "一些評論家過去常常貶低漫畫只是給孩子看的廉價娛樂，但如今許多大學都開設圖像小說的課程，肯定其複雜的敘事和強大的藝術成就。", "as": "Rather than disparage his rival's education proposal, the candidate first praised its laudable goals before calmly explaining why its budget numbers were simply not tenable.", "at": "這位候選人沒有貶低對手的教育提案，而是先稱讚其值得嘉許的目標，然後冷靜地解釋為何其預算數字根本站不住腳。"}, {"w": "discursive", "p": "adj.", "d": "moving from topic to topic without clear organization; digressive.", "c": "離題的；漫無邊際的", "s": "The professor's lectures were so discursive that students often lost track of the main topic; a single class might wander from Roman aqueducts to modern plumbing, jazz music, and his childhood summers in Italy.", "t": "這位教授的課講得天馬行空、漫無邊際，學生常常跟不上主題；一堂課可能從羅馬水道橋一路扯到現代水管工程、爵士樂，再到他童年在義大利度過的夏天。", "as": "The novelist's discursive style frustrated readers who wanted a fast plot, but admirers praised her tangential reflections as the most edifying parts of the book.", "at": "這位小說家漫談式的風格讓想看快節奏情節的讀者感到挫折，但支持者稱讚她那些離題的思索是全書最具啟發性的部分。"}]}, {"unit": 16, "level": 4, "cards": [{"w": "redress", "p": "v.", "d": "To set right or remedy a wrong or injustice.", "c": "糾正；補救（錯誤或不公）", "s": "After an internal audit revealed that women in the research department had been paid significantly less than their male colleagues, the university pledged to redress the imbalance by raising salaries and publishing an annual pay-equity report.", "t": "內部稽核發現研究部門的女性薪資明顯低於男性同事後，大學承諾透過調薪並發布年度薪資公平報告來糾正這種不平衡。", "as": "The historian argued that the government's belated apology could not fully redress decades of injustice, and she dismissed officials' claims of progress as mere platitudes laced with sophistry.", "at": "這位歷史學家認為，政府遲來的道歉無法完全彌補數十年的不公，並將官員們聲稱的進展斥為摻雜詭辯的陳腔濫調。"}, {"w": "anomalous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Deviating from what is normal, standard, or expected.", "c": "異常的；反常的", "s": "The astronomers initially assumed that the strange spike in their data was caused by faulty equipment, but when the same anomalous signal appeared in observations from three separate telescopes, they began to suspect a genuine cosmic event.", "t": "天文學家起初以為數據中奇怪的峰值是設備故障造成的，但當三座不同望遠鏡的觀測中都出現同樣的異常訊號時，他們開始懷疑這是真實的宇宙事件。", "as": "The geologist's anomalous readings, initially dismissed by colleagues as a trivial foible of her instruments, were later corroborated by satellite data that revealed a previously unknown fault line.", "at": "這位地質學家的異常讀數起初被同事視為儀器的小毛病而不予理會，後來卻獲得衛星資料證實，揭露了一條先前未知的斷層。"}, {"w": "obsequious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Too eager to please or obey; excessively flattering.", "c": "諂媚的；奉承的", "s": "Critics of the royal court noted that the advisers who rose fastest were not the most competent but the most obsequious, constantly praising the king's every decision and eagerly agreeing with him even when his policies were clearly failing.", "t": "批評王室宮廷的人指出，晉升最快的顧問並非最有能力的人，而是最諂媚的人——他們不斷讚美國王的每項決定，即使國王的政策明顯失敗，也急切地附和他。", "as": "The new intern's obsequious manner, which included laughing loudly at every one of the manager's jokes, struck his more urbane colleagues as transparent and ingratiating rather than genuinely friendly.", "at": "這位新實習生的諂媚舉止——包括對經理的每個笑話都捧場大笑——在較為老練世故的同事看來，顯得明顯是在討好，而非真心友善。"}, {"w": "didactic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Intended to teach, often in a moralizing way.", "c": "說教的；教誨的", "s": "Although the novel was praised for its vivid characters, several reviewers found its tone overly didactic, complaining that the author interrupted the story every few pages to lecture readers about honesty, hard work, and the dangers of greed.", "t": "雖然這部小說因人物鮮活而受到讚揚，但幾位書評家認為其語氣過於說教，抱怨作者每隔幾頁就打斷故事，向讀者講述誠實、勤奮與貪婪之害的道理。", "as": "Medieval fables were often openly didactic, using a talking fox or a foolish crow to censure greed and vanity while offering readers a laconic moral at the very end.", "at": "中世紀寓言往往公然帶有說教意味，藉由會說話的狐狸或愚蠢的烏鴉來譴責貪婪與虛榮，並在結尾給讀者一句簡潔的寓意。"}, {"w": "truncate", "p": "v.", "d": "To shorten something by cutting off part of it.", "c": "截短；刪節", "s": "Because the conference was running nearly an hour behind schedule, the organizers asked the final speaker to truncate her presentation, so she skipped the historical background and went directly to her most important findings about coral reef recovery.", "t": "由於研討會進度落後將近一小時，主辦單位請最後一位講者縮短簡報，於是她略過歷史背景，直接說明她關於珊瑚礁復育最重要的研究發現。", "as": "Facing a sudden dearth of funding, the museum was forced to truncate its exhibition schedule, a decision that critics called short-sighted but administrators defended as prudent.", "at": "面臨資金突然短缺，博物館被迫縮減展覽檔期；批評者稱此決定目光短淺，但館方行政人員則辯稱這是審慎之舉。"}, {"w": "abstemious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Moderate and restrained, especially in eating and drinking.", "c": "有節制的；（飲食）節制的", "s": "Researchers studying communities with unusually long life spans found that most residents were remarkably abstemious, eating small portions of simple vegetables and grains, rarely drinking alcohol, and stopping meals well before they felt completely full.", "t": "研究異常長壽社群的學者發現，大多數居民都非常節制，只吃少量簡單的蔬菜和穀物，很少飲酒，並在完全吃飽之前就停止進食。", "as": "Unlike his gluttonous and opulent contemporaries, the philosopher lived an abstemious life, viewing excess as a foible that clouded judgment and fostered an insatiable appetite for luxury.", "at": "不同於那些貪食又奢華的同時代人，這位哲學家過著節制的生活，認為過度享受是一種會蒙蔽判斷力、助長對奢侈品貪得無厭之欲望的缺點。"}, {"w": "ethereal", "p": "adj.", "d": "Extremely delicate and light, as if heavenly.", "c": "空靈的；超凡脫俗的", "s": "Visitors to the cathedral often describe the choir's singing as ethereal; the high, soft voices seem to float weightlessly beneath the vaulted ceiling, creating an atmosphere so delicate that it feels almost like something from another world.", "t": "造訪這座大教堂的遊客常形容唱詩班的歌聲空靈脫俗；高亢而柔和的嗓音彷彿毫無重量地飄浮在拱頂之下，營造出一種細膩得近乎來自另一個世界的氛圍。", "as": "Critics agreed that the composer's ethereal melodies, at once ephemeral and haunting, made the bombastic marching music of her rivals seem crude and banal by comparison.", "at": "評論家一致認為，這位作曲家空靈的旋律既轉瞬即逝又縈繞心頭，相較之下，她對手那些浮誇的進行曲顯得粗糙又平庸。"}, {"w": "bombastic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Using pompous, inflated language with little real meaning.", "c": "浮誇的；誇大其詞的", "s": "The candidate's speech was full of grand phrases about 'a glorious new dawn' and 'the eternal destiny of our people,' but voters found it bombastic and empty, noting that he never explained a single concrete policy.", "t": "這位候選人的演講充滿「光榮的新黎明」和「我們人民永恆的命運」之類的華麗詞句，但選民認為它浮誇又空洞，並指出他從未說明任何一項具體政策。", "as": "Beneath the senator's bombastic rhetoric lay a surprisingly tenuous argument, and during the televised debate a journalist's trenchant questions quickly exposed how little evidence supported his claims.", "at": "在這位參議員浮誇的言辭之下，是一個出奇薄弱的論點；在電視辯論中，一位記者犀利的提問很快就揭露了他的主張幾乎毫無證據支持。"}, {"w": "senescent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Growing old; showing the effects of aging.", "c": "衰老的；老化的", "s": "Biologists have discovered that senescent cells, which have stopped dividing but refuse to die, can release chemicals that damage nearby healthy tissue, and removing them from older mice appears to extend the animals' healthy lifespan.", "t": "生物學家發現，衰老細胞雖已停止分裂卻不肯死亡，會釋放損害附近健康組織的化學物質；而從年老小鼠體內移除這些細胞，似乎能延長牠們的健康壽命。", "as": "The once-prolific author, now senescent and increasingly lethargic, still received a steady stream of visitors eager to venerate the writer whose novels had shaped their youth.", "at": "這位曾經多產的作家如今年邁衰老、日益倦怠，卻仍有絡繹不絕的訪客前來，渴望向這位以小說形塑他們青春的作家致敬。"}, {"w": "pernicious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Causing great harm, often gradually or in a hidden way.", "c": "有害的；惡性的", "s": "Public-health experts warn that misinformation about vaccines is especially pernicious because it spreads quietly through social media, slowly eroding public trust and eventually leading to outbreaks of diseases that had nearly disappeared.", "t": "公共衛生專家警告，有關疫苗的錯誤資訊特別有害，因為它在社群媒體上悄悄傳播，逐漸侵蝕大眾信任，最終導致幾近絕跡的疾病再度爆發。", "as": "The report concluded that nepotism had a pernicious effect on the agency, quietly rewarding mediocre insiders while driving away its most astute and judicious employees.", "at": "報告結論指出，任人唯親對該機構造成了有害的影響：它悄悄獎勵平庸的自己人，同時逼走了最精明、最有判斷力的員工。"}, {"w": "catholic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Broad and wide-ranging in tastes or interests; universal.", "c": "廣泛的；包羅萬象的", "s": "The bookstore owner has remarkably catholic taste in literature; her shelves hold everything from ancient Greek poetry and Japanese manga to modern science fiction, cookbooks, and obscure academic studies of medieval farming techniques.", "t": "這位書店老闆的文學品味極為廣泛；她的書架上從古希臘詩歌、日本漫畫到現代科幻小說、食譜，以及冷門的中世紀農耕技術學術研究，應有盡有。", "as": "The professor's catholic interests made her a prolific writer, but critics complained that her essays were often discursive, wandering from topic to topic without a clear argument.", "at": "這位教授興趣廣泛，使她成為多產的作家，但批評者抱怨她的文章常常離題散漫，從一個主題遊走到另一個主題，缺乏明確的論點。"}, {"w": "objurgation", "p": "n.", "d": "A harsh scolding or severe rebuke.", "c": "嚴厲斥責；痛罵", "s": "When the young officer disobeyed orders and nearly caused a disaster during the training exercise, the general delivered a fierce objurgation in front of the entire unit, leaving no doubt about how seriously he viewed the mistake.", "t": "這名年輕軍官在訓練演習中違抗命令、差點釀成災難後，將軍當著全隊的面嚴厲斥責他，讓人毫不懷疑他對這次錯誤有多麼重視。", "as": "The editor's objurgation, though harsh, was not gratuitous; she simply wanted to admonish the careless young reporter whose incessant errors had repeatedly damaged the newspaper's reputation.", "at": "總編輯的嚴厲斥責雖然刻薄，卻並非無端之舉；她只是想告誡那位粗心的年輕記者，因為他接連不斷的錯誤已一再損害報社的聲譽。"}, {"w": "effusive", "p": "adj.", "d": "Expressing feelings in an unrestrained, gushing way.", "c": "熱情洋溢的；感情奔放的", "s": "Although the scientist was usually reserved, she became unusually effusive at the award ceremony, hugging her colleagues, thanking dozens of people by name, and repeatedly declaring that this was the happiest day of her life.", "t": "雖然這位科學家平時很拘謹，但她在頒獎典禮上卻異常熱情洋溢，擁抱同事、一一點名感謝數十人，並一再宣稱這是她人生中最快樂的一天。", "as": "His effusive praise for the mediocre film seemed so obsequious that readers began to suspect a hidden complicity between the critic and the Hollywood studio.", "at": "他對這部平庸電影的熱烈讚美顯得如此諂媚，讓讀者開始懷疑這位影評人與好萊塢片廠之間暗中勾結。"}, {"w": "umbrage", "p": "n.", "d": "Offense or resentment, especially at a perceived insult.", "c": "不快；（受冒犯而）生氣", "s": "When the visiting scholar suggested that the local museum's ancient pottery collection was 'mostly fakes,' the curators took umbrage at the remark and publicly demanded that he provide evidence for such an insulting accusation.", "t": "當這位客座學者暗示當地博物館的古代陶器收藏「大多是贗品」時，策展人們對這番話感到被冒犯，並公開要求他為如此侮辱人的指控提出證據。", "as": "The veteran diplomat took umbrage at the young reporter's question, but his irascible reply only seemed to corroborate rumors that the negotiations had reached an embarrassing impasse.", "at": "這位資深外交官對年輕記者的提問感到不悅，但他暴躁的回應似乎只是證實了談判已陷入尷尬僵局的傳言。"}, {"w": "vicissitude", "p": "n.", "d": "An unexpected change of circumstances, often for the worse.", "c": "變遷；（人生的）起伏變化", "s": "The family-owned bakery has survived more than a century of wars, economic depressions, and changing tastes; its owners say that the secret to enduring every vicissitude of fortune is to adapt quickly while never abandoning the original recipes.", "t": "這家家族經營的麵包店歷經一個多世紀的戰爭、經濟蕭條與口味變遷而屹立不搖；店主表示，度過每一次命運起伏的秘訣，是在迅速應變的同時，絕不捨棄原始配方。", "as": "Through twenty years of the vicissitudes of exile and poverty, the poet maintained a stoic equanimity, patiently transmuting her personal suffering into verses of remarkable beauty and lasting power.", "at": "在二十年流亡與貧困的起伏變化中，這位詩人始終保持堅忍沉著，耐心地將個人苦難轉化為美麗非凡、力量恆久的詩句。"}, {"w": "contentious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Causing or likely to cause strong disagreement.", "c": "有爭議的；好爭論的", "s": "Plans to build a highway through the protected wetland proved highly contentious; environmental groups organized protests, local farmers filed lawsuits, and city council meetings on the issue frequently ended in shouting matches between residents.", "t": "在受保護濕地上興建高速公路的計畫引發極大爭議；環保團體發起抗議，當地農民提起訴訟，而市議會針對此議題召開的會議也經常以居民之間的激烈爭吵收場。", "as": "During the contentious debate over the new curriculum, several board members grew openly pugnacious, more eager to disparage their opponents' motives than to address the substance of the proposal.", "at": "在關於新課綱的爭議性辯論中，幾位委員變得公然好鬥，熱衷於貶低對手的動機，而非討論提案的實質內容。"}, {"w": "obeisance", "p": "n.", "d": "A gesture of deep respect, such as a bow.", "c": "敬禮；鞠躬致敬", "s": "In the imperial court of ancient China, officials approaching the emperor were required to perform an elaborate obeisance, kneeling and touching their foreheads to the floor several times to show their complete respect and submission.", "t": "在中國古代的皇宮中，覲見皇帝的官員必須行繁複的大禮，跪下並多次以額觸地，以表示完全的尊敬與臣服。", "as": "The courtiers made deep obeisance to the young king each morning, but their sycophantic gestures merely concealed a clandestine plot to seize the throne before winter.", "at": "朝臣們每天早晨都向年輕的國王深深行禮，但他們諂媚的舉動不過是在掩飾一場要在冬天之前奪取王位的秘密陰謀。"}, {"w": "assiduous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Showing great care, effort, and persistence.", "c": "勤勉的；孜孜不倦的", "s": "Thanks to her assiduous research, which included reading thousands of handwritten letters and spending six summers in dusty regional archives, the historian was finally able to reconstruct the daily lives of nineteenth-century factory workers.", "t": "多虧她孜孜不倦的研究——包括閱讀數千封手寫信件，以及花了六個夏天待在布滿灰塵的地方檔案館——這位歷史學家終於得以重建十九世紀工廠工人的日常生活。", "as": "Despite her assiduous efforts to expunge every error from the manuscript, the fastidious editor still found a few typos in the published edition, a discovery she found deeply mortifying.", "at": "儘管她孜孜不倦地努力刪除手稿中的每個錯誤，這位一絲不苟的編輯仍在出版版本中發現了幾個錯字，令她深感懊惱。"}, {"w": "duplicity", "p": "n.", "d": "Deliberate deceitfulness; saying one thing but doing another.", "c": "欺騙；表裡不一", "s": "Investigators uncovered the accountant's duplicity only after discovering that, while he had been assuring company directors that their finances were perfectly healthy, he had secretly been transferring millions of dollars into his own private account.", "t": "調查人員直到發現這名會計一邊向公司董事保證財務狀況完全健全、一邊暗中將數百萬美元轉入自己的私人帳戶後，才揭穿他的欺騙行徑。", "as": "The spy's duplicity was so skillful that even his closest allies were beguiled, and only years later did historians unravel the subterfuge behind his apparent loyalty.", "at": "這名間諜的欺騙手法高明到連最親近的盟友都被蒙騙，直到多年後，歷史學家才揭開他表面忠誠背後的詭計。"}, {"w": "insouciant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Casually unconcerned; carefree and indifferent.", "c": "漫不經心的；無憂無慮的", "s": "While his teammates nervously reviewed their notes before the national debate final, Marcus remained completely insouciant, chatting cheerfully with the audience and joking about the weather as though the outcome did not matter to him at all.", "t": "當隊友們在全國辯論決賽前緊張地複習筆記時，馬可斯卻完全漫不經心，愉快地和觀眾聊天、拿天氣開玩笑，彷彿比賽結果對他一點也不重要。", "as": "Her insouciant attitude toward deadlines, which colleagues had once found charmingly droll, eventually began to nettle the project manager, who considered such levity deeply unprofessional.", "at": "她對截止期限漫不經心的態度，同事們起初覺得頗為逗趣，最終卻開始惹惱專案經理，他認為這種輕率的態度極不專業。"}]}, {"unit": 17, "level": 4, "cards": [{"w": "myrmidon", "p": "n.", "d": "A loyal follower who carries out orders without question.", "c": "唯命是從的手下；爪牙", "s": "The dictator rarely appeared in public himself; instead, he relied on a trusted myrmidon to silence journalists, arrest critics, and enforce his harsh decrees, knowing that this follower would obey any command without asking why.", "t": "這位獨裁者很少親自公開露面，而是倚賴一名親信手下去讓記者噤聲、逮捕批評者並執行他的嚴苛法令，因為他知道這名追隨者會不問緣由地服從任何命令。", "as": "The tyrant's myrmidons were notoriously unscrupulous, carrying out every brutal order with complete complicity and never once daring to remonstrate with their master, even when innocent villagers were harmed.", "at": "這名暴君的爪牙出了名地肆無忌憚，以完全共謀的姿態執行每一道殘酷的命令，即使無辜村民受到傷害，也從不敢向主子提出任何抗議。"}, {"w": "nascent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Just beginning to exist or develop.", "c": "新生的；初期的", "s": "In the early 1980s, the personal computer industry was still nascent; only a handful of small companies were building home machines, and few people imagined that these simple devices would one day transform nearly every aspect of daily life.", "t": "在1980年代初期，個人電腦產業仍處於萌芽階段；只有少數幾家小公司在製造家用電腦，很少有人想像得到，這些簡單的裝置有一天會改變日常生活的幾乎每個層面。", "as": "The nascent democracy faced a myriad of challenges, from intractable corruption to the lingering animosity between rival ethnic groups who had fought each other for several decades.", "at": "這個新生的民主國家面臨無數挑戰，從難以根除的貪腐，到彼此交戰數十年的敵對族群之間揮之不去的敵意。"}, {"w": "accede", "p": "v.", "d": "To agree to a demand or request, often reluctantly.", "c": "同意；應允", "s": "After the students collected more than two thousand signatures and staged a peaceful sit-in outside the main office, the school board finally decided to accede to their request for healthier cafeteria lunches and longer library hours.", "t": "在學生們蒐集了兩千多份連署並在行政大樓外和平靜坐後，學校董事會終於決定同意他們提出的更健康的餐廳午餐與延長圖書館開放時間的要求。", "as": "Although the union eventually acceded to the company's terms, its leaders made it clear that their reluctant acquiescence should not be construed as approval of the new policy.", "at": "雖然工會最終同意了公司的條件，但工會領袖明確表示，他們勉強的默許不應被解讀為認可這項新政策。"}, {"w": "magnanimous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Generous and forgiving, especially toward a rival or enemy.", "c": "寬宏大量的；大度的", "s": "After winning the bitter election, the new mayor was surprisingly magnanimous; rather than punishing her opponents, she praised their ideas in her victory speech and invited several of them to serve on her advisory committee.", "t": "在贏得這場激烈的選舉後，新市長出人意料地寬宏大量；她並未懲罰對手，反而在勝選演說中讚揚他們的理念，並邀請其中幾位加入她的諮詢委員會。", "as": "In a magnanimous gesture, the victorious general chose to exonerate the defeated soldiers rather than seek vindictive retribution for their long and bloody resistance in the mountains.", "at": "這位獲勝的將軍以寬宏大量的姿態，選擇赦免戰敗的士兵，而非為他們在山區長期的血腥抵抗進行報復性的懲罰。"}, {"w": "nonage", "p": "n.", "d": "The period of legal minority; a period of immaturity.", "c": "未成年期；幼稚期", "s": "Because the young king was only nine years old when his father died, his uncle governed the kingdom as regent during the boy's nonage, holding power until the prince was legally old enough to rule on his own.", "t": "由於這位年輕國王在父親去世時年僅九歲，他的叔父在他未成年期間以攝政身分治理王國，直到王子達到可以親政的法定年齡為止。", "as": "During the nonage of the film industry, critics dismissed movies as a puerile novelty, never imagining that this callow art form would someday produce works of lasting genius.", "at": "在電影產業的幼稚期，評論家將電影斥為幼稚的新奇玩意，從未想到這種青澀的藝術形式有一天會產生具有恆久價值的天才之作。"}, {"w": "invective", "p": "n.", "d": "Harsh, abusive language used to attack someone.", "c": "痛罵；謾罵", "s": "Online forums about politics are often filled with invective, as users hurl insults, curses, and personal attacks at one another instead of calmly discussing the actual arguments behind each side's position.", "t": "政治相關的網路論壇常常充斥著謾罵，使用者彼此丟出侮辱、咒罵和人身攻擊，而不是冷靜地討論各方立場背後的實際論點。", "as": "The pamphlet's vitriolic invective against the government, filled with scurrilous accusations, failed to persuade moderate readers and only served to vitiate the credibility of the entire reform movement.", "at": "這本小冊子對政府尖酸刻薄的謾罵，充斥著惡毒的指控，不但未能說服溫和的讀者，反而損害了整個改革運動的可信度。"}, {"w": "machination", "p": "n.", "d": "A secret, crafty plot or scheme, usually to do harm.", "c": "陰謀；詭計", "s": "Shakespeare's Othello is destroyed not by any enemy army but by the cunning machination of his own officer Iago, who secretly plants false evidence and lies to convince the general that his wife has betrayed him.", "t": "莎士比亞筆下的奧賽羅並非毀於敵軍之手，而是毀於他自己的部下伊阿古的狡猾陰謀；伊阿古暗中栽贓假證據並撒謊，讓將軍相信妻子背叛了他。", "as": "Historians have long debated the clandestine machinations of the royal court, where ambitious nobles used every subterfuge imaginable to win the favor of the aging king.", "at": "歷史學家長久以來爭論著王室宮廷裡的秘密陰謀；在那裡，野心勃勃的貴族使出各種想像得到的詭計，以博取年邁國王的青睞。"}, {"w": "docile", "p": "adj.", "d": "Quiet, obedient, and easy to control or teach.", "c": "溫順的；馴服的", "s": "Scientists believe that dogs became docile over thousands of years because early humans chose to keep and breed only the gentlest, most obedient wolves, gradually producing animals that were easy to train and control.", "t": "科學家認為，狗在數千年間變得溫順，是因為早期人類只選擇飼養並繁殖最溫和、最聽話的狼，逐漸培育出容易訓練和控制的動物。", "as": "Some critics argue that the education system rewards docile students who memorize facts, while it subtly ostracizes the iconoclasts whose original questions challenge established ideas.", "at": "有些批評者認為，教育體制獎勵死背事實的溫順學生，卻暗中排擠那些以原創問題挑戰既定觀念的叛逆者。"}, {"w": "redoubtable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Formidable and worthy of respect or fear.", "c": "令人敬畏的；可怕的", "s": "The young chess player knew she faced a redoubtable opponent in the final: the reigning champion had not lost a single tournament game in three years and was famous for destroying even the strongest challengers.", "t": "這位年輕的棋手知道她在決賽中面對的是一位令人敬畏的對手：這位衛冕冠軍三年來在比賽中未曾輸過一局，並以擊潰最強挑戰者而聞名。", "as": "The redoubtable senator, known for her trenchant questions and impeccable preparation, could reduce even the most glib witness to stammering silence during a congressional hearing.", "at": "這位令人敬畏的參議員以犀利的提問和無懈可擊的準備而聞名，在國會聽證會上，即使是最油嘴滑舌的證人也會被她問得結結巴巴、啞口無言。"}, {"w": "prognosticate", "p": "v.", "d": "To predict or forecast a future event.", "c": "預言；預測", "s": "Economists find it extremely difficult to prognosticate exactly when the next recession will begin, because unexpected events such as natural disasters, wars, and sudden changes in consumer confidence can quickly upset even the most careful forecasts.", "t": "經濟學家發現，要準確預測下一次經濟衰退何時開始極為困難，因為天災、戰爭和消費者信心驟變等突發事件，即使是最謹慎的預測也可能很快被推翻。", "as": "Pundits who prognosticate about elections often rely on conjecture rather than data, yet they deliver their forecasts with such categorical confidence that viewers rarely question them.", "at": "那些預測選舉結果的名嘴往往依賴臆測而非數據，卻以斬釘截鐵的自信發表預測，使觀眾很少質疑他們。"}, {"w": "engender", "p": "v.", "d": "To cause or give rise to a feeling or situation.", "c": "引起；產生", "s": "Teachers have found that giving students real choices about their research topics tends to engender genuine curiosity and enthusiasm, whereas assigning the same topic to everyone often produces boredom and minimal effort.", "t": "老師們發現，讓學生真正自行選擇研究主題，往往能激發真正的好奇心與熱忱；反之，讓每個人做同樣的主題，常常只會帶來無聊和敷衍了事。", "as": "The mayor's decision to rescind the popular housing program engendered widespread resentment, and a vocal group of dissidents soon organized noisy weekly protests outside City Hall.", "at": "市長廢除這項深受歡迎的住宅計畫的決定引發了廣泛不滿，一群直言不諱的異議人士很快便在市政府外組織了每週一次的喧鬧抗議活動。"}, {"w": "fetid", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having a strong, extremely unpleasant smell.", "c": "惡臭的；腐臭的", "s": "When the sanitation workers went on strike for three weeks during the summer heat wave, garbage piled up on every corner, and the fetid air became so unbearable that many residents refused to open their windows.", "t": "清潔隊員在夏季熱浪期間罷工三週，垃圾堆滿了每個街角，空氣惡臭難當，許多居民都不肯打開窗戶。", "as": "Nineteenth-century reformers described the squalid tenements of London, where entire families lived in fetid, airless rooms, and they repeatedly urged Parliament to ameliorate such dangerous conditions.", "at": "十九世紀的改革者描述倫敦骯髒的廉價公寓，整個家庭住在惡臭、不通風的房間裡，他們一再敦促國會改善這種危險的狀況。"}, {"w": "pedantic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Overly concerned with minor details or rules; showing off learning.", "c": "賣弄學問的；拘泥細節的", "s": "Students complained that the lecturer was pedantic, interrupting class discussions to correct tiny grammar errors and showing off his knowledge of obscure Latin terms instead of helping them understand the main ideas.", "t": "學生們抱怨這位講師賣弄學問又吹毛求疵，常打斷課堂討論去糾正微小的文法錯誤，並炫耀他對冷僻拉丁術語的知識，而不是幫助他們理解主要概念。", "as": "Her pedantic insistence on perfect citations seemed excessive to her classmates, yet her erudite analysis of the poem's esoteric symbols ultimately impressed even the most skeptical professor.", "at": "她對完美引用格式的執著在同學眼中似乎過頭了，但她對這首詩深奧象徵所做的博學分析，最終連最持懷疑態度的教授也為之折服。"}, {"w": "capitulate", "p": "v.", "d": "To surrender or give in, especially after resisting.", "c": "投降；屈服", "s": "After surrounding the fortress and cutting off its food supply for six months, the invading army finally forced the starving defenders to capitulate, and the gates were opened without another shot being fired.", "t": "入侵的軍隊包圍要塞並切斷糧食供應六個月後，終於迫使飢餓的守軍投降，城門在未再開一槍的情況下打開了。", "as": "Although the obstinate committee members initially refused to compromise, they finally capitulated when the scientific evidence became so unequivocal that any further resistance seemed futile.", "at": "雖然這些固執的委員起初拒絕妥協，但當科學證據明確到任何進一步的抵抗都顯得徒勞時，他們終於讓步了。"}, {"w": "inchoate", "p": "adj.", "d": "Just begun and not yet fully formed or developed.", "c": "初期的；未成形的", "s": "The architect's first sketches were still inchoate, consisting of a few rough lines and scribbled notes, but over the following months these vague ideas developed into detailed plans for an award-winning public library.", "t": "這位建築師最初的草圖仍未成形，只有幾條粗略的線條和潦草的筆記，但在接下來的幾個月裡，這些模糊的想法發展成一座獲獎公共圖書館的詳細設計圖。", "as": "The young writer's inchoate ideas about justice slowly coalesced into a lucid philosophy, and her final essay was praised as both trenchant and remarkably mature.", "at": "這位年輕作家對正義的初步想法逐漸凝聚成清晰的哲學，她的最後一篇文章被讚譽為既犀利又出奇成熟。"}, {"w": "exponent", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who supports, promotes, or explains an idea.", "c": "倡導者；擁護者", "s": "Rachel Carson, whose book Silent Spring warned the world about the dangers of pesticides, became the most famous exponent of the modern environmental movement, inspiring millions of readers to support stricter protections for nature.", "t": "瑞秋．卡森在其著作《寂靜的春天》中警告世人農藥的危害，她成為現代環保運動最著名的倡導者，激勵數百萬讀者支持更嚴格的自然保護措施。", "as": "A leading exponent of minimalist design, the architect eschewed ornate decoration, insisting that simple, austere spaces could convey far more emotion than any ostentatious facade.", "at": "身為極簡設計的主要倡導者，這位建築師避免華麗的裝飾，堅稱簡單樸素的空間遠比任何浮誇的外觀更能傳達情感。"}, {"w": "mendacious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Not telling the truth; habitually lying.", "c": "說謊的；虛假的", "s": "The investigation revealed that the company's advertisements were deliberately mendacious: its so-called miracle supplement had never been tested in any clinical trial, and the glowing customer reviews had been written by paid employees.", "t": "調查顯示，這家公司的廣告是蓄意虛假的：其所謂的神奇保健食品從未經過任何臨床試驗，而那些讚不絕口的顧客評論都是由受雇員工撰寫的。", "as": "The mendacious witness tried to obfuscate the facts with an elaborate story, but the prosecutor's meticulous questions eventually forced him to recant and incriminate his former partner.", "at": "那名說謊的證人企圖用精心編造的故事混淆事實，但檢察官縝密的提問最終迫使他翻供，並指控了他昔日的同夥。"}, {"w": "strident", "p": "adj.", "d": "Loud, harsh, and grating; forceful in a harsh way.", "c": "刺耳的；強硬的", "s": "The new fire alarm was so strident that students covered their ears during the drill, and several teachers asked the school to replace it with a system that was loud enough to be effective but less painfully harsh.", "t": "新的火災警報聲非常刺耳，學生在演習時都摀住了耳朵，幾位老師還要求學校換一套音量足以發揮作用、但不那麼刺耳難受的系統。", "as": "The activist's strident tirades against the factory alienated potential allies, many of whom agreed with her environmental goals but found her pugnacious tone counterproductive and exhausting.", "at": "這位社運人士對工廠尖銳刺耳的長篇抨擊疏遠了潛在的盟友，其中許多人認同她的環保目標，卻覺得她好鬥的語氣適得其反又令人疲憊。"}, {"w": "oligarchy", "p": "n.", "d": "Government by a small group of powerful people.", "c": "寡頭政治；寡頭統治集團", "s": "Although the country officially held elections every four years, political scientists described it as an oligarchy, since real power remained in the hands of about a dozen wealthy families who controlled the banks, newspapers, and military.", "t": "雖然這個國家官方上每四年舉行一次選舉，政治學家卻稱它為寡頭政治，因為實權始終掌握在約十幾個控制銀行、報紙和軍隊的富豪家族手中。", "as": "Under the oligarchy, nepotism flourished as powerful families placed incompetent relatives in lucrative government posts, while ordinary citizens across the country remained indigent and almost entirely voiceless.", "at": "在寡頭統治下，任人唯親的風氣盛行，權勢家族將無能的親屬安插在油水豐厚的政府職位上，而全國的普通百姓依舊貧困，幾乎完全沒有發聲管道。"}, {"w": "refulgent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Shining very brightly; radiant with light.", "c": "燦爛的；光輝的", "s": "As the sun rose over the desert, the ancient temple's gold-covered dome became refulgent, reflecting the morning light so brilliantly that pilgrims approaching from miles away could see it shining on the horizon.", "t": "當太陽在沙漠上升起時，古老神廟鍍金的圓頂變得燦爛奪目，將晨光反射得如此耀眼，使得從數英里外前來的朝聖者都能看見它在地平線上閃耀。", "as": "The refulgent stained-glass windows of the cathedral drew a myriad of visitors, who stood in pensive silence as colored light flooded the ancient stone floor.", "at": "大教堂燦爛奪目的彩繪玻璃窗吸引了無數遊客，他們沉思般地靜立著，看著彩色光芒灑滿古老的石頭地板。"}]}, {"unit": 18, "level": 4, "cards": [{"w": "nepotism", "p": "n.", "d": "Favoritism shown to relatives, especially in giving jobs.", "c": "裙帶關係；任人唯親", "s": "Employees grew frustrated when the CEO appointed his inexperienced nephew as head of marketing over several highly qualified candidates, and many openly accused the company of nepotism rather than promotion based on merit.", "t": "執行長任命他毫無經驗的姪子擔任行銷主管，而非幾位資歷優秀的候選人，員工們對此感到不滿，許多人公開指責公司任人唯親，而非依能力升遷。", "as": "Critics argued that the mayor's blatant nepotism had created an oligarchy of cousins and in-laws, and they demanded an independent inquiry to restore public trust in local government.", "at": "批評者認為，市長明目張膽的任人唯親已造就了一個由表親和姻親組成的寡頭集團，他們要求展開獨立調查，以恢復民眾對地方政府的信任。"}, {"w": "ribald", "p": "adj.", "d": "Humorous in a coarse, vulgar, or irreverent way.", "c": "粗俗幽默的；下流的", "s": "Literature professors note that Chaucer's Canterbury Tales mixes deeply religious stories with ribald comic episodes full of crude jokes, which shocked some Victorian editors who removed those passages from school editions of the book.", "t": "文學教授指出，喬叟的《坎特伯里故事集》將虔誠的宗教故事與充滿粗俗笑話的滑稽段落交織在一起，這讓一些維多利亞時代的編輯大為震驚，因而將那些段落從學校版本中刪除。", "as": "The scholar argued that the play's ribald humor was not gratuitous but a deliberate way to satirize the sanctimonious officials who had tried to censor popular theater.", "at": "這位學者認為，這齣劇粗俗的幽默並非多餘，而是刻意用來諷刺那些曾試圖審查大眾戲劇、故作清高的官員。"}, {"w": "avuncular", "p": "adj.", "d": "Kind and friendly toward younger people, like an uncle.", "c": "像叔伯般慈祥的；和藹的", "s": "Students loved the retired physics teacher who volunteered in the school library; with his avuncular manner, gentle jokes, and endless patience, he made nervous freshmen feel as comfortable as they would with a favorite relative.", "t": "學生們都很喜歡這位在學校圖書館當志工的退休物理老師；他像叔伯般慈祥的態度、溫和的玩笑和無盡的耐心，讓緊張的新生感覺就像和最喜歡的長輩相處一樣自在。", "as": "The senator's avuncular charm and jovial anecdotes concealed a sagacious political mind, and many young rivals underestimated him until he quietly outmaneuvered them during a crucial budget vote in committee.", "at": "這位參議員像叔伯般和藹的魅力和詼諧的趣聞軼事，掩蓋了他精明的政治頭腦；許多年輕對手都低估了他，直到他在委員會一場關鍵的預算表決中悄悄以謀略擊敗他們。"}, {"w": "supplicate", "p": "v.", "d": "To ask or beg humbly and earnestly.", "c": "懇求；哀求", "s": "In the ancient Greek tragedy, the defeated king kneels before the conqueror's throne to supplicate for his children's lives, humbly pleading with tears in his eyes that they be spared the fate of slavery.", "t": "在這部古希臘悲劇中，戰敗的國王跪在征服者的王座前懇求饒恕他孩子的性命，含淚謙卑地哀求讓他們免於淪為奴隸的命運。", "as": "Rather than supplicate the irascible governor for mercy, the imprisoned journalist chose to remain stoic, refusing to recant the articles that had exposed widespread corruption in the provincial treasury.", "at": "這位入獄的記者並未向脾氣暴躁的總督哀求饒恕，而是選擇保持堅忍，拒絕撤回那些揭露省庫普遍貪腐的報導。"}, {"w": "irascible", "p": "adj.", "d": "Easily made angry; quick-tempered.", "c": "易怒的；脾氣暴躁的", "s": "The famous chef was notoriously irascible; a slightly overcooked steak or a misplaced spoon could send him into a shouting rage, and few young cooks lasted more than a month in his demanding kitchen.", "t": "這位名廚是出了名的脾氣暴躁；一塊稍微煎過頭的牛排或一支放錯位置的湯匙，都可能讓他暴怒大吼，很少有年輕廚師能在他要求嚴苛的廚房裡撐過一個月。", "as": "The irascible old professor would castigate any student who arrived late, yet beneath his cantankerous exterior lay a genuine devotion to teaching that his former pupils still remember.", "at": "這位脾氣暴躁的老教授會嚴厲斥責任何遲到的學生，但在他乖戾的外表下，卻是一份對教學真摯的投入，至今仍令他昔日的學生難以忘懷。"}, {"w": "inexorable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Impossible to stop, change, or prevent.", "c": "無法阻擋的；不可動搖的", "s": "Climate scientists warn that unless emissions are reduced dramatically, the inexorable rise of sea levels will continue for centuries, slowly swallowing coastal farmland and forcing millions of people to abandon their homes.", "t": "氣候科學家警告，除非大幅減少排放，否則海平面無法阻擋的上升將持續數個世紀，緩慢吞沒沿海農地，迫使數百萬人放棄家園。", "as": "The inexorable march of technology has rendered many once-lucrative trades defunct, leaving many older workers to ruminate sadly on careers that vanished within a single generation.", "at": "科技無可阻擋的進展，已使許多曾經利潤豐厚的行業消失殆盡，讓許多年長的工作者只能感傷地反覆思索那些在一個世代內就消逝的職業。"}, {"w": "parvenu", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who has suddenly become rich but lacks social acceptance.", "c": "暴發戶；新貴", "s": "In Edith Wharton's novels, old New York families often sneer at the parvenu who has made a fortune in railroads, mocking his flashy mansion and refusing to invite him to their exclusive dinner parties.", "t": "在伊迪絲．華頓的小說中，紐約的老派家族常常嘲笑靠鐵路致富的暴發戶，譏諷他浮誇的豪宅，並拒絕邀請他參加他們的上流晚宴。", "as": "The aristocrats treated the wealthy parvenu with supercilious disdain, mocking his ostentatious carriages and gold-plated furniture as clear proof that money alone could never buy true refinement.", "at": "貴族們以高傲輕蔑的態度對待這位富有的暴發戶，嘲笑他炫耀的馬車和鍍金家具，認為這清楚證明了光靠金錢永遠買不到真正的教養。"}, {"w": "salubrious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Promoting health; healthful and pleasant.", "c": "有益健康的；宜人的", "s": "During the nineteenth century, doctors often sent patients with lung diseases to mountain resorts, believing that the clean, cool air and peaceful surroundings provided a salubrious environment in which the body could slowly heal itself.", "t": "在十九世紀，醫生常將肺病患者送往山區療養地，相信那裡清新涼爽的空氣與寧靜的環境，能提供一個有益健康的環境，讓身體慢慢自我療癒。", "as": "The doctor recommended a move to a more salubrious climate, convinced that the patient's chronic lethargy would abate once she escaped the city's fetid, polluted air.", "at": "醫生建議搬到氣候更有益健康的地方，深信患者一旦逃離城市惡臭汙濁的空氣，她長期的倦怠就會減輕。"}, {"w": "hyperbole", "p": "n.", "d": "Deliberate exaggeration used for emphasis or effect.", "c": "誇張法；誇大其詞", "s": "When the student wrote that she had 'a million pages of homework' and 'had not slept in a hundred years,' her English teacher explained that such hyperbole can make writing lively but should never be mistaken for fact.", "t": "當這名學生寫下她有「一百萬頁的作業」而且「一百年沒睡覺了」時，她的英文老師解釋說，這種誇飾法可以讓文章生動，但絕不能被當成事實。", "as": "Advertisers rely heavily on hyperbole, promising that a simple shampoo is a panacea that will transform one's life, but thoughtful consumers recognize such grandiloquent claims as mere puffery.", "at": "廣告商大量依賴誇大其詞，保證一瓶普通的洗髮精是能改變人生的萬靈丹，但有思考力的消費者看得出這種浮誇的宣傳不過是吹噓而已。"}, {"w": "sanctimonious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Acting morally superior to others in a self-righteous way.", "c": "偽善的；道貌岸然的", "s": "Readers found the columnist increasingly sanctimonious; each week he lectured them about wasting energy and eating meat, while reporters later revealed that he owned three large houses and flew on private jets.", "t": "讀者覺得這位專欄作家越來越偽善；他每週都對讀者說教，批評他們浪費能源、吃肉，但記者後來揭露，他擁有三棟大房子，還搭乘私人飛機。", "as": "The sanctimonious politician's moralizing speeches about honesty became utterly risible when investigators revealed his duplicity in accepting large secret payments from the very developers he claimed to oppose.", "at": "當調查人員揭露這位道貌岸然的政客暗中收受鉅額款項的欺騙行徑——而付款者正是他聲稱反對的開發商——他那些關於誠實的說教演講就變得十分可笑。"}, {"w": "alacrity", "p": "n.", "d": "Cheerful readiness, eagerness, and speed.", "c": "欣然；敏捷", "s": "When the coach asked for volunteers to help clean up the park after the typhoon, the entire team responded with alacrity, raising their hands immediately and arriving the next morning with gloves, rakes, and trash bags.", "t": "當教練徵求志工在颱風過後協助清理公園時，全隊都欣然響應，立刻舉手，並在隔天早上帶著手套、耙子和垃圾袋前來。", "as": "The new intern accepted every assignment with alacrity, and her assiduous work ethic soon earned the approbation of even the most demanding senior editors at the magazine.", "at": "這位新實習生欣然接受每項任務，她勤勉的工作態度很快就贏得了雜誌社裡連最嚴格的資深編輯都給予的讚許。"}, {"w": "obviate", "p": "v.", "d": "To remove or prevent a need or difficulty in advance.", "c": "消除；排除（需要或困難）", "s": "Engineers designed the new bridge with sensors that constantly monitor cracks and vibrations, hoping to obviate the need for expensive manual inspections that previously required closing the road for several days each year.", "t": "工程師在新橋上設計了能持續監測裂縫和震動的感測器，希望免除昂貴的人工檢查需求——過去每年都必須為此封閉道路好幾天。", "as": "A clear, lucid set of instructions would obviate most of the confusion, the manager argued, and render the lengthy, discursive training sessions for new employees entirely unnecessary.", "at": "經理認為，一套清楚明瞭的說明就能消除大部分的困惑，並使那些為新進員工舉辦的冗長散漫訓練課程完全沒有必要。"}, {"w": "emolument", "p": "n.", "d": "Payment received for work or for holding an office.", "c": "報酬；薪資", "s": "The city charter states that council members may receive no emolument other than their official salary, so accepting gifts or consulting fees from businesses that seek government contracts is strictly forbidden.", "t": "市憲章規定，市議員除了官方薪俸之外不得收受任何報酬，因此嚴格禁止接受尋求政府合約的企業所提供的禮物或顧問費。", "as": "The ambassador's post offered only a modest emolument, but she valued it as a sinecure free of onerous duties, leaving ample time for her scholarly writing.", "at": "這個大使職位只提供微薄的報酬，但她重視它是一份沒有繁重職責的閒差，讓她有充裕的時間從事學術寫作。"}, {"w": "intransigent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Refusing to compromise or change one's position.", "c": "不妥協的；固執的", "s": "The peace talks collapsed after only two days because both sides remained completely intransigent, each refusing to give up even a small piece of territory or to discuss any proposal suggested by the other.", "t": "和平談判僅兩天就破裂，因為雙方都完全不肯妥協，各自拒絕讓出哪怕一小塊領土，也拒絕討論對方提出的任何提案。", "as": "The intransigent negotiators refused to accede to even minor requests, and the mediator finally concluded that further talks would only protract the bitter dispute over fishing rights.", "at": "這些頑固的談判代表連微小的要求都拒絕同意，調解人最終認定，進一步的談判只會拖長這場關於漁權的激烈爭端。"}, {"w": "mordant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Bitingly sarcastic or cutting in humor or criticism.", "c": "尖刻的；辛辣的", "s": "Mark Twain was famous for his mordant wit; his sharp, sarcastic comments about politicians and religious hypocrites made audiences laugh while also leaving his targets feeling deeply wounded and embarrassed.", "t": "馬克．吐溫以尖刻的機智聞名；他對政客和宗教偽君子尖銳又諷刺的評論，讓觀眾發笑的同時，也讓被批評的對象深感受傷與難堪。", "as": "The critic's mordant review, full of acerbic remarks about the film's vapid dialogue, quickly became far more popular online than the expensive movie itself ever was.", "at": "這位影評人辛辣的評論，充滿對電影空洞對白的尖刻挖苦，很快就在網路上變得比這部高成本電影本身還要受歡迎得多。"}, {"w": "sagacious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having sound judgment and keen, practical wisdom.", "c": "睿智的；有遠見的", "s": "Villagers often brought their disputes to the sagacious old farmer, who listened patiently to both sides, asked a few careful questions, and usually proposed a solution that left everyone feeling fairly treated.", "t": "村民們常把糾紛帶到這位睿智的老農夫面前，他耐心聆聽雙方說法，提出幾個審慎的問題，通常能提出讓每個人都覺得受到公平對待的解決辦法。", "as": "The sagacious investor refused to join the frenzy, warning his clients that the volatile market was built on specious promises and would inevitably collapse within months.", "at": "這位睿智的投資人拒絕加入這股狂熱，他警告客戶，這個動盪的市場建立在似是而非的承諾上，必然會在幾個月內崩盤。"}, {"w": "acerbic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Sharp and harsh in tone or manner; biting.", "c": "尖酸的；刻薄的", "s": "The film critic's reviews were so acerbic that directors dreaded reading them; she once described a famous action movie as 'two hours of noise searching desperately for a single original idea.'", "t": "這位影評人的評論極為尖酸刻薄，導演們都害怕讀到；她曾形容一部知名動作片是「兩小時的噪音，拚命尋找一個原創點子」。", "as": "Her acerbic memoir did not merely disparage her former colleagues at the magazine; it also excoriated the entire publishing industry for its obsequious treatment of wealthy celebrity authors.", "at": "她尖酸的回憶錄不僅貶低她在雜誌社的昔日同事，還嚴厲抨擊整個出版業對富有名人作家的諂媚態度。"}, {"w": "variegated", "p": "adj.", "d": "Marked with patches or streaks of different colors; varied.", "c": "雜色的；多樣的", "s": "Gardeners prize the plant for its variegated leaves, whose green surfaces are streaked with irregular patches of cream, yellow, and pale pink, making each leaf look slightly different from every other one.", "t": "園丁們珍視這種植物的斑葉，其綠色葉面上帶有不規則的乳白、黃色和淡粉紅色斑紋，讓每片葉子看起來都與其他葉子略有不同。", "as": "The small museum's variegated collection, spanning bucolic landscapes, ancient pottery, and abstract sculptures, reflected the founder's catholic taste and her lifelong curiosity about art from every culture.", "at": "這座小型博物館多元的館藏，從田園風景畫、古代陶器到抽象雕塑，反映了創辦人廣泛的品味以及她畢生對各種文化藝術的好奇心。"}, {"w": "succor", "p": "n.", "d": "Help and support given in a time of hardship.", "c": "救助；援助", "s": "After the earthquake destroyed much of the mountain village, volunteers from across Taiwan arrived to offer succor to the survivors, bringing food, blankets, medicine, and comforting words to families who had lost everything.", "t": "地震摧毀了這座山村的大部分地區後，來自台灣各地的志工前來救助倖存者，為失去一切的家庭帶來食物、毛毯、藥品和安慰的話語。", "as": "The small religious order devoted itself to bringing succor to indigent families during the famine, and its members' altruism became a model for charities throughout the region.", "at": "這個小型修會在饑荒期間致力於救助貧困家庭，其成員的無私奉獻成為整個地區慈善團體的榜樣。"}, {"w": "importune", "p": "v.", "d": "To ask or beg someone persistently and annoyingly.", "c": "糾纏；強求", "s": "Celebrities often complain that fans and photographers importune them everywhere they go, following them into restaurants and repeatedly demanding photos and autographs even after they have politely refused several times.", "t": "名人常抱怨粉絲和攝影師走到哪裡都糾纏著他們，一路跟進餐廳，即使他們已經禮貌拒絕好幾次，仍一再要求合照和簽名。", "as": "The persistent salesman continued to importune the elderly couple with incessant phone calls, until their exasperated daughter threatened to report his unscrupulous tactics to the police.", "at": "這名糾纏不休的推銷員不斷打電話給這對老夫婦，直到他們惱火的女兒威脅要向警方舉報他不擇手段的推銷方式為止。"}]}, {"unit": 19, "level": 4, "cards": [{"w": "palliate", "p": "v.", "d": "To lessen the severity of something without curing it.", "c": "減輕（痛苦）；掩飾（過錯）", "s": "Because the disease had no known cure, the hospice team focused on medications that could palliate the patient's pain and breathlessness, allowing her to spend her final weeks at home with her family rather than in an intensive-care ward.", "t": "由於這種疾病尚無已知的治療方法，安寧照護團隊專注於能減輕病人疼痛與呼吸困難的藥物，讓她得以在家中與家人共度最後幾週，而不是待在加護病房。", "as": "Rather than palliate the senator's egregious misconduct, the editorial board published a trenchant critique, refusing to offer the specious excuses that his allies had so eagerly circulated.", "at": "社論委員會沒有替這位參議員惡劣至極的不當行為開脫，而是發表了一篇犀利的評論，拒絕提出他的盟友們熱切散布的那些似是而非的藉口。"}, {"w": "wizened", "p": "adj.", "d": "Shriveled and wrinkled, especially because of old age.", "c": "乾癟的；滿是皺紋的", "s": "The documentary opens with a close-up of a wizened farmer whose deeply lined face and thin, bent fingers reveal nearly seventy years of labor under the harsh sun of the Chianan Plain.", "t": "這部紀錄片以一位乾癟、滿臉皺紋的農夫特寫開場，他深刻的皺紋與細瘦彎曲的手指，透露出在嘉南平原烈日下近七十年的辛勞。", "as": "The wizened archivist, famously captious about citation errors, spent an afternoon showing the neophyte researchers how to spot spurious documents among the library's collection of colonial-era land deeds.", "at": "那位滿臉皺紋的檔案管理員以對引用錯誤吹毛求疵聞名，他花了一個下午教導這些新手研究員，如何在圖書館收藏的殖民時期地契中辨識偽造的文件。"}, {"w": "captious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Quick to find fault over trivial matters.", "c": "吹毛求疵的；愛挑剔的", "s": "Although the novel received glowing reviews from most critics, one captious reviewer devoted an entire column to complaining about a few misplaced commas and a single misspelled street name, ignoring the book's powerful themes entirely.", "t": "雖然這本小說獲得多數評論家的好評，但有一位吹毛求疵的評論者用一整篇專欄抱怨幾個放錯位置的逗號和一個拼錯的街名，完全忽略了這本書強而有力的主題。", "as": "The captious committee member raised one trivial cavil after another, yet her fastidious objections did nothing to weaken the study's well-documented findings about urban air pollution.", "at": "那位愛挑剔的委員接二連三提出瑣碎的異議，然而她過分講究的反對意見，絲毫無損於這項研究關於都市空氣污染、證據充分的研究結果。"}, {"w": "emendation", "p": "n.", "d": "A correction or change made to a text.", "c": "（文稿的）校訂；修正", "s": "When scholars compared the surviving manuscripts of the poem, they agreed that the word \"dove\" in line twelve was a copyist's error, and their proposed emendation restored the original word \"love,\" which fit the rhyme scheme perfectly.", "t": "學者們比對這首詩現存的手稿後，一致認為第十二行的「dove」一字是抄寫者的錯誤，而他們提出的校訂恢復了原本的字「love」，完全符合押韻格式。", "as": "The translator's careful emendations clarified several abstruse passages in the ancient treatise, though a few pedantic critics complained that she had taken liberties with the original text.", "at": "譯者細心的校訂釐清了這部古代論著中幾段深奧難懂的段落，不過仍有少數迂腐的評論家抱怨她對原文過於自由發揮。"}, {"w": "truculent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Eager to argue or fight; aggressively defiant.", "c": "好鬥的；凶狠挑釁的", "s": "When reporters asked about the missing funds, the truculent official jabbed his finger at the cameras, accused the journalists of spreading lies, and threatened to sue anyone who repeated the question, turning a routine press conference into a shouting match.", "t": "當記者詢問那筆下落不明的資金時，這位好鬥的官員用手指戳向攝影機，指控記者散布謊言，並威脅要控告任何重複提問的人，把一場例行記者會變成了叫罵大會。", "as": "The truculent striker, notoriously irascible on and off the field, was finally ostracized by teammates after he angrily shoved a referee during the championship match.", "at": "這位好鬥的前鋒無論在場上或場下都以脾氣暴躁出名，在冠軍賽中憤怒地推了裁判之後，終於遭到隊友排擠。"}, {"w": "expurgate", "p": "v.", "d": "To remove offensive or objectionable parts from a text.", "c": "刪除（書中不當內容）；刪改", "s": "Before the school board would approve the anthology for ninth graders, it insisted that the publisher expurgate several passages containing crude language, a decision that sparked a heated debate about censorship among teachers and librarians.", "t": "在學校董事會核准這本選集供九年級學生使用之前，它堅持要求出版社刪除幾段含有粗俗語言的段落，這項決定在教師與圖書館員之間引發了一場關於審查制度的激烈辯論。", "as": "Censors expurgated the dissident journalist's memoir so thoroughly that whole chapters vanished, an act of literary vandalism that only made the clandestine, uncut edition more sought after.", "at": "審查人員把這位異議記者的回憶錄刪改得如此徹底，以至於整章整章消失不見；這種文學破壞行為，反而使那本秘密流傳的未刪節版本更加搶手。"}, {"w": "reprobate", "p": "n.", "d": "A morally corrupt person with no principles.", "c": "墮落的人；無賴", "s": "In the eighteenth-century novel, the charming nobleman is gradually revealed to be a reprobate who gambles away his family's estate, lies to everyone who trusts him, and abandons his friends without the slightest sense of guilt.", "t": "在這部十八世紀小說中，那位迷人的貴族逐漸被揭露是個墮落之徒：他賭光了家族產業、對每個信任他的人撒謊，並毫無愧疚地拋棄朋友。", "as": "Historians once dismissed the pirate captain as an incorrigible reprobate, but newly discovered letters reveal a man capable of genuine contrition and surprising acts of altruism toward his crew.", "at": "歷史學家曾將這位海盜船長斥為無可救藥的無賴，但新發現的信件顯示，他也能真心悔改，並對船員展現出令人意外的無私善行。"}, {"w": "spurious", "p": "adj.", "d": "False or fake, though made to look genuine.", "c": "偽造的；似是而非的", "s": "The researchers warned that the apparent link between ice-cream sales and shark attacks was spurious, since both simply increase during hot summer months, and they urged students to distinguish genuine causes from mere coincidences in statistical data.", "t": "研究人員提醒，冰淇淋銷量與鯊魚攻擊之間看似存在的關聯是虛假的，因為兩者都只是在炎熱的夏季月份同步增加；他們呼籲學生在統計資料中區分真正的成因與純粹的巧合。", "as": "The charlatan's spurious credentials fooled many gullible investors until a diligent reporter discovered that the prestigious university listed on his résumé did not even exist.", "at": "這名騙子偽造的學經歷騙倒了許多輕信的投資人，直到一位認真的記者發現，他履歷上列出的那所名校根本不存在。"}, {"w": "volition", "p": "n.", "d": "The power to make choices by one's own will.", "c": "意志；自由意志；自願", "s": "Although her parents had always hoped she would study medicine, Mei-ling switched to environmental engineering of her own volition, explaining that no one had pressured her and that the decision reflected her lifelong passion for protecting coastal wetlands.", "t": "雖然父母一直希望她讀醫學，美玲卻出於自己的意願轉讀環境工程；她解釋沒有人逼她，這個決定反映了她長久以來對保護沿海濕地的熱情。", "as": "The witness insisted she had come forward of her own volition, not because prosecutors had coerced her, and her lucid, unequivocal testimony helped exonerate the wrongly accused teenager.", "at": "這位證人堅稱她是出於自願挺身而出，而非受到檢察官脅迫；她清晰而明確的證詞，幫助洗清了那名被冤枉的青少年的罪嫌。"}, {"w": "interpolate", "p": "v.", "d": "To insert words or material into a text or conversation.", "c": "插入（文字或意見）；竄改（文稿）", "s": "Textual scholars now believe that a medieval scribe chose to interpolate several lines praising the king into the ancient chronicle, because the vocabulary and style of those passages differ sharply from the rest of the original manuscript.", "t": "文本學者如今認為，一位中世紀抄寫員刻意在這部古老編年史中插入了幾行讚揚國王的文字，因為那些段落的用字與風格和原稿其他部分截然不同。", "as": "The biographer was accused of duplicity after critics discovered she had interpolated fabricated quotations into the general's diaries to embellish her own flattering portrait of him.", "at": "評論家發現這位傳記作家在將軍的日記中插入捏造的引文，用來美化她自己筆下對他的恭維形象，她因此被指控欺瞞不實。"}, {"w": "adduce", "p": "v.", "d": "To offer something as evidence or proof.", "c": "引證；舉出（證據、理由）", "s": "In her senior thesis on urban heat islands, Ting-yu was able to adduce temperature data from forty weather stations across Taipei to support her claim that neighborhoods with more trees stay noticeably cooler during summer afternoons.", "t": "在她關於都市熱島效應的畢業論文中，婷宇得以引用台北四十個氣象站的溫度資料，來支持她的論點：樹木較多的社區在夏日午後明顯較為涼爽。", "as": "To corroborate his theory, the astute geologist adduced fossil samples from three continents, a demonstrable pattern that eventually silenced even the most skeptical of his colleagues.", "at": "為了證實自己的理論，這位精明的地質學家舉出來自三大洲的化石樣本作為證據，這個明確可證的模式最終讓同事中最持懷疑態度的人也無話可說。"}, {"w": "miscreant", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who behaves badly or breaks the law.", "c": "惡棍；違法亂紀者", "s": "After someone spray-painted graffiti across the newly restored temple gate, local residents installed security cameras, hoping to identify the miscreant responsible and to prevent further damage to one of the oldest buildings in the district.", "t": "在有人用噴漆在剛修復好的廟門上塗鴉之後，當地居民裝設了監視器，希望找出應負責的惡徒，並防止這座區內最古老的建築之一再遭破壞。", "as": "The miscreants who vandalized the memorial showed no contrition in court, prompting the judge to castigate them publicly before imposing a sentence that most residents considered commensurate with the crime.", "at": "那些破壞紀念碑的惡徒在法庭上毫無悔意，促使法官在宣判前公開嚴厲斥責他們；大多數居民認為該刑罰與罪行相當。"}, {"w": "quixotic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Extremely idealistic but unrealistic and impractical.", "c": "不切實際的；異想天開的", "s": "Critics called the startup's plan to replace every plastic bag in Taiwan within six months quixotic, arguing that its noble goal ignored the enormous costs, supply shortages, and stubborn consumer habits that would make such rapid change impossible.", "t": "評論者認為這家新創公司想在六個月內取代台灣所有塑膠袋的計畫不切實際，指出這個崇高的目標忽略了龐大的成本、供應短缺，以及會讓如此快速的改變無法實現的頑固消費習慣。", "as": "Some dismissed the young activist's campaign as quixotic, yet her ebullience and fervent speeches eventually persuaded lawmakers to rescind the controversial logging permits in the mountains.", "at": "有些人認為這位年輕運動人士的訴求不切實際，然而她洋溢的熱情與熱烈的演說，最終說服了立法者撤銷山區那些具爭議性的伐木許可。"}, {"w": "suppurate", "p": "v.", "d": "To form or discharge pus, as an infected wound does.", "c": "化膿；流膿", "s": "The nineteenth-century surgeon's notebook records that, without antiseptics, even minor cuts would often become infected and suppurate within days, which is why historians consider Joseph Lister's introduction of sterile techniques such a turning point in medicine.", "t": "這位十九世紀外科醫師的筆記記載，在沒有消毒劑的年代，即使是小傷口也常在數日內感染並化膿；這正是歷史學家將約瑟夫・李斯特引進無菌技術視為醫學轉捩點的原因。", "as": "Left untreated in the squalid field hospital, the soldier's wound began to suppurate, and the deleterious infection spread so quickly that doctors feared it would prove fatal.", "at": "在骯髒簡陋的野戰醫院裡未獲治療，這名士兵的傷口開始化膿，有害的感染蔓延得如此迅速，醫生們擔心會致命。"}, {"w": "martinet", "p": "n.", "d": "A very strict person who demands complete obedience.", "c": "嚴守紀律的人；嚴厲的管教者", "s": "The new orchestra conductor proved to be a martinet who stopped rehearsals whenever a single violinist came in late, demanded that every musician arrive thirty minutes early, and publicly scolded anyone who dared to question her instructions.", "t": "新任管弦樂團指揮原來是個極度嚴厲的人：只要有一位小提琴手慢了拍子進入，她就中斷排練；她要求每位樂手提早三十分鐘到場，還會公開斥責任何膽敢質疑她指示的人。", "as": "Though students regarded the chemistry teacher as an austere martinet, her exacting standards and judicious feedback helped transform callow freshmen into confident, careful young researchers.", "at": "雖然學生們認為這位化學老師是個嚴峻的紀律狂，但她嚴格的標準與明智的回饋，幫助那些稚嫩的新生蛻變為自信且細心的年輕研究者。"}, {"w": "compunction", "p": "n.", "d": "A feeling of guilt or uneasiness about doing wrong.", "c": "內疚；良心不安", "s": "The documentary reveals that the factory owners felt no compunction about dumping toxic waste into the river, even after local fishermen reported dying fish and children in nearby villages began developing mysterious skin rashes.", "t": "這部紀錄片揭露，工廠老闆們對於將有毒廢棄物傾倒入河中毫無愧疚，即使當地漁民通報魚群死亡、附近村莊的孩童開始出現不明皮疹，他們依然如此。", "as": "The unscrupulous lobbyist showed no compunction about using flattery and subterfuge to beguile lawmakers into supporting a bill that would harm thousands of small farmers.", "at": "這名不擇手段的說客毫無愧疚地以奉承與詭計誘騙立法者，支持一項會傷害成千上萬小農的法案。"}, {"w": "mercurial", "p": "adj.", "d": "Changing moods or behavior suddenly and unpredictably.", "c": "反覆無常的；善變的", "s": "Band members found their lead singer increasingly difficult to work with, since his mercurial temperament meant he might be joking warmly with fans one moment and storming furiously out of the recording studio the next.", "t": "樂團成員發現主唱越來越難相處，因為他喜怒無常的性情意味著他可能前一刻還熱情地和歌迷說笑，下一刻就怒氣沖沖地衝出錄音室。", "as": "The mercurial poet could shift from jovial banter to lugubrious silence within minutes, a volatile pattern that both fascinated and exhausted the friends who gathered at his salon.", "at": "這位喜怒無常的詩人能在幾分鐘內從愉快的說笑轉為陰鬱的沉默，這種多變的模式讓聚集在他沙龍裡的朋友們既著迷又疲憊。"}, {"w": "nostrum", "p": "n.", "d": "A questionable remedy or scheme claimed to cure problems.", "c": "（成效可疑的）秘方；萬靈丹式的對策", "s": "Traveling salesmen in the nineteenth-century American West often sold a bottled nostrum that supposedly cured everything from baldness to rheumatism, though chemists later discovered that most of these mixtures contained little more than alcohol and sugar.", "t": "十九世紀美國西部的巡迴推銷員常販售一種瓶裝秘方，號稱能治好從禿頭到風濕的各種毛病，不過化學家後來發現，這些混合物大多只不過是酒精和糖。", "as": "The traveling peddler marketed his herbal nostrum as a panacea for every ailment, but physicians warned that its claims were fallacious and its ingredients potentially pernicious.", "at": "這位巡迴小販把他的草藥秘方宣傳成能治百病的萬靈丹，但醫師們警告，其宣稱的療效毫無根據，成分還可能有害。"}, {"w": "propitiate", "p": "v.", "d": "To win the favor of someone by pleasing them.", "c": "討好；撫慰（以平息怒氣）", "s": "Archaeologists believe the ancient farmers buried jade ornaments and bowls of rice beneath the village fields in an effort to propitiate the gods of rain, whom they blamed for the droughts that repeatedly destroyed their harvests.", "t": "考古學家認為，古代農民在村莊田地下埋藏玉飾和一碗碗米飯，是為了討好雨神，因為他們將一再摧毀收成的乾旱歸咎於雨神。", "as": "To propitiate the irate shareholders, the board offered a contrite apology and promised to redress their grievances, though few believed these gestures would truly mollify them.", "at": "為了安撫憤怒的股東，董事會誠心道歉並承諾補救他們的不滿，但很少人相信這些舉動真能平息他們的怒氣。"}, {"w": "efficacy", "p": "n.", "d": "The ability to produce the intended result.", "c": "功效；效力", "s": "Before the vaccine could be approved for public use, researchers conducted large clinical trials involving thousands of volunteers to measure its efficacy, comparing infection rates between those who received the vaccine and those who were given a placebo.", "t": "在這款疫苗獲准供大眾使用之前，研究人員進行了涉及數千名志願者的大型臨床試驗來評估其效力，比較接種疫苗者與服用安慰劑者之間的感染率。", "as": "Although the advertisements made copious claims about the supplement's efficacy, independent studies found the benefits negligible and judged several of the cited trials to be poorly designed or even spurious.", "at": "雖然廣告對這款營養補充品的功效大肆宣傳，但獨立研究發現其益處微乎其微，並認為所引用的幾項試驗設計不良，甚至根本是虛假的。"}]}, {"unit": 20, "level": 4, "cards": [{"w": "tantamount", "p": "adj.", "d": "Equivalent in effect or seriousness to something else.", "c": "等同於的；相當於的", "s": "Environmental groups argued that approving the new highway through the wetland reserve would be tantamount to signing a death warrant for the endangered black-faced spoonbill, since the birds depend on that habitat for winter feeding.", "t": "環保團體主張，核准新公路穿越濕地保護區，就等同於替瀕危的黑面琵鷺簽下死刑令，因為這些鳥類仰賴該棲地度過冬季覓食期。", "as": "The senator's refusal to answer the committee's germane questions was, in the eyes of many voters, tantamount to an admission of guilt and a sign of his supercilious contempt for public accountability.", "at": "這位參議員拒絕回答委員會切中要點的質詢，在許多選民眼中無異於認罪，也顯示出他對公共問責的傲慢輕蔑。"}, {"w": "pariah", "p": "n.", "d": "A person rejected and avoided by society; an outcast.", "c": "被社會排斥者；賤民", "s": "After the scientist publicly admitted that she had falsified her research data, she became a pariah in the academic community, as former colleagues refused to collaborate with her and journals rejected every paper she submitted.", "t": "這位科學家公開承認偽造研究數據後，在學術界成了被排斥的人：昔日同事拒絕與她合作，期刊也退回她投出的每一篇論文。", "as": "After his scandalous memoir exposed the duplicity of his former allies, the politician became a pariah, ostracized by the party he had once led with such grandiloquent confidence.", "at": "在他那本醜聞纏身的回憶錄揭露昔日盟友的口是心非之後，這位政治人物成了過街老鼠，被他曾以浮誇的自信領導的政黨所排擠。"}, {"w": "germane", "p": "adj.", "d": "Closely relevant to the subject being discussed.", "c": "密切相關的；切題的", "s": "During the debate tournament, judges deducted points from speakers who wandered into unrelated stories, rewarding instead those who kept every argument germane to the motion about whether cities should ban private cars from downtown areas.", "t": "在辯論比賽中，評審對偏離主題、講起不相干故事的辯士扣分，反而獎勵那些讓每個論點都緊扣「城市是否應禁止私家車進入市中心」這項辯題的人。", "as": "The professor urged students to cull every anecdote that was not germane to their thesis, warning that discursive essays rarely persuade even the most patient readers.", "at": "教授敦促學生刪去所有與論點無關的軼事，並提醒他們，離題漫談的文章就連最有耐心的讀者也很少能說服。"}, {"w": "licentious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Disregarding accepted rules of morality or conduct.", "c": "放蕩的；不受道德約束的", "s": "Historians note that Puritan leaders in seventeenth-century England closed the London theaters, condemning them as licentious places that openly encouraged drunkenness, gambling, and other behavior they believed threatened public morality.", "t": "歷史學家指出，十七世紀英格蘭的清教徒領袖關閉了倫敦的劇院，譴責那些地方是放蕩之所，公然助長酗酒、賭博以及他們認為危害公共道德的其他行為。", "as": "Victorian critics condemned the poet's verses as licentious and demanded that publishers expurgate them, yet later scholars praised the same poems for their mellifluous language and candor.", "at": "維多利亞時代的評論家譴責這位詩人的詩作放蕩不羈，要求出版商刪改；然而後世學者卻讚揚這些詩語言優美流暢、坦率真誠。"}, {"w": "superannuated", "p": "adj.", "d": "Too old to be useful; outdated or retired.", "c": "老舊過時的；年老退休的", "s": "The school's computer lab still relied on superannuated machines from the early 2000s, which took ten minutes to start up and could not run the software students needed for their coding and graphic design classes.", "t": "這所學校的電腦教室仍仰賴二〇〇〇年代初期的老舊電腦，開機要花十分鐘，還無法執行學生上程式設計與平面設計課所需的軟體。", "as": "The superannuated factory, once a symbol of the city's industrial renaissance, now stands as a defunct ruin whose rusting machinery reminds residents of a more prosperous era.", "at": "這座老舊過時的工廠曾是城市工業復興的象徵，如今卻是一片廢棄的廢墟，鏽蝕的機器讓居民憶起一個更繁榮的年代。"}, {"w": "egregious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Outstandingly bad in a way that is shocking or obvious.", "c": "極其惡劣的；駭人聽聞的", "s": "The investigative report exposed an egregious waste of public money: the city had spent nearly two hundred million dollars on a new sports stadium that sat empty for years because it had been built without a single access road.", "t": "這份調查報告揭露了一起極其惡劣的公帑浪費：市政府花費將近兩億元興建一座新體育館，卻因為蓋好時連一條聯外道路都沒有而閒置多年。", "as": "The auditors uncovered egregious accounting fraud, revealing that senior executives had quietly peculated millions of dollars while issuing fallacious quarterly reports that assured investors the company was thriving.", "at": "稽核人員揭發了極其惡劣的會計舞弊，發現高階主管一面暗中侵吞數百萬美元公款，一面發布不實的季報，向投資人保證公司營運蒸蒸日上。"}, {"w": "vapid", "p": "adj.", "d": "Lacking interest, energy, or meaningful ideas; dull.", "c": "乏味的；空洞無趣的", "s": "Although the pop song topped the charts for weeks, music critics dismissed its vapid lyrics, which repeated the same three clichés about summer love without offering a single original image or thought.", "t": "雖然這首流行歌曲連續數週登上排行榜冠軍，樂評家卻對其空洞乏味的歌詞嗤之以鼻，因為歌詞反覆堆砌三句關於夏日戀情的陳腔濫調，沒有任何原創的意象或想法。", "as": "The film's vapid dialogue and banal plot could not be redeemed by its opulent costumes, and most critics left the premiere feeling that they had squandered an entire evening.", "at": "這部電影空洞乏味的對白與陳腐的劇情，再華麗的戲服也無法挽救，多數影評人離開首映會時都覺得白白浪費了一整個晚上。"}, {"w": "crotchet", "p": "n.", "d": "A strange, whimsical idea or opinion; an odd notion.", "c": "怪念頭；古怪的想法", "s": "The eccentric inventor had a peculiar crotchet that all of his best ideas came to him while standing on one foot, so his assistants grew used to seeing him balanced awkwardly beside his workbench for hours.", "t": "這位古怪的發明家有個奇特的怪念頭，認為他最好的點子都是單腳站立時想到的，因此他的助手們漸漸習慣看到他好幾個小時笨拙地單腳站在工作台旁。", "as": "Her colleagues tolerated the novelist's crotchets with good humor, regarding her insistence on writing only by candlelight as a harmless idiosyncrasy rather than a sign of ostentatious affectation.", "at": "同事們以幽默包容這位小說家的種種怪念頭，認為她堅持只在燭光下寫作是無傷大雅的個人怪癖，而非刻意炫耀、矯揉造作的表現。"}, {"w": "epigraph", "p": "n.", "d": "A quotation at the start of a book or chapter.", "c": "（書或章節開頭的）題辭；引言", "s": "Each chapter of the historical novel begins with an epigraph, a short quotation from a real nineteenth-century diary, which hints at the themes that will unfold in the pages that follow.", "t": "這部歷史小說的每一章都以一段題辭開頭，那是取自一本真實十九世紀日記的簡短引文，暗示了接下來篇章將展開的主題。", "as": "The author chose a laconic line from an ancient philosopher as her epigraph, a salient choice that foreshadowed the stoic resilience of the protagonist throughout the novel.", "at": "作者選了一句古代哲學家簡潔的話作為書前題辭，這個醒目的選擇預示了主角在整部小說中堅忍不拔的韌性。"}, {"w": "expatiate", "p": "v.", "d": "To speak or write at great length about something.", "c": "詳細闡述；長篇大論", "s": "Given only five minutes for her presentation, the graduate student could not expatiate on every aspect of her coral reef research, so she focused on the single most surprising finding about rising ocean temperatures.", "t": "這位研究生的報告只有五分鐘，無法詳細闡述她珊瑚礁研究的每個面向，因此她專注介紹關於海水溫度上升最令人驚訝的那項發現。", "as": "The garrulous tour guide would expatiate on every obscure detail of the palace's history, and his verbose lectures left many visitors wishing for a more succinct and cursory tour.", "at": "這位多話的導遊會對宮殿歷史的每個冷門細節長篇大論，他冗長的講解讓許多遊客希望能有一趟更簡潔、走馬看花式的導覽。"}, {"w": "sinecure", "p": "n.", "d": "A paid position requiring little or no work.", "c": "閒差；掛名的肥缺", "s": "Reporters discovered that the governor had given his nephew a sinecure at the tourism bureau, a well-paid advisory post that required him to attend only one meeting a year and produce no written reports.", "t": "記者發現州長替他的姪子在觀光局安排了一份閒差，那是一個高薪的顧問職位，他每年只需出席一次會議，也不必撰寫任何書面報告。", "as": "Critics charged that the mayor's flagrant nepotism had created a lucrative sinecure for his cousin, whose annual emolument far exceeded that of the city's most experienced and hardest-working engineers.", "at": "批評者指控市長明目張膽地任人唯親，為他的表弟安插了一個油水豐厚的閒差，其年薪遠超過市府最資深、最勤奮的工程師們。"}, {"w": "predilection", "p": "n.", "d": "A strong preference or liking for something.", "c": "偏好；偏愛", "s": "The biography notes that the composer had a predilection for minor keys and slow tempos, which explains why so many of his symphonies sound melancholy even when their titles suggest celebration or joy.", "t": "這本傳記指出，這位作曲家偏好小調與緩慢的節拍，這也說明了為何他許多交響曲即使標題暗示著慶祝或喜悅，聽起來仍帶有憂鬱之感。", "as": "The critic's predilection for abstruse, experimental fiction led her to disparage nearly every popular novel, a proclivity that some readers found refreshing and others considered narrow-minded and snobbish.", "at": "這位評論家偏愛深奧難懂的實驗小說，使她幾乎貶低每一本通俗小說；這種傾向有些讀者覺得耳目一新，有些人則認為心胸狹隘又自命清高。"}, {"w": "imbroglio", "p": "n.", "d": "A complicated, confusing, and embarrassing situation.", "c": "錯綜複雜的困境；糾紛", "s": "What began as a simple dispute over a parking space turned into an imbroglio involving three neighbors, two lawyers, a city councilor, and a viral video that drew thousands of angry comments online.", "t": "一場原本只是停車位的小糾紛，最後演變成牽涉三位鄰居、兩名律師、一位市議員，以及一段在網路上引來數千則憤怒留言的爆紅影片的複雜爛攤子。", "as": "The minister hoped to extricate herself from the political imbroglio, but each new allegation only deepened the morass and made her vague explanations seem less tenable.", "at": "這位部長希望讓自己脫離這場政治糾葛，但每一項新的指控都只讓困境更加深陷，也讓她模稜兩可的解釋顯得更站不住腳。"}, {"w": "ineffable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Too great or extreme to be expressed in words.", "c": "難以言喻的；不可言傳的", "s": "Climbers who reach the summit of Yushan before dawn often describe an ineffable sense of wonder as the sun rises over a sea of clouds, insisting that neither photographs nor words can capture the experience.", "t": "在黎明前登上玉山主峰的登山客，常形容當太陽從雲海升起時那種難以言喻的震撼，並堅稱無論照片或文字都無法捕捉那樣的體驗。", "as": "Mystics across many cultures have tried to describe an ineffable union with the divine, though such esoteric experiences tend to elude the prosaic language of ordinary conversation.", "at": "許多文化中的神秘主義者都曾試圖描述與神合一那種難以言喻的感受，然而這類深奧玄妙的體驗，往往難以用日常對話平淡的語言表達。"}, {"w": "stolid", "p": "adj.", "d": "Calm and showing little emotion or sensitivity.", "c": "不動聲色的；感覺遲鈍的", "s": "While the other contestants cried, cheered, or covered their faces when the results were announced, the stolid chess champion simply nodded, shook hands with the judges, and calmly packed up his pieces as if nothing had happened.", "t": "當結果宣布時，其他參賽者有的哭、有的歡呼、有的掩面，這位不動聲色的西洋棋冠軍卻只是點點頭、和評審握手，然後若無其事地平靜收拾棋子。", "as": "The stolid farmer endured years of drought and flood with stoic equanimity, never succumbing to the lugubrious complaints that filled the crowded village teahouse each evening after the harvest.", "at": "這位不動聲色的農夫以堅忍的沉著熬過多年的乾旱與洪水，從不像收成後每晚擠滿村裡茶館的那些人一樣陷入悲戚的抱怨。"}, {"w": "offal", "p": "n.", "d": "The internal organs of a butchered animal; refuse.", "c": "（屠宰後的）內臟；下水；廢料", "s": "In many traditional cuisines, cooks use offal such as liver, kidneys, and intestines in hearty stews, a practice that historians link to times when poor families could not afford to waste any part of an animal.", "t": "在許多傳統料理中，廚師會把肝臟、腎臟和腸子等內臟用來燉煮濃郁的燉菜；歷史學家認為，這種做法與貧窮人家負擔不起浪費動物任何部位的年代有關。", "as": "Fastidious diners may balk at dishes made from offal, yet many chefs consider stews of tripe and liver to be a felicitous way to honor frugal culinary traditions.", "at": "講究的食客可能對內臟料理望之卻步，然而許多廚師認為，牛肚與肝臟燉菜是向節儉飲食傳統致敬的絕佳方式。"}, {"w": "lissome", "p": "adj.", "d": "Slim, flexible, and graceful in movement.", "c": "柔軟輕盈的；體態優美的", "s": "The choreographer chose a lissome young dancer for the lead role in the ballet, praising the way her slender body seemed to bend and leap across the stage as effortlessly as a willow branch in the wind.", "t": "編舞家為這齣芭蕾舞劇的主角選了一位體態輕盈柔軟的年輕舞者，讚美她纖細的身軀在舞台上彎曲、跳躍時，宛如風中的柳枝般毫不費力。", "as": "The lissome acrobat moved with such alacrity and grace that the audience found her performance almost ethereal, as if gravity had briefly ceased to apply to her.", "at": "這位體態輕盈的特技演員動作如此敏捷優雅，觀眾覺得她的表演幾乎超凡脫俗，彷彿重力短暫地在她身上失效了。"}, {"w": "mellifluous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Sweet, smooth, and pleasant to hear.", "c": "（聲音）甜美流暢的；悅耳的", "s": "The radio host's mellifluous voice made her late-night program a favorite among insomniacs, many of whom wrote letters saying her smooth, gentle tone helped them relax after long and stressful days.", "t": "這位電台主持人甜美悅耳的嗓音，讓她的深夜節目深受失眠者喜愛，許多人寫信表示，她圓潤溫柔的聲音幫助他們在漫長而壓力重重的一天後放鬆下來。", "as": "The actor's mellifluous narration lent the documentary a soothing quality, softening even its most poignant scenes and contrasting sharply with the strident commentary of rival programs.", "at": "這位演員悅耳流暢的旁白為紀錄片增添了撫慰人心的特質，就連最令人心酸的場景也因此變得柔和，與對手節目刺耳的評論形成強烈對比。"}, {"w": "surfeit", "p": "n.", "d": "An excessive amount of something.", "c": "過量；過剩", "s": "Nutritionists warn that a surfeit of sugary drinks during adolescence can lead to long-term health problems, from tooth decay to diabetes, even among teenagers who exercise regularly and appear perfectly healthy.", "t": "營養師警告，青春期過量攝取含糖飲料可能導致長期的健康問題，從蛀牙到糖尿病都有可能，即使是規律運動、看似非常健康的青少年也不例外。", "as": "A surfeit of information can be as debilitating as a dearth of it, leaving voters overwhelmed by a plethora of conflicting claims and unable to make judicious decisions.", "at": "資訊過量可能與資訊匱乏一樣令人無所適從，讓選民被大量互相矛盾的說法淹沒，無法做出明智的判斷。"}, {"w": "blandishment", "p": "n.", "d": "Flattering words or actions used to persuade someone.", "c": "甜言蜜語；哄騙；奉承", "s": "The salesperson tried every blandishment she could think of, praising the customer's excellent taste and promising exclusive discounts, but the cautious buyer refused to sign the contract until she had compared prices online.", "t": "這位銷售員用盡她想得到的各種甜言蜜語，稱讚顧客品味絕佳並承諾獨家折扣，但謹慎的買家堅持要先上網比價，才肯簽下合約。", "as": "Resisting the sycophant's blandishments, the incorruptible judge remained impervious to flattery and gifts alike and rendered a verdict based solely on the evidence presented in open court.", "at": "這位清廉的法官抵擋住那名諂媚者的甜言蜜語，無論奉承或餽贈都不為所動，僅依據公開審理中提出的證據作出判決。"}]}, {"unit": 21, "level": 5, "cards": [{"w": "prolix", "p": "adj.", "d": "Using too many words; tediously long.", "c": "冗長的；囉嗦的", "s": "The committee rejected the first draft of the policy proposal as prolix, noting that its forty pages repeated the same three recommendations so many times that busy lawmakers would never bother to read past the introduction.", "t": "委員會退回了這份政策提案的初稿，認為內容冗長，並指出其四十頁的篇幅反覆陳述同樣的三項建議太多次，忙碌的立法者根本不會讀到引言以後的部分。", "as": "The professor's prolix lectures, full of tangential digressions and pedantic footnotes, left students longing for the laconic clarity of the guest speaker who had visited the week before.", "at": "這位教授冗長的講課充滿離題的枝節與迂腐的註腳，讓學生們懷念起上週來訪那位客座講者簡潔明瞭的風格。"}, {"w": "apocryphal", "p": "adj.", "d": "Of doubtful truth, though widely repeated as true.", "c": "真實性可疑的；杜撰的", "s": "The popular story that George Washington chopped down his father's cherry tree and then confessed is almost certainly apocryphal, since historians have traced it to a biographer who invented the tale decades after Washington's death.", "t": "喬治・華盛頓砍倒父親的櫻桃樹後坦承認錯的這則流行故事，幾乎可以確定是杜撰的，因為歷史學家已追溯到這是一位傳記作家在華盛頓死後數十年才捏造出來的。", "as": "The apocryphal anecdote about the scientist's sudden epiphany has been repeated so often that it has acquired undeserved credence, though no extant letters or notebooks corroborate it.", "at": "關於這位科學家突然頓悟的那則杜撰軼事被反覆傳誦，以至於獲得了不應有的可信度，儘管現存的書信或筆記中沒有任何一份能證實它。"}, {"w": "cupidity", "p": "n.", "d": "Intense greed, especially for money or possessions.", "c": "貪婪；貪財", "s": "The novel's villain is driven by cupidity, secretly buying up the villagers' farmland at unfairly low prices so that he can sell it to a mining company and become the richest man in the province.", "t": "這部小說的反派受貪婪驅使，暗中以不公平的低價收購村民的農地，好轉賣給一家礦業公司，讓自己成為全省最富有的人。", "as": "The tycoon's cupidity knew no bounds; despite his opulent lifestyle, he remained insatiable, scheming to peculate even the modest pension funds of his loyal employees.", "at": "這位大亨的貪婪毫無止境；儘管生活奢華，他仍貪得無厭，甚至盤算著侵吞忠心員工微薄的退休基金。"}, {"w": "vernal", "p": "adj.", "d": "Relating to or occurring in the spring.", "c": "春天的；春季的", "s": "Each March, ecologists record the vernal migration of frogs across the mountain road near Yangmingshan, when thousands of the small amphibians leave the forest to lay eggs in ponds warmed by the first mild weeks of spring.", "t": "每年三月，生態學家都會記錄陽明山附近山路上青蛙的春季遷徙，那時成千上萬的小型兩棲動物會離開森林，到被初春溫和時節曬暖的池塘裡產卵。", "as": "The vernal landscape, replete with variegated blossoms after the long winter, inspired the painter to abandon the lugubrious palette that had dominated her earlier work.", "at": "漫長冬季過後，春天的景色處處開滿五彩繽紛的花朵，激勵這位畫家拋棄了主導她早期作品的那種陰鬱色調。"}, {"w": "temerity", "p": "n.", "d": "Excessive confidence or boldness; reckless nerve.", "c": "魯莽；冒失；膽大妄為", "s": "The new intern had the temerity to interrupt the company president during an important meeting and declare that the entire marketing strategy was a waste of money, a bold move that shocked every senior manager in the room.", "t": "這位新來的實習生竟膽敢在一場重要會議中打斷公司總裁，宣稱整套行銷策略都是浪費錢，這個大膽的舉動讓在場每一位高階主管都大為震驚。", "as": "Few junior officials would have the temerity to censure the minister publicly, yet the young auditor's trenchant report exposed his venal dealings for all to see.", "at": "很少有基層官員敢公開譴責部長，然而這位年輕稽核員犀利的報告，卻讓部長的貪腐勾當公諸於世。"}, {"w": "rapprochement", "p": "n.", "d": "The restoration of friendly relations between rivals.", "c": "（敵對雙方的）修好；和解", "s": "Historians often point to the 1972 meeting between American and Chinese leaders as the beginning of a rapprochement between the two nations, which had refused to maintain official diplomatic contact for more than two decades.", "t": "歷史學家常將一九七二年中美領導人的會面視為兩國修好的開端，在此之前，兩國已拒絕維持正式外交往來達二十多年。", "as": "The unexpected rapprochement between the feuding families ended a vendetta that had lasted three generations, and both sides finally acceded to a magnanimous plan for sharing the disputed orchard.", "at": "這兩個世仇家族出人意料的和解，終結了一場延續三代的冤仇，雙方終於同意一項寬宏大量的計畫，共享那片有爭議的果園。"}, {"w": "disquisition", "p": "n.", "d": "A long, formal discussion or essay on a subject.", "c": "專題論文；長篇論述", "s": "Asked a simple question about why leaves change color, the botany professor launched into a forty-minute disquisition on chlorophyll, pigments, and seasonal chemistry that impressed some students and put several others to sleep.", "t": "被問到一個為什麼樹葉會變色的簡單問題時，這位植物學教授發表了一場長達四十分鐘的專題論述，談葉綠素、色素和季節性化學作用，讓一些學生印象深刻，也讓好幾位學生睡著了。", "as": "Her erudite disquisition on Italian painting, though somewhat long and dense in places, offered such lucid analysis of color and composition that even skeptical critics conceded its lasting value to the field.", "at": "她關於義大利繪畫的博學論述雖然有些地方略顯冗長艱澀，卻對色彩與構圖提供了極為清晰的分析，就連持懷疑態度的評論家也承認它對該領域的長遠價值。"}, {"w": "proscribe", "p": "v.", "d": "To officially forbid or prohibit something.", "c": "禁止；查禁", "s": "To protect the coral reefs around Kenting, local authorities decided to proscribe the use of certain chemical sunscreens on nearby beaches, citing research showing that the ingredients can bleach and kill delicate reef organisms.", "t": "為了保護墾丁周邊的珊瑚礁，地方主管機關決定禁止在附近海灘使用某些化學防曬乳，並引用研究指出這些成分會使脆弱的珊瑚礁生物白化甚至死亡。", "as": "The military regime proscribed all dissident publications and jailed their editors, but clandestine presses hidden in basements continued to promulgate pamphlets criticizing the government's brutal treatment of student protesters.", "at": "該軍事政權查禁所有異議刊物並監禁其編輯，但藏身地下室的秘密印刷所仍持續散布小冊子，批評政府對學生抗議者的殘暴對待。"}, {"w": "munificence", "p": "n.", "d": "Great generosity, especially in giving money or gifts.", "c": "慷慨；寬宏大量的施予", "s": "Thanks to the munificence of a retired engineer who donated nearly his entire fortune, the rural township was able to build a modern library, fund scholarships for local students, and repair its aging elementary school.", "t": "多虧一位退休工程師的慷慨解囊，捐出了幾乎全部財產，這個鄉下小鎮得以興建一座現代化圖書館、設立在地學生獎學金，並修繕老舊的國小。", "as": "The philanthropist's munificence was legendary; his altruism funded hospitals across the region, yet he eschewed every accolade and refused to have buildings named after him.", "at": "這位慈善家的慷慨眾所皆知；他無私的善舉資助了全區的醫院，但他避開所有讚譽，也拒絕讓任何建築物以他命名。"}, {"w": "probity", "p": "n.", "d": "Complete honesty and strong moral principles.", "c": "正直；誠實", "s": "The retired judge was admired across the political spectrum for her probity; in forty years on the bench, she never accepted a gift, never hid a conflict of interest, and never let personal friendships influence a ruling.", "t": "這位退休法官因其正直而受到各政治陣營的敬重；在四十年的法官生涯中，她從未收受任何禮物、從未隱瞞利益衝突，也從未讓私交影響判決。", "as": "The mayor's reputation for probity made the allegations especially shocking, and many residents refused to believe he could have been complicit in such a venal scheme.", "at": "市長素以正直著稱，使得這些指控格外令人震驚，許多居民不願相信他會參與如此貪腐的計畫。"}, {"w": "puissant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having great power or influence.", "c": "有權勢的；強大的", "s": "In medieval Europe, a puissant king could raise vast armies and command the loyalty of countless nobles, yet even the strongest rulers often depended on the church to confirm their authority in the eyes of ordinary people.", "t": "在中世紀歐洲，一位強大的國王能召集龐大的軍隊並號令無數貴族效忠，然而即使是最強勢的統治者，也常需仰賴教會在平民眼中確認其權威。", "as": "The puissant trade guild once held omnipotent sway over the port, but its power proved ephemeral once new shipping routes rendered the old harbor obsolete.", "at": "這個勢力強大的貿易公會曾對港口擁有無所不能的支配力，但一旦新的航線讓舊港口遭到淘汰，它的權勢便顯得短暫易逝。"}, {"w": "peculate", "p": "v.", "d": "To steal money that one has been trusted with.", "c": "盜用（公款）；侵吞", "s": "Auditors discovered that the charity's treasurer had found a way to peculate donations by creating fake invoices from nonexistent suppliers, secretly moving nearly two million dollars into his own bank account over five years.", "t": "稽核人員發現，這家慈善機構的財務長利用不存在的供應商開立假發票來侵吞捐款，在五年內暗中將將近兩百萬元轉入自己的銀行帳戶。", "as": "The city officials who peculated public funds for nearly a decade employed elaborate subterfuge to hide their crimes, but an astute young accountant eventually uncovered the egregious fraud.", "at": "那些侵吞公款將近十年的市府官員用盡精心設計的詭計掩蓋罪行，但一位精明的年輕會計師最終揭發了這起惡劣至極的舞弊。"}, {"w": "diffident", "p": "adj.", "d": "Shy and lacking confidence in oneself.", "c": "缺乏自信的；羞怯的", "s": "Though she was the most talented pianist in her class, Hsin-yi was so diffident that she rarely volunteered to perform, often apologizing for minor mistakes that no one in the audience had even noticed.", "t": "雖然欣怡是班上最有天分的鋼琴手，她卻缺乏自信到很少主動上台表演，還常為了台下沒有任何人察覺的小失誤道歉。", "as": "The diffident scholar, unlike his garrulous and bombastic colleagues, rarely spoke at conferences, yet his meticulous research proved more influential than all their grandiloquent speeches.", "at": "這位缺乏自信的學者與他那些多話又浮誇的同事不同，很少在研討會上發言，然而他嚴謹的研究卻比他們所有誇誇其談的演說更具影響力。"}, {"w": "venal", "p": "adj.", "d": "Open to bribery; willing to act dishonestly for money.", "c": "可收買的；貪贓的", "s": "The documentary exposed a network of venal customs officers who accepted cash payments to let smuggled goods pass through the port without inspection, costing the government millions in lost tax revenue every year.", "t": "這部紀錄片揭露了一群貪贓枉法的海關官員，他們收受現金，讓走私貨物不經查驗就通過港口，每年使政府損失數百萬元的稅收。", "as": "The venal official took bribes from contractors while feigning probity in public, a duplicity that was finally exposed when reporters obtained his clandestine bank records.", "at": "這名貪贓的官員一面收受承包商賄賂，一面在公開場合裝出清廉正直的模樣，這種兩面手法終於在記者取得他的秘密銀行紀錄後被揭穿。"}, {"w": "parsimonious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Extremely unwilling to spend money; stingy.", "c": "吝嗇的；極度節儉的", "s": "Even after becoming a millionaire, the parsimonious inventor refused to heat his house in winter, reused old envelopes for years, and once walked five kilometers in the rain rather than pay a small bus fare.", "t": "即使成了百萬富翁，這位吝嗇的發明家冬天仍不肯開暖氣、多年來重複使用舊信封，還曾經冒雨走了五公里路，只為了不付一點點公車費。", "as": "The parsimonious company refused to raise wages even after record profits, and its workers, laboring in squalid conditions for a mere pittance, finally voted to strike.", "at": "這家吝嗇的公司即使創下獲利新高仍拒絕加薪，那些在骯髒環境中只領微薄薪資勞動的工人，終於投票決定罷工。"}, {"w": "pusillanimous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Lacking courage; timid and cowardly.", "c": "膽小的；懦弱的", "s": "Critics described the council's decision to cancel the controversial art exhibition as pusillanimous, arguing that the members had abandoned the artists simply because a few loud protesters threatened to complain on social media.", "t": "批評者認為市議會取消這場具爭議性藝術展的決定十分懦弱，指出議員們只因少數大聲抗議者揚言要在社群媒體上抱怨，就拋棄了這些藝術家。", "as": "Historians have castigated the pusillanimous diplomats who chose to acquiesce to the dictator's territorial demands in 1938, arguing that their timidity only emboldened his aggression across Europe.", "at": "歷史學家嚴厲批評那些在一九三八年選擇默許獨裁者領土要求的懦弱外交官，認為他們的膽怯只助長了他在歐洲各地的侵略。"}, {"w": "extant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Still existing; not destroyed or lost.", "c": "現存的；尚存的", "s": "Of the roughly ninety plays the ancient Greek dramatist is believed to have written, only seven remain extant today, so scholars must reconstruct his career largely from fragments and descriptions by later writers.", "t": "據信這位古希臘劇作家寫過大約九十部劇作，如今僅七部現存，因此學者必須主要依靠殘篇和後世作家的描述來重建他的創作生涯。", "as": "Scholars study the few extant manuscripts with assiduous care, hoping these fragile, water-stained pages will finally explain the abstruse rituals of a civilization long since vanished.", "at": "學者們孜孜不倦地研究那少數現存的手稿，希望這些脆弱且帶有水漬的書頁終能解釋一個早已消逝的文明中那些深奧難解的儀式。"}, {"w": "meretricious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Attractive on the surface but having no real value.", "c": "華而不實的；虛有其表的", "s": "The film won awards for its dazzling special effects, but several critics dismissed it as meretricious, arguing that its spectacular explosions and glamorous costumes only disguised a shallow plot and characters with no emotional depth.", "t": "這部電影以炫目的特效獲獎，但幾位評論家認為它華而不實，指出那些壯觀的爆炸場面與華麗的戲服，只是掩飾了淺薄的劇情和缺乏情感深度的角色。", "as": "The candidate's meretricious rhetoric, full of specious promises and ostentatious displays of patriotism, could not hide from careful voters the vacuous core of his entire political program.", "at": "這位候選人華而不實的言辭充滿似是而非的承諾與炫耀式的愛國表演，卻無法向細心的選民掩飾他整個政治綱領空洞的核心。"}, {"w": "xenophobia", "p": "n.", "d": "Fear or hatred of foreigners or strangers.", "c": "仇外心理；排外情緒", "s": "Sociologists studying the economic crisis found that xenophobia increased sharply as unemployment rose, with some politicians blaming immigrant workers for problems that were actually caused by global market forces and poor domestic policies.", "t": "研究這場經濟危機的社會學家發現，隨著失業率上升，排外情緒急遽升高，一些政治人物把實際上由全球市場力量和國內政策失當所造成的問題，歸咎於移工身上。", "as": "The demagogue shamelessly exploited xenophobia to win votes, and his invective against immigrants engendered a climate of animosity that persisted long after the election had ended.", "at": "這名煽動家無恥地利用排外情緒來拉票，他對移民的惡毒抨擊造成了一種敵對氛圍，在選舉結束後仍久久不散。"}, {"w": "quotidian", "p": "adj.", "d": "Occurring every day; ordinary or commonplace.", "c": "每日的；平凡的", "s": "Rather than painting kings or battles, the Dutch artist preferred quotidian scenes of ordinary life, such as a maid pouring milk or children playing in a courtyard, finding quiet beauty in moments most people overlooked.", "t": "這位荷蘭畫家不畫君王或戰役，而偏好描繪日常生活的平凡場景，例如女僕倒牛奶或孩子在庭院嬉戲，在大多數人忽略的時刻中發現靜謐之美。", "as": "The novelist transforms quotidian events such as morning coffee into poignant meditations on time, revealing that even the most mundane moments can carry an almost ineffable significance.", "at": "這位小說家將早晨的咖啡等日常瑣事轉化為對時間令人動容的沉思，揭示了即使是最平凡的時刻，也可能承載著幾乎難以言喻的意義。"}]}, {"unit": 22, "level": 5, "cards": [{"w": "exigency", "p": "n.", "d": "An urgent need or a situation demanding immediate action.", "c": "緊急情況；迫切需要", "s": "Faced with the exigency of a rapidly spreading wildfire, the county council suspended its usual three-week review process and approved emergency funding for evacuation buses within a single afternoon session last August.", "t": "面對迅速蔓延的野火這一緊急情況，縣議會暫停了平常為期三週的審查程序，並於去年八月在一個下午的會議中便核准了疏散巴士的緊急經費。", "as": "The exigency of the flood rendered the mayor's customarily dilatory approach indefensible, so she eschewed lengthy debate and expedited the release of relief funds within hours.", "at": "洪水的緊急情況使市長一貫拖延的作風站不住腳，因此她避開冗長的辯論，在數小時內便加速撥發救災經費。"}, {"w": "pulchritude", "p": "n.", "d": "Physical beauty, especially of a person.", "c": "美貌；美麗", "s": "Nineteenth-century reviewers lavished attention on the pulchritude of the actress, describing her flawless complexion and graceful features in detail, yet they rarely commented on the intelligence of her performances or her skill in managing the theater company.", "t": "十九世紀的評論家大肆關注那位女演員的美貌，詳細描述她無瑕的膚色與優雅的五官，卻很少評論她表演中展現的智慧，或她經營劇團的能力。", "as": "Critics who once lionized the actress chiefly for her pulchritude later conceded that her erudite interpretations of Shakespeare were the true cynosure of every performance.", "at": "曾經主要因美貌而將那位女演員捧為名人的評論家，後來承認她對莎士比亞博學的詮釋，才是每場演出真正引人矚目的焦點。"}, {"w": "denouement", "p": "n.", "d": "The final resolution of a story's plot or situation.", "c": "結局；（情節的）最終解決", "s": "In the novel's denouement, the long-lost letters are finally discovered in the attic, revealing who betrayed the family decades earlier and allowing the estranged siblings to reconcile in the closing chapter.", "t": "在小說的結局中，失散已久的信件終於在閣樓被發現，揭露了數十年前是誰背叛了這個家族，也讓疏遠的兄弟姊妹得以在最後一章和解。", "as": "The play's denouement felt contrived to critics, who complained that an adventitious inheritance resolved every quandary and that the hero's sudden contrition seemed entirely unearned.", "at": "評論家認為這齣戲的結局顯得牽強，他們抱怨一筆意外得來的遺產解決了所有困境，而主角突如其來的懺悔也顯得完全不合情理。"}, {"w": "fugacious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Lasting only a very short time; fleeting.", "c": "短暫的；轉瞬即逝的", "s": "Because the desert wildflowers are so fugacious, blooming for only a few days after the rare spring rains before withering in the heat, botanists must plan their field trips carefully to photograph them at all.", "t": "由於沙漠野花如此短暫易逝，只在罕見的春雨後綻放幾天，便在高溫中枯萎，植物學家必須仔細規劃野外考察行程，才拍得到它們。", "as": "The poet ruminated in his final collection that celebrity is fugacious and fickle, whereas genuine probity, though rarely praised, earns a respect that outlasts any transient applause.", "at": "詩人在最後一本詩集中沉思道，名氣轉瞬即逝又反覆無常，而真正的正直雖然很少受到讚揚，卻能贏得比任何短暫掌聲都更長久的尊敬。"}, {"w": "turbid", "p": "adj.", "d": "Cloudy or muddy; also confused and unclear.", "c": "混濁的；（思想、文字）混亂不清的", "s": "After the heavy typhoon rains, the normally clear mountain stream became so turbid with silt and debris that the researchers could no longer see the fish they had been counting on the riverbed.", "t": "颱風帶來大雨後，平常清澈的山澗因夾帶泥沙與碎屑而變得極為混濁，研究人員再也看不見他們原本在河床上計數的魚群。", "as": "The professor's turbid prose, filled with abstruse asides and undefined technical terms, left even the most diligent students in the seminar unable to construe his central argument about postwar economic policy.", "at": "這位教授的文字混亂晦澀，充斥著深奧難懂的旁枝論述與未加定義的術語，連研討課上最用功的學生也無法理解他關於戰後經濟政策的核心論點。"}, {"w": "indefeasible", "p": "adj.", "d": "Unable to be annulled, cancelled, or taken away.", "c": "不可廢除的；不可剝奪的", "s": "The nation's founders described freedom of conscience as an indefeasible right, one that no future legislature, court, or emergency decree could ever lawfully revoke, suspend, or transfer to the government under any circumstances.", "t": "這個國家的開國元勳將良心自由描述為一項不可剝奪的權利，任何未來的立法機關、法院或緊急命令，在任何情況下都不得依法撤銷、中止或將其轉移給政府。", "as": "The treaty affirmed the tribe's indefeasible title to its ancestral lands, a provision so unequivocal that later attempts to abrogate it were deemed specious by the court.", "at": "該條約確認了部落對其祖傳土地不可廢除的所有權，此條款明確無誤，以致後來企圖廢除它的主張都被法院認定為似是而非。"}, {"w": "disingenuous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Not sincere; pretending to know less than one does.", "c": "不真誠的；虛偽的", "s": "It was disingenuous of the company to claim it had no idea its factory was polluting the river, since internal emails showed that managers had discussed the contamination reports at several meetings the previous year.", "t": "這家公司聲稱完全不知道其工廠正在污染河川，實在不誠實，因為內部電子郵件顯示，管理階層前一年曾在數次會議中討論過污染報告。", "as": "The senator's disingenuous claim that he had never seen the memo was soon refuted by aides who could corroborate his complicity in the scheme to conceal the budget shortfall.", "at": "這位參議員宣稱從未看過那份備忘錄，這種不誠實的說法很快就被幕僚推翻，他們能證實他參與了隱瞞預算缺口的計畫。"}, {"w": "scurrilous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Making coarse, false claims meant to damage someone's reputation.", "c": "誹謗中傷的；粗俗謾罵的", "s": "During the bitter 1800 presidential campaign, partisan newspapers printed scurrilous pamphlets accusing candidates of crimes they had never committed, spreading rumors so outrageous that some readers stopped trusting the press altogether.", "t": "在激烈的1800年總統選戰中，黨派報紙印行了誹謗中傷的小冊子，指控候選人犯下他們從未犯過的罪行，散播的謠言荒誕到讓部分讀者完全不再信任新聞媒體。", "as": "The scurrilous tabloid sought to vilify the scientist, but her impeccable record and the candor of her public response soon exposed its accusations as baseless.", "at": "那份惡意中傷的小報企圖詆毀這位科學家，但她無懈可擊的紀錄與公開回應時的坦率，很快就揭穿了那些指控毫無根據。"}, {"w": "recrudescence", "p": "n.", "d": "A fresh outbreak of something after a period of inactivity.", "c": "復發；再度爆發", "s": "Public health officials warned that relaxing vaccination requirements too quickly could trigger a recrudescence of measles, a disease that had nearly disappeared from the region but could return rapidly in communities with low immunity.", "t": "公共衛生官員警告，過快放寬疫苗接種規定可能引發麻疹再度爆發；這種疾病在該地區幾乎已絕跡，但在免疫力低的社區可能迅速捲土重來。", "as": "Historians attribute the recrudescence of xenophobia in the United States during the 1920s partly to economic anxiety and partly to demagogues who exploited public animosity toward recent immigrants.", "at": "歷史學家將1920年代美國仇外情緒的再度興起，部分歸因於經濟焦慮，部分歸因於利用大眾對新移民敵意的煽動政客。"}, {"w": "defenestrate", "p": "v.", "d": "To throw someone or something out of a window.", "c": "將…扔出窗外；（喻）將…趕下台", "s": "In 1618, angry Protestant nobles in Prague decided to defenestrate two imperial officials, hurling them from a castle window in a dramatic protest that helped ignite the Thirty Years' War across central Europe.", "t": "1618年，布拉格憤怒的新教貴族決定將兩名帝國官員扔出窗外，他們把官員從城堡窗戶拋下，這場戲劇性的抗議助長了席捲中歐的三十年戰爭。", "as": "When the board voted to defenestrate the chief executive, critics called the move a vindictive machination by rival directors rather than a prudent response to falling profits.", "at": "董事會投票將執行長趕下台時，批評者稱此舉是對手董事懷恨報復的陰謀，而非因應獲利下滑的審慎對策。"}, {"w": "dilatory", "p": "adj.", "d": "Slow to act; tending to cause delay.", "c": "拖延的；遲緩的", "s": "The city's dilatory response to repeated complaints about the cracked bridge, which officials postponed inspecting for nearly two years, drew sharp criticism after a section of the railing finally collapsed into the river.", "t": "市政府對橋梁龜裂的多次投訴反應遲緩，官員將檢查延宕了將近兩年，直到一段欄杆終於崩落河中，才招致嚴厲批評。", "as": "The committee's dilatory tactics, which included interminable debates and gratuitous procedural objections, ultimately served to protract the negotiations until the federal funding deadline for the project had quietly passed.", "at": "委員會採取拖延戰術，包括沒完沒了的辯論與毫無必要的程序異議，最終拖長了協商，直到該計畫的聯邦經費期限悄然過去。"}, {"w": "vilify", "p": "v.", "d": "To speak or write about someone in an abusive way.", "c": "詆毀；中傷", "s": "Rather than engaging with the economist's actual data, her opponents chose to vilify her personally, calling her dishonest and incompetent in interviews even though none of them had read her report carefully.", "t": "她的反對者沒有針對這位經濟學家的實際數據進行討論，反而選擇對她進行人身詆毀，在訪談中稱她不誠實又無能，儘管他們沒有一個人仔細讀過她的報告。", "as": "Pamphleteers who once vilified the reformer as a dangerous iconoclast later venerated him as a visionary once his policies demonstrated undeniable efficacy in reducing child poverty.", "at": "曾把這位改革者詆毀為危險的反傳統者的小冊子作者們，在他的政策證明確實能有效減少兒童貧窮之後，轉而將他奉為有遠見的人而加以崇敬。"}, {"w": "phlegmatic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Calm and unemotional; not easily excited or upset.", "c": "冷靜的；沉著的；不易激動的", "s": "Even when the experiment exploded in a cloud of smoke and alarms began ringing, the phlegmatic lab supervisor simply opened the windows, checked that everyone was safe, and calmly began writing up the incident report.", "t": "即使實驗在一團煙霧中爆炸、警報大作，那位冷靜沉著的實驗室主管也只是打開窗戶、確認大家都平安，然後從容地開始撰寫事故報告。", "as": "Her phlegmatic temperament proved an asset during the prolonged crisis; while colleagues grew irascible and voluble, she maintained an equanimity that steadied the entire negotiating team.", "at": "在這場漫長的危機中，她冷靜沉著的性格成了一大優勢；當同事們變得暴躁又喋喋不休時，她始終保持鎮定，穩住了整個談判團隊。"}, {"w": "adventitious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Happening by chance or coming from outside; not inherent.", "c": "偶然的；外來的；非固有的", "s": "The archaeologists stressed that the coins found near the temple were adventitious rather than part of the original offerings, since soil analysis showed they had been washed into the site by floods centuries later.", "t": "考古學家強調，在神廟附近發現的錢幣是偶然外來之物，而非原始供品的一部分，因為土壤分析顯示它們是在數百年後才被洪水沖進遺址的。", "as": "The novelist insisted that the adventitious encounter in chapter three was not a gratuitous plot device but a deliberate attempt to juxtapose two seemingly incongruous worlds.", "at": "小說家堅稱，第三章中那場偶然的相遇並非多餘的情節安排，而是刻意將兩個看似格格不入的世界並置。"}, {"w": "desiccated", "p": "adj.", "d": "Completely dried out; lacking moisture or vitality.", "c": "乾燥的；脫水的；（喻）枯燥乏味的", "s": "After months without rain, the once-fertile farmland had become so desiccated that deep cracks split the soil and the farmers' remaining crops withered before they could produce any grain for the harvest.", "t": "數月未降雨後，曾經肥沃的農地變得極度乾涸，土壤裂出深深的縫隙，農民僅存的作物還沒結出任何穀粒就枯萎了。", "as": "The museum's desiccated specimens, preserved for centuries in the arid tombs, allowed scientists to corroborate conjectures about ancient diets that had long been dismissed as mere supposition.", "at": "博物館裡那些在乾燥墓穴中保存了數百年的脫水標本，讓科學家得以證實關於古代飲食的推測，而這些推測長久以來一直被視為純屬臆測。"}, {"w": "comity", "p": "n.", "d": "Courtesy and mutual respect, especially between nations.", "c": "禮讓；（國際間的）友好禮讓", "s": "In a spirit of comity, the two neighboring countries agreed to recognize each other's court rulings and professional licenses, a gesture of mutual respect that made it easier for citizens to work across the border.", "t": "本著相互禮讓的精神，兩個鄰國同意承認彼此的法院判決與專業執照，這種相互尊重的表現讓人民更容易跨境工作。", "as": "Diplomats hoped the summit would restore comity between the rival states, but the foreign minister's acerbic remarks and the envoys' mutual recriminations soon dashed any prospect of rapprochement.", "at": "外交官原本希望這場高峰會能恢復兩個敵對國家之間的友好禮讓，但外交部長尖酸刻薄的言論以及代表們的相互指責，很快就讓和解的希望化為泡影。"}, {"w": "specious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Seemingly plausible or correct but actually false.", "c": "似是而非的；貌似有理的", "s": "The advertisement's argument seemed convincing at first, but the statistics professor showed her class that it was specious, relying on a tiny sample and ignoring several factors that completely undermined its conclusion.", "t": "這則廣告的論點乍看之下很有說服力，但統計學教授向她的學生證明它其實似是而非，只依賴極小的樣本，並忽略了幾個足以完全推翻其結論的因素。", "as": "The lawyer's specious reasoning, an artful blend of sophistry and hyperbole, initially beguiled the jury, but the judge's carefully worded instructions exposed its fatal logical flaws.", "at": "律師似是而非的推理巧妙融合了詭辯與誇大，起初迷惑了陪審團，但法官措辭嚴謹的指示揭露了其中致命的邏輯漏洞。"}, {"w": "noisome", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having an extremely offensive smell; harmful or disgusting.", "c": "惡臭的；有害的", "s": "Residents near the landfill complained that a noisome odor of rotting garbage drifted into their homes every summer evening, forcing them to keep their windows closed even during the hottest weeks of the year.", "t": "垃圾掩埋場附近的居民抱怨，每到夏天傍晚，腐爛垃圾的惡臭便飄進他們家中，逼得他們即使在一年中最炎熱的幾週也得緊閉窗戶。", "as": "Nineteenth-century reformers described the noisome, squalid tenements of London, where indigent families shared a single fetid courtyard, to galvanize public support for the city's first comprehensive sanitation laws.", "at": "十九世紀的改革者描述倫敦惡臭污穢的廉價公寓——貧困家庭在那裡共用一個臭氣熏天的庭院——藉此激發大眾對該市第一部全面性衛生法規的支持。"}, {"w": "calumny", "p": "n.", "d": "A false statement made to damage someone's reputation.", "c": "誹謗；中傷", "s": "The young senator refused to dignify the anonymous calumny with a reply, trusting that voters would recognize the fabricated story about his finances as a deliberate attempt to damage his reputation before the election.", "t": "這位年輕的參議員不屑回應那則匿名的誹謗，他相信選民會看穿那個關於他財務狀況的捏造故事，是有人刻意在選前損害他的名聲。", "as": "Though subjected to years of calumny in the state-controlled press, the dissident never resorted to invective herself; her stoic dignity eventually won over even former detractors.", "at": "儘管多年來在官方控制的媒體上遭受誹謗，這位異議人士從未以惡言回擊；她堅忍的尊嚴最終甚至贏得了昔日批評者的支持。"}, {"w": "excoriate", "p": "v.", "d": "To criticize someone or something very severely.", "c": "嚴厲批評；痛斥", "s": "In a scathing editorial, the newspaper went on to excoriate the governor for cutting school funding while approving raises for his own staff, calling the decision both hypocritical and harmful to the state's children.", "t": "在一篇措辭嚴厲的社論中，該報進一步痛斥州長一面削減學校經費、一面為自己的幕僚加薪，稱這項決定既虛偽又傷害了全州的孩子。", "as": "Reviewers excoriated the memoir as a sanctimonious exercise in self-promotion, noting that its grandiloquent prose could not obscure the author's evident duplicity toward former colleagues.", "at": "書評家痛斥這本回憶錄是一場自以為是的自我吹捧，並指出其浮誇的文字掩蓋不了作者對昔日同事明顯的表裡不一。"}]}, {"unit": 23, "level": 5, "cards": [{"w": "lassitude", "p": "n.", "d": "A state of physical or mental tiredness; lack of energy.", "c": "疲倦；倦怠；無精打采", "s": "A lingering lassitude followed her bout of influenza; for weeks she lacked the energy to climb stairs, concentrate on her reading, or even hold a conversation for more than a few minutes without resting.", "t": "她得了流感之後，揮之不去的倦怠感一直纏著她；好幾週來，她連爬樓梯、專心閱讀，甚至與人交談幾分鐘而不休息的力氣都沒有。", "as": "The oppressive summer heat induced a pervasive lassitude among the delegates, and the conference soon devolved into a series of banal speeches and perfunctory debates.", "at": "悶熱的夏日高溫讓與會代表普遍感到倦怠，會議很快就淪為一連串陳腐的演說與敷衍了事的辯論。"}, {"w": "traduce", "p": "v.", "d": "To damage someone's reputation by telling lies about them.", "c": "誹謗；中傷", "s": "The biographer accused earlier historians of trying to traduce the queen, arguing that they had invented stories of cruelty and greed simply to make her rivals appear more heroic by comparison.", "t": "這位傳記作家指控早期的歷史學家企圖詆毀這位女王，認為他們捏造了殘酷與貪婪的故事，只為了讓她的對手相形之下顯得更英勇。", "as": "Columnists who traduced the whistle-blower as a mercenary opportunist were later forced to issue retractions when documents vindicated her and exposed the company's mendacious executives.", "at": "那些把這位吹哨者詆毀為唯利是圖的投機分子的專欄作家，後來在文件證明她清白並揭露公司高層說謊成性之後，被迫發表更正聲明。"}, {"w": "dishabille", "p": "n.", "d": "The state of being casually or only partly dressed.", "c": "衣著隨便；衣衫不整", "s": "The famous portrait shows the poet in dishabille, wearing a loose dressing gown and slippers with his hair uncombed, as though the artist had surprised him at his writing desk early one morning.", "t": "這幅著名的肖像畫描繪詩人衣著隨便的模樣：他穿著寬鬆的晨袍和拖鞋、頭髮未梳，彷彿畫家某天清晨在他的書桌前出其不意地撞見了他。", "as": "Startled by the fire alarm, the guests gathered on the lawn in various states of dishabille, a scene the droll innkeeper later described with considerable levity.", "at": "被火警驚動的房客們衣衫不整地聚集在草坪上，那位風趣的旅店老闆後來相當輕鬆詼諧地描述了這一幕。"}, {"w": "saturnalia", "p": "n.", "d": "A period of wild, unrestrained celebration and revelry.", "c": "狂歡；狂歡節", "s": "When the team won its first championship in fifty years, the quiet college town erupted into a three-day saturnalia of street parties, fireworks, and parades that left the main square littered with confetti.", "t": "當球隊贏得五十年來第一座冠軍時，這座寧靜的大學城爆發了一場為期三天的狂歡，街頭派對、煙火與遊行不斷，讓主廣場上滿地彩紙。", "as": "The festival, once a solemn harvest rite, had degenerated into a noisy saturnalia, and village elders began to remonstrate against the ostentatious spending and nightly cacophony.", "at": "這個節慶原本是莊嚴的豐收儀式，如今已墮落為一場喧鬧的狂歡，村中長老開始抗議那些鋪張炫耀的花費與夜夜不休的嘈雜聲。"}, {"w": "extirpate", "p": "v.", "d": "To destroy completely; to root out.", "c": "根除；滅絕", "s": "Conservation officers launched an ambitious program to extirpate the invasive rats from the island, hoping that once every last rodent was gone, the native seabirds would be able to nest safely again.", "t": "保育官員展開了一項雄心勃勃的計畫，要將入侵的老鼠從島上徹底根除，希望一旦最後一隻鼠類消失，原生海鳥就能再次安全築巢。", "as": "The new governor vowed to extirpate the nepotism that had long plagued the provincial finance ministry, but entrenched officials, skilled at bureaucratic subterfuge, proved remarkably intractable.", "at": "新任省長誓言根除長期困擾省財政部的任人唯親之風，但那些根深蒂固、擅長官僚式推託伎倆的官員卻出奇地難以對付。"}, {"w": "flagitious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Extremely wicked, criminal, or shamefully villainous.", "c": "極惡的；罪大惡極的", "s": "The war crimes tribunal described the bombing of the hospital as a flagitious act, one so deliberately cruel and shocking that it violated every principle of international law and basic human decency.", "t": "戰爭罪法庭將轟炸醫院的行為形容為罪大惡極的暴行，其蓄意殘酷與駭人程度違反了國際法與基本人性尊嚴的每一項原則。", "as": "The tyrant's flagitious reign, marked by mass arrests and the ruthless persecution of every dissident, was finally condemned by historians as an egregious betrayal of the revolution's ideals.", "at": "這位暴君罪大惡極的統治以大規模逮捕和無情迫害每一位異議人士為特徵，最終被歷史學家譴責為對革命理想極其惡劣的背叛。"}, {"w": "peripatetic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Traveling from place to place; not staying in one location.", "c": "巡迴的；四處奔走的", "s": "As a peripatetic music teacher, Ms. Lin spent each week driving among five rural elementary schools, carrying her violin and sheet music in the back of her car from one village to the next.", "t": "身為巡迴音樂老師，林老師每週開車往返於五所偏鄉國小之間，把她的小提琴和樂譜放在車子後座，從一個村莊奔波到下一個村莊。", "as": "The peripatetic scholar, who had lectured on four continents, remained an itinerant teacher by choice, eschewing the sinecure of a tenured post in favor of perpetual travel.", "at": "這位曾在四大洲講學的遊歷學者，出於自願始終當個巡迴教師，寧可永遠四處旅行，也不要終身教職那種清閒的閒差。"}, {"w": "cachinnate", "p": "v.", "d": "To laugh loudly and without restraint.", "c": "大聲狂笑；哄笑", "s": "The comedian's absurd impression of the principal caused the entire auditorium to cachinnate, with students laughing so loudly and uncontrollably that the next performer had to wait several minutes before beginning her act.", "t": "這位喜劇演員對校長荒謬的模仿讓整個禮堂哄堂大笑，學生們笑得震天價響、停不下來，下一位表演者只好等了好幾分鐘才開始她的節目。", "as": "Even the most taciturn members of the audience began to cachinnate at the playwright's droll satire, though a few sanctimonious critics sat in stony silence.", "at": "連觀眾中最沉默寡言的人都對這位劇作家詼諧逗趣的諷刺劇放聲狂笑，只有少數自命清高的評論家面無表情地坐著不吭聲。"}, {"w": "manumit", "p": "v.", "d": "To release someone from slavery.", "c": "解放（奴隸）；使獲得自由", "s": "In his will, the eighteenth-century planter chose to manumit all of the enslaved people on his estate, granting them legal freedom and leaving each family a small plot of land on which to farm.", "t": "在遺囑中，這位十八世紀的莊園主選擇解放莊園上所有被奴役的人，賦予他們法律上的自由，並留給每個家庭一小塊可耕種的土地。", "as": "Although he publicly professed altruism, the merchant refused to manumit his own servants, a duplicity that abolitionist pamphleteers were quick to excoriate in scathing editorials.", "at": "這位商人雖然公開宣稱自己樂善好施，卻拒絕解放自己的奴僕，廢奴主義的小冊子作者很快就在措辭尖銳的社論中痛斥他這種表裡不一的行徑。"}, {"w": "expiation", "p": "n.", "d": "The act of making amends for wrongdoing; atonement.", "c": "贖罪；補過", "s": "As an act of expiation for the factory's decades of pollution, the company's new owners funded the cleanup of the river and built a public park along the banks where the waste had once been dumped.", "t": "為了彌補這間工廠數十年來造成的污染以示贖罪，公司的新業主出資清理河川，並在過去傾倒廢棄物的河岸邊興建了一座公園。", "as": "The novel's protagonist seeks expiation for his youthful peccadilloes, yet his contrition is so showy that readers suspect his penance is merely another form of narcissism.", "at": "小說主角為年輕時犯下的小過錯尋求贖罪，但他的悔悟表現得如此招搖，讓讀者懷疑他的懺悔不過是另一種自戀。"}, {"w": "jejune", "p": "adj.", "d": "Naive and simplistic; also dull and lacking substance.", "c": "幼稚的；膚淺的；枯燥無味的", "s": "The professor dismissed the student's essay on world hunger as jejune, noting that its simple claim that farmers should just grow more food ignored the complex political and economic causes of the problem.", "t": "教授認為那名學生關於世界飢荒的文章過於幼稚膚淺，並指出文中「農民只要多種糧食就好」的簡單主張，忽略了這個問題背後複雜的政治與經濟成因。", "as": "Critics found the young director's debut film jejune, its puerile humor and banal dialogue a far cry from the trenchant social commentary promised in the trailer.", "at": "評論家認為這位年輕導演的處女作幼稚膚淺，片中幼稚的笑點與陳腔濫調的對白，與預告片所承諾的犀利社會評論相去甚遠。"}, {"w": "paucity", "p": "n.", "d": "The presence of something in very small quantities; scarcity.", "c": "缺乏；不足；稀少", "s": "The paucity of reliable records from the ancient kingdom makes it difficult for historians to determine even basic facts, such as how many kings ruled or how large the capital city actually was.", "t": "這個古王國可靠的紀錄極為稀少，讓歷史學家難以確定即使是最基本的事實，例如究竟有多少位國王統治過，或首都實際上有多大。", "as": "Given the paucity of corroborating evidence, the panel regarded the researcher's sweeping claims as mere conjecture and urged her to temper her hyperbole in future publications.", "at": "鑑於佐證證據極度缺乏，審查小組將這名研究人員的廣泛主張視為純屬推測，並敦促她在日後的發表中收斂誇大之詞。"}, {"w": "minatory", "p": "adj.", "d": "Expressing or suggesting a threat; menacing.", "c": "威脅的；恐嚇的", "s": "The dark clouds massing over the harbor looked increasingly minatory, and the fishermen, recognizing the threat of an approaching storm, hurried to secure their boats before the first gusts of wind arrived.", "t": "聚集在港口上空的烏雲看起來越來越具威脅性，漁民們意識到暴風雨即將來臨，趕在第一陣強風到來前匆忙繫緊船隻。", "as": "The dictator's minatory speeches, filled with bombastic warnings and thinly veiled threats against dissidents, were clearly intended to intimidate rather than to edify his listeners.", "at": "獨裁者那些充滿威脅意味的演說，滿是浮誇的警告與幾乎不加掩飾地針對異議人士的恐嚇，其目的顯然是恐嚇聽眾，而非教化他們。"}, {"w": "putative", "p": "adj.", "d": "Generally believed or assumed to be; supposed.", "c": "公認的；推定的；被認為的", "s": "The putative author of the anonymous eighteenth-century pamphlet, long assumed to be a famous statesman, may actually have been his secretary, according to a new analysis of the handwriting and vocabulary.", "t": "這本十八世紀匿名小冊子的推定作者，長久以來被認為是一位著名政治家，但根據對筆跡與用字的新分析，真正的作者可能是他的祕書。", "as": "The putative benefits of the new drug, touted as a panacea by its manufacturer, proved largely spurious when independent researchers at three universities scrutinized the clinical data.", "at": "這款新藥被製造商吹捧為萬靈丹，但當三所大學的獨立研究人員仔細檢視臨床數據後，其所謂的療效大多被證實是虛假的。"}, {"w": "lucubration", "p": "n.", "d": "Laborious study or writing, especially late at night.", "c": "（深夜）苦讀；苦心鑽研；苦心之作", "s": "After many years of late-night lucubration by candlelight, the self-taught astronomer finally published a detailed catalog of comets, an achievement that astonished professional scientists who had never heard of him.", "t": "經過許多年在燭光下深夜苦讀鑽研，這位自學的天文學家終於出版了一份詳盡的彗星目錄，這項成就讓從未聽說過他的專業科學家們大為驚訝。", "as": "The philosopher's lucubrations, though learned, were so abstruse and prolix that even his most assiduous disciples struggled to finish a single volume of his collected works.", "at": "這位哲學家的苦心著述雖然學識淵博，卻深奧冗長到連他最勤奮的弟子都難以讀完他全集中的任何一冊。"}, {"w": "troglodyte", "p": "n.", "d": "A cave dweller; a person seen as primitive or reclusive.", "c": "穴居人；守舊落伍或離群索居的人", "s": "My brother lives like a troglodyte during exam season, hiding in his dark basement room for weeks, refusing to answer the phone, and emerging only occasionally to grab instant noodles from the kitchen.", "t": "每到考試季，我哥哥就過得像個穴居人，好幾週躲在陰暗的地下室房間裡，不接電話，只偶爾出來到廚房拿碗泡麵。", "as": "Dismissed as a technological troglodyte for refusing to own a smartphone, the novelist responded with gentle levity, arguing that his reclusive habits fostered the pensive solitude his work required.", "at": "這位小說家因拒絕擁有智慧型手機而被譏為科技原始人，他以溫和輕鬆的口吻回應，主張自己的隱居習慣正好培養出創作所需、適於沉思的孤獨。"}, {"w": "aleatory", "p": "adj.", "d": "Depending on chance, luck, or random outcomes.", "c": "偶然的；憑運氣的；不確定的", "s": "The composer created an aleatory piece in which performers roll dice to decide the order of the musical passages, so that no two concerts ever sound exactly alike, even when the same orchestra plays it.", "t": "這位作曲家創作了一首機遇音樂作品，演奏者以擲骰子決定各樂段的順序，因此即使由同一個樂團演奏，也沒有任何兩場音樂會聽起來完全相同。", "as": "Because farming in the region was so aleatory, dependent on capricious monsoons, prudent families diversified their income rather than wagering everything on a single harvest.", "at": "由於該地區的農業極度仰賴運氣、受制於變化無常的季風，審慎的家庭會分散收入來源，而不是把一切都押在一次收成上。"}, {"w": "farrago", "p": "n.", "d": "A confused mixture of unrelated things; hodgepodge.", "c": "大雜燴；混雜物", "s": "The committee rejected the proposal as a farrago of unrelated ideas, pointing out that it mixed plans for a new stadium, a tax reform, and a poetry festival without explaining how any of them connected.", "t": "委員會駁回了這項提案，認為它是由毫不相干的想法拼湊而成的大雜燴，並指出提案把新體育場、稅制改革與詩歌節的計畫混在一起，卻沒有說明它們之間有何關聯。", "as": "The senator's speech was a farrago of half-truths and platitudes, so riddled with non sequiturs that even sympathetic journalists found it impossible to paraphrase coherently.", "at": "這位參議員的演說是半真半假之言與陳腔濫調的大雜燴，充滿前後不連貫的推論，連同情他的記者都無法條理清楚地轉述其內容。"}, {"w": "cynosure", "p": "n.", "d": "A person or thing that is the center of attention.", "c": "注目的焦點；眾人矚目的對象", "s": "With its glittering glass dome and dramatic lighting, the new concert hall quickly became the cynosure of the city's skyline, drawing photographers and tourists from around the world to admire its design.", "t": "這座新音樂廳憑藉閃耀的玻璃圓頂與戲劇性的燈光，迅速成為城市天際線的焦點，吸引來自世界各地的攝影師與遊客前來欣賞其設計。", "as": "The young violinist, the cynosure of the gala, accepted the accolades with a diffident smile, seemingly oblivious to the obsequious patrons jostling for her attention.", "at": "這位年輕的小提琴家是晚會上眾所矚目的焦點，她帶著羞怯的微笑接受讚譽，似乎完全沒注意到那些爭相討好、搶著吸引她注意的贊助者。"}, {"w": "badinage", "p": "n.", "d": "Playful, witty conversation; good-humored teasing.", "c": "打趣；逗趣的玩笑話", "s": "The two old friends who hosted the radio show were known for their lively badinage, teasing each other about their terrible singing and fashion choices in a way that listeners found warm and funny rather than mean.", "t": "主持這個廣播節目的兩位老朋友以活潑逗趣的鬥嘴聞名，他們互相取笑對方糟糕的歌聲與穿衣品味，聽眾覺得這樣的打趣溫馨又好笑，而非刻薄。", "as": "The novelist's dialogue sparkles with urbane badinage between the aging siblings, yet beneath their jovial exchanges lies a poignant meditation on loneliness, regret, and loss.", "at": "這位小說家筆下年邁手足之間的對話洋溢著文雅的打趣，但在他們歡快的交談底下，卻是對孤獨、遺憾與失落的深刻沉思。"}]}, {"unit": 24, "level": 5, "cards": [{"w": "hieratic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Relating to priests; priestly or highly formal and stylized.", "c": "祭司的；神聖莊嚴的", "s": "Unlike the lively, naturalistic figures painted on village pottery, the statues guarding the temple entrance were rigid and solemn, their hieratic poses reflecting centuries of priestly tradition that dictated exactly how gods and pharaohs must be portrayed.", "t": "與村落陶器上生動寫實的人物圖像不同，守衛神廟入口的雕像僵直而莊嚴，其祭司式的姿態反映了數百年來的宗教傳統，這些傳統嚴格規定了神祇與法老必須如何被描繪。", "as": "The museum's curator argued that the hieratic gestures of the figures were not merely ornamental but conveyed an esoteric code that only an erudite viewer could construe.", "at": "博物館策展人主張，這些人物祭司般莊嚴的手勢並非單純裝飾，而是傳達了一套只有學識淵博的觀者才能解讀的深奧密碼。"}, {"w": "saturnine", "p": "adj.", "d": "Gloomy, sullen, and bitter in temperament.", "c": "陰沉的；憂鬱的", "s": "Although the novelist was charming in his letters, visitors who met him in person described a saturnine man who rarely smiled, spoke in brief, gloomy sentences, and seemed perpetually weighed down by some private disappointment.", "t": "雖然這位小說家在信中迷人風趣，但當面見過他的訪客卻形容他是個陰沉憂鬱的人，鮮少微笑，說話簡短而沮喪，彷彿總被某種私人的失望所壓垮。", "as": "The saturnine critic, whose reviews were famously acerbic, regularly dismissed even the most laudable performances of the season as jejune exercises unworthy of serious attention from thoughtful audiences.", "at": "這位陰沉的評論家以尖酸刻薄的評論聞名，經常把當季最值得讚賞的演出也貶為枯燥乏味、不值得有思想的觀眾認真看待的作品。"}, {"w": "execrate", "p": "v.", "d": "To denounce bitterly; to detest and curse.", "c": "痛罵；憎惡", "s": "Many nineteenth-century reformers came to execrate the factory owners who forced young children to work fourteen-hour shifts, publicly cursing them in pamphlets and speeches as the most heartless men of their age.", "t": "許多十九世紀的改革者開始痛斥那些強迫幼童每天工作十四小時的工廠主，在小冊子與演說中公開咒罵他們是那個時代最冷酷無情的人。", "as": "Though citizens came to execrate the oligarchy for its shameless nepotism, few dared to remonstrate openly while its secret police still watched every street corner.", "at": "儘管民眾開始痛恨這個寡頭政權明目張膽的任人唯親，但在祕密警察仍監視著每個街角的情況下，很少人敢公開抗議。"}, {"w": "vitiate", "p": "v.", "d": "To spoil, weaken, or make legally invalid.", "c": "損害；使無效", "s": "The researchers discovered that a single contaminated sample could vitiate the entire study, since the faulty data would distort every later calculation and make the published conclusions about the vaccine's effectiveness unreliable.", "t": "研究人員發現，單一受污染的樣本就可能使整個研究失效，因為錯誤的數據會扭曲後續所有的計算，使已發表的疫苗效力結論變得不可靠。", "as": "The judge ruled that the surreptitious changes to the contract would vitiate the entire agreement, rendering its most salient provisions legally void and unenforceable in any court.", "at": "法官裁定，對合約所做的祕密修改會使整份協議失效，令其中最重要的條款在法律上無效，且在任何法院都無法強制執行。"}, {"w": "venial", "p": "adj.", "d": "Minor and easily forgiven; pardonable.", "c": "可原諒的；輕微的", "s": "The editor treated a misplaced comma as a venial error that could be quickly corrected, but she considered plagiarism an unforgivable offense that would end any writer's relationship with the magazine.", "t": "這位編輯把放錯位置的逗號視為可以迅速修正的小錯，但她認為抄襲是不可原諒的罪行，任何作家一旦犯下，與雜誌的合作關係就會就此終止。", "as": "Compared with the egregious fraud committed by the board, the intern's tardiness was a venial lapse, a mere peccadillo hardly worth mentioning in the final report.", "at": "與董事會所犯下的嚴重詐欺相比，那名實習生的遲到只是可以原諒的小過失，不過是微不足道的小毛病，幾乎不值得在最終報告中提及。"}, {"w": "risible", "p": "adj.", "d": "So foolish or absurd that it causes laughter.", "c": "可笑的；荒唐的", "s": "The company's claim that its new energy drink could improve students' test scores by fifty percent was so risible that the science teacher read the advertisement aloud to her class simply to make everyone laugh.", "t": "這家公司宣稱其新款能量飲料能讓學生的考試成績提高百分之五十，這種說法實在太荒謬可笑，以至於自然老師把廣告大聲唸給全班聽，只為了逗大家發笑。", "as": "The candidate's grandiloquent promises were so risible that even his most gullible supporters began to doubt the bombastic speeches he delivered at every rally across the state.", "at": "這位候選人浮誇的承諾荒謬可笑，以至於連他最容易受騙的支持者都開始懷疑他在全州每場造勢大會上發表的誇大演說。"}, {"w": "lionize", "p": "v.", "d": "To treat someone as a celebrity or hero.", "c": "把……捧為名人；奉為偶像", "s": "After her research on drought-resistant rice saved thousands of farms, the scientist was surprised to see newspapers and talk shows lionize her, treating a once-unknown laboratory worker like a famous movie star.", "t": "在她關於抗旱稻米的研究拯救了數千座農場之後，這位科學家驚訝地發現報紙和談話節目都把她捧為名人，將一個原本默默無聞的實驗室工作者當作電影明星般看待。", "as": "The media tend to lionize young entrepreneurs, yet such adulation can be ephemeral, vanishing as soon as an ostensible success proves to be illusory under closer scrutiny.", "at": "媒體往往將年輕創業家捧為名人，然而這樣的崇拜可能轉瞬即逝，一旦表面上的成功經仔細檢視後被證明是假象，便會隨即消失。"}, {"w": "contretemps", "p": "n.", "d": "An awkward, embarrassing mishap or minor disagreement.", "c": "令人尷尬的意外；小爭執", "s": "The diplomatic dinner was nearly ruined by a minor contretemps when the ambassador's translator mispronounced the host's name, causing an awkward silence before both sides laughed and agreed to forget the embarrassing incident.", "t": "這場外交晚宴差點因一段小插曲而泡湯：大使的翻譯念錯了主人的名字，造成一陣尷尬的沉默，直到雙方都笑了出來，同意忘掉這件難堪的事。", "as": "The brief contretemps between the two senators, though widely reported, was soon followed by a rapprochement that allowed them to concur on the final budget.", "at": "兩位參議員之間短暫的口角雖然被廣泛報導，但很快便迎來了和解，使他們得以在最終預算案上達成共識。"}, {"w": "rodomontade", "p": "n.", "d": "Boastful, bragging talk or behavior.", "c": "大話；吹牛", "s": "Behind the general's rodomontade about crushing the enemy in a single afternoon lay a far weaker reality: his troops were exhausted, poorly supplied, and outnumbered, facts his loud boasting could not conceal for long.", "t": "在這位將軍揚言要在一個下午內擊潰敵軍的大話背後，是遠為不堪的現實：他的部隊精疲力竭、補給不足且寡不敵眾，而這些事實是他高聲吹噓也無法長久掩蓋的。", "as": "Voters tired of the governor's rodomontade, preferring a laconic challenger whose modest promises seemed more tenable than the incumbent's endless and self-congratulatory boasting about his past achievements.", "at": "選民厭倦了州長的大話，轉而支持一位寡言的挑戰者，因為比起現任者沒完沒了、自我吹捧過往政績的誇誇其談，這位挑戰者務實的承諾顯得更站得住腳。"}, {"w": "hebetude", "p": "n.", "d": "Mental dullness or sluggishness; lethargy.", "c": "遲鈍；呆滯", "s": "After weeks of sleeping only four hours a night before final exams, Marcus fell into a state of hebetude so deep that he could stare at a simple math problem for ten minutes without understanding it.", "t": "期末考前連續數週每晚只睡四個小時後，馬可斯陷入極度遲鈍的狀態，甚至能盯著一道簡單的數學題看上十分鐘仍無法理解。", "as": "The lethargy and hebetude that followed the long winter made the villagers seem phlegmatic to visitors, though spring would soon restore their natural ebullience and good humor.", "at": "漫長冬季過後的倦怠與遲鈍，讓村民在訪客眼中顯得冷淡無精打采，不過春天很快就會讓他們恢復與生俱來的熱情與好心情。"}, {"w": "sanguine", "p": "adj.", "d": "Cheerfully optimistic and confident, especially in difficult times.", "c": "樂觀的；充滿自信的", "s": "Despite the hurricane's damage to the harbor, the mayor remained sanguine about the town's future, confidently predicting that tourism would recover within a year and that the rebuilt docks would be stronger than before.", "t": "儘管颶風重創了港口，市長對小鎮的未來依然樂觀，充滿信心地預測觀光業將在一年內復甦，而重建後的碼頭會比以前更加堅固。", "as": "Even the most sanguine economists conceded that the recovery would be protracted, since the dearth of skilled workers posed an intractable problem for manufacturers nationwide.", "at": "即使是最樂觀的經濟學家也承認，經濟復甦將會曠日費時，因為技術工人的短缺對全國的製造業者而言是個棘手的難題。"}, {"w": "deipnosophist", "p": "n.", "d": "A person skilled in witty conversation at meals.", "c": "善於席間談話的人；餐桌健談者", "s": "A gifted deipnosophist, the professor could keep an entire dinner table entertained for hours, moving effortlessly from Roman history to modern poetry while guests forgot their meals and leaned in to hear more.", "t": "這位教授是個善於席間談話的高手，能讓整桌賓客聽得津津有味好幾個小時，從羅馬史一路自然地聊到現代詩，讓客人們忘了吃飯，紛紛探身想聽更多。", "as": "The urbane deipnosophist, whose badinage was always droll yet never unkind, became the most sought-after guest at the city's many literary banquets and formal diplomatic dinners.", "at": "這位溫文儒雅、擅長席間談話的人，其妙語總是逗趣卻從不刻薄，因此成為該城眾多文學宴會與正式外交晚宴上最受歡迎的賓客。"}, {"w": "frangible", "p": "adj.", "d": "Easily broken or shattered; fragile.", "c": "易碎的；脆弱的", "s": "Museum workers wrapped the ancient glass vases in several layers of padding, because the frangible objects had survived two thousand years underground but could shatter from a single careless bump during shipping.", "t": "博物館人員用好幾層襯墊包裹這些古代玻璃花瓶，因為這些易碎的文物雖然在地底保存了兩千年，卻可能在運送途中因一次不小心的碰撞而碎裂。", "as": "The treaty proved as frangible as the alliance it created, collapsing under the vicissitudes of war despite the diplomats' assiduous efforts to preserve it at all costs.", "at": "這份條約就像它所締造的同盟一樣脆弱，儘管外交官們不遺餘力地想不惜一切代價維護它，它仍在戰爭的變局中瓦解。"}, {"w": "apodictic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Absolutely certain and clearly proven; beyond dispute.", "c": "無可爭辯的；確鑿的", "s": "In geometry class, students learn that a valid proof is apodictic: once each step follows logically from the last, the conclusion is not merely likely but absolutely certain, beyond any reasonable dispute.", "t": "在幾何課上，學生學到有效的證明是無可辯駁的：只要每個步驟都合乎邏輯地承接前一步，結論就不只是可能成立，而是絕對確定、毫無爭議的。", "as": "The professor's tone was so apodictic that students hesitated to cavil, even though some suspected his categorical claims rested on fallacious reasoning about ancient trade routes.", "at": "這位教授的語氣是如此斬釘截鐵，以至於學生們不敢吹毛求疵，儘管有些人懷疑他那些絕對的論斷是建立在關於古代貿易路線的謬誤推理之上。"}, {"w": "fulminate", "p": "v.", "d": "To criticize or protest loudly and angrily.", "c": "猛烈抨擊；怒斥", "s": "Every time the city council approved another parking lot, the elderly environmentalist would rise at the public meeting to fulminate against the decision, shouting that the officials were destroying the last green spaces in town.", "t": "每當市議會批准另一座停車場時，這位年長的環保人士就會在公開會議上起身大肆抨擊這項決定，高喊官員們正在摧毀鎮上最後的綠地。", "as": "Rather than fulminate against his critics, the senator chose to mollify them, a judicious decision that helped assuage the anger of many of his constituents back home.", "at": "這位參議員沒有猛烈抨擊批評者，反而選擇安撫他們，這個明智的決定幫助平息了他許多家鄉選民的怒氣。"}, {"w": "scarify", "p": "v.", "d": "To criticize harshly; to wound with cutting words.", "c": "嚴厲批評；尖刻抨擊", "s": "The theater critic was known to scarify young playwrights in her reviews, using such cruel and cutting language that several promising writers quit the stage after reading what she had published about their debut work.", "t": "這位劇評家以在評論中嚴厲抨擊年輕劇作家而聞名，她用詞殘酷尖刻，好幾位前途看好的作家在讀了她對其處女作的評論後便離開了劇壇。", "as": "The editor would scarify any manuscript that seemed verbose, castigating authors whose prolix sentences obscured rather than clarified their ideas and wasted readers' valuable time.", "at": "這位編輯會嚴厲批評任何顯得冗長的稿件，痛斥那些用囉嗦句子掩蓋而非闡明自身想法、浪費讀者寶貴時間的作者。"}, {"w": "hebdomadal", "p": "adj.", "d": "Happening once a week; weekly.", "c": "每週的；每七天一次的", "s": "The science club holds hebdomadal meetings every Thursday afternoon, and members who miss more than two of these weekly sessions in a semester lose their place on the regional robotics competition team.", "t": "科學社每週四下午舉行每週例會，一學期內缺席這些每週聚會超過兩次的社員，將失去參加區域機器人競賽隊伍的資格。", "as": "The newspaper's hebdomadal column offered a cursory summary of the week's news, though its banal commentary rarely engaged the thoughtful readers who wanted genuine analysis.", "at": "這份報紙的每週專欄對一週新聞只做了粗略的摘要，其陳腔濫調的評論很少能吸引那些想要真正分析的有思想讀者。"}, {"w": "divagate", "p": "v.", "d": "To wander or stray, especially from the main topic.", "c": "離題；漫遊", "s": "Our history teacher tends to divagate from the lesson plan, wandering from the causes of the French Revolution into long stories about his travels in Paris, so we rarely finish a chapter on schedule.", "t": "我們的歷史老師常常偏離教學計畫，從法國大革命的起因扯到他在巴黎旅行的長篇故事，所以我們很少能按進度上完一章。", "as": "Speakers who divagate risk losing their audience; a discursive lecture full of tangential anecdotes rarely leaves students with a lucid understanding of the topic at hand.", "at": "說話離題的講者有失去聽眾的風險；一場充滿枝微末節軼事、東拉西扯的演講，很少能讓學生對眼前的主題有清楚的理解。"}, {"w": "iatrogenic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Caused by a doctor or by medical treatment.", "c": "醫源性的；因醫療引起的", "s": "Hospital reviewers found that some patients' infections were iatrogenic, caused not by their original illnesses but by contaminated equipment and unnecessary procedures performed during their treatment in the hospital itself.", "t": "醫院審查人員發現，部分病患的感染屬於醫源性感染，並非由原本的疾病所致，而是由院內治療期間受污染的器材與不必要的醫療程序所引起。", "as": "Doctors must remain circumspect when prescribing powerful drugs, since iatrogenic complications, though often negligible, can sometimes prove pernicious to elderly patients whose immune systems are already weakened.", "at": "醫師在開立強效藥物時必須謹慎，因為醫源性併發症雖然通常微不足道，有時卻會對免疫系統早已衰弱的年長病患造成嚴重危害。"}, {"w": "tergiversation", "p": "n.", "d": "Evasive shifting of position; abandoning a cause or side.", "c": "推託搪塞；變節", "s": "Reporters grew frustrated with the minister's constant tergiversation; whenever they asked whether he supported the new trade agreement, he gave vague, shifting answers and seemed to change his position from one week to the next.", "t": "記者們對這位部長不斷的推託閃躲感到挫折；每當他們詢問他是否支持新貿易協定時，他總是給出含糊、反覆的答案，立場似乎每週都在改變。", "as": "The politician's tergiversation on climate policy, which critics called rank duplicity, alienated voters who had admired his once resolute stance on renewable energy and conservation.", "at": "這位政客在氣候政策上的反覆搖擺被批評者稱為十足的表裡不一，疏遠了那些曾欣賞他在再生能源與環境保育議題上堅定立場的選民。"}]}, {"unit": 25, "level": 5, "cards": [{"w": "nacreous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having the shimmering, iridescent luster of mother-of-pearl.", "c": "珍珠母般的；珍珠光澤的", "s": "Marine biologists explained that oysters coat irritating grains of sand with layer after layer of a nacreous substance, gradually producing the smooth, rainbow-colored shine that makes pearls so valuable to jewelers.", "t": "海洋生物學家解釋，牡蠣會用一層又一層帶有珍珠光澤的物質包覆刺激性的沙粒，逐漸形成光滑、彩虹般的光澤，這正是珍珠對珠寶商如此珍貴的原因。", "as": "The nacreous clouds that appeared above Antarctica were so ethereal and refulgent that the scientists, normally stoic, paused their measurements simply to admire the shimmering colors.", "at": "出現在南極上空的珍珠母雲如此空靈而光彩奪目，連平時不動聲色的科學家們都暫停測量，只為欣賞那閃爍的色彩。"}, {"w": "fainéant", "p": "n.", "d": "An idle, lazy person who avoids work.", "c": "懶人；遊手好閒者", "s": "While his classmates volunteered to clean the beach, Leo lounged under an umbrella all afternoon, and by the end of the day everyone had labeled him a fainéant who would never lift a finger to help.", "t": "當同學們自願去清理海灘時，里歐整個下午都懶洋洋地躺在陽傘下，到了傍晚，大家都認定他是個遊手好閒、絕不會動一根手指幫忙的懶人。", "as": "Historians once dismissed the king as a fainéant who held a sinecure-like throne, but recent research suggests his apparent lethargy masked shrewd political machinations behind the scenes.", "at": "歷史學家曾把這位國王貶為一個坐擁閒差般王位的懶散之人，但近來的研究顯示，他表面上的怠惰其實掩蓋了幕後精明的政治謀略。"}, {"w": "hispid", "p": "adj.", "d": "Covered with stiff, bristly hairs.", "c": "有剛毛的；多硬毛的", "s": "Gardeners should wear gloves when handling the plant, because its stems and leaves are hispid, covered with stiff, prickly hairs that can irritate the skin and leave an itchy rash for several days.", "t": "園丁處理這種植物時應該戴上手套，因為它的莖和葉都長滿剛毛，那些堅硬扎人的毛會刺激皮膚，留下持續數天的發癢紅疹。", "as": "The botanist found the hispid caterpillar both fascinating and noisome, noting that its bristles, while innocuous-looking, could be quite deleterious to anyone who touched them carelessly.", "at": "這位植物學家覺得這隻多剛毛的毛毛蟲既迷人又令人討厭，並指出牠的剛毛雖然看似無害，卻可能對任何不小心觸碰牠的人造成相當的傷害。"}, {"w": "longanimity", "p": "n.", "d": "Patient endurance of hardship, injury, or offense.", "c": "堅忍；長久忍耐", "s": "The prisoner's longanimity astonished his guards; through twenty-seven years of harsh confinement he endured every insult and hardship calmly, never seeking revenge and emerging with his dignity and good will intact.", "t": "這名囚犯的堅忍令獄卒們驚嘆：在二十七年的嚴酷監禁中，他平靜地忍受每一次侮辱與苦難，從未尋求報復，出獄時尊嚴與善意依然完好無損。", "as": "Her longanimity in the face of constant calumny earned the approbation of even her former critics, who eventually conceded that her equanimity was genuine rather than feigned.", "at": "她面對接連不斷的誹謗時所展現的堅忍，甚至贏得了昔日批評者的讚許，他們最終承認她的沉著是真誠的，而非裝出來的。"}, {"w": "sciolist", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who pretends to be knowledgeable; a superficial scholar.", "c": "一知半解的人；假充內行者", "s": "The self-proclaimed history expert turned out to be a sciolist; he could recite a few impressive dates, but when students asked him basic questions about the causes of the war, his knowledge proved shallow.", "t": "這位自稱的歷史專家原來是個一知半解的人；他能背出幾個令人印象深刻的日期，但當學生問他有關戰爭起因的基本問題時，他的知識便顯得十分淺薄。", "as": "The sciolist's glib references to quantum physics impressed the gullible audience, but the erudite professor quickly exposed his superficial understanding with a few pointed questions.", "at": "這個一知半解者對量子物理信口開河的引用讓容易受騙的聽眾印象深刻，但那位學識淵博的教授只用了幾個尖銳的問題，就迅速揭穿了他膚淺的理解。"}, {"w": "propinquity", "p": "n.", "d": "Nearness in place, time, or relationship; proximity.", "c": "鄰近；親近", "s": "Sociologists have found that propinquity plays a surprising role in friendship: college students who live on the same dormitory floor are far more likely to become close friends than those who live across campus.", "t": "社會學家發現，鄰近性在友誼中扮演著出人意料的角色：住在同一層宿舍的大學生，比住在校園另一端的學生更有可能成為好友。", "as": "The propinquity of the two rival nations, together with their deep animosity, made a peaceful rapprochement seem almost chimerical to the diplomats sent to negotiate between them.", "at": "這兩個敵對國家地理位置相近，加上彼此根深柢固的敵意，使得和平和解在被派去居中斡旋的外交官眼中幾乎是空想。"}, {"w": "factitious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Artificial; produced deliberately rather than arising naturally.", "c": "人為的；虛假的", "s": "Economists argued that the sudden shortage of concert tickets was factitious, created on purpose by resellers who bought thousands of seats in minutes simply to drive prices up, not caused by genuine public demand.", "t": "經濟學家主張，演唱會門票的突然短缺是人為製造的，是黃牛在幾分鐘內搶購數千個座位、純粹為了哄抬價格所刻意造成的，而非真正的大眾需求所致。", "as": "The candidate's factitious outrage, carefully staged for the cameras, was soon exposed as specious, and reporters began to question whether his earlier fervent speeches had been sincere.", "at": "這位候選人為了鏡頭精心安排的虛假憤怒很快就被揭穿是做作的，記者們也開始質疑他先前那些熱切的演說是否出於真心。"}, {"w": "plexiform", "p": "adj.", "d": "Forming a complex, interwoven network, like a plexus.", "c": "叢狀的；網狀交織的", "s": "Under the microscope, the nerve fibers formed a plexiform pattern, branching and weaving through one another like a tangled web rather than running in neat, parallel lines as the students had expected.", "t": "在顯微鏡下，神經纖維呈現網狀交織的形態，彼此分支交錯有如糾纏的網，而不是像學生們預期的那樣排列成整齊的平行線。", "as": "The plexiform arrangement of the roots, so intricate as to seem almost inscrutable, allowed the ancient tree to remain impervious to storms that toppled younger trees nearby.", "at": "這棵古樹的根系呈網狀交織排列，錯綜複雜到幾乎難以看透，使它在附近較年輕的樹木被暴風吹倒時依然屹立不搖。"}, {"w": "susurrus", "p": "n.", "d": "A soft whispering or rustling sound; murmur.", "c": "沙沙聲；低語聲", "s": "As the lights dimmed before the concert began, a gentle susurrus spread through the audience, the quiet whispering of hundreds of people slowly fading into complete silence as the conductor raised his baton.", "t": "音樂會開始前燈光漸暗，觀眾席間傳來一陣輕柔的低語聲，數百人的竊竊私語逐漸消失，直到指揮舉起指揮棒時全場一片寂靜。", "as": "The soft susurrus of the wind through the pines provided a welcome respite from the cacophony of the city, and the hikers grew pensive as they walked.", "at": "風吹過松林的輕柔沙沙聲，讓人從城市的喧囂中得到難得的喘息，健行者們邊走邊陷入沉思。"}, {"w": "triturate", "p": "v.", "d": "To grind or crush into a fine powder.", "c": "研磨成粉；磨碎", "s": "Before mixing the medicine, the pharmacist used a mortar and pestle to triturate the hard tablets, grinding them into a fine powder that would dissolve easily in the syrup for the young patient.", "t": "在調配藥物之前，藥劑師用研缽與研杵把堅硬的藥片磨碎，研磨成能輕易溶於糖漿的細粉，以便給年幼的病患服用。", "as": "Medieval apothecaries would triturate dried herbs into powders they promoted as a panacea, though most of these nostrums had little efficacy against the diseases they claimed to cure.", "at": "中世紀的藥劑師會把乾燥草藥研磨成粉，並將其宣傳為萬靈丹，然而這些祕方對它們聲稱能治癒的疾病大多沒什麼療效。"}, {"w": "protean", "p": "adj.", "d": "Able to change form or adapt easily; highly versatile.", "c": "多變的；多才多藝的", "s": "The protean actor could play a cruel king one night and a shy schoolboy the next, transforming his voice, posture, and personality so completely that audiences often failed to recognize him.", "t": "這位多變的演員能在某晚飾演殘暴的國王，隔晚又演出害羞的學童，徹底轉換聲音、姿態與個性，觀眾常常認不出他來。", "as": "The virus proved protean, its mercurial mutations limiting the efficacy of each new vaccine and deeply frustrating the researchers who had long hoped for a lasting, effective treatment.", "at": "這種病毒證明是變化多端的，其反覆無常的突變限制了每一種新疫苗的效力，令長久以來期盼找到持久有效療法的研究人員深感挫折。"}, {"w": "crepitate", "p": "v.", "d": "To make a crackling or popping sound.", "c": "發出劈啪聲；嘎吱作響", "s": "As the campers tossed dry pine branches onto the fire, the burning wood began to crepitate loudly, popping and snapping so sharply that the younger children jumped back from the glowing flames.", "t": "當露營者把乾燥的松枝丟進火堆時，燃燒的木頭開始劈啪作響，爆裂聲如此尖銳，嚇得年幼的孩子們從熊熊火焰旁跳開。", "as": "Doctors listened as the patient's lungs began to crepitate, a salient sign that the infection was not transient but would require a protracted course of treatment.", "at": "醫師聽到病患的肺部開始發出細碎的劈啪聲，這是一個明顯的徵兆，表示感染並非短暫，而是需要長期的治療。"}, {"w": "noctivagant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Wandering about at night.", "c": "夜間遊蕩的；夜行的", "s": "Wildlife cameras revealed that the noctivagant red foxes in the suburb left their dens only after sunset, roaming through the neighborhood's gardens and alleys all night before disappearing again just before dawn.", "t": "野生動物攝影機顯示，郊區這些夜間遊蕩的赤狐只在日落後離開巢穴，整夜在社區的花園與巷弄間徘徊，直到天亮前才又消失無蹤。", "as": "The noctivagant poet, an itinerant soul who shunned diurnal routines, composed his most poignant verses while wandering alone through the empty, silent streets of the old city long after midnight.", "at": "這位夜間遊蕩的詩人是個居無定所的靈魂，避開白天的作息，常在午夜過後獨自漫步於老城區空蕩寂靜的街道上，寫下他最動人的詩句。"}, {"w": "fuliginous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Sooty or smoky; dark and murky.", "c": "煤煙的；烏黑的", "s": "During the Industrial Revolution, the skies above Manchester became fuliginous, as thousands of coal-burning factories filled the air with thick black smoke that stained buildings and darkened the sun for decades.", "t": "工業革命期間，曼徹斯特上空變得煙霧瀰漫，數以千計燒煤的工廠讓空氣中充滿濃厚的黑煙，數十年來不但燻黑了建築物，也遮蔽了陽光。", "as": "The fuliginous haze from the wildfire hung over the valley, making the air fetid and turbid, and officials urged residents to stay indoors until it cleared.", "at": "山火所產生的煙塵陰霾籠罩著山谷，使空氣惡臭而混濁，官員呼籲居民在空氣轉好之前待在室內。"}, {"w": "hortatory", "p": "adj.", "d": "Urging or encouraging someone to take action.", "c": "勸告的；激勵的", "s": "The principal's hortatory speech at the assembly urged every student to volunteer at least ten hours this semester, encouraging them to see community service not as a duty but as a chance to grow.", "t": "校長在朝會上發表激勵人心的演說，敦促每位學生這學期至少參與十小時的志工服務，鼓勵他們把社區服務視為成長的機會，而非義務。", "as": "The general's hortatory address galvanized his weary troops, whose lassitude gave way to alacrity as they prepared for the arduous march across the frozen mountains.", "at": "將軍激勵人心的講話振奮了疲憊的部隊，他們的倦怠轉為振奮，準備踏上翻越冰封山脈的艱苦行軍。"}, {"w": "heliolatry", "p": "n.", "d": "The worship of the sun.", "c": "太陽崇拜；拜日教", "s": "Archaeologists believe that heliolatry was central to the ancient Inca religion, since the empire's grandest temples were built to honor the sun god and were aligned with sunrise on the winter solstice.", "t": "考古學家認為，太陽崇拜是古代印加宗教的核心，因為該帝國最宏偉的神廟都是為了榮耀太陽神而建，並且與冬至的日出方向對齊。", "as": "Some scholars construe the ancient monument as evidence of heliolatry, though others dismiss this interpretation as mere conjecture, unsupported by any extant written records from the civilization that built it.", "at": "有些學者將這座古代遺跡解讀為太陽崇拜的證據，但其他人則認為這種詮釋不過是臆測，因為建造它的文明並沒有留下任何現存的文字紀錄可供佐證。"}, {"w": "sciamachy", "p": "n.", "d": "Fighting imaginary enemies; a pointless or futile struggle.", "c": "與假想敵作戰；徒勞的爭鬥", "s": "Critics called the senator's campaign against the nonexistent threat of robot voters a form of sciamachy, an exhausting battle against an imaginary enemy that wasted months of debate on a problem nobody had found.", "t": "批評者稱這位參議員對抗根本不存在的「機器人選民」威脅的行動是一種與假想敵的搏鬥，這場對抗虛構敵人的消耗戰在一個沒人發現過的問題上浪費了數月的辯論。", "as": "Much of the scholarly debate was mere sciamachy, a quixotic contest in which each side attacked arguments no rival had ever actually made, rendering the dispute utterly vacuous.", "at": "這場學術辯論大多只是與假想敵作戰，一場不切實際的較量，雙方都在攻擊對手從未真正提出過的論點，使整場爭論變得空洞無物。"}, {"w": "glabrous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having a smooth surface without hairs.", "c": "光滑無毛的；無毛的", "s": "Unlike its fuzzy relative the peach, the nectarine has glabrous skin, perfectly smooth and free of the soft hairs that cover a peach, which makes it easier to eat without peeling.", "t": "與表皮毛茸茸的近親桃子不同，油桃的果皮光滑無毛，完全沒有覆蓋在桃子上的細毛，因此不用削皮就能輕鬆食用。", "as": "The botanist contrasted the glabrous leaves of one species with the hispid foliage of its relative, a discernible difference that helped students learn the plants' complex nomenclature.", "at": "這位植物學家將某一物種光滑無毛的葉片與其近親多剛毛的葉子相對比，這個顯而易見的差異幫助學生學習這些植物複雜的命名法。"}, {"w": "pettifogger", "p": "n.", "d": "A petty, unscrupulous lawyer who quibbles over trivial details.", "c": "訟棍；愛在小事上爭辯的人", "s": "The client soon realized she had hired a pettifogger; instead of addressing the real issues in her case, her lawyer wasted hours arguing over trivial technicalities and padding his bill with pointless motions.", "t": "這位委託人很快就發現自己請到了一個訟棍；她的律師不但不處理案件中真正的問題，反而花好幾個小時爭論瑣碎的技術細節，並用毫無意義的動議灌水帳單。", "as": "The cunning pettifogger tried to obfuscate the facts with specious arguments, but the judge, losing patience, firmly admonished him to address the actual evidence before the jury.", "at": "這名狡猾的訟棍企圖用似是而非的論點混淆事實，但失去耐心的法官嚴正告誡他要在陪審團面前針對實際的證據來論述。"}, {"w": "epicene", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having characteristics of both sexes or neither; gender-neutral.", "c": "兼具兩性特徵的；中性的", "s": "Linguists note that English has few truly epicene pronouns, which is why many style guides now accept the singular \"they\" when a writer wishes to refer to a person without specifying gender.", "t": "語言學家指出，英文中真正中性的代名詞很少，這就是為什麼如今許多寫作風格指南接受使用單數的「they」，讓作者在提及某人時無須指明性別。", "as": "Elizabethan theater relied on epicene performers, since boys played every female role; this convention seems anomalous today but was perfectly mundane to audiences of that era.", "at": "伊莉莎白時代的戲劇仰賴兼具兩性特質的演員，因為所有女性角色都由男孩飾演；這種慣例在今日看來不尋常，但對當時的觀眾而言再平常不過。"}]}];
